 to a note\n\nOperator ruling 2026-08-11.\n\nD3 ratified, but the two halves get opposite treatment rather than a uniform\nre-scope. #372 (the spike) narrows hard to \"author a diagram and round-trip it\nback to the Mermaid canon\" — its rendering half already has a measured answer, so\nwhat is left is authoring and persistence, and a spike needs a question that can\nbe called pass or fail. #368 (the research) deliberately keeps its wide aperture:\nits weekly watch exists to catch a mentor changing direction, and the tracked\ncaveat is that Pocock has experimented with React-authored diagrams INSTEAD of\ntldraw — a ticket framed around \"tldraw for editing\" would point the watch away\nfrom the signal worth having. Spikes want narrow questions; research wants wide\napertures. The earlier draft narrowed both.\n\nThe ruling carries its own scope limit so it cannot be over-cited later: the\nviewing answer rests on one prototype, ~66 nodes, static layout, no persistence.\nIncremental re-layout, hit-testing past a few hundred nodes, undo, selection\ngroups, gesture parity, a11y on a raw SVG DOM and view-state persistence are all\nuntested.\n\nD4 demoted from Decisions to Notes. diagram-conventions.md already says canvas\nsurfaces are \"viewers/editors over the canon, never the store\" — it permits\nediting and forbids only ownership — so \"this one is read-only\" describes what\nwas built rather than constraining what gets built next. Left in Decisions it\nwould have been cited as a fleet prohibition on editable canvases that nobody\nruled.\n\nAlso records, under Not yet specified, that D3 assumes view and edit are\nseparable — the seam most likely to be wrong, since the Destination''s\nsnapshot-lineage target is a persistence problem neither side owns.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a6c36635160180ba9c1b3007da7337181d3fe8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/5a6c36635160180ba9c1b3007da7337181d3fe8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/939c2cd4e1910094ccd27e2ade96e02bb093ff02","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/939c2cd4e1910094ccd27e2ade96e02bb093ff02","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKDkzOWMyY2Q0ZTE5MTAwOTRjY2QyN2UyYWRlOTZlMDJiYjA5M2ZmMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/339b74fa028d965aefbd36ac785cc7b04699cec7","sha":"339b74fa028d965aefbd36ac785cc7b04699cec7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/339b74fa028d965aefbd36ac785cc7b04699cec7"}],"sha":"939c2cd4e1910094ccd27e2ade96e02bb093ff02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/939c2cd4e1910094ccd27e2ade96e02bb093ff02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/339b74fa028d965aefbd36ac785cc7b04699cec7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T20:07:41Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T20:08:59Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"decision(wayfinder): ratify D7/D8, close #340, re-scope #338 to the cadence question\n\nOperator rulings 2026-08-11 on cockpit-northstar-conversation.\n\nD7 ratified — threads keyed {global | repo} with a per-thread share-to-global\ntoggle; a focus change repoints the inspector and leaves the thread pinned to the\nscope it was opened in. Closes #340. Two residues are called out rather than\nfolded in: thread RETENTION is an undecided question (parked in Not yet specified,\nwants its own ticket — tracker numbers are not reservable, so it is not minted\nhere), and the store migration is delivery work for a roadmap slice, since\nchat-store.ts holds one unkeyed global thread today.\n\nD8 ratified — the fleet canvas is a main-column surface (>=700px comfortable,\n~560px workable) and the 372px rail holds inspector above threaded chat.\n\n#338 re-scoped, not closed. The original title asked two questions and the\nprototype answered only the placement one. The ticket is now \"does the ladder\ncadence survive a chat rail\", with the rail width a GIVEN rather than a variable:\nbuild the variants at 372px against the layout D8 fixed. #339 stays blocked behind\nit because voice still prejudges one-question-at-a-time.\n\nMap status charting -> working, now that a ticket has closed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"30bb6751ae7bd6c3c42bbd0d4a83d45e0c4ce650","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/30bb6751ae7bd6c3c42bbd0d4a83d45e0c4ce650"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/339b74fa028d965aefbd36ac785cc7b04699cec7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/339b74fa028d965aefbd36ac785cc7b04699cec7","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKDMzOWI3NGZhMDI4ZDk2NWFlZmJkMzZhYzc4NWNjN2IwNDY5OWNlYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/807b6c8ddc4735750bcdf2a8c5063fae8f33155b","sha":"807b6c8ddc4735750bcdf2a8c5063fae8f33155b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/807b6c8ddc4735750bcdf2a8c5063fae8f33155b"}],"sha":"339b74fa028d965aefbd36ac785cc7b04699cec7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/339b74fa028d965aefbd36ac785cc7b04699cec7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/807b6c8ddc4735750bcdf2a8c5063fae8f33155b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T17:42:20Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T17:43:17Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"feat(canon): generate D5 from the registry; close out cockpit-v2 wayfinder evidence\n\nLands the core-side half of the cockpit v2 design handoff (four items, one PR).\n\nD5 becomes generated. scripts/lib/fleet-map-d5.mjs reads the northstar registry and\nemits a dark-native mermaid fence (config: theme: dark — a light render in a dark\nsurface was a named prototype defect); scripts/fleet-map-d5.mjs appends it to\n~/selfco/diagrams/fleet-map.md per the standing file''s append discipline. Cluster\ngrouping stays a presentation constant inside the generator, not a data file: the\ncluster tier is designed-not-built (RFQ-004) and a new list would have become fleet\nenumeration surface #16. Unmapped registrations land in a visible Unclustered node\nplus a warning. Golden-file test + 6 behaviour tests. D6-D8 stay authored.\n\nWayfinder maps take evidence, not closures. cockpit-northstar-conversation records\nthe #338 measurement (canvas needs >=560px; the 372px rail gets inspector + threaded\nchat) and the #340 recommendation (keyed {global|repo} threads, focus-change pins the\nthread), as proposed-unratified D7/D8 with both tickets moved to \"answered — awaiting\nratification\"; #339 stays blocked until the operator rules. diagram-first-output\nrecords that a hand-rolled ~200-line SVG viewer carried 66 nodes, so tldraw is scoped\nto EDITABLE canvases only (D3/D4 proposed).\n\nTD-007: the cockpit fleet-structure pane joins the surface matrix as row 15,\nREGISTRY-GENERATED, with a reconcile step that catches a generated surface acquiring\na hand list — drift a name-diff cannot see.\n\nToken vocabulary registered as phase-1 read-only (/explain /ladder /gap /open\n/draft-handoff) with a capability class each. Core verbs as tokens are recorded as\nNOT registered and requiring a new operator decision, with the reasoning, so the\nabsence cannot later read as an oversight.\n\nAlso fixes trailing ''#'' comments in the registry that corrupted buddy-check''s parsed\nslug and tier (the frontmatter parser cannot strip them — values legitimately contain\n''#''). 3 deviations logged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nRebased onto the S3 domain-knowledge decomposition: GLOSSARY.md and\ndiagram-conventions.md edits moved to domain-knowledge/universal/, and\nchat-token-vocabulary.md now lives in domain-knowledge/apps/ with a\n\"morning-cockpit\" manifest entry and a flat symlink, so the installer ships it\nto the repo that implements the tokens.","tree":{"sha":"70d6257628cb10aebad4ecdd7e1950177e807126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/70d6257628cb10aebad4ecdd7e1950177e807126"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/807b6c8ddc4735750bcdf2a8c5063fae8f33155b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/807b6c8ddc4735750bcdf2a8c5063fae8f33155b","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKDgwN2I2YzhkZGM0NzM1NzUwYmNkZjJhOGM1MDYzZmFlOGYzMzE1NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/1a586db81030f9ee06ac2fc18efee08db7bcb73d","sha":"1a586db81030f9ee06ac2fc18efee08db7bcb73d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/1a586db81030f9ee06ac2fc18efee08db7bcb73d"}],"sha":"807b6c8ddc4735750bcdf2a8c5063fae8f33155b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/807b6c8ddc4735750bcdf2a8c5063fae8f33155b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/1a586db81030f9ee06ac2fc18efee08db7bcb73d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:39:29Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:40:41Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"data(northstar): file core decomposition as rm-l2-ojfbot PH7, slices S34-S39\n\nThe decomposition program has been running since 2026-08-08 with no tracker item\n— no issue, no roadmap slice — so three merged slices existed only as beads and\nPRs. This files the whole ladder.\n\nPH7 \"Core decomposition\" with S34-S39 mapping the ladder''s S1-S6:\n  S34 = fleet reconciler in shadow            merged (#436)\n  S35 = personal exile + attic + dead delete  merged (#438)\n  S36 = manifest-driven domain-knowledge      merged (#443)\n  S37 = decisions hygiene                     queued\n  S38 = honest caches                         queued\n  S39 = promote reconciler to blocking        queued\n\nFiled under ns:l2-ojfbot#P2 following the S32/S33 precedent — same TD-006/TD-007\nsubstrate lineage — rather than inventing a new northstar property. No northstar\nfile is touched and no current: is written; movement is proposed below for the\noperator, not asserted here.\n\nMovement chain continues the PH-series from S33''s 47, one point per slice.\nEach merged slice carries a check: that verifies the delivered state on disk;\nall three pass at this commit. S35''s first draft grepped for ''tbcony-job-target''\nand failed on the explanatory NOTE comment S2 deliberately left behind — corrected\nto assert the deleted PERSONAL_SRC machinery instead of the word.\n\nMovement proposal: ns:l2-ojfbot#P2 30 -> 50\n\nroadmap-lint --check and northstar-lint --check both exit 0 (57 slices, 0 errors).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6b584db08c9a6f9af97e5c967ba8517f20d7b962","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/6b584db08c9a6f9af97e5c967ba8517f20d7b962"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/1a586db81030f9ee06ac2fc18efee08db7bcb73d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/1a586db81030f9ee06ac2fc18efee08db7bcb73d","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKDFhNTg2ZGI4MTAzMGY5ZWUwNmFjMmZjMThlZmVlMDhkYjdiY2I3M2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/870c3a58f99acc11e2562c805ffcaed63a2799a8","sha":"870c3a58f99acc11e2562c805ffcaed63a2799a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/870c3a58f99acc11e2562c805ffcaed63a2799a8"}],"sha":"1a586db81030f9ee06ac2fc18efee08db7bcb73d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/1a586db81030f9ee06ac2fc18efee08db7bcb73d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/870c3a58f99acc11e2562c805ffcaed63a2799a8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:34:47Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:35:57Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"refactor(core): manifest-driven domain-knowledge, universal/ + apps/ (decomposition S3)\n\ndomain-knowledge/ was a flat pile of 26 files, and what shipped where was\nasserted twice inside install-agents.sh: a UNIVERSAL=() array and a\ncase \"$REPO_NAME\" switch. Nothing tied either to the files on disk.\n\ndomain-knowledge/manifest.json is now the single source of truth. Sources move\ninto universal/ (13 files, shipped to every repo) and apps/ (13 files, shipped\nonly to the repo they map to). Both hardcoded lists are deleted; the installer\nreads the manifest, resolving repo-name aliases from it.\n\nTargets are unchanged: every repo still receives a FLAT domain-knowledge/<file>.\nCore keeps that same flat view via tracked symlinks into universal//apps/, so all\n~77 existing references keep resolving and no path rewrite was needed. Always\nreference the flat path — a universal/ or apps/ path breaks in sibling repos.\n\nFixes a live bug the manifest surfaced: coding-standards.md,\ndiagram-conventions.md and opm-modeling.md are read by fleet-distributed skills\n(/tdd, /pr-review, /diagram, /doc-refactor, /skill-loader, /vault, /opm) but were\nnever in UNIVERSAL, so all 30 sibling repos pointed at missing files —\ncoding-standards.md declares itself \"read... in any ojfbot repo\" in its own first\nline. Verified missing in blogengine before fixing. Also maps four files that\nbelonged to nobody: corereader-ux-research (core-reader), shell-mayor-spec and\nshell-mf-integration (shell), daily-cleaner-staleness-spec (daily-logger).\n\nDeleting the case-switch made the S1 reconciler report that surface UNPARSED —\nworking as designed. Retargeted it to the manifest (parseInstallCaseSwitch ->\nparseDomainKnowledgeManifest) with fixture and tests updated.\n\nVerified: installer links 13 universal + mapped app files, resolves the\ntripplanner alias, idempotent (0 created / 116 already-linked), zero dead\nsymlinks in installed targets; fleet-manifest drift identical to the origin/main\nbaseline apart from that surface''s own rename; full suite 542 passed / 0 failed;\nlint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"189855efc9d3d41ac7fd512aebd0100d9af36e8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/189855efc9d3d41ac7fd512aebd0100d9af36e8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/870c3a58f99acc11e2562c805ffcaed63a2799a8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/870c3a58f99acc11e2562c805ffcaed63a2799a8","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKDg3MGMzYTU4Zjk5YWNjMTFlMjU2MmM4MDVmZmNhZWQ2M2EyNzk5YTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/e12805cb01ef37458474041be39a5eed9ece4c29","sha":"e12805cb01ef37458474041be39a5eed9ece4c29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/e12805cb01ef37458474041be39a5eed9ece4c29"}],"sha":"870c3a58f99acc11e2562c805ffcaed63a2799a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/870c3a58f99acc11e2562c805ffcaed63a2799a8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_ur