/api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/322efd948cbff7c8fa21da0ca12207ca57c4bd4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T23:44:48Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T23:49:50Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"fix(workflows): await the bead event-log write instead of firing and forgetting\n\nFilesystemBeadStore.create/update/close fired appendEventLog() without awaiting\nit, then relied on a pendingWrites/trackWrite/drainPendingWrites() apparatus and\nper-test-file teardown discipline to paper over the consequences.\n\nTwo real defects, not just a test flake:\n- events are lost if the process exits before an unawaited write lands;\n- the write races a recursive fs.rm(root), re-creating events/<date>.jsonl\n  between rm''s unlink and its rmdir. That surfaced as the intermittent\n  `ENOTEMPTY: rmdir ''.../events''` on PR #103 and again on PR #392.\n\nAwaiting removes the race by construction, so the whole drain apparatus goes\nwith it (29 lines out, 10 in) along with both test-side drain calls. Confirmed\nno consumer of drainPendingWrites() outside the package before removing it.\n\nLocked in with three `event log durability` tests. Negative control verified\nindependently: reverting to `void this.appendEventLog(...)` fails exactly 2 of\nthem. Full suite 541 passed / 0 failed; no measurable cost to awaiting.\n\nSalvaged from the abandoned claude/gifted-lamarr-05695a worktree, where this sat\nuncommitted while its 12 bead commits went stale. Session ledger entries carried\ninto implementation-notes.md, including a correction: that session''s note says\n\"all 10 test-side drain calls\" were deleted, but only 2 ever existed on main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3ae5d44ddb5fdf135b64b8a885ed0dbdc3f0f322","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/3ae5d44ddb5fdf135b64b8a885ed0dbdc3f0f322"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/322efd948cbff7c8fa21da0ca12207ca57c4bd4b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/322efd948cbff7c8fa21da0ca12207ca57c4bd4b","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKDMyMmVmZDk0OGNiZmY3YzhmYTIxZGEwY2ExMjIwN2NhNTdjNGJkNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/5745933a06f7c6f3dc8480b5c74f76682a96f751","sha":"5745933a06f7c6f3dc8480b5c74f76682a96f751","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/5745933a06f7c6f3dc8480b5c74f76682a96f751"}],"sha":"322efd948cbff7c8fa21da0ca12207ca57c4bd4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/322efd948cbff7c8fa21da0ca12207ca57c4bd4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/5745933a06f7c6f3dc8480b5c74f76682a96f751/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T22:11:34Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T23:37:36Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"refactor(core): personal exile + attic + dead-structure delete (decomposition S2)\n\nThree cleanups that all reduce what core carries, gated on S1 (695bb3c).\n\nPersonal exile:\n- core/personal-knowledge/ (16 entries) moved to ~/selfco/career/, gitignored at\n  both ends. No git surgery — the dir was never tracked.\n- install-agents.sh §5 DROPPED rather than retargeted. It distributed exactly one\n  file (tbcony-job-target.md, superseded 2026-02-27) into 30 repos, and no skill\n  or script read it at that path.\n- frame-os-context.md: career framing stripped, product context kept. That file is\n  symlinked fleet-wide, so job-target framing reached every repo.\n- Skills that read personal-knowledge/ retargeted to ~/selfco/career/.\n\nAttic:\n- 9 dated audits + SURVEY.md moved to docs/audits/ with an index README.\n  CLAUDE-MD-ROLLOUT.md and implementation-notes.md stay (script-read state).\n\nDead structure:\n- Deleted empty skills/, packages/cli, packages/vscode-extension (history preserves\n  them); fixed every README/docs/CLAUDE.md claim about the CLI and VS Code extension.\n- Dropped skills/ from the /techdebt allowlist (source + docs), which had drifted\n  from ALLOWED_ROOTS in three places.\n\nruns/ was NOT deleted from .gitignore: writeRun() in utils/runs.ts creates it at\nruntime from runner.ts. It is a live output dir, not dead structure.\n\nVerified: typecheck + build clean; vitest 538 passed / 0 failed; fleet-manifest\noutput byte-identical to the 695bb3c baseline (zero new drift); installer idempotent\n(115 created -> 0 created / 112 already-linked) with zero dead symlinks and no\npersonal-knowledge/ created.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1317e6c0907ebe0f6a7102e6ad1ad48c1afef9ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/1317e6c0907ebe0f6a7102e6ad1ad48c1afef9ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/5745933a06f7c6f3dc8480b5c74f76682a96f751","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscription