9f75e3083c32f204f6b8d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T19:22:37Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T19:38:54Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"adopt-stack: mattpocock/skills v1.2 absorbed (D37–D43)\n\nPin 84fdeff (v1.2.3, 2026-08-06). Zero upstream files enter the tree.\n\n- /wait-what (new, user-scope): comprehension repair; ≤4-line body by design;\n  complement to /caveman (listener-state vs output-register)\n- /to-questionnaire (new, user-scope): async discovery questionnaire;\n  grill the send, not the subject\n- CONTEXT.md convention materialized: root glossary + bounded → deeper: pointers;\n  loader-manifest role rejected (stays in CLAUDE.md per ADR-0081);\n  core seeded; ADR draft context-md-glossary-pointer-convention\n- /grill-with-docs: frontier-rounds pacing w/ independence guard (D41);\n  CONTEXT.md path re-pointed domain-knowledge/ → root\n- /investigate: redaction-before-showing principle (D42)\n- Plugin-channel install REJECTED (D43, reaffirms ADR-0083); compensating\n  weekly upstream watch routine scheduled separately\n- /wizard: ABSORB recorded, build deferred to tracked follow-up (D39)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"605d49303035199102b25be2acd75f257b222830","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/605d49303035199102b25be2acd75f257b222830"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/f505c2f4f25e8819519f75e3083c32f204f6b8d8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/f505c2f4f25e8819519f75e3083c32f204f6b8d8","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKGY1MDVjMmY0ZjI1ZTg4MTk1MTlmNzVlMzA4M2MzMmYyMDRmNmI4ZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/24647cf5aced25de076755a953d293569c3fcce4","sha":"24647cf5aced25de076755a953d293569c3fcce4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/24647cf5aced25de076755a953d293569c3fcce4"}],"sha":"f505c2f4f25e8819519f75e3083c32f204f6b8d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/f505c2f4f25e8819519f75e3083c32f204f6b8d8"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/24647cf5aced25de076755a953d293569c3fcce4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T03:02:52Z","email":"wedge.freeze-1x@icloud.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T03:04:05Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"wayfinder: chart teach-persistence map (#412)\n\n/teach shipped and was used three times the same day. The write half is mechanized; the read\nhalf is a paragraph, and learning records carry no comprehension data — the TD-006 shape\nreproduced inside an architecture built to prevent it.\n\nMotivating evidence: the corpus''s first real comprehension data, a 0/3, had nowhere durable to\ngo and was hand-written into a record. Read as a placement failure, not a comprehension one.\n\nDestination grilled with the operator: full loop (record then place from it), files canonical\nwith the app as an appending view, hosted on the Pi, anchored to ns:l1-core#P5 whose target\nalready requires capture quality be green before uplift is published.\n\n8 tickets, 4 on the frontier. Host state measured and it is the biggest exposed risk: the Pi''s\nvault is behind, has no teach/ directory, and lists no timers.\n\nZero tickets resolved — charting only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"20a73a605e1c916348111844c9895ffed0237518","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/20a73a605e1c916348111844c9895ffed0237518"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/24647cf5aced25de076755a953d293569c3fcce4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/24647cf5aced25de076755a953d293569c3fcce4","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKDI0NjQ3Y2Y1YWNlZDI1ZGUwNzY3NTVhOTUzZDI5MzU2OWMzZmNjZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/6cfeb67edd2b48d19d3182ef6d61ec7deeefefc5","sha":"6cfeb67edd2b48d19d3182ef6d61ec7deeefefc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/6cfeb67edd2b48d19d3182ef6d61ec7deeefefc5"}],"sha":"24647cf5aced25de076755a953d293569c3fcce4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/24647cf5aced25de076755a953d293569c3fcce4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/6cfeb67edd2b48d19d3182ef6d61ec7deeefefc5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T02:40:51Z","email":"wedge.freeze-1x@icloud.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T02:42:02Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"fix(teach): references default to markdown, and stop silently dropping them\n\nSecond /teach invocation authored a markdown reference. The deposit dropped it without an\nerror — classifyArtifacts filtered reference/ to .html only, so the dry run reported\n''1 lesson'' and no reference.\n\nTwo problems. The filter was too narrow, and the convention behind it was wrong for this\nfleet. D24 says reference/*.html; D24''s own argument overturns it. Because a reference is the\nartifact most likely to be reopened, its format is decided by where it gets reopened — the\nvault — and Obsidian will not render a standalone .html as a page (the R5 finding that put\nteach/index.md in markdown). An HTML reference is an attachment you must bounce to a browser:\nthe worst handling for a desk copy.\n\nMarkdown is now the default and links into the vault with wikilinks. HTML stays accepted for\ngenuinely print-quality cheat-sheets, where layout carries meaning. Deliberate divergence,\nsame class as D25.\n\nWorth noting the shape: an artifact vanished with nothing emitted, and the reconciler could not\nhave caught it because the lesson still deposited. Silent drops are what this architecture is\nsupposed to prevent.\n\n38 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4408d7fafbaf7171118cd57286940afeffb4641b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/4408d7fafbaf7171118cd57286940afeffb4641b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/6cfeb67edd2b48d19d3182ef6d61ec7deeefefc5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/6cfeb67edd2b48d19d3182ef6d61ec7deeefefc5","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKDZjZmViNjdlZGQyYjQ4ZDE5ZDMxODJlZjZkNjFlYzdkZWVlZmVmYzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/6d13e38b752bc140e6556f70b1f985372e7eb64e","sha":"6d13e38b752bc140e6556f70b1f985372e7eb64e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/6d13e38b752bc140e6556f70b1f985372e7eb64e"}],"sha":"6cfeb67edd2b48d19d3182ef6d61ec7deeefefc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/6cfeb67edd2b48d19d3182ef6d61ec7deeefefc5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/6d13e38b752bc140e6556f70b1f985372e7eb64e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T02:24:20Z","email":"wedge.freeze-1x@icloud.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T02:25:32Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"fix(teach): quiz runs without JavaScript — the side panel never executes it\n\nOperator reported lesson 0001''s quiz buttons did nothing on first real /teach use.\n\nCause: the side panel renders a lesson as a static snapshot. Inlined CSS applies; the inline\nscript never runs. This inverts #386, which measured in a browser and concluded ''presentation\nis the fragile part, not interactivity — the inline quiz JS survives.'' In the surface the map''s\nDestination actually targets, presentation survives and interactivity dies.\n\n#386''s stylesheet ruling is untouched and still correct — self-contained still wins, and that\nis why the CSS was there to survive at all.\n\nQuiz is now radio inputs + :checked selectors: no JS, keyboard-reachable, works in the side\npanel, a browser, an Obsidian attachment, and print (where explanations show unconditionally).\nlesson-format.md documents the pattern, the markup invariants the selectors depend on, and the\nmeasurement behind it.\n\nAlso logs the deposit''s missing supersession path, found by the same invocation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4f0abd5966b21bc91f357763899311065283157","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/e4f0abd5966b21bc91f357763899311065283157"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/6d13e38b752bc140e6556f70b1f985372e7eb64e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/6d13e38b752bc140e6556f70b1f985372e7eb64e","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKDZkMTNlMzhiNzUyYmMxNDBlNjU1NmY3MGIxZjk4NTM3MmU3ZWI2NGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/d21fadca953464e2c30195ebe8473058e14f4390","sha":"d21fadca953464e2c30195ebe8473058e14f4390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/d21fadca953464e2c30195ebe8473058e14f4390"}],"sha":"6d13e38b752bc140e6556f70b1f985372e7eb64e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/6d13e38b752bc140e6556f70b1f985372e7eb64e"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/d21fadca953464e2c30195ebe8473058e14f4390/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T01:56:27Z","email":"wedge.freeze-1x@icloud.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T01:57:20Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"adr(teach-corpus-deposit-architecture): record decayed evidence, don''t silently edit it\n\nA concurrent vault session committed both ~/selfco/diagrams/ files (877e93f) hours after\nthis decision merged, so the ''untracked'' row no longer reproduces. Flagged in that session''s\ndeviation log.\n\nThe load-bearing measurement is unaffected — 0 ledger rows record a diagram deposit, then and\nnow — so the ruling stands. Marking the decay in place rather than rewriting the table: this\ndecision is specifically about mechanisms that fail without anyone noticing, and a record whose\ncited evidence quietly stops reproducing is how a ruling becomes folklore.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a755d641d383dc11c04e88b16e6317fe2734af49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/a755d641d383dc11c04e88b16e6317fe2734af49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/d21fadca953464e2c30195ebe8473058e14f4390","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/d21fadca953464e2c30195ebe8473058e14f4390","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKGQyMWZhZGNhOTUzNDY0ZTJjMzAxOTVlYmU4NDczMDU4ZTE0ZjQzOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/a546db40a7307c9606d0e7771aa45feb29485e07","sha":"a546db40a7307c9606d0e7771aa45feb29485e07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/a546db40a7307c9606d0e7771aa45feb29485e07"}],"sha":"d21fadca953464e2c30195ebe8473058e14f4390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/d21fadca953464e2c30195ebe8473058e14f4390"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/a546db40a7307c9606d0e7771aa45feb29485e07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T01:50:30Z","email":"wedge.freeze-1x@icloud.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T01:51:56Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"feat(teach): build /teach — workspace, lesson authoring, and a deposit that emits evidence\n\nEnacts the decided subset of the teach-in-the-loop map: D18-D25 (#380), the #386\nself-containment amendment, #382''s deposit architecture, and #384''s placement authority.\nThe five open tickets (#383/#385/#391/#393/#406) do not gate this slice.\n\nThe load-bearing piece is the deposit, not the skill prose. A worktree is disposable by\ndefinition, so a convention-based deposit loses the lesson silently — measured: /diagram''s\ndeposit is a prose principle and ~/selfco/diagrams/ holds 2 files, untracked, with 0 ledger\nrows, against 540/194/90/60 rows in the four hook-emitted channels.\n\nSo deposit.mjs performs three acts that ship together (#382 R2/R5): copy artifacts to\n~/selfco/teach/<topic-slug>/, append harness:lesson-deposited to teach-sessions.jsonl, and\nappend the teach/index.md entry. It refuses to emit when there is nothing to deposit — an\nempty deposit is a failure, and a row claiming otherwise would launder it into evidence.\n\nEmission alone is not enough: it makes a performed deposit visible and a skipped one\ninvisible, which is how TD-006 ran 96 days unnoticed. reconcile-teach-deposits.mjs compares\npushed teach/* branches against deposit rows and reports orphan branches, empty deposits,\nand orphan deposits. SHADOW per adr:control-gated-slices — reports, never blocks, exits 0.\n\ninline-css.mjs enacts #386: assets/lesson.css is the authoring source, the shipped lesson is\nbuild output with CSS inlined. It leaves an unresolvable link in place rather than shipping a\nsilent Times/8px fallback.\n\nCatalog entry is scope:[\"user\"] so install-agents.sh --user-scope symlinks it fleet-wide.\nNot added to CLAUDE.md — neither /merge-quiz nor /diagram is registered there; the catalog is\nthe registry (ADR-0081 loading discipline).\n\n36 new tests, 524 passing overall; typecheck and lint clean.\n\nRefs #382, #384, #380, #386\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"18ee87b84d83d303d124a2877032fc78328198a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/18ee87b84d83d303d124a2877032fc78328198a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/a546db40a7307c9606d0e7771aa45feb29485e07","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/a546db40a7307c9606d0e7771aa45feb29485e07","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKGE1NDZkYjQwYTczMDdjOTYwNmQwZTc3NzFhYTQ1ZmViMjk0ODVlMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/bddcc676d67faa0af36eb9d8b7e18ee4859d595a","sha":"bddcc676d67faa0af36eb9d8b7e18ee4859d595a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/bddcc676d67faa0af36eb9d8b7e18ee4859d595a"}],"sha":"a546db40a7307c9606d0e7771aa45feb29485e07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/a546db40a7307c9606d0e7771aa45feb29485e07"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/bddcc676d67faa0af36eb9d8b7e18ee4859d595a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:05:32Z","email":"wedge.freeze-1x@icloud.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T23:06:57Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"wayfinder(teach-in-the-loop): resolve #382 — teach corpus is a sink whose deposit emits evidence\n\nThe operator ruled the location (per-repo worktree authoring → ~/selfco/teach/ corpus;\nsibling repo rejected). This resolves what was left: the deposit mechanism, branch\ndisposition, learning-record location, read path, D6, and the vault schema rows.\n\nThe /diagram precedent cited in support of the location was measured and is the cautionary\ncase, not the reassuring one: its deposit is a prose principle, and ~/selfco/diagrams/ holds\n2 files (both stamped the hour the convention was written), untracked, with 0 ledger rows\nrecording a deposit — against 540 / 194 / 90 / 60 rows in the four hook-emitted channels.\n\nRulings: deposit = skill step emitting harness:lesson-deposited + a shadow reconciler that\nflags its absence (TD-006''s failure was the unwatched absence, which emission alone misses);\nauthoring branch pushed-never-merged per #386, so a miss is recoverable and the reconciler\nhas a left-hand side; learning records as files under teach/<topic-slug>/learning-records/,\nclosing the #382↔#384 seam by role not duplication; teach/index.md appended by the same\nemitting step, since Obsidian won''t render a standalone .html as a page; corpus keyed by\ntopic slug per adr:adr-slug-identity; D6 answered by a stated test (no claim/assignment/\nclosure state → sink, not surface).\n\nAlso repairs the dropped diagrams/ row in the vault template: ADR-0088 exists to prevent\nexactly that loss and the row was dropped anyway, within a day, in the same table.\n\nGraduates the trigger-points fog to #406 — the map''s own condition (corpus-location and\nZPD-sensor both closed) is now met.\n\nRecord: decisions/adr/draft-teach-corpus-deposit-architecture.md\nCloses #382\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0901a700a8bd4f56ef42f3f677979db7b893f1fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/0901a700a8bd4f56ef42f3f677979db7b893f1fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/bddcc676d67faa0af36eb9d8b7e18ee4859d595a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/bddcc676d67faa0af36eb9d8b7e18ee4859d595a","node_id":"C_kwDORWW6tdoAKGJkZGNjNjc2ZDY3ZmFhMGFmMzZlYjlkOGI3ZTE4ZWU0ODU5ZDU5NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/core/commit/9eae619379e8d0a43f57849d635c89f94eb4d953","sha":"9eae619379e8d0a43f57849d635c89f94eb4d953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/9eae619379e8d0a43f57849d635c89f94eb4d953"}],"sha":"bddcc676d67faa0af36eb9d8b7e18ee4859d595a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/bddcc676d67faa0af36eb9d8b7e18ee4859d595a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/commits/9eae619379e8d0a43f57849d635c89f94eb4d953/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T22:52:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T22:57:09Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"wayfinder(teach-in-the-loop): resolve #384 — heatmap augments ZPD placement, never rules its own uplift\n\nRuling on the ZPD-sensor ticket: NOT AS-IS. The merge-quiz comprehension\nheatmap augments D22''s per-workspace records+mission floor and never\noverrides it (R1, min-n gated); P5''s uplift is read only from a\npre-registered holdout of cells placement did not select (R2); cells\nre-key to bounded context x mode with repo demoted to metadata (R3);\nlearning records stay files-canonical with a lesson-served ledger event\nas the machine index (R4); cold start is a min-n gate with no backfill\n(R5); the P5 text divergence is noted and its amendment deferred to the\nbuilding slice (R6).\n\nMeasured: the heatmap is empty — 0 harness:quiz-taken rows, 0 cells, 0\ndomain values ever written, across 89 observations and 25 qualifying\nmerges in 5 days. Per-question difficulty/facet is generated then\ndiscarded at --record, so a 60 from missing hard questions is\nindistinguishable from a 60 from missing easy ones.\n\nDid not touch the comprehension-GATE question (parked in #366 fog).\nUnblocks #385.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7597ce7509270a49ac042d1a4dfef0fbbb54cdb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/trees/7597ce7509270a49ac042d1a4dfef0fbbb54cdb9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/core/git/commits/9eae619379e8d0a43f57849d635c89f94eb4d953","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.