s/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esola-thomas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esola-thomas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/esola-thomas","id":93721212,"login":"esola-thomas","node_id":"U_kgDOBZYSfA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esola-thomas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esola-thomas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esola-thomas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esola-thomas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/esola-thomas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/esola-thomas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Huitzo-Inc/pack-claude-env/commits/eaa4243d4eca48b71c95745a2803ee16085cb794/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T22:48:26Z","email":"93721212+esola-thomas@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ernesto Sola-Thomas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T22:48:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(claude): correct the .huitzo-dashboard token-resolution claim (#15)\n\n* fix(claude): correct the .huitzo-dashboard token-resolution claim\n\nSix places across the seed told agents the `.huitzo-dashboard` wrapper class\nwas required because brand tokens would not resolve without it. Against the\nshipped SDK that is false, and it was never true at any version: tokens are\ndeclared on `:root` inside `@layer huitzo-tokens`, so they resolve\ndocument-wide as soon as `@huitzo/dashboard-sdk-react/styles` is imported\nonce. No shipped CSS selects the class.\n\nThe wrapper stays mandatory -- it is the scope a dashboard''s own CSS nests\nunder (the CLI scaffold''s index.css sets the base font/colour on it and nests\nits button/a rules beneath), so those rules style the dashboard tree and never\nthe Hub shell. Only the stated reason changes.\n\nAlso corrected: hub-contract.md claimed theme switching depends on the wrapper\n(it does not -- `data-theme` is set on `<html>`, as /dashboard-dev already\ndocumented), and dashboard-e2e told readers to set `data-theme` on the wrapper.\n\nAdds a regression guard to scripts/check_api_surface.py that asserts the\nmechanism rather than the wording: `:root` must live inside\n`@layer huitzo-tokens` and declare the core tokens, and no `.huitzo-dashboard`\nrule may declare custom properties. A wording-only guard in validate_env.py\nwould not have worked -- it exempts any line containing the cross mark, and two\nof the six claims sit on such lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QZ7w6ZGyiXTLtCsiFxrZMf\n\n* fix(claude): tighten wrapper rationale and reserve \"hook\" for data-hz-*\n\nFollow-up to a1be7f6, from an adversarial review of that commit.\n\n- dashboard-design.md: the Theme-awareness bullet still carried the inverted\n  leakage causality (\"it scopes your own CSS so nothing leaks into the Hub\n  host\"). Dropping the wrapper does not cause leakage -- leakage is prevented\n  by the scaffold PREFIXING its selectors, so without the wrapper those\n  prefixed rules simply stop matching. Reworded to match the sibling copies,\n  and it no longer contradicts the anti-pattern bullet below it.\n- check_api_surface.py: the new guard called the wrapper a \"CSS-scoping hook\".\n  \"Hook\" is reserved in this codebase for the `data-hz-*` DOM contract --\n  TemplateFrame states \"the stable hooks are the `data-hz-*` attributes\" and\n  that class names are explicitly not stable. Now \"CSS scope selector\".\n\nGuard re-validated against six cases: passes real-shaped and minified CSS and\na comment mentioning the class, and goes red when the wrapper declares custom\nproperties, when tokens move out of the cascade layer, and when a token is\nsilently dropped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QZ7w6ZGyiXTLtCsiFxrZMf\n\n* fix(scripts): drop monorepo-internal doc paths from the vendored legal script\n\n`validate_env.py`''s information-boundary check has been failing on\n`scripts/check_legal_headers.py:13,14,17`, which cite\n`docs/governance/ip-protection.md` -- a path that exists only in the private\nmonorepo. This repository is public, and its own contributor rule is \"only\npublic knowledge, no private repository links\".\n\nThis is a pre-existing breakage on `main`, not introduced here: CI run #2\n(18dc0ee) was green and run #3 (00b0451, \"Enhance documentation for\ncheck_legal_headers.py\") went red by expanding this docstring and reintroducing\nthe internal paths -- the same thing 18dc0ee had removed, noting at the time\nthat the \"vendored legal script no longer exempt (its header no longer names\ninternal docs)\".\n\nFixed rather than left red, because it blocks this PR''s `structure, accuracy\nand boundary checks` job and the fix is three lines. The `Implements:` block\ngoes away entirely, which also matches the house style -- this was the only\nscript in scripts/ carrying one; check_links.py, simulate_seed.py,\ncheck_api_surface.py and validate_env.py all use plain Module/Description/Usage.\nNo behaviour change: the docstring is the entire diff.\n\nVerified locally, the full CI job: check_legal_headers.py OK, validate_env\nclean (was 3 findings), `bash -n claude/hooks/*.sh`, test_hooks.sh and\nsimulate_seed.py all exit 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QZ7w6ZGyiXTLtCsiFxrZMf\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7c3ddcc109a9e64739aae5f81876cf5633e62f45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Huitzo-Inc/pack-claude-env/git/trees/7c3ddcc109a9e64739aae5f81876cf5633e62f45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Huitzo-Inc/pack-claude-env/git/commits/eaa4243d4eca48b71c95745a2803ee16085cb794","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c3ddcc109a9e64739aae5f81876cf5633e62f45\nparent 00b0451e2121797cb9aa8fc825bd1ff91b230d07\nauthor Ernesto Sola-Thomas <93721212+esola-thomas@users.noreply.github.com> 1789685306 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789685306 -0400\n\nfix(claude): correct the .huitzo-dashboard token-resolution claim (#15)\n\n* fix(claude): correct the .huitzo-dashboard token-resolution claim\n\nSix places across the seed told agents the `.huitzo-dashboard` wrapper class\nwas required because brand tokens would not resolve without it. Against the\nshipped SDK that is false, and it was never true at any version: tokens are\ndeclared on `:root` inside `@layer huitzo-tokens`, so they resolve\ndocument-wide as soon as `@huitzo/dashboard-sdk-react/styles` is imported\nonce. No shipped CSS selects the class.\n\nThe wrapper stays mandatory -- it is the scope a dashboard''s own CSS nests\nunder (the CLI scaffold''s index.css sets the base font/colour on it and nests\nits button/a rules beneath), so those rules style the dashboard tree and never\nthe Hub shell. Only the stated reason changes.\n\nAlso corrected: hub-contract.md claimed theme switching depends on the wrapper\n(it does not -- `data-theme` is set on `<html>`, as /dashboard-dev already\ndocumented), and dashboard-e2e told readers to set `data-theme` on the wrapper.\n\nAdds a regression guard to scripts/check_api_surface.py that asserts the\nmechanism rather than the wording: `:root` must live inside\n`@layer huitzo-tokens` and declare the core tokens, and no `.huitzo-dashboard`\nrule may declare custom properties. A wording-only guard in validate_env.py\nwould not have worked -- it exempts any line containing the cross mark, and two\nof the six claims sit on such lines.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QZ7w6ZGyiXTLtCsiFxrZMf\n\n* fix(claude): tighten wrapper rationale and reserve \"hook\" for data-hz-*\n\nFollow-up to a1be7f6, from an adversarial review of that commit.\n\n- dashboard-design.md: the Theme-awareness bullet still carried the inverted\n  leakage causality (\"it scopes your own CSS so nothing leaks into the Hub\n  host\"). Dropping the wrapper does not cause leakage -- leakage is prevented\n  by the scaffold PREFIXING its selectors, so without the wrapper those\n  prefixed rules simply stop matching. Reworded to match the sibling copies,\n  and it no longer contradicts the anti-pattern bullet below it.\n- check_api_surface.py: the new guard called the wrapper a \"CSS-scoping hook\".\n  \"Hook\" is reserved in this codebase for the `data-hz-*` DOM contract --\n  TemplateFrame states \"the stable hooks are the `data-hz-*` attributes\" and\n  that class names are explicitly not stable. Now \"CSS scope selector\".\n\nGuard re-validated against six cases: passes real-shaped and minified CSS and\na comment mentioning the class, and goes red when the wrapper declares custom\nproperties, when tokens move out of the cascade layer, and when a token is\nsilently dropped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QZ7w6ZGyiXTLtCsiFxrZMf\n\n* fix(scripts): drop monorepo-internal doc paths from the vendored legal script\n\n`validate_env.py`''s information-boundary check has been failing on\n`scripts/check_legal_headers.py:13,14,17`, which cite\n`docs/governance/ip-protection.md` -- a path that exists only in the private\nmonorepo. This repository is public, and its own contributor rule is \"only\npublic knowledge, no private repository links\".\n\nThis is a pre-existing breakage on `main`, not introduced here: CI run #2\n(18dc0ee) was green and run #3 (00b0451, \"Enhance documentation for\ncheck_legal_headers.py\") went red by expanding this docstring and reintroducing\nthe internal paths -- the same thing 18dc0ee had removed, noting at the time\nthat the \"vendored legal script no longer exempt (its header no longer names\ninternal docs)\".\n\nFixed rather than left red, because it blocks this PR''s `structure, accuracy\nand boundary checks` job and the fix is three lines. The `Implements:` block\ngoes away entirely, which also matches the house style -- this was the only\nscript in scripts/ carrying one; check_links.py, simulate_seed.py,\ncheck_api_surface.py and validate_env.py all use plain Module/Description/Usage.\nNo behaviour change: the docstring is the entire diff.\n\nVerified locally, the full CI job: check_legal_headers.py OK, validate_env\nclean (was 3 findings), `bash -n claude/hooks/*.sh`, test_hooks.sh and\nsimulate_seed.py all exit 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QZ7w6ZGyiXTLtCsiFxrZMf\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrG46CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcrAQAB+I0hBig7GQG6qjoC3tQeSK\nW5gOb8ajRXr0zfe6kzNMPJzkAeZcJ0honA6qr+KOnetiVt/9nlre3ATvgsKuyCM0\nE7EWR8pmtfO/cE8APwBtyyosHIInNmbmfWHbpXdItH4uLTu2stp7sEu/WFLXlkKB\nPLbb9eFGcx4sxo/qNPep6JLLH+g9bWcQ2CvcWS5Sobr5yhXqAqGhiU20emIpyPfw\n8TbDWMJMZKowHwvXHle/WtlexVN814S6VjEdfMeQuS1xqEpcqN5Lo6+EChNdFPVu\nPOmKRmoALzGYMFwjwrOmNdB5iW5DnvONF5G0Z8lLEwzxV3TSB8AYb/p9vO8UBU+w\nEEROXeDig+IQB8nIDIFWz2oCbFeH4UY42hhCF+U4tDgaHh0muW+R1smmLGIQTLvm\n+o0g9pinLZuQjkh084pW3gUiabXGMyQoEDtMctvZ9zvf7LzX81SWPIMcu65ybF6o\nsJ857VVI9YcrPiiw3tLHNrJbo3d2zUMoQknNUnCctKUU2vMA+mPRuA817C4j/s2x\nu72BwyfJo1hs0aCogIL4aM5sFGkeZ/EFu/lzfmNClxbDxklnkwyJvSQScxbxH1GP\nHw1AcozydBSXWjYFAVWCRA29+JiYVVWZoe62LOO5Tn5q3J2CrHcr5sDNvFwvuZnB\nMlNdQ4YClxUxbjam1roE\n=Wd5R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T22:48:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https:/