5@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matthew Short"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T05:56:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: serialize plugin rspack in the AIO image build and e2e script fix (#177)\n\n* fix(web): serialize plugin rspack in the AIO image build\n\nA single plugins:build multi-compiler EMFILEs on PF icon chunks under the\ncontainer nofile limit and flakes E2E AIO image jobs.\n\n* fix(e2e): parse Podman machine keyring quotas without a # SSH separator\n\npodman machine ssh joins argv into one remote shell string, so ###...###\nwas treated as a comment and local e2e died before Playwright started.\n\n* fix(web): emit one PF icon chunk and raise image builder nofile\n\nSettings still EMFILEs when writing ~2885 pf-icon files, even one remote\nat a time. Collapse loadPfIcon to a single lazy-once chunk and raise\nnofile to 65536. Restore the plugins multi-compiler in Dockerfile.web.\n\n* revert(web): keep per-icon PF chunks; rely on image builder nofile\n\nThe lazy-once pf-icons split was not required once the web image RUN\nraises nofile to 65536.","tree":{"sha":"2ad9f6f78cf08942bbfadbbe29acec66ff8cdc07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/2ad9f6f78cf08942bbfadbbe29acec66ff8cdc07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/e2e5021054e780ca8b73cdd92a2338f9ea80af4c","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ad9f6f78cf08942bbfadbbe29acec66ff8cdc07\nparent 796558125c8eedc7ec31b87d2f9d6b3b2e6519e5\nauthor Matthew Short <97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com> 1788414975 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788414975 -0700\n\nfix: serialize plugin rspack in the AIO image build and e2e script fix (#177)\n\n* fix(web): serialize plugin rspack in the AIO image build\n\nA single plugins:build multi-compiler EMFILEs on PF icon chunks under the\ncontainer nofile limit and flakes E2E AIO image jobs.\n\n* fix(e2e): parse Podman machine keyring quotas without a # SSH separator\n\npodman machine ssh joins argv into one remote shell string, so ###...###\nwas treated as a comment and local e2e died before Playwright started.\n\n* fix(web): emit one PF icon chunk and raise image builder nofile\n\nSettings still EMFILEs when writing ~2885 pf-icon files, even one remote\nat a time. Collapse loadPfIcon to a single lazy-once chunk and raise\nnofile to 65536. Restore the plugins multi-compiler in Dockerfile.web.\n\n* revert(web): keep per-icon PF chunks; rely on image builder nofile\n\nThe lazy-once pf-icons split was not required once the web image RUN\nraises nofile to 65536.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmQv/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuQkQAInHGghc9NIEGpVe3h3BcuQi\nWcZTJPYXgf1kKBQWL9ZEWxZaEkFnxEyamOeFhML3qTYK7PZL7gJFU+LWwZ+DjvDt\nB5rb8nulTFjvHHhzlTSpeSV8TqqOw7c5qHsHHag8aei4kFMs0WyhkX3dC11JLYFq\nUKChTB1klTL1wgu/5fQbfQNvt9t8syaxHqDsaKXs/T1JLW7jpocy8Lw1lGgTrkYm\n8bxkaxmqYXXJtPnz7+3wfn2PdFY6gCHLGItZ2j5hBaPYtsAOMwxezX0cP5FntPCi\nRsO9GEtYyvx+oNNPPZwJ5V82A0L3EGgP9tFTMRb7t5VOHV1lBsWIkeimOiyL5AA8\nEa65OvD9XYNz7LvLh6McyLFOs8iq4U00ebC9L2xJsBilMCpV4KXHvdraXOhWa/tn\n/V+gSgaWdG+qOm8HCXChic+hmWxt9kazKqZ0NTgOSgP1e0a54rfbN471QXJ7klD5\n6llYiDGK6rSu5C28RPE1o+Wk0WDmQQTYK2uDHrr2D5O2BrLxZ9Xqi093fJfgcg0W\n+FSGA2YvTSaEYa7LUvc19du2SL5jIEfrXBytDrIyWQ+Age1hidqPCO8LWWTwCtkB\nqg/uudriTyz7c/ytrlJ+VLvwDNhbGcbUD034sElcZiUoe54qgmMMJWamkFDhwPvc\nXWIWBW1wdvCiUah5zRjt\n=jxoc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T05:56:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/e2e5021054e780ca8b73cdd92a2338f9ea80af4c","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKGUyZTUwMjEwNTRlNzgwY2E4YjczY2RkOTJhMjMzOGY5ZWE4MGFmNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/796558125c8eedc7ec31b87d2f9d6b3b2e6519e5","sha":"796558125c8eedc7ec31b87d2f9d6b3b2e6519e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/796558125c8eedc7ec31b87d2f9d6b3b2e6519e5"}],"sha":"e2e5021054e780ca8b73cdd92a2338f9ea80af4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/e2e5021054e780ca8b73cdd92a2338f9ea80af4c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97869221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mshort55","id":97869221,"login":"mshort55","node_id":"U_kgDOBdVdpQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/796558125c8eedc7ec31b87d2f9d6b3b2e6519e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T04:41:29Z","email":"97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matthew Short"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T04:41:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"OME-298: pin Kind topologies, raise keyring quotas, and cover remaining CLI e2e journeys (#176)\n\n* Expand CLI e2e for Kind topology, keyring quotas, discovery, and failure paths.\n\nPooled clusters can pin a requested node spec. Sandbox and CI fail fast when\nrootless keyring quotas are too low. New journeys cover worker topology,\nrejected applies, deletion during target outage, login isolation, and\nextension resource discovery.\n\n* Require Kind cluster e2e requests to declare spec.\n\nUse \"any\" for unconstrained topology so omitted spec is no longer a wildcard and {} can pin the default.\n\n* Wait for async resource delete in CLI tests.\n\nDelete returns DELETING; poll GET until NotFound. Also correct the testserver package comment.\n\n* Harden CLI e2e Kind leases and remain-until assertions.\n\nRequire spec in declarations, wait for every provision before release, and fail remain-until holds on the first mismatch.\n\n* Note deferred in-memory SQLite for testserver.\n\n* Wait for unactivated Kind pool deletes to finish.\n\n* Treat empty Kind node image as the default.","tree":{"sha":"fb4fa47a30f843c33f5470bdb4a3a519fabe0053","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/fb4fa47a30f843c33f5470bdb4a3a519fabe0053"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/796558125c8eedc7ec31b87d2f9d6b3b2e6519e5","verification":{"payload":"tree fb4fa47a30f843c33f5470bdb4a3a519fabe0053\nparent 74966593edfba39d9f788797b15c3353b7144541\nauthor Matthew Short <97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com> 1788410489 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788410489 -0700\n\nOME-298: pin Kind topologies, raise keyring quotas, and cover remaining CLI e2e journeys (#176)\n\n* Expand CLI e2e for Kind topology, keyring quotas, discovery, and failure paths.\n\nPooled clusters can pin a requested node spec. Sandbox and CI fail fast when\nrootless keyring quotas are too low. New journeys cover worker topology,\nrejected applies, deletion during target outage, login isolation, and\nextension resource discovery.\n\n* Require Kind cluster e2e requests to declare spec.\n\nUse \"any\" for unconstrained topology so omitted spec is no longer a wildcard and {} can pin the default.\n\n* Wait for async resource delete in CLI tests.\n\nDelete returns DELETING; poll GET until NotFound. Also correct the testserver package comment.\n\n* Harden CLI e2e Kind leases and remain-until assertions.\n\nRequire spec in declarations, wait for every provision before release, and fail remain-until holds on the first mismatch.\n\n* Note deferred in-memory SQLite for testserver.\n\n* Wait for unactivated Kind pool deletes to finish.\n\n* Treat empty Kind node image as the default.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmPp5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAawgQAFAv/9wll/Bj2/IHEkXjGCt/\n7rL7vpJih7ldr/xLbOB25/SND2tI/i8fgKH4kU/waZ3y3gGDlP2nVRmIWNtFpQiM\na9bPS+3IFIF2VNosM4P9TbZ5ze8IfM/7OPqfjDlj2YiUZXfQMMZ9Yq4RzrYV5trH\nrWg38UBH0sHXy26/ZVY3VXOiCylnR8CEV0hTfP/14I9ocHdseM3mi1oe+f8kv5OD\ncPeqymls8Caui1UNfcy/QEDiqvBh72P+WurT99e9ViKRYIK4o+1StXLwdB+CtWBb\nUI9X18903FsTb7PJd/5UF3iG3A/jexamuvkOvQPOf/oHcPWPPWtEeTNFWXooN+TV\nZQK2C5fi50DMm+cbfeY1y7YSvmEWLeeQwY2sNUfDbHTL9KxPmkd8QdD3xQyiUGmQ\naYr8nEOPtCJTTI/BYySGr8studQeFl6ACnj793ENOrpfg2WYhaGty6Azpyyf29oV\nfW4WEeqSjoqsp5aSUmPh9tNyX80FMKBsZgO+iHJzzoSyb38UJfU2l3+mrJYEV/U2\nTg/fsTtnUbARQoE+ch/5BCx/UCrPAeYC5JbrkM+9kpbQOKWqneBLFDMYWEkHNy2X\nC/+EqPKGcCYu20gWvEB1jCRz8iLVQt/KoZWMdYPG2NuuYv8OdfI6R+hHQ7NoMRX1\nGQq5+dl9R1BFDCqi5i3H\n=EkK0\n-----END PGP SIGNA