tshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/de9cfa0340637eea6c2a14419d14b3ae9674d252","sha":"de9cfa0340637eea6c2a14419d14b3ae9674d252","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/de9cfa0340637eea6c2a14419d14b3ae9674d252"}],"sha":"8bb5ba0f3fd361fddc6347282b0db0afa59fdcc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/8bb5ba0f3fd361fddc6347282b0db0afa59fdcc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97869221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mshort55","id":97869221,"login":"mshort55","node_id":"U_kgDOBdVdpQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/de9cfa0340637eea6c2a14419d14b3ae9674d252/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T00:17:12Z","email":"97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matthew Short"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T00:17:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"OME-254, OME-256 (partial), OME-278: Fleetctl backend suite, Kind lifecycle, and Nx gotestsum (#169)\n\n* feat(e2e): add Fleetctl backend suite and build the AIO image once in CI\n\nBackend tests start the AIO from this checkout, log in through fleetctl and Playwright Dex, and read the bootstrap deployment. CI builds the image once and runs UI and backend jobs in parallel from that tar.\n\n* feat(e2e): run Kind cluster lifecycle on the user podman.socket\n\nBackend tests create a Kind cluster, deliver a ConfigMap, and delete it. CI and the harness mount the user podman.socket (not a /tmp API service) so uid 1000 can reach the host engine the same way as local Linux.\n\n* feat(e2e): probe Kind OIDC before ConfigMap and fail fast on paused apply\n\nRequire cluster Ready=True, include fleetctl stdout in wait failures, and\nresolve Darwin engine sockets via podman-mac-helper or podman info.\n\n* refactor(e2e): split Kind cluster steps from shared helpers\n\nKeep fleetctl cluster JSON and kubernetes-target helpers generic so later cluster types can share them.\n\n* fix(e2e): log expected Unauthenticated fleetctl probes\n\nMark begin/end so a later failure dump is not mistaken for an auth outage.\n\n* feat(test): Nx gotestsum runner, live backend e2e, and resilient fleetctl auth\n\nRun Go tests through a shared gotestsum wrapper (Nx + CI JUnit). Backend\nscenarios render as live testdox steps with throttled wait logs; later\nsteps skip after a failure. fleetctl still sends RPCs when the OIDC CA is\nmissing, refreshes only when needed, and stores --oidc-ca-file as an\nabsolute path.\n\n* fix(ci): sync Nx lockfile and keep AIO /data off the image overlay\n\nAlign Nx packages at 23.1.1 so npm ci on Node 22 matches the lockfile.\nRun the UI sandbox with tmpfs /data and --pull=never, and fail the wait\nimmediately if the container has already stopped.\n\n* fix(ci): save AIO cache as distinct images, not extra tags on the server\n\npodman save without --multi-image-archive made UI e2e run fleetshift-server under the AIO tag.\n\n* fix(ci): drop AIO tmpfs /data and smoke kind as container root\n\ntmpfs was a workaround for the mis-tagged server image. uid 1000 exec does not get the socket group AIO packaging applies.\n\n* fix(ci): reuse the cached AIO image in backend e2e instead of rebuilding\n\nLocal TestMain still runs nx image:aio. CI loads the aio-image tar and sets FLEETSHIFT_E2E_AIO_PREBUILT=1. setup-e2e roles are cache (writer) and e2e (test jobs).\n\n* fix: harden CLI credentials and bound e2e harness commands\n\nFileStore now chmods 0600, requires an absolute dir, and omits expired\ntokens. Harness podman/npx calls get deadlines; Kind CA is stdout-only.\n\n* comment fix\n\n* fix: refuse FileStore dir/file symlinks and world-writable dirs\n\nLstat the config dir so a symlink or group/other-writable path is rejected.\nRefuse a non-regular credentials file so a planted symlink is not followed.","tree":{"sha":"7cb932c3fceb3420a4a3f0668ad88408b6cfe928","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/7cb932c3fceb3420a4a3f0668ad88408b6cfe928"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/de9cfa0340637eea6c2a14419d14b3ae9674d252","verification":{"payload":"tree 7cb932c3fceb3420a4a3f0668ad88408b6cfe928\nparent 9548dbb0177344c416cd43e151c4e42f26cdcd62\nauthor Matthew Short <97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com> 1787617032 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787617032 -0700\n\nOME-254, OME-256 (partial), OME-278: Fleetctl backend suite, Kind lifecycle, and Nx gotestsum (#169)\n\n* feat(e2e): add Fleetctl backend suite and build the AIO image once in CI\n\nBackend tests start the AIO from this checkout, log in through fleetctl and Playwright Dex, and read the bootstrap deployment. CI builds the image once and runs UI and backend jobs in parallel from that tar.\n\n* feat(e2e): run Kind cluster lifecycle on the user podman.socket\n\nBackend tests create a Kind cluster, deliver a ConfigMap, and delete it. CI and the harness mount the user podman.socket (not a /tmp API service) so uid 1000 can reach the host engine the same way as local Linux.\n\n* feat(e2e): probe Kind OIDC before ConfigMap and fail fast on paused apply\n\nRequire cluster Ready=True, include fleetctl stdout in wait failures, and\nresolve Darwin engine sockets via podman-mac-helper or podman info.\n\n* refactor(e2e): split Kind cluster steps from shared helpers\n\nKeep fleetctl cluster JSON and kubernetes-target helpers generic so later cluster types can share them.\n\n* fix(e2e): log expected Unauthenticated fleetctl probes\n\nMark begin/end so a later failure dump is not mistaken for an auth outage.\n\n* feat(test): Nx gotestsum runner, live backend e2e, and resilient fleetctl auth\n\nRun Go tests through a shared gotestsum wrapper (Nx + CI JUnit). Backend\nscenarios render as live testdox steps with throttled wait logs; later\nsteps skip after a failure. fleetctl still sends RPCs when the OIDC CA is\nmissing, refreshes only when needed, and stores --oidc-ca-file as an\nabsolute path.\n\n* fix(ci): sync Nx lockfile and keep AIO /data off the image overlay\n\nAlign Nx packages at 23.1.1 so npm ci on Node 22 matches the lockfile.\nRun the UI sandbox with tmpfs /data and --pull=never, and fail the wait\nimmediately if the container has already stopped.\n\n* fix(ci): save AIO cache as distinct images, not extra tags on the server\n\npodman save without --multi-image-archive made UI e2e run fleetshift-server under the AIO tag.\n\n* fix(ci): drop AIO tmpfs /data and smoke kind as container root\n\ntmpfs was a workaround for the mis-tagged server image. uid 1000 exec does not get the socket group AIO packaging applies.\n\n* fix(ci): reuse the cached AIO image in backend e2e instead of rebuilding\n\nLocal TestMain still runs nx image:aio. CI loads the aio-image tar and sets FLEETSHIFT_E2E_AIO_PREBUILT=1. setup-e2e roles are cache (writer) and e2e (test jobs).\n\n* fix: harden CLI credentials and bound e2e harness commands\n\nFileStore now chmods 0600, requires an absolute dir, and omits expired\ntokens. Harness podman/npx calls get deadlines; Kind CA is stdout-only.\n\n* comment fix\n\n* fix: refuse FileStore dir/file symlinks and world-writable dirs\n\nLstat the config dir so a symlink or group/other-writable path is rejected.\nRefuse a non-regular credentials file so a planted symlink is not followed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjN8ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACW8QACumMHy08c9BmJfRVQQm+E9L\n5Zlb6RtS+H1MfGZ0AQ3xuyrAAD+RjlEBUUgCx3XdZrrCB338oETnL1f3GXVxzFvo\nFTh+WcGw1kh02NADc1unebF8orV2revsrK/G8IMNQWgaW7q11LQbb3ueBhoupjhx\nQEbhcDRbgg5g6LwQB2DOONSXgxkSgXF6B8MXqDWwszJUzTO6jMnp4iQMIG466r27\novHL4gqShG2D4EjRXS7XlPrMACN5XT5j5JvirDsqTveFU/LETNaEeVOOd1aj0d/U\nf3OfdwLWDkAD1CYeFZ8sJNOqBqD7REYP63MUsUS4ByPk8xwgHuNLBOhLkexOfUJc\nKnPbNDgmTDYQd2+BThNRhjRI+8SMJWBowSYgkun9vKdd+/X0P5nZ8Gu6SsK/72f6\ni+ptdZcA3pUJSDfAasusn5QeDYsQJ7vD1PmGmp9LQ+fu0soXZDDv2yBp1lJ4hEe8\nITShM80azdAqvLVAy2mtVF8P1YuFavMnzuLEsj3eVAH1HU03XzdCTKY24kNeW/7+\n9pfg5GVoHTwWlYkuJ9AEljyH7Ffw2QOh+dOHHjtgEQj1FLUjEgAQs83dxB0yNzDG\n3q/TbEGYiUmb0tpM8aE19m70L9DlXVjy443QKmpfdH16e44kjXxSNrkt4POn7Cc6\nclxYSLNOpLXqKw1OSH1o\n=aXoP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T00:17:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/de9cfa0340637eea6c2a14419d14b3ae9674d252","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKGRlOWNmYTAzNDA2MzdlZWE2YzJhMTQ0MTlkMTRiM2FlOTY3NGQyNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/9548dbb0177344c416cd43e151c4e42f26cdcd62","sha":"9548dbb0177344c416cd43e151c4e42f26cdcd62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/9548dbb0177344c416cd43e151c4e42f26cdcd62"}],"sha":"de9cfa0340637eea6c2a14419d14b3ae9674d252","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/de9cfa0340637eea6c2a14419d14b3ae9674d252"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33311905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sherine-k/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sherine-k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sherine-k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sherine-k/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sherine-k","id":33311905,"login":"sherine-k","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMzExOTA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sherine-k/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sherine-k/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sherine-k/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sherine-k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sherine-k/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sherine-k","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/9548dbb0177344c416cd43e151c4e42f26cdcd62/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T14:13:22Z","email":"skhoury@redhat.com","name":"Sherine Khoury"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T14:13:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"OME-269: feat: add test:stress task (#114)\n\n* OME-269: feat: add orchestration stress test (task test:stress)\n\nAdd a stress test that exercises the orchestration loop under sustained\ndeployment creation and update pressure, measuring how the system handles\ngeneration skipping (where updates arrive faster than deliveries complete).\n\nTest structure (three files in fleetshift-server/internal/application/):\n  stress_test.go         -- test entry point, workload runner, drain, convergence loop\n  stress_harness_test.go -- config, mock delivery agent, observer, Pareto distribution\n  stress_report_test.go  -- latency distributions, convergence, JSON dump\n\nTest phases:\n  1. Setup: Postgres testcontainer (tuned: 1 GiB /dev/shm, configurable\n     shared_buffers/max_wal_size/max_connections), go-workflows backend\n     sharing the same database, 50 targets, mock delivery agent.\n  2. Workload: fire ops at configurable rate for configurable duration.\n     Pareto distribution (alpha=7.21, 80/20 hotspot) selects deployments;\n     new ones are created, existing ones get direct store mutations\n     followed by an async convergence loop.\n  3. Drain: wait for all created fulfillments to reconcile at least once.\n  4. Report: latency distributions (reconciliation, ack, completion,\n     overhead, mutation-to-dispatch), generation advancement stats,\n     convergence snapshot, JSON dump with per-delivery details and\n     connection pool time series.\n\nAlso adds:\n  - scripts/plot_stress.py for visualizing mutation-to-dispatch latency\n    and connection pool utilization over time\n  - OpenStressDB in postgres/testdb.go for stress-tuned testcontainers\n  - test:stress task in Taskfile.yml\n  - docs/design/orchestration_stress_test.md recapping experiment\n    learnings: connection pool sizing, workflow engine choice,\n    deployment update patterns, latency degradation analysis, and\n    generation skipping correctness\n\nEnvironment variables: STRESS_DEPLOYMENTS, STRESS_RATE, STRESS_DURATION,\nSTRESS_ACK_DELAY_{MIN,MAX}, STRESS_COMPLETION_DELAY_{MIN,MAX},\nSTRESS_FAILURE_RATE, STRESS_POSTGRES_MAX_CONNS, STRESS_WORKFLOW_POLLERS\n\n* Update next steps after design session","tree":{"sha":"ce48448c0720e07eeb77c8d1ce148a7d6c67b6c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/ce48448c0720e07eeb77c8d1ce148a7d6c67b6c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/9548dbb0177344c416cd43e151c4e42f26cdcd62","verification":{"payload":"tree ce48448c0720e07eeb77c8d1ce148a7d6c67b6c6\nparent 5b80cf856274330b396e2aafb1447af3fe73546e\nauthor Sherine Khoury <skhoury@redhat.com> 1787321602 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787321602 -0700\n\nOME-269: feat: add test:stress task (#114)\n\n* OME-269: feat: add orchestration stress test (task test:stress)\n\nAdd a stress test that exercises the orchestration loop under sustained\ndeployment creation and update pressure, measuring how the system handles\ngeneration skipping (where updates arrive faster than deliveries complete).\n\nTest structure (three files in fleetshift-server/internal/application/):\n  stress_test.go         -- test entry point, workload runner, drain, convergence loop\n  stress_harness_test.go -- config, mock delivery agent, observer, Pareto distribution\n  stress_report_test.go  -- latency distributions, convergence, JSON dump\n\nTest phases:\n  1. Setup: Postgres testcontainer (tuned: 1 GiB /dev/shm, configurable\n     shared_buffers/max_wal_size/max_connections), go-workflows backend\n     sharing the same database, 50 targets, mock delivery agent.\n  2. Workload: fire ops at configurable rate for configurable duration.\n     Pareto distribution (alpha=7.21, 80/20 hotspot) selects deployments;\n     new ones are created, existing ones get direct store mutations\n     followed by an async convergence loop.\n  3. Drain: wait for all created fulfillments to reconcile at least once.\n  4. Report: latency distributions (reconciliation, ack, completion,\n     overhead, mutation-to-dispatch), generation advancement stats,\n     convergence snapshot, JSON dump with per-delivery details and\n     connection pool time series.\n\nAlso adds:\n  - scripts/plot_stress.py for visualizing mutation-to-dispatch latency\n    and connection pool utilization over time\n  - OpenStressDB in postgres/testdb.go for stress-tuned testcontainers\n  - test:stress task in Taskfile.yml\n  - docs/design/orchestration_stress_test.md recapping experiment\n    learnings: connection pool sizing, workflow engine choice,\n    deployment update patterns, latency degradation analysis, and\n    generation skipping correctness\n\nEnvironment variables: STRESS_DEPLOYMENTS, STRESS_RATE, STRESS_DURATION,\nSTRESS_ACK_DELAY_{MIN,MAX}, STRESS_COMPLETION_DELAY_{MIN,MAX},\nSTRESS_FAILURE_RATE, STRESS_POSTGRES_MAX_CONNS, STRESS_WORKFLOW_POLLERS\n\n* Update next steps after design session","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiF0CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvv0QAKU6SSsrf1kyMaF1r2ui+azK\nMoHgNSQLhO16+/NnveicHgxN7Ah2TzXPqUQBs0u1Zd1WVOPDcDYvVXzUBerpEpxf\nJ2qZfqhJzyEgd1aG905e9h5WCbcyURIUPTeuTypeqLtWKbT/HGvZwnPNtOwRQBFI\nYHRQ1zgLyiDfzApg/Avd7Y7P62Io1IY/YXosxVjqwsZOQxZap8UKfTs3YxLAB06t\nasm+GAidAH6GS7lxKp8/2ad8Gu1Vvn+AJie/ZIs+Xq+iYSXhwSKg8IWij9E6G9+S\ndWw1aq3ow1R2S7mllHAJhaoLgW6xfzsljC1O4eT+TyFt936m74zVZUOe9ONn4Uhw\nzRHxQzF1SeMR9XqfmZB9v86Q8cgiKLf4uCYCG6EuLu7LAQjepJ6rRnFp94wakPR5\nPpYljFglKDY9q3pzySH9SzLPdVyOgumWioLY8CHdVJ3O2ZkD3Pz5LcvaZcMYtM91\nryWLMK+lr0WyRcYCZNZ2eg21uCnHaz/jF+1BBL8GPHe7FrbcsmxGcqjKkdzPjdxz\nz7dnwdGOKq/6FOr0aLGjpxDfafnUHdmnRBMdEsJVe2URQ7K/YGYv7JDYy2n6jMBw\nZfoNwdwc0cAVGTK7zCcYg9u/TrsG7QaReSyGSh+g/jHcZYQVLMfeujCR+a1lLkMH\nB1wmB/hU57mu52bm7k8W\n=UU0B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T14:13:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/9548dbb0177344c416cd43e151c4e42f26cdcd62","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKDk1NDhkYmIwMTc3MzQ0YzQxNmNkNDNlMTUxYzRlNDJmMjZjZGNkNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/5b80cf856274330b396e2aafb1447af3fe73546e","sha":"5b80cf856274330b396e2aafb1447af3fe73546e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/5b80cf856274330b396e2aafb1447af3fe73546e"}],"sha":"9548dbb0177344c416cd43e151c4e42f26cdcd62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/9548dbb0177344c416cd43e151c4e42f26cdcd62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3496559?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alechenninger","id":3496559,"login":"alechenninger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTY1NTk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/5b80cf856274330b396e2aafb1447af3fe73546e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T12:24:08Z","email":"ahenning@redhat.com","name":"Alec Henninger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T12:24:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"poc: (NEEDS WORK, see PR) drive controller-runtime cache with stock Reflector (#131)\n\n* poc: drive controller-runtime cache with stock Reflector\n\nReplace the hand-rolled fsInformer loop with a kube ListerWatcher over\nthe projection store so SharedIndexInformer owns relist, restart, and\ncache population.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* poc: mirror Delivery status to DeliveryReporter via StatusHook\n\nKeep controllers on the kube client only; report-before-persist so a\nfailed platform report fails Status().Update and requeues like kube.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"527ae9163044fc72cbffdf14e45fee8416daebcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/527ae9163044fc72cbffdf14e45fee8416daebcb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/5b80cf856274330b396e2aafb1447af3fe73546e","verification":{"payload":"tree 527ae9163044fc72cbffdf14e45fee8416daebcb\nparent 64981c9d75eae9c7c3dc6bcdb3877f0d6bc38046\nauthor Alec Henninger <ahenning@redhat.com> 1787228648 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787228648 -0400\n\npoc: (NEEDS WORK, see PR) drive controller-runtime cache with stock Reflector (#131)\n\n* poc: drive controller-runtime cache with stock Reflector\n\nReplace the hand-rolled fsInformer loop with a kube ListerWatcher over\nthe projection store so SharedIndexInformer owns relist, restart, and\ncache population.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* poc: mirror Delivery status to DeliveryReporter via StatusHook\n\nKeep controllers on the kube client only; report-before-persist so a\nfailed platform report fails Status().Update and requeues like kube.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhvHoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7DoQADqlDrVLQYABu6zXi1YXior1\nvwlSzfyNNnNB6/BptZXQRrRwBJk9ZZGbMr+w4+VFSLIjEI7s7GK6qhZ4kmrA+Se2\nSX6NAKknV587pmkDWLlr6X6JIV5MmijKT7E2q/04tGBQJf6k8nh237YQirQzon3Y\nTbIWWkkIAnogxpzjoK+ZHMZosfawAK/dVZgT24DAvr8UvASsfsD3PH9YzKdXXrdL\nPyEJ3tuezH51idvbrvRhjTSCNtjESP+dETnf6mvZHtBYNQJpSY2S0HPebXK++gaz\nWwTBtG1T0epFIMn87x+OVGNdJAzrvXjFrn500EJYTH00xEQEKTlqsXZMj1YHFaps\no0y6TjRVpqSzCsnu6+Hi+UBZpM1JBFTPDVPKnoh9i4B/UlZeSv+hEfMn3xrqjwbp\nb5flZ8fiJ1DnXTekX/Afv5I/RLpv4qG2rYZiqws6UeWziw/vufX4YupsFcaBGL/q\nh82OFsF+1ybfz8i/oTE1I9ZwngBqylYLBjSsLi/dr+nnIYenaNIHLXBXDPgKEtZU\nI4KK/AqlIMnVug+njw2d/t/6Gcab/EXMLGriO7nzYSFGfR2sDEoKDKLg0/z6ADV6\nF69MdreiLN/wypha/Rr7jNFVT54ZLrHkAlfvsgEW+UBEhn392wdQM8zZs3gDHvLf\nqC4COKKs1SazzWtV4ExI\n=yL2y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T12:24:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/5b80cf856274330b396e2aafb1447af3fe73546e","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKDViODBjZjg1NjI3NDMzMGIzOTZlMmFhZmIxNDQ3YWYzZmU3MzU0NmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/64981c9d75eae9c7c3dc6bcdb3877f0d6bc38046","sha":"64981c9d75eae9c7c3dc6bcdb3877f0d6bc38046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/64981c9d75eae9c7c3dc6bcdb3877f0d6bc38046"}],"sha":"5b80cf856274330b396e2aafb1447af3fe73546e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/5b80cf856274330b396e2aafb1447af3fe73546e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22619452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Hyperkid123","id":22619452,"login":"Hyperkid123","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5NDUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/64981c9d75eae9c7c3dc6bcdb3877f0d6bc38046/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:16:36Z","email":"marvusm.mmi@gmail.com","name":"Martin Marosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:16:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Dex UI connect (#164)\n\n* feat: enable sandbox IDP for UI\n\n* chore: add npx nx pd:trust-cert\n\n* chore(web): remove obsolete auth setup page\n\n* chore(kc): add new web origin/callback URLs\n\n* docs: update dev/deployment instructions after AIO migration\n\n* fix(build): force aio to always use locally build images\n\n* feat(auth): loopback OIDC proxy so browser skips sandbox CA trust\n\nThe AIO''s peer Dex issues at https://127.0.0.1:5556/dex with a self-signed\nsandbox CA. Browser login previously required importing that CA into the OS\nkeychain (pd:trust-cert) — clicking through the interstitial was insufficient\nbecause the SPA''s background token requests fail TLS silently.\n\nInstead, reverse-proxy the loopback Dex under the server''s own HTTP origin\n(/dex) whenever the issuer is a loopback HTTPS URL with a CA bundle (auto-gated,\nno user-facing flag). The browser reaches every OIDC endpoint over plain HTTP;\nonly the discovery fetch is redirected via oidc.metadataUrl. The ID-token `iss`,\nthe browser `authority`, and server-side token validation all keep the internal\nhttps://127.0.0.1:5556/dex identity untouched — the discovery `issuer` field is\ndeliberately not rewritten.\n\nfleetctl still reaches Dex over HTTPS directly, so the sandbox CA is still\ncopied to .certs/ca.crt for --oidc-ca-file. Remove the now-dead browser\nkeychain-trust machinery (trust-dex-ca.sh, pd:trust-cert) and update docs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(web): add cluster journey tests\n\n* Adapt PR 164 onto the PR 165 single HTTPS origin.\n\nDrop the loopback OIDC proxy and trust-cert workaround so aio-proxy keeps terminating TLS for /app and /idp. Retarget e2e and docs to https://fleetshift-sandbox.localhost:8085, and remove leftover Keycloak overlay / dummy-app workspace wiring.\n\n* Leave OIDC_UI_SCOPE unset so AIO Dex-on keeps the Dex audience scope.\n\nDrop the AUTH=external leftover and delete ome.sh.\n\n* Remove the podman test-attestation task, script, and docs.\n\n* Trim dishonest deploy comments and thin .env.template.\n\nDrop dead Keycloak/compose leftovers and stop pd:clean from deleting an unused kind cluster.\n\n* Fix PR 164 review nits for cache, IdP URIs, and e2e names.\n\nHash Taskfile.yml in the AIO image cache key, register silent-renew on external issuers, untrack .certs, and UUID Kind e2e cluster names.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Short <mshort@redhat.com>","tree":{"sha":"24f7606e88da88a30d00ca1cb7f1dbe1f87974ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/24f7606e88da88a30d00ca1cb7f1dbe1f87974ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/64981c9d75eae9c7c3dc6bcdb3877f0d6bc38046","verification":{"payload":"tree 24f7606e88da88a30d00ca1cb7f1dbe1f87974ef\nparent 8027c172c365fa4ff9a305720acd52dabcb68463\nauthor Martin Marosi <marvusm.mmi@gmail.com> 1787181396 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787181396 -0700\n\nDex UI connect (#164)\n\n* feat: enable sandbox IDP for UI\n\n* chore: add npx nx pd:trust-cert\n\n* chore(web): remove obsolete auth setup page\n\n* chore(kc): add new web origin/callback URLs\n\n* docs: update dev/deployment instructions after AIO migration\n\n* fix(build): force aio to always use locally build images\n\n* feat(auth): loopback OIDC proxy so browser skips sandbox CA trust\n\nThe AIO''s peer Dex issues at https://127.0.0.1:5556/dex with a self-signed\nsandbox CA. Browser login previously required importing that CA into the OS\nkeychain (pd:trust-cert) — clicking through the interstitial was insufficient\nbecause the SPA''s background token requests fail TLS silently.\n\nInstead, reverse-proxy the loopback Dex under the server''s own HTTP origin\n(/dex) whenever the issuer is a loopback HTTPS URL with a CA bundle (auto-gated,\nno user-facing flag). The browser reaches every OIDC endpoint over plain HTTP;\nonly the discovery fetch is redirected via oidc.metadataUrl. The ID-token `iss`,\nthe browser `authority`, and server-side token validation all keep the internal\nhttps://127.0.0.1:5556/dex identity untouched — the discovery `issuer` field is\ndeliberately not rewritten.\n\nfleetctl still reaches Dex over HTTPS directly, so the sandbox CA is still\ncopied to .certs/ca.crt for --oidc-ca-file. Remove the now-dead browser\nkeychain-trust machinery (trust-dex-ca.sh, pd:trust-cert) and update docs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(web): add cluster journey tests\n\n* Adapt PR 164 onto the PR 165 single HTTPS origin.\n\nDrop the loopback OIDC proxy and trust-cert workaround so aio-proxy keeps terminating TLS for /app and /idp. Retarget e2e and docs to https://fleetshift-sandbox.localhost:8085, and remove leftover Keycloak overlay / dummy-app workspace wiring.\n\n* Leave OIDC_UI_SCOPE unset so AIO Dex-on keeps the Dex audience scope.\n\nDrop the AUTH=external leftover and delete ome.sh.\n\n* Remove the podman test-attestation task, script, and docs.\n\n* Trim dishonest deploy comments and thin .env.template.\n\nDrop dead Keycloak/compose leftovers and stop pd:clean from deleting an unused kind cluster.\n\n* Fix PR 164 review nits for cache, IdP URIs, and e2e names.\n\nHash Taskfile.yml in the AIO image cache key, register silent-renew on external issuers, untrack .certs, and UUID Kind e2e cluster names.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Matthew Short <mshort@redhat.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhjlUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxAQQAD2wghhIs6W4HK1TC1VYwV9g\naWUbqVdGqdeKQT/ZOZvpLNrJyAETYN7wXANbNU56ITnCXBtBswBl4VdBdHEWo0tr\nKVlhmDOrc7eDQktlL2K8O1j6nd4h15HMv0jMGP/Nc7ip6OfOgvRbyrI0BNCMerqz\nMiYMMBqSEPK4kKymjRVSfeldgpMyoy8WZvhv8xgLgj40hyWrza6RbtdMlO4LZC+R\nfQTfP+yEcJ9QmWAoHfrI9NBn+iKty0FiB75ihKkuBY3pqxndW9BjipcD4MP3Fe4l\nxwpIb8eFkiyzo9aw/A7vM5uqFvTRyq+1Yn0evVaGTS+vpVUGiyHlHumwBAX1Q9h5\nRo2HjhyjgX4MvAA84LZ0V1E+g7vtzm8AGqIeh/tOavqvQnkBBxNQlNPChdPhOzyb\n6f8rpK/ktWpWvWlmWboB2LZEZBLQU/5yT0UiVaSsHwmNwPsiFHONj+QnPLCAmKAZ\nq5Su+J3MFrIqp+9nnOPYnhj48L1/PMGGATl2Ek5nTpKaYla6cGvAoQmyozXKblip\nsb2+Z4h5bR4SlL8O/MNlnp3Hpr0vEsHLjlCysVOvYjsFXJyhTRFCknTlMgUHxRJC\n5pu+BVz0yqrL5KKgpn20aDvMZMVRp6uI/qsZOh5Lb6q6Sb0ct+kjogcT7yuYnNDh\n6sBRaW8NyUdvIOlUwmVP\n=k5Bw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T23:16:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/64981c9d75eae9c7c3dc6bcdb3877f0d6bc38046","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKDY0OTgxYzlkNzVlYWU5YzdjM2RjNmJjZGIzODc3ZjBkNmJjMzgwNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/8027c172c365fa4ff9a305720acd52dabcb68463","sha":"8027c172c365fa4ff9a305720acd52dabcb68463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/8027c172c365fa4ff9a305720acd52dabcb68463"}],"sha":"64981c9d75eae9c7c3dc6bcdb3877f0d6bc38046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/64981c9d75eae9c7c3dc6bcdb3877f0d6bc38046"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3496559?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alechenninger","id":3496559,"login":"alechenninger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTY1NTk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/8027c172c365fa4ff9a305720acd52dabcb68463/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:26:59Z","email":"ahenning@redhat.com","name":"Alec Henninger"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:26:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix orchestration hot-loop when target not yet registered (#116)\n\n* Fix orchestration hot-loop when target not yet registered\n\nWhen a deployment''s static placement targets a cluster that hasn''t been\nregistered yet, StaticPlacement.Resolve returns ErrNotFound. This\ntriggered releaseLockAndContinue → ContinueAsNew with no delay,\ncreating a tight retry loop. In go-workflows the activity retry policy\n(20 attempts, exponential backoff) burned ~4+ minutes per cycle on\nfutile retries against the same stale pool snapshot, keeping the\ndeployment stuck in \"creating\".\n\nAdd a configurable RetryDelay (default 5 s) to OrchestrationWorkflowSpec.\nreleaseLockAndContinue now performs a durable sleep before restarting,\ngiving external processes (e.g. kind cluster provisioning) time to\nregister the target before the next pool reload.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Sync late-target registration to RetryDelayStarted so the test hits ContinueAsNew instead of racing a sleep.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"0653abd53670974611fbb14ec47e16325f4366ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/0653abd53670974611fbb14ec47e16325f4366ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/8027c172c365fa4ff9a305720acd52dabcb68463","verification":{"payload":"tree 0653abd53670974611fbb14ec47e16325f4366ae\nparent d8ea19a4be07ae08566140b5df7d31e359b5c7e4\nauthor Alec Henninger <ahenning@redhat.com> 1787164019 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787164019 -0400\n\nFix orchestration hot-loop when target not yet registered (#116)\n\n* Fix orchestration hot-loop when target not yet registered\n\nWhen a deployment''s static placement targets a cluster that hasn''t been\nregistered yet, StaticPlacement.Resolve returns ErrNotFound. This\ntriggered releaseLockAndContinue → ContinueAsNew with no delay,\ncreating a tight retry loop. In go-workflows the activity retry policy\n(20 attempts, exponential backoff) burned ~4+ minutes per cycle on\nfutile retries against the same stale pool snapshot, keeping the\ndeployment stuck in \"creating\".\n\nAdd a configurable RetryDelay (default 5 s) to OrchestrationWorkflowSpec.\nreleaseLockAndContinue now performs a durable sleep before restarting,\ngiving external processes (e.g. kind cluster provisioning) time to\nregister the target before the next pool reload.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Sync late-target registration to RetryDelayStarted so the test hits ContinueAsNew instead of racing a sleep.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhfVzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaYUQAHNwH7vmOh0bh9ss+1tzYv7J\n+UQADpaifWG8THxWNL3RNa9APGHTlOdbg8V87yWhJbciP1Ir0/csbtj4rGOBs1R0\nUUd5yOvQ6y0Q+09VKlcU3hcOOCcoMMpfofle1uaOmkw0g78191HsFixjeKfEtQOc\nCSSyA6RYTqT8Er1F2aDa9a8bJf8ahcLIRqa7DzvkKzDA/gMC/dy9lNPJfxkuKant\n+vwP5M57YDAHBzDzVU3o8W71TXAzc/W+1Yo7ALsCq0pl3ZGyK4TcnAR5LVMMY/3o\nseHoh9RnH3emim1vrx1BQHviRGW/8vnCCx5nJ/uYOswbYBRVTXuWmzdYDQLkHd3s\nyYpBsFLSifYdAdbyJkEur584HnTUg/y46jX0bkicoUFnAc0j9axyjgUG/qszQ2vE\n9l/aExRyVopVTU0NwLxDdCG2JEXqhxFYnErun/qiWrLOV7wX3HD6VrSjAqcHiwht\n8if4TR8g3hDs7DawQlr5p19G3JaiOFq7EhRHzweNJoa6wJOHKMwdh3Wb1FOX+BGU\n6tIe++e3/WPnm+xJmqT/zEVcJ6H9/yNdDkK+b2J2Qj3+0FZ69tFymfwL0gKNMKW4\nWhTeR6TPub9niX9n04+jwtal/hreNFhFUC8gBTgmj6lZ9sHbBsHZbXZezXyhX/LL\nOfDLpuXImWRCSCF22gNd\n=agx1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T18:27:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcj