://api.github.com/users/mshort55/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mshort55","id":97869221,"login":"mshort55","node_id":"U_kgDOBdVdpQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/05ca459e9d663bf098fac0dfb1367d871273be65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:45:01Z","email":"97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matthew Short"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:45:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"OME-287: Put the AIO sandbox on a single HTTPS origin (#165)\n\n* Put the AIO sandbox on a single HTTPS origin.\n\nTerminate TLS at an AIO-only reverse proxy so the UI, API, and peer Dex share https://fleetshift-sandbox.localhost:8085 without publishing Dex or installing a host CA.\n\n* Rename edgeproxy to aioproxy and keep comments on the code they describe.\n\nMatch cmd/aio-proxy with internal/aioproxy, move Kind issuer-host helpers into issuerhost.go, and drop private-plan wording from comments and docs.\n\n* Simplify AIO single-origin wiring.\n\nDerive the public origin from one host and port, fold issuer hostAliases into loopback forward, and drop unused --ui-origin.\n\n* Type OIDC config as AuthProviderNoUserManagerProps.\n\nAuthProviderProps is a union, so settings fields like authority were not visible to TypeScript.\n\n* Cover issuer-host wiring, proxy edge cases, and expired sandbox leafs.\n\nKind create only gained hostAliases through untested resolveConfig, and the TLS edge did not assert encoded /dex routing or the full forwarding-header list.\n\n* Mount the SPA under /app and move peer Dex to /idp on the AIO edge.\n\n* minor doc, keycloak, and compose tweaks\n\n* minor doc, go tweak\n\n* improve readme to make clear different AIO default values and their purposes\n\n* Rename the aio-proxy catch-all upstream to FleetShift and drop stdlib-redundant header/size settings.\n\nKeep stripping hop/identity headers Rewrite does not delete, and still assert the four Rewrite-dropped names never reach Dex or FleetShift.\n\n* Run aio-proxy as uid 1002 so the TLS edge cannot read FleetShift or Dex state.\n\nThe gateway leaf key is owned by that uid; serve stays 1000 and Dex stays 1001.\n\n* Lead the root README with AIO podman run recipes.\n\nKeep compose, Nx, and packaging internals after a Start here section so a sandbox trial does not require the developer toolchain first.\n\n* Fix AuthGate retry and empty OIDC scope so failed logins can recover and the client still requests openid.\n\n* Format SPA auth files with Prettier and surface hosts-file close errors after append.","tree":{"sha":"d8b7f19c2a0d81f37d3c10d9f38eca50188c2f57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/d8b7f19c2a0d81f37d3c10d9f38eca50188c2f57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/05ca459e9d663bf098fac0dfb1367d871273be65","verification":{"payload":"tree d8b7f19c2a0d81f37d3c10d9f38eca50188c2f57\nparent 43e9f97f999d4903c94ee2644acfbe8bd8ea00a3\nauthor Matthew Short <97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com> 1787085901 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787085901 -0700\n\nOME-287: Put the AIO sandbox on a single HTTPS origin (#165)\n\n* Put the AIO sandbox on a single HTTPS origin.\n\nTerminate TLS at an AIO-only reverse proxy so the UI, API, and peer Dex share https://fleetshift-sandbox.localhost:8085 without publishing Dex or installing a host CA.\n\n* Rename edgeproxy to aioproxy and keep comments on the code they describe.\n\nMatch cmd/aio-proxy with internal/aioproxy, move Kind issuer-host helpers into issuerhost.go, and drop private-plan wording from comments and docs.\n\n* Simplify AIO single-origin wiring.\n\nDerive the public origin from one host and port, fold issuer hostAliases into loopback forward, and drop unused --ui-origin.\n\n* Type OIDC config as AuthProviderNoUserManagerProps.\n\nAuthProviderProps is a union, so settings fields like authority were not visible to TypeScript.\n\n* Cover issuer-host wiring, proxy edge cases, and expired sandbox leafs.\n\nKind create only gained hostAliases through untested resolveConfig, and the TLS edge did not assert encoded /dex routing or the full forwarding-header list.\n\n* Mount the SPA under /app and move peer Dex to /idp on the AIO edge.\n\n* minor doc, keycloak, and compose tweaks\n\n* minor doc, go tweak\n\n* improve readme to make clear different AIO default values and their purposes\n\n* Rename the aio-proxy catch-all upstream to FleetShift and drop stdlib-redundant header/size settings.\n\nKeep stripping hop/identity headers Rewrite does not delete, and still assert the four Rewrite-dropped names never reach Dex or FleetShift.\n\n* Run aio-proxy as uid 1002 so the TLS edge cannot read FleetShift or Dex state.\n\nThe gateway leaf key is owned by that uid; serve stays 1000 and Dex stays 1001.\n\n* Lead the root README with AIO podman run recipes.\n\nKeep compose, Nx, and packaging internals after a Start here section so a sandbox trial does not require the developer toolchain first.\n\n* Fix AuthGate retry and empty OIDC scope so failed logins can recover and the client still requests openid.\n\n* Format SPA auth files with Prettier and surface hosts-file close errors after append.","reason"