ps://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Hyperkid123","id":22619452,"login":"Hyperkid123","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5NDUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/a7d4bcf7e04ee21207218279c4bf98f580b0e202/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T09:01:56Z","email":"marvusm.mmi@gmail.com","name":"Martin Marosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T09:01:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(build): implement NX remote cache (#152)\n\n* feat(build): implement NX remote cache\n\n* fix: address CodeRabbit review feedback on NX remote cache PR\n\nAdd OCP restricted-v2 securityContext to MinIO containers, fix mc\nconfig-dir for non-root execution, proper 401/403 in proxy auth,\nrspack cache.version for multi-compiler isolation, preserve persistent\ncache in build commands, add build outputs to project.json, remove\ncredential printing from deploy.sh, and fix gitignore pattern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: graceful MinIO degradation and harden bucket-job\n\nProxy now returns cache-miss (404/200) instead of 500 when MinIO is\nunreachable, so builds degrade to uncached rather than failing.\n\nBucket job improvements:\n- set -eu to propagate mc failures\n- Bounded retry loop (15 attempts + activeDeadlineSeconds: 120)\n- Idempotent lifecycle via mc ilm import instead of ilm rule add\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: promote NX cache ARGs to ENV in Dockerfile.web\n\nARG → ENV promotion ensures Nx sees proper environment variables.\nMulti-stage build prevents them from leaking into the final image.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: wire NX_CACHE flag into podman:up task\n\n`task podman:up -- -f overrides/nx-cache.yaml` silently ignored the\noverride file. Add NX_CACHE var (like DEV/LOCAL_WEB) that appends\nthe nx-cache.yaml compose override when set to true.\n\nUsage: NX_CACHE=true task podman:up\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2607ac9b09c3c88a6c2a18889cce8e02791a8a40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/2607ac9b09c3c88a6c2a18889cce8e02791a8a40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/a7d4bcf7e04ee21207218279c4bf98f580b0e202","verification":{"payload":"tree 2607ac9b09c3c88a6c2a18889cce8e02791a8a40\nparent 6f3b58e5070ca757745d50a02b8b6edb01d17e37\nauthor Martin Marosi <marvusm.mmi@gmail.com> 1786438916 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786438916 +0200\n\nfeat(build): implement NX remote cache (#152)\n\n* feat(build): implement NX remote cache\n\n* fix: address CodeRabbit review feedback on NX remote cache PR\n\nAdd OCP restricted-v2 securityContext to MinIO containers, fix mc\nconfig-dir for non-root execution, proper 401/403 in proxy auth,\nrspack cache.version for multi-compiler isolation, preserve persistent\ncache in build commands, add build outputs to project.json, remove\ncredential printing from deploy.sh, and fix gitignore pattern.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: graceful MinIO degradation and harden bucket-job\n\nProxy now returns cache-miss (404/200) instead of 500 when MinIO is\nunreachable, so builds degrade to uncached rather than failing.\n\nBucket job improvements:\n- set -eu to propagate mc failures\n- Bounded retry loop (15 attempts + activeDeadlineSeconds: 120)\n- Idempotent lifecycle via mc ilm import instead of ilm rule add\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: promote NX cache ARGs to ENV in Dockerfile.web\n\nARG → ENV promotion ensures Nx sees proper environment variables.\nMulti-stage build prevents them from leaking into the final image.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: wire NX_CACHE flag into podman:up task\n\n`task podman:up -- -f overrides/nx-cache.yaml` silently ignored the\noverride file. Add NX_CACHE var (like DEV/LOCAL_WEB) that appends\nthe nx-cache.yaml compose override when set to true.\n\nUsage: NX_CACHE=true task podman:up\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqeuUECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzScQAA1dgiu87+L16e4aF8Vt6J3/\nLLRS8dzMbgmOgEuYhj+ryxqIITM5hRcNAeqTfhpvvFOIaRohW8PjcugkzZUbleuX\nfMTgikwOTRkSNEaZ051lTLba2dvDO469XcWnZOXU8lIxThumhuULVVafk1sv9KXx\nOeX+LD48Pm0q5LH/nEPLulZ8RnyPSrXRRVJfUYm8gtQJW6Z7N/18YxBVxsNetK/v\nhf1SH5YtIv36m+nMN862WBWYM2ECXDw607dhjJ+ARTB9AH5OudPiW3IVtoHxLFM1\nIGtW5M63v9h2U1yxeTENWDFgbkfBtqsi6yn2CGZrjYFfWeXvpzHHGu9PmhRlCJUR\n9TdHueZmCHHk9qrC+h7N1KrNshslBoMReCmuux2O1ESfmI+fVDS/ftE3eummAwE+\ng/oWuLKWkXPfNfhIorG+Ctd/O+VIZMo1hJJSBR3xdmlJZwX+blJdW9civ13J9zHx\nV5Kkvz5B8eIz17X2q6TCxm3tgg+Ud2SlUazOoChfUjz1WIgSgZbr0M+6Kd3qh7wn\nhucunDl1+4eR55p29aGdOzkSfbZmV2zD6tQDln5iH0UJQ25/x4BH2udDSCg4cqDz\ni5xdIV7gzaYGSR8SKNKkL67yO6clzotsZxwJ5z0fLKDw3o6PflEhepkbiHeoqjF3\ny0TcMNjioTyC1RF+tbRK\n=b/SC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-11T09:01:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/a7d4bcf7e04ee21207218279c4bf98f580b0e202","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKGE3ZDRiY2Y3ZTA0ZWUyMTIwNzIxODI3OWM0YmY5OGY1ODBiMGUyMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/6f3b58e5070ca757745d50a02b8b6edb01d17e37","sha":"6f3b58e5070ca757745d50a02b8b6edb01d17e37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/6f3b58e5070ca757745d50a02b8b6edb01d17e37"}],"sha":"a7d4bcf7e04ee21207218279c4bf98f580b0e202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/a7d4bcf7e04ee21207218279c4bf98f580b0e202"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22619452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Hyperkid123","id":22619452,"login":"Hyperkid123","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5NDUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/6f3b58e5070ca757745d50a02b8b6edb01d17e37/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T07:21:19Z","email":"marvusm.mmi@gmail.com","name":"Martin Marosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T07:21:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"OME-270: Restructure monorepo directory layout (#149)\n\n* OME-270: restructure monorepo directory layout\n\nFlatten the directory hierarchy per the OME-242 spike:\n\n  fleetshift-server/ → server/\n  fleetshift-cli/    → cli/\n  fleetshift-ui/gui/ → client/web/\n  fleetshift-ui/common/ → sdk/common/\n  fleetshift-ui/build-utils/ → sdk/build-utils/\n  fleetshift-ui/mock-ui-plugins/ → extensions/core/client/\n  fleetshift-ui/scripts/*.mjs → tools/*.mjs\n\nUpdate all Nx project.json files, TypeScript configs, Dockerfiles,\nCI workflows, Taskfile, buf.gen.yaml, vitest config, and deploy\noverrides to match new paths. Move eslint and stylelint configs to\nrepo root. Move UI docs/spikes to docs/ui/. Remove the legacy\nfleetshift-ui/ directory.\n\nGo module paths are intentionally unchanged (separate future task).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update path references for restructured directories\n\nUpdate fleetshift-server/ → server/ in docs, AGENTS.md, README,\nand POC readmes. Remove stale fleetshift-ui/ directory reference.\nAnchor /web/ and /web in .gitignore/.dockerignore to avoid matching\nclient/web/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* MOve kind/gcphcp to extensions dir/packages\n\n* migrate all package.json scripts in packages to project.json\n\n* Replace some implicit dependecies with proper deps reference\n\n* rename gui to web\n\n* OME-274: optimize UI bundles with dynamic module splitting for @fleetshift/common\n\nMirror the PatternFly dynamic-modules pattern for @fleetshift/common to\neliminate unused module bundling across MF plugins. Previously the barrel\nexport caused every plugin to bundle all common modules including a 3.3MB\nPF icons chunk from pfIconLoader — even plugins that never use the icon\npicker. Non-cached page load drops to ~29kB JS transferred / ~430ms.\n\n- Add build-time generator that parses index.ts and produces\n  common-modules.json + dist/dynamic/ per-file entry points\n- Add SWC transformImport + correction plugin for @fleetshift/common\n  (createCommonTransformImport, createCommonModuleReplacementPlugin)\n- Add getCommonDynamicModules() to register per-module MF shared entries\n- Replace @fleetshift/common barrel in MF shared config with per-module\n  dynamic entries across all 4 rspack configs (core, gcphcp, kind, web)\n- Switch rspack mode from hardcoded \"development\" to NODE_ENV-based\n  (production for builds, development for dev watch)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f0f729bfaba14ea9eab337556e5ee4dc07aee5aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/f0f729bfaba14ea9eab337556e5ee4dc07aee5aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/6f3b58e5070ca757745d50a02b8b6edb01d17e37","verification":{"payload":"tree f0f729bfaba14ea9eab337556e5ee4dc07aee5aa\nparent 8daaffc5eb756e301b5938c1551a276f723710b5\nauthor Martin Marosi <marvusm.mmi@gmail.com> 1786000879 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786000879 +0200\n\nOME-270: Restructure monorepo directory layout (#149)\n\n* OME-270: restructure monorepo directory layout\n\nFlatten the directory hierarchy per the OME-242 spike:\n\n  fleetshift-server/ → server/\n  fleetshift-cli/    → cli/\n  fleetshift-ui/gui/ → client/web/\n  fleetshift-ui/common/ → sdk/common/\n  fleetshift-ui/build-utils/ → sdk/build-utils/\n  fleetshift-ui/mock-ui-plugins/ → extensions/core/client/\n  fleetshift-ui/scripts/*.mjs → tools/*.mjs\n\nUpdate all Nx project.json files, TypeScript configs, Dockerfiles,\nCI workflows, Taskfile, buf.gen.yaml, vitest config, and deploy\noverrides to match new paths. Move eslint and stylelint configs to\nrepo root. Move UI docs/spikes to docs/ui/. Remove the legacy\nfleetshift-ui/ directory.\n\nGo module paths are intentionally unchanged (separate future task).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update path references for restructured directories\n\nUpdate fleetshift-server/ → server/ in docs, AGENTS.md, README,\nand POC readmes. Remove stale fleetshift-ui/ directory reference.\nAnchor /web/ and /web in .gitignore/.dockerignore to avoid matching\nclient/web/.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* MOve kind/gcphcp to extensions dir/packages\n\n* migrate all package.json scripts in packages to project.json\n\n* Replace some implicit dependecies with proper deps reference\n\n* rename gui to web\n\n* OME-274: optimize UI bundles with dynamic module splitting for @fleetshift/common\n\nMirror the PatternFly dynamic-modules pattern for @fleetshift/common to\neliminate unused module bundling across MF plugins. Previously the barrel\nexport caused every plugin to bundle all common modules including a 3.3MB\nPF icons chunk from pfIconLoader — even plugins that never use the icon\npicker. Non-cached page load drops to ~29kB JS transferred / ~430ms.\n\n- Add build-time generator that parses index.ts and produces\n  common-modules.json + dist/dynamic/ per-file entry points\n- Add SWC transformImport + correction plugin for @fleetshift/common\n  (createCommonTransformImport, createCommonModuleReplacementPlugin)\n- Add getCommonDynamicModules() to register per-module MF shared entries\n- Replace @fleetshift/common barrel in MF shared config with per-module\n  dynamic entries across all 4 rspack configs (core, gcphcp, kind, web)\n- Switch rspack mode from hardcoded \"development\" to NODE_ENV-based\n  (production for builds, development for dev watch)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdDXvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOCsQAHjIPSLw7S4Mom1b97THCFW0\n2GvnXgWmmmz5nfy/2TFD2hhj6iS+gAe1MdpI1tC+XFEqOHvIDgUxSJdwzySC9/pE\ntG3PXH8EoIumI5VpHBmncRmKbjEvpeKEWSDfrymA9Pij442cxICIWq0ThkUJobJl\n6+/qhLeAa8P2uS7BxxjzCWSftCnZxjfhxPDqLLISpoNAGZ0+5wwQwJzFDVrmarxh\nk0LcJTG0Fyq0bBBBeQNF4/7A4ePUuCM+vChs310Iy2B6FsM7yiSQ0xZNdfnxhyTx\nNM5DDfkyE2d+FfoX6FiqyxpqgOy8PSPjzsvSGGEICp4JlUlmgkswKdqo32X99sCS\n/IuUhOe2VRE2h5yU1gDDmmRXNmj85QdHPy8rlzwEvDoXcdLLr0TTGMIKw17KnShi\nJkKDRl940Oo2NcCBXNWMgVsyBmK8MSn8eTr7BRQ5Bl8G5NfmTgOssKf/o4auhw+J\nEOZCdlrEjDFEN78yJdrppcM+3/Yy6erZJem5W3lVotVWbLQSebF/33ObPCnZ5yP6\nJxYtfekugrwQRc+pX9Eh4rRCtf6HYuSBIaCKD87Q4mIE/MYmOR6AY4Z1GUdRW3fj\nx4AOemME2lOpeFneIEksJFl8PD4YiB99bs+Rcyctprxa9KsvJoEm1zixOWGnznDS\nXqNkI59kvaSNMQYOGeV+\n=Z0ax\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-06T07:21:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/6f3b58e5070ca757745d50a02b8b6edb01d17e37","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKDZmM2I1OGU1MDcwY2E3NTc3NDVkNTBhMDJiOGI2ZWRiMDFkMTdlMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/8daaffc5eb756e301b5938c1551a276f723710b5","sha":"8daaffc5eb756e301b5938c1551a276f723710b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/8daaffc5eb756e301b5938c1551a276f723710b5"}],"sha":"6f3b58e5070ca757745d50a02b8b6edb01d17e37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/6f3b58e5070ca757745d50a02b8b6edb01d17e37"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22619452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Hyperkid123","id":22619452,"login":"Hyperkid123","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5NDUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/8daaffc5eb756e301b5938c1551a276f723710b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:41:19Z","email":"marvusm.mmi@gmail.com","name":"Martin Marosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T08:41:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"OME-243: Replace Task CLI with direct commands in Nx targets (#148)\n\n* feat: replace Task CLI with direct commands in Nx build/test targets\n\nBuild, test, proto, and image Nx targets now call Go/buf/podman\ndirectly instead of shelling out to `task`. Infra targets (pd:*, kc:*,\nk8s:*) still wrap Taskfile — to be migrated in a later phase.\n\n- Inline go build/test commands in server and cli project.json\n- Inline buf generate in proto project.json\n- Make build:all, test:all, protogen pure dependsOn aggregation targets\n- Use envFile + shell variable expansion for image targets\n- Multi-stage Dockerfile.web: ubi9-micro runtime with static assets only\n- Update AGENTS.md to reflect new Nx target structure\n\nCloses: OME-243\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: disable Nx caching for Go test targets\n\n-count=1 bypasses Go''s test cache but Nx''s caching layer still\napplies. Add cache: false so tests always run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4814610c37dc092995e2d4a25d5cdec74150f04c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/4814610c37dc092995e2d4a25d5cdec74150f04c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/8daaffc5eb756e301b5938c1551a276f723710b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 4814610c37dc092995e2d4a25d5cdec74150f04c\nparent a2ba8955b116dc4cceb54dbde68ee597a66f792c\nauthor Martin Marosi <marvusm.mmi@gmail.com> 1785832879 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785832879 +0200\n\nOME-243: Replace Task CLI with direct commands in Nx targets (#148)\n\n* feat: replace Task CLI with direct commands in Nx build/test targets\n\nBuild, test, proto, and image Nx targets now call Go/buf/podman\ndirectly instead of shelling out to `task`. Infra targets (pd:*, kc:*,\nk8s:*) still wrap Taskfile — to be migrated in a later phase.\n\n- Inline go build/test commands in server and cli project.json\n- Inline buf generate in proto project.json\n- Make build:all, test:all, protogen pure dependsOn aggregation targets\n- Use envFile + shell variable expansion for image targets\n- Multi-stage Dockerfile.web: ubi9-micro runtime with static assets only\n- Update AGENTS.md to reflect new Nx target structure\n\nCloses: OME-243\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: disable Nx caching for Go test targets\n\n-count=1 bypasses Go''s test cache but Nx''s caching layer still\napplies. Add cache: false so tests always run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcaWvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgOwQAKlyhlxgv5+nTnMQ1c8dIrCh\nRDzp31OVLVllefnI67vwBuvegnidvq6oZCsiWpqdvKXiZVDNsAfGZmZxAHGRMSd5\n/aew/vbKmnpF277AeW8DkhU6v37zUOUmjpB1VC5V3WNzki2lhN9wEOwH8Skc7gXP\nxlwCDxWBW0rC9YzDjqw4IbtNWbxaIuxwIoEbGrXHkthOTNjPRJzYZlIJrUWNtkzL\nUS5X7fEbqx/ALm3pd+mXIZWUksff9CfkShVJBJWzcQhkz7wQmY8Th0KtT0HrhuS2\nkGrJg9nQ1Qbje32oXUwbybdYt7GR/qGCxFSmQrio6X33N/9mqwA77gy/JPUwwFl6\nPxMYO4pEb/u8k5GcB8VnUJLfWgJEgMBZeJ2K8ochW06tZy+NfgKe/ctPj6CBzbik\njF6QouEtGdfsJ1fa5pt8g/mWo1WZK6+hGiChFcO4txwE6wICL5sxEUni+Zi8uP8x\n2f7ok/x5GymBPMl/63tTDVIsZXW0m+ls6F/5F06eB57GORE2CrxSXmOz/miRHjtg\nyY7wDWp01r4hDASHOWg8RFpDDPga+LWGb/XdHEMcdLHU8GvGnay9y0DR9lqZCLDK\nAe1zdMU0bQsRleqc9vu+bpaULIhbQDxveYmrDkesg0bh5KTBoVo+eSz3D1yrjbLF\nQSjmcZrkBLCHOAip7r2E\n=3bGa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-04T08:41:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/8daaffc5eb756e301b5938c1551a276f723710b5","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKDhkYWFmZmM1ZWI3NTZlMzAxYjU5MzhjMTU1MWEyNzZmNzIzNzEwYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/a2ba8955b116dc4cceb54dbde68ee597a66f792c","sha":"a2ba8955b116dc4cceb54dbde68ee597a66f792c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/a2ba8955b116dc4cceb54dbde68ee597a66f792c"}],"sha":"8daaffc5eb756e301b5938c1551a276f723710b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/8daaffc5eb756e301b5938c1551a276f723710b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97869221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mshort55","id":97869221,"login":"mshort55","node_id":"U_kgDOBdVdpQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/a2ba8955b116dc4cceb54dbde68ee597a66f792c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-04T01:47:42Z","email":"97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matthew Short"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-04T01:47:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"OME-252: Add hermetic-api testenv harness and first e2e API scenarios (#147)\n\n* Add hermetic-api testenv harness and first e2e API scenarios.\n\nIntroduce runner-neutral internal/testenv over shared bootstrap, scripted delivery and controlled inventory controllers, and two focused public API e2e scenarios with allow-listed artifacts.\n\n* slimmed down main test scenario file to be ultra readable. moved everything into helper funcs. moved 1 test.\n\n* Scope hermetic naming to the hermetic-api profile; rename e2e test files for clarity\n\nReword testenv doc comments that described profile-agnostic Env/StartT/\nIssueToken/InventoryController as inherently \"hermetic\" — misleading now\nthat Env already models kind/oci-smoke/production-deps profiles. Rename\ne2e/api_scenario_test.go -> hermetic_api_fixture_test.go and\ne2e/hermetic_api_test.go -> hermetic_api_scenarios_test.go to separate\nthe scenario fixture from the actual scenario tests.\n\n* remove ca file creation from oidc fake\n\n* testenv: delete work dirs on pass; keep private server.log on fail\n\nStop unbounded /tmp accumulation for green StartT runs, while retaining\nthe work dir (with server.log outside artifacts/) for failure diagnosis.\n\n* testenv: isolate Finish tests from ambient KEEP env\n\nClear FLEETSHIFT_TESTENV_KEEP in default test helpers so a shell KEEP=1\ndoes not break delete-on-pass assertions.\n\n* testenv: use in-memory SQLite and dump DBFile on retain\n\nAvoid file-backed DB I/O during hermetic runs via WithSQLiteDB +\nOpenMemory; VACUUM INTO fleetshift.db only when the work dir is kept.\n\n* Harden hermetic testenv review follow-ups.\n\nRedact Postgres log formatting, require registry with injected SQLite,\nunblock fake gates on mode switch, dump DB when server close forces\nretention, and tighten e2e wait assertions.","tree":{"sha":"06986650828e3a27511feeff2220c56d5d0ab0da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/06986650828e3a27511feeff2220c56d5d0ab0da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/a2ba8955b116dc4cceb54dbde68ee597a66f792c","verification":{"payload":"tree 06986650828e3a27511feeff2220c56d5d0ab0da\nparent 0ff9066edf58aeb85b709c6037023206855214b0\nauthor Matthew Short <97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com> 1785808062 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785808062 -0700\n\nOME-252: Add hermetic-api testenv harness and first e2e API scenarios (#147)\n\n* Add hermetic-api testenv harness and first e2e API scenarios.\n\nIntroduce runner-neutral internal/testenv over shared bootstrap, scripted delivery and controlled inventory controllers, and two focused public API e2e scenarios with allow-listed artifacts.\n\n* slimmed down main test scenario file to be ultra readable. moved everything into helper funcs. moved 1 test.\n\n* Scope hermetic naming to the hermetic-api profile; rename e2e test files for clarity\n\nReword testenv doc comments that described profile-agnostic Env/StartT/\nIssueToken/InventoryController as inherently \"hermetic\" — misleading now\nthat Env already models kind/oci-smoke/production-deps profiles. Rename\ne2e/api_scenario_test.go -> hermetic_api_fixture_test.go and\ne2e/hermetic_api_test.go -> hermetic_api_scenarios_test.go to separate\nthe scenario fixture from the actual scenario tests.\n\n* remove ca file creation from oidc fake\n\n* testenv: delete work dirs on pass; keep private server.log on fail\n\nStop unbounded /tmp accumulation for green StartT runs, while retaining\nthe work dir (with server.log outside artifacts/) for failure diagnosis.\n\n* testenv: isolate Finish tests from ambient KEEP env\n\nClear FLEETSHIFT_TESTENV_KEEP in default test helpers so a shell KEEP=1\ndoes not break delete-on-pass assertions.\n\n* testenv: use in-memory SQLite and dump DBFile on retain\n\nAvoid file-backed DB I/O during hermetic runs via WithSQLiteDB +\nOpenMemory; VACUUM INTO fleetshift.db only when the work dir is kept.\n\n* Harden hermetic testenv review follow-ups.\n\nRedact Postgres log formatting, require registry with injected SQLite,\nunblock fake gates on mode switch, dump DB when server close forces\nretention, and tighten e2e wait assertions.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcUS+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgIoQAH57zyJuu7JOhp/JpZ8mGgGE\njfD9evlHFCZnUJNbmq3lKKjvN/1K15I905cZuxSvAZaf1rB71L6KdmU63xKPtKTo\nZiZTE9Vcxlsrrems696clP3H9weFjqWe3+dlFvbPz9K5zW+U+YEtiYMGXTnEFIU8\noEQjUCoNVO+6cF1UD9yg0LvYWwenGAaN8lJg5x1X4OGfheJgKbty90mpCxMF/czC\nb8zSZtfdr6p5BQzcYJLH7aAYJZQD36PEVRbD3iaYOLgALv2eBxog1Z99z9T/wLOc\nrDl1GH59DJaEfH5IC8xojKwaP2qqiU01RVOWdYUwI24jqLvYY729FC/GdyACcx39\nb8oF5M91B6263ljQP0qDfK1NHc50dWgXt9TtpPe6T9lqILhPMRqlSNm2XKa3R1Ad\noqIZEwwWH/7eLL350/3LPrMCuAtIC63XG7PirRBGWIAl6hyqOlnAiaF0NxHquFft\njJmSvE0oy5sNHq34V3mWinoOTp/5y5snzwVWH1DB5m9pGqKHgCgZ0PH39j02W/Wn\nbVrA4lbwm4wFHcqTj5g5W7Ya2c7UqhZ3Op8ygSJWbh2I3TvbIh4Gt0UFCe6WE5Id\n4BOWvJk+K+SYXkpY17d0MPJYdpWFbjK2grXjpy12oCpoMqticnR/4nwYOy8YzgYt\nF1OvgaJMO3YXDV8MKoH/\n=cPCY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-04T01:47:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/a2ba8955b116dc4cceb54dbde68ee597a66f792c","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKGEyYmE4OTU1YjExNmRjNGNjZWI1NGRiZGU2OGVlNTk3YTY2Zjc5MmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/0ff9066edf58aeb85b709c6037023206855214b0","sha":"0ff9066edf58aeb85b709c6037023206855214b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/0ff9066edf58aeb85b709c6037023206855214b0"}],"sha":"a2ba8955b116dc4cceb54dbde68ee597a66f792c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/a2ba8955b116dc4cceb54dbde68ee597a66f792c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22619452?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Hyperkid123","id":22619452,"login":"Hyperkid123","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjE5NDUy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hyperkid123","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/0ff9066edf58aeb85b709c6037023206855214b0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T10:06:49Z","email":"marvusm.mmi@gmail.com","name":"Martin Marosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T10:06:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"OME-260: migrate UI nx targets to first-party executors and flatten package structure (#146)\n\n* feat(ui): migrate nx targets to first-party executors and flatten package structure\n\nReplace nx:run-commands with @nx/eslint:lint and @nx/playwright:playwright\nwhere practical. Flatten fleetshift-ui/packages/ to fleetshift-ui/ — each\npackage (gui, common, build-utils, mock-ui-plugins, e2e) now lives directly\nunder fleetshift-ui/. Move root Nx targets from package.json to project.json.\nUpdate Docker build context, vitest config, and rspack paths to match new\nstructure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: include root tsconfig and README updates from flattening\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ui): update paths after packages/ flattening\n\nRemove stale packages/ prefix from file references in README,\ndesign docs, and LikeC4 diagrams. Update workspace commands\nto use Nx instead of npm workspace scripts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add UI tests to CI and keycloak/kubernetes Nx targets\n\nAdd ui-test job to GitHub Actions running vitest unit tests and\nPlaywright component tests (gui + plugins) on every push/PR to main.\n\nAdd kc:* (5) and k8s:* (11) Nx targets wrapping all remaining\nTaskfile commands that lacked Nx equivalents.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): build common before Playwright CT tests\n\nplugins:test:ct imports @fleetshift/common from dist (not source alias),\nso common:build must run first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: migrate Playwright from deprecated executor to inferred plugin\n\nReplace @nx/playwright:playwright executor (deprecated, removed in v24)\nwith @nx/playwright/plugin inferred targets. Rename playwright-ct.config.ts\nto playwright.config.ts so the plugin auto-detects them. Remove explicit\ntest:ct targets from project.json — plugin infers test:ct and atomized\ntest:ct:ci targets automatically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ui): update playwright config filename in AGENTS.md\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: move Dockerfile.web to repo root\n\nBuild context is the monorepo root — all other Dockerfiles (Dockerfile,\nDockerfile.local, Dockerfile.fleetshift) already live at root. Align\nDockerfile.web with the same convention.\n\nUpdated references in Taskfile.yml, deploy/podman/overrides/dev.yaml,\ndeploy/podman/README.md, and fleetshift-ui/README.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"541a58e5b96529f4f6cf480da67630e1d4ba7c5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/541a58e5b96529f4f6cf480da67630e1d4ba7c5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/0ff9066edf58aeb85b709c6037023206855214b0","verification":{"payload":"tree 541a58e5b96529f4f6cf480da67630e1d4ba7c5d\nparent 94fc0619eed99745e72875ba067dff64079bd2d3\nauthor Martin Marosi <marvusm.mmi@gmail.com> 1785751609 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785751609 +0200\n\nOME-260: migrate UI nx targets to first-party executors and flatten package structure (#146)\n\n* feat(ui): migrate nx targets to first-party executors and flatten package structure\n\nReplace nx:run-commands with @nx/eslint:lint and @nx/playwright:playwright\nwhere practical. Flatten fleetshift-ui/packages/ to fleetshift-ui/ — each\npackage (gui, common, build-utils, mock-ui-plugins, e2e) now lives directly\nunder fleetshift-ui/. Move root Nx targets from package.json to project.json.\nUpdate Docker build context, vitest config, and rspack paths to match new\nstructure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: include root tsconfig and README updates from flattening\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ui): update paths after packages/ flattening\n\nRemove stale packages/ prefix from file references in README,\ndesign docs, and LikeC4 diagrams. Update workspace commands\nto use Nx instead of npm workspace scripts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add UI tests to CI and keycloak/kubernetes Nx targets\n\nAdd ui-test job to GitHub Actions running vitest unit tests and\nPlaywright component tests (gui + plugins) on every push/PR to main.\n\nAdd kc:* (5) and k8s:* (11) Nx targets wrapping all remaining\nTaskfile commands that lacked Nx equivalents.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(ci): build common before Playwright CT tests\n\nplugins:test:ct imports @fleetshift/common from dist (not source alias),\nso common:build must run first.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: migrate Playwright from deprecated executor to inferred plugin\n\nReplace @nx/playwright:playwright executor (deprecated, removed in v24)\nwith @nx/playwright/plugin inferred targets. Rename playwright-ct.config.ts\nto playwright.config.ts so the plugin auto-detects them. Remove explicit\ntest:ct targets from project.json — plugin infers test:ct and atomized\ntest:ct:ci targets automatically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ui): update playwright config filename in AGENTS.md\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: move Dockerfile.web to repo root\n\nBuild context is the monorepo root — all other Dockerfiles (Dockerfile,\nDockerfile.local, Dockerfile.fleetshift) already live at root. Align\nDockerfile.web with the same convention.\n\nUpdated references in Taskfile.yml, deploy/podman/overrides/dev.yaml,\ndeploy/podman/README.md, and fleetshift-ui/README.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcGg5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcPUQAEEfNcn4XvVXHo67w1kZRJ3P\nIy8TuB+TOlBvm27BXEiO6X0BpqC2qpjT0g5mD23xC/w2RrUifBkMCUD8TZ589FSM\ny/BKvCdZ/HRbDkvkvv+PlJaz/7v8Y+7NOPs+6Nhq08/tWCbni6t8qtYEccFvsZ/W\n/u2eHLu8HStQvjwB7h6ZvOnRsREbKqaX76TeBgEiY1ESjGMSmoM1zsfTWnvbAt0y\nhsay8RvmEJnsVkwNAcq7jAvW67sSRE7GtDmHI4s2rZm+6Dqb4Chka/0uYnWL789I\n/sCYpBnM9dB5ESBKdgKYyujGDNdX9RCDGMcvPOyavTZn3F4vZC0sd79jlmML8tLu\ncLDWQRcVXz1Xlc08OQpzcoH4SKS79rCmFglhskZNwHwsUmczdj+nGZBtwnzqWQGM\n2y4Wy1AvhuAzbX5AYfu/Ws/ZVhLZANCnHTtTO89IV6MSs/OuK3r+hQ2NwOQ98GaY\n462g1SAlo5gWa7dZucsGZE68qXQwXl9eBk8XU4cl033VR7dyf+xl3xv1bPL8+qof\n/4I2dbw/Yzjw8fXhEflOauuCKVEWpaLC753KZRd4yWxD3b2sKep7fkQ1eO2jD4dE\nz6rX2cPQ2xm5ED5XMiRL4nSfYl44afMziH5+yh5ijsLCcZeMM/N0yqoBREgWc+OQ\nwfytb2kEcWcYADt305hO\n=Q9Z8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T10:06:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/0ff9066edf58aeb85b709c6037023206855214b0","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKDBmZjkwNjZlZGY1OGFlYjg1YjcwOWM2MDM3MDIzMjA2ODU1MjE0YjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/94fc0619eed99745e72875ba067dff64079bd2d3","sha":"94fc0619eed99745e72875ba067dff64079bd2d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/94fc0619eed99745e72875ba067dff64079bd2d3"}],"sha":"0ff9066edf58aeb85b709c6037023206855214b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/0ff9066edf58aeb85b709c6037023206855214b0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97869221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mshort55","id":97869221,"login":"mshort55","node_id":"U_kgDOBdVdpQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/94fc0619eed99745e72875ba067dff64079bd2d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:06:01Z","email":"97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matthew Short"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T15:06:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"OME-250 OME-251: Extract production composition into shared serverapp lifecycle (#145)\n\n* Normalize serve configuration into serverapp before resource I/O.\n\nParse CLI/env/file inputs into typed Config with a sealed Database sum type so invalid DB, addon, CA, and GCP combinations fail without opening storage.\n\n* Extract production composition into serverapp Start/Wait/Close.\n\nCLI and testserver share one eager builder with readiness and bounded\nshutdown. JWKS registration is fail-fast and recoverable without blocking\nprocess start.\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review findings on the shared serverapp lifecycle.\n\nReject empty --database-url-file content so an unpopulated URL file cannot\nsilently select the default SQLite path. Stop gRPC/HTTP with the same\ngraceful-then-forced ingress path when readiness fails after Serve starts.\nMake GoWorkflowRuntime cancel on Close and memoize WaitForCompletion so\nshutdown is self-contained and idempotent. Deduplicate the OIDC CA-bundle\nHTTP client used by identity and addon assembly. Relax the JWKS-down Start\ntiming assertion to an 8s CI-tolerant ceiling. Bound testserver.Start with\na 30s context. Tighten expected-surface HTTP family/probe alignment to\nprefix-only matching. Drop the duplicate CLI database-url-file test case.\nReject nil Connect.Agent when DeliveryCapability is claimed; keep the Kind\nfacade delivery-free so create/delete semantics stay intact. Register JWKS\nURIs under a per-URI mutex so network I/O does not hold the key-set lock or\nshare one caller''s context across waiters.\n\n* Rename serverapp to bootstrap.\n\nAvoids ambiguity with the application layer while naming the composition/lifecycle edge.\n\n* Rename bootstrap App to Server and app.go to server.go.\n\nAlign the lifecycle handle and entry file with the package, and use srv/s naming at call sites.\n\n* Fold workflow Start/Wait/Close into domain.Registry.\n\nDrop the bootstrap WorkflowRuntime wrapper; infrastructure registries own lifecycle.\n\n* Document JWKS registerLocks bounds and outage retry TODO.\n\nAlso drop unnecessary blank receive in the concurrent RegisterKeySet test.\n\n* Tighten bootstrap/OIDC comments and drop unused dial-address errors.\n\n* Rename bootstrap OIDC deps and related composition identifiers.\n\n* Simplify bootstrap Start: extract helpers and drop duplicated deps.\n\nShare one inventory report service and OIDC HTTP client, parse GCP config once, and remove dead CLI parseAddons / unused Server fields.\n\n* Harden bootstrap lifecycle tests and Close wait-budget semantics.\n\nExpand Gate 2 surface/lifecycle coverage, share MustCAPEM, and make Close\nhonor independent caller deadlines without aborting shared cleanup.\n\n* Simplify Close to sync shared shutdown per revised D31.\n\nDrop independent in-flight Close wait budgets; first caller finishes\ncleanup and concurrent callers share the result.\n\n* Share one Close-owned ClientConn for gRPC-gateway handlers.\n\nAvoid HandlerFromEndpoint tied to the start context, which tore down\nloopback conns when testserver cancelled that context after Start.","tree":{"sha":"f7426ce0805aa8c6fe304ab419e2a0b9f753e253","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/f7426ce0805aa8c6fe304ab419e2a0b9f753e253"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/94fc0619eed99745e72875ba067dff64079bd2d3","verification":{"payload":"tree f7426ce0805aa8c6fe304ab419e2a0b9f753e253\nparent 9972b5c290d63049b0b180a9d054aa9b6ba56ff7\nauthor Matthew Short <97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com> 1785510361 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785510361 -0700\n\nOME-250 OME-251: Extract production composition into shared serverapp lifecycle (#145)\n\n* Normalize serve configuration into serverapp before resource I/O.\n\nParse CLI/env/file inputs into typed Config with a sealed Database sum type so invalid DB, addon, CA, and GCP combinations fail without opening storage.\n\n* Extract production composition into serverapp Start/Wait/Close.\n\nCLI and testserver share one eager builder with readiness and bounded\nshutdown. JWKS registration is fail-fast and recoverable without blocking\nprocess start.\n\n* Address CodeRabbit review findings on the shared serverapp lifecycle.\n\nReject empty --database-url-file content so an unpopulated URL file cannot\nsilently select the default SQLite path. Stop gRPC/HTTP with the same\ngraceful-then-forced ingress path when readiness fails after Serve starts.\nMake GoWorkflowRuntime cancel on Close and memoize WaitForCompletion so\nshutdown is self-contained and idempotent. Deduplicate the OIDC CA-bundle\nHTTP client used by identity and addon assembly. Relax the JWKS-down Start\ntiming assertion to an 8s CI-tolerant ceiling. Bound testserver.Start with\na 30s context. Tighten expected-surface HTTP family/probe alignment to\nprefix-only matching. Drop the duplicate CLI database-url-file test case.\nReject nil Connect.Agent when DeliveryCapability is claimed; keep the Kind\nfacade delivery-free so create/delete semantics stay intact. Register JWKS\nURIs under a per-URI mutex so network I/O does not hold the key-set lock or\nshare one caller''s context across waiters.\n\n* Rename serverapp to bootstrap.\n\nAvoids ambiguity with the application layer while naming the composition/lifecycle edge.\n\n* Rename bootstrap App to Server and app.go to server.go.\n\nAlign the lifecycle handle and entry file with the package, and use srv/s naming at call sites.\n\n* Fold workflow Start/Wait/Close into domain.Registry.\n\nDrop the bootstrap WorkflowRuntime wrapper; infrastructure registries own lifecycle.\n\n* Document JWKS registerLocks bounds and outage retry TODO.\n\nAlso drop unnecessary blank receive in the concurrent RegisterKeySet test.\n\n* Tighten bootstrap/OIDC comments and drop unused dial-address errors.\n\n* Rename bootstrap OIDC deps and related composition identifiers.\n\n* Simplify bootstrap Start: extract helpers and drop duplicated deps.\n\nShare one inventory report service and OIDC HTTP client, parse GCP config once, and remove dead CLI parseAddons / unused Server fields.\n\n* Harden bootstrap lifecycle tests and Close wait-budget semantics.\n\nExpand Gate 2 surface/lifecycle coverage, share MustCAPEM, and make Close\nhonor independent caller deadlines without aborting shared cleanup.\n\n* Simplify Close to sync shared shutdown per revised D31.\n\nDrop independent in-flight Close wait budgets; first caller finishes\ncleanup and concurrent callers share the result.\n\n* Share one Close-owned ClientConn for gRPC-gateway handlers.\n\nAvoid HandlerFromEndpoint tied to the start context, which tore down\nloopback conns when testserver cancelled that context after Start.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbLnZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4bMQAI0Nh3EnBcwwEZ+XmbNzG8vz\nqO1JuyyYxgYEp3Qfl3eb2aUOQ2n1kxy4nF5Tx3oUaTASCMHdQNJbjK11O92g1wFc\nSbR7tyhSpC2kZwWLYD85DgLfSWkLT1R8omSERIyF7Yzu6K2z8dEClDMm8lUphaTK\nICHSj1tPAIIWl++Vs9Q3eJ+K9olpxDgvG7ALZTOZKkNf7Md0Ci8Q5Da2jIkPkABM\n5hSA53+nAatfOUACcbpLvdgDQBvWzPkg8Lwp8UvO8xbX1d0NtMDBbucC9pomajld\njipuF16oglV6pxzN7KxoLPq7jtXgwXrQIocUF2pW1fj+ReHP97+Ve5xEouEujrXf\nbV8BquVtS4axjINjyid470LU