:{"date":"2026-07-15T19:36:10Z","email":"alechenninger@gmail.com","name":"Alec Henninger"},"message":"Remove type_name from inventory delete query","tree":{"sha":"b349be4a1bc648c369c645fc2bb0f47cdaff814d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/b349be4a1bc648c369c645fc2bb0f47cdaff814d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/e2b00bd1d5679a030935863d2a4386375c703d4f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3496559?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/alechenninger","id":3496559,"login":"alechenninger","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0OTY1NTk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alechenninger","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/e2b00bd1d5679a030935863d2a4386375c703d4f","node_id":"C_kwDORXFOSdoAKGUyYjAwYmQxZDU2NzlhMDMwOTM1ODYzZDJhNDM4NjM3NWM3MDNkNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commit/d9b9bbf3b9a2deb30718ac1001692b3f45a0a88b","sha":"d9b9bbf3b9a2deb30718ac1001692b3f45a0a88b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/d9b9bbf3b9a2deb30718ac1001692b3f45a0a88b"}],"sha":"e2b00bd1d5679a030935863d2a4386375c703d4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/e2b00bd1d5679a030935863d2a4386375c703d4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97869221?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/mshort55","id":97869221,"login":"mshort55","node_id":"U_kgDOBdVdpQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mshort55","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/commits/d9b9bbf3b9a2deb30718ac1001692b3f45a0a88b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T18:51:59Z","email":"97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Matthew Short"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T18:51:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"OME-115 (partial), OME-116, OME-117: Kubernetes in-process indexing on extension-resource inventory (#123)\n\n* Phase 0: snapshot Kubernetes addon source from feat/inventory-agent02\n\nVerbatim, byte-for-byte copy of all 26 files under\nfleetshift-server/internal/addon/kubernetes/ on feat/inventory-agent02\n(commit 3b2254827f6511602902c3b326cfe31431d417d4) into a new\n_legacy_agent02/ subdirectory, per docs/fleetshift/inventory/kubernetes-indexing-refactor/07-phased-implementation-plan.md.\n\nNo content changes, no import fixes, no gofmt. The leading underscore\nexcludes the directory from go build/vet/test. Full directory (including\nthe 4 files that already have an equivalent on main) copied per repo\nowner preference for easy side-by-side diffing.\n\n* Phase 1: platform delete/resync/subtree primitives\n\nAdd the missing delete half of the extension-resource inventory\nwrite contract: DeleteInventoryResources, PruneInventoryCollection,\nand DeleteInventorySubtree on ExtensionResourceRepository (SQLite +\nPostgres), plus application-layer DeleteBatch, ReplaceCollection, and\nDeleteCollection on InventoryReportService. Zero Kubernetes code —\nthis only closes platform gaps 1-3 from the kubernetes-indexing-refactor\ndoc set (docs/fleetshift/inventory/kubernetes-indexing-refactor/03-delete-resync-contract.md)\nso the future indexer has somewhere to report deletes and resync\nprunes.\n\nSource commit for the port plan: 3b2254827f6511602902c3b326cfe31431d417d4\n\n* Phase 2: target lifecycle plumbing and cleaner boundary\n\nAdd a generic, Kubernetes-agnostic TargetOutputHooks port on\nOrchestrationWorkflowSpec (AfterTargetRegistered / BeforeTargetDeleted)\nso orchestration depends on one field instead of raw notifier/cleaner\nregistries. The application TargetOutputHookService implements it,\ncomposing a non-failing TargetRuntimeNotifier with a\ntarget-type-to-TargetIndexedInventoryCleaner registry: an undeclared\ntarget type has no indexed inventory, a declared-but-nil cleaner is a\nwiring error, and a cleaner''s failure blocks target row deletion.\n\nSplit the single CleanupDeliveryData activity into\nPlanDeliveryOutputCleanup -> CleanupTargetIndexedInventory ->\nCleanupDeliveryData so target-owned indexed inventory is always\ncleaned up before the target row is deleted. Add\nTargetInventoryCleanupService.DeleteOwnedInventorySubtree as the\nowner-validated, resource-type-scoped subtree-delete primitive\nconcrete cleaners will call.\n\nNo concrete cleaner is registered yet, so existing delivery-only\nbehavior is unaffected.\n\n* Genericize Kubernetes/cluster vocabulary in new inventory-cleanup code\n\nReplace Kubernetes- and cluster-specific wording in the new\ndelete/resync/subtree comments and test fixtures with\nprovider-agnostic terms, keeping the platform target-type-neutral.\n\n* Phase 3: Kubernetes identity/naming contract\n\nAdd a standalone identity.go for the Kubernetes addon: ObjectResourceName\nbuilds \"clusters/{target}/apiResources/{gvr}/objects/{uid}\" through\ndomain.ParseResourceName, path-encoding every dynamic segment so a\ntarget ID containing \"/\" can''t shift the surrounding path structure.\nTargetObjectSubtree gives target-scoped cleanup its parent name, GVRKey\ncollapses group/version/resource into a tilde-separated key that\nsurvives inside one resource-name segment, and\nObjectLabels/ObjectObservation/ObjectConditions produce the query\nlabels, observation payload, and normalized condition set for a\nwatched object -- including generic per-object metadata\n(deletionTimestamp, ownerReferences) alongside the core identity\nfields.\n\nNo indexer wiring yet -- this only adds the identity contract the\nfuture writer and cleaner will call.\n\n* Phase 4: Kubernetes capability and schema registration\n\nDeclare an InventoryResourceCapability and the generic Object\ninventory schema on the Kubernetes addon descriptor, alongside its\nexisting delivery capability. The addon''s ID now reuses the AddonID\nconstant instead of duplicating the literal service name.\n\nCovers both layers: unit tests pin the schema''s exact field shape\n(including fields the platform never reads back for inventory-only\nschemas), and AddonManager tests prove Enable/Connect accept it,\nregister the inventory type, and correctly skip dynamic API\nactivation.\n\n* Phase 3 fix: rename identity.go to object.go, tighten AddonID ownership\n\nEvery symbol in the file is about the identity of a watched Kubernetes\nobject specifically, not the addon in general, and the package is\nabout to gain a roughly equal amount of delivery-side code alongside\nit -- object.go makes that boundary obvious the way informer.go/\nwriter.go already do, matching the file''s own Object* symbol prefix.\n\nAddonID moves to descriptor.go, its only consumer, and\nObjectResourceType is now built from AddonID instead of repeating the\nservice-name literal, so the two can''t drift apart.\n\n* Phase 5: Kubernetes target inventory cleaner\n\nAdd KubernetesTargetIndexedInventoryCleaner: it ignores non-Kubernetes\ntarget types, and otherwise deletes a terminating target''s Kubernetes\nobject subtree through TargetInventoryCleanupService''s owner-validated\nDeleteOwnedInventorySubtree. It never calls the Kubernetes API, so\ncleanup succeeds with the Kubernetes addon disconnected, the target\ncluster gone, or no local watcher running. The subtree-delete\ndependency is declared as an interface inside the kubernetes package\nrather than imported from application, so this addon package still\nnever depends on the application layer.\n\nUnit tests cover the cleaner''s own dispatch logic (ignored target\ntypes, subtree ref shape, error propagation, empty target ID) against\na fake. A further test composes the real TargetInventoryCleanupService\nand TargetOutputHookService with a real store, seeding rows across\nmultiple GVR collections for one target plus a same-prefix sibling\ntarget via InventoryReportService''s ReplaceCollection, and asserts\ncleanup deletes exactly the target''s subtree.\n\nServer composition -- registering this cleaner and wiring the\nreconciliation controller into serve.go -- is not done here.\n\n* Phase 6: InventoryReporter and no-op edge sink\n\nAdd InventoryReporter as the reusable inventory report boundary for the\nKubernetes indexing core, with LocalInventoryReporter adapting onto\nInventoryReportBackend (ReplaceBatch/DeleteBatch/collection/subtree) so\nthe addon package never imports application. Empty ApplyDelta is a\nnoop (no heartbeat). Also add EdgeSink/NoopEdgeSink, and typed\nTarget/APIResource/Object CollectionID constants used by object naming\nhelpers and Schema.\n\n* Phase 7a: Discovery/filter/informer/edge/schema types\n\nPort discovery, namespace filter, informer, edge computation, and schema\ntype definitions from _legacy_agent02 into the live kubernetes package.\nMove EdgeType/Edge/EdgeSink/NoopEdgeSink from inventory_reporter into\nedge.go, and EventOp/ResourceEvent/ResyncEvent into informer.go. Add\nfull unit coverage for the ported surface (including RunContinuous via\nan injectable reconcile interval).\n\nDisposition:\n- discovery.go(+test), namespace_filter.go(+test), schema.go,\n  informer.go(+test), edge_test.go: ported as-is\n- edge.go: EdgeType/Edge/NodeStore/commonEdges ported; EdgeDelta/EdgeSink/\n  NoopEdgeSink adapted from Phase 6 inventory_reporter into edge.go;\n  unreachable empty-ownerUID guard in commonEdges dropped\n- EventOp/ResourceEvent/ResyncEvent: ported from legacy writer.go into\n  informer.go (writer remains for 7d; must not redeclare)\n- inventory_reporter.go: edge symbols removed (now in edge.go)\n\n* Phase 7b: Extraction contract adaptation\n\nAdapt ExtractObservedResource to emit InventoryObjectReport via\nObjectResourceName/ObjectLabels/ObjectObservation/ObjectConditions\ninstead of domain.InventoryItem. Schema fields and ComputeExtra land\nin observation.extracted; fix typed-nil map/slice leakage from field\ncoercion. Full unit coverage of the extraction surface.\n\nDisposition:\n- ExtractObservedResource: adapted (InventoryObjectReport + error)\n- extractConditions: adapted to extractRawConditions + ObjectConditions\n- extractAnnotations, extractSingleField, collectSlice, coerceNumber,\n  coerceMapString, memoryToBytes, stringFromMap: ported as-is\n- Flat observed keys namespace/generation/deletionTimestamp/\n  controllingOwnerUID: intentionally dropped (covered by\n  ObjectObservation metadata / inventoryNode fields)\n\n* Phase 7c: Default schema hooks\n\nPort DefaultKubernetesSchema and per-kind ComputeExtra/BuildEdges hooks\nfrom _legacy_agent02 as-is. Adapt through-extraction tests for the 7b\nExtractObservedResource signature and expand unit coverage of pod\nstatus, node roles, and edge-builder edge cases.\n\nDisposition:\n- DefaultKubernetesSchema, defaultEntries, computePodStatus,\n  buildPodEdges, buildServiceEdges, matchesSelector, buildPVCEdges,\n  computeNodeRoles: ported as-is\n- schema_hooks_test.go: adapted ExtractObservedResource call sites;\n  coverage expanded beyond the legacy suite\n\n* Phase 7d: Writer, per-target indexer, InventoryReporter wiring\n\nAdapt the writer and indexer onto InventoryReporter and EdgeSink.\nWatch deletes use ObjectResourceName; resync uses ReplaceCollection;\nGVR removal uses DeleteCollection. Drop idle ApplyDelta heartbeats and\ninformer shutdown/LIST stale EventDeletes that duplicated collection\nprune. Wire InformerManager removeCh for reconcile-only GVR removal.\n\nDisposition:\n- edgeKey, EventCh/ResyncCh, batching/dedup/late-delete/edge-diff,\n  retry shape, indexer IndexConfig and start lifecycle: ported as-is\n- EventOp/ResourceEvent/ResyncEvent: already in informer.go from 7a\n- Writer/NewWriter/Run/flush/sendResync: adapted to InventoryReporter,\n  EdgeSink, ObjectResourceName, ReplaceCollection\n- pendingDeletes UID→GVR, RemoveCh/removeGVR, schemaEntry/resourceRef/\n  diffEdges: new for the reporter contract\n- idle empty-ApplyDelta heartbeat: intentionally dropped\n- informer shutdown EventDelete storm and LIST stale EventDeletes:\n  intentionally dropped (ReplaceCollection owns LIST prune; StopAll\n  must not persist cache eviction)\n- indexerDelegate/newIndexerDelegate/start: adapted to reporter,\n  EdgeSink, RemoveCh\n- writer_test: adapted; TestHeartbeat→TestNoIdleHeartbeat;\n  TestMockInventoryWriter_ResyncFunc dropped; coverage expanded\n- indexer_test: new (legacy had no dedicated indexer unit tests)\n\n* Phase 8: in-process index controller, host, and serve wiring.\n\nAdd reconcile/lifecycle control for per-target indexers, DirectInventoryReporter rename, and composition adapters with full unit coverage.\n\n* Phase 9: Delivery agent reconciliation.\n\nKeep main''s stateless delivery Agent separate from indexing; extract applier;\nprove delivery succeeds when the indexer is absent or failing; dispose legacy\nmanager/delivery/applier/agent/descriptor snapshot files.\n\nDisposition: AgentPool.Deliver/Remove dropped (indexing was a delivery\nprerequisite); deliveryDelegate dropped in favor of main Agent; applier\nported to applier.go; combined per-target Agent dropped; descriptor legacy\ncopy removed as duplicate-of-main.\n\n* Clarify kubernetes addon delivery vs inventory organization.\n\nPrefix files by role, rename Agent/Schema for capability, and share cluster connection helpers.\n\n* Phase 10: Test suite reconciliation and hardening.\n\nPort kind-backed inventory e2e onto the in-process host and extension-resource\ninventory model, drop DB edge assertions, and remove the empty legacy snapshot.\n\nDisposition: integration_test.go adapted to KubernetesInProcessIndexHost +\nDirectInventoryReporter + ObjectResourceType; IncomingEdges and edge DB awaits\ndropped; _legacy_agent02/ removed.\n\n* Add inventory composition coverage and split Docker integration tests.\n\nCover stop-before-cleanup, inventory mode, GVR delete/resync prune, serve-style\ncontroller wiring, and orchestration cleanup with the real Kubernetes cleaner.\nGate Docker kind tests behind task test:integration.\n\n* Fix listFailTx stub after domain.Tx gained Queries().\n\n* Apply SQLite busy timeout to every pooled connection\n\nPRAGMA busy_timeout is connection-local. Configuring it through db.Exec only updated whichever pooled connection executed the statement, leaving connections opened later with SQLite''s zero-timeout default. Concurrent controller and workflow database access could therefore fail immediately with SQLITE_BUSY.\n\nConfigure busy_timeout through modernc''s DSN pragmas so every physical connection receives the five-second timeout. Add a file-backed regression test that pins two pooled connections and verifies the setting on both.\n\n* Own Kubernetes index controller lifecycle\n\nThe in-process controller was launched as an untracked goroutine before later addon initialization completed. runServe could return and close the application database while controller and indexer shutdown work was still running.\n\nGive the controller and hosted indexers a shared child context, launch the controller only after all addon connection and recovery work, and cancel and join its tracked done channel before database closure. Add deterministic coverage proving the lifecycle owner waits for controller shutdown.\n\n* Harden in-process indexer shutdown and await descendants\n\nCancel all indexers concurrently, join informers (including CRD) before the writer flush under a shared deadline, bound Kubernetes client requests, and cover the races with dedicated tests plus CI/Task race and kubernetes integration runs.\n\n* Make target termination a durable failing barrier\n\nCompare-and-swap ready to draining, then OnTargetDraining must stop local\nruntime work before indexed-inventory cleanup. Stop failures block cleanup\nand retry instead of racing a still-running indexer.\n\n* Convert inventory writer tests to synctest\n\nReplace wall-clock sleeps with synctest bubbles so batching and flush\ntiming assertions are deterministic.\n\n* Keep indexing REST configs without a global client timeout.\n\nLong-lived watches share BuildTargetRESTConfig; bound Timeout only on short-lived delivery clients.\n\n* Phase A: fold inventory hard-delete into ReplaceInventory IsDelete\n\n* Phase B: route inventory deletes through ReplaceBatch only\n\n* Phase C: Kubernetes mixed replace + per-GVR ReportedUIDs convergence\n\nGate WATCH on LIST write ack; retain/retry failed resyncs; resume from\nbookmark cursor and relist on unsafe watch endings.\n\n* Phase D: drop dead delete/prune surfaces and align tests\n\n* Remove target inventory cleanup path\n\nDrop the cleanup service, Kubernetes cleaner, CleanupTargetIndexedInventory activity, and related wiring/tests. Target deletion no longer removes source-owned indexed inventory.\n\n* Phase A: replace inventory host with IndexProcessManager\n\nAdd EnsureIndexer readiness, generation fencing, and stop-by-TargetID.\n\n* Phase B+B.5: move Kubernetes indexing to producer-owned IndexingRuntime\n\nKind/GCP EnsureIndexer before Delivered and StopIndexer at teardown, with\nstartup replay and IndexerClients DI; remove the store-driven controller.\n\n* Phase C: remove target output hooks and draining TransitionState\n\n* Phase D: align indexing lifecycle tests with producer-owned start\n\nCover EnsureIndexer retry, ReportResult retry, recover-delete StopIndexer,\nno credential retention, replay miss, and Kind docker ensure/stop wiring.\n\n* Fix Kind Remove logger wiring and kubernetes e2e compile breakage\n\nRemove was passing a nil kind logger, which panics under real provider\ndetection; restore the Object type seed helper deleted with cleanup tests.\n\n* minor tweaks and fixes\n\n* Fix Kind test helpers and inventory-only schema activation expectations.\n\nAlign newTestAgent call sites with the ownership helper signature, and\nexpect inventory-only schemas to activate for QueryResources scoping.\n\n* Fix Kind inflight race and fs-- naming in integration tests.\n\nClear inflight before terminal ReportResult so same-ID redelivery is not dropped, and use ownership-encoded kind names in docker/k8s e2e fixtures.\n\n* CodeRabbit fixes: harden indexing review follow-ups and tests.\n\nAddress PR #123 review: race-safe indexer cancel/done, edge flush after\nresync/removal, namespace glob validation, retry/backoff cleanup, and\nrevert the unused delivery cleanup plan split.\n\n* Harden inventory writer generation/resync and reporter guards.\n\nDrop pending work on generation adopt, treat LIST presence separately from extract success, skip NoopEdgeSink edge diffs, and add regression coverage.\n\n* Retry failed edge flushes without blocking resync ACK.\n\nTrack edgeDirty when flushEdges fails after membership advances and retry on the batch ticker so topology can catch up once the sink recovers.","tree":{"sha":"7f6c625e422046f4b51936249f21e3c65515e4e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/trees/7f6c625e422046f4b51936249f21e3c65515e4e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fleetshift/fleetshift-poc/git/commits/d9b9bbf3b9a2deb30718ac1001692b3f45a0a88b","verification":{"payload":"tree 7f6c625e422046f4b51936249f21e3c65515e4e1\nparent 1715c7cf4c16cf11a68d6a9051391b5798be7586\nauthor Matthew Short <97869221+mshort55@users.noreply.github.com> 1784141519 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784141519 -0700\n\nOME-115 (partial), OME-116, OME-117: Kubernetes in-process indexing on extension-resource inventory (#123)\n\n* Phase 0: snapshot Kubernetes addon source from feat/inventory-agent02\n\nVerbatim, byte-for-byte copy of all 26 files under\nfleetshift-server/internal/addon/kubernetes/ on feat/inventory-agent02\n(commit 3b2254827f6511602902c3b326cfe31431d417d4) into a new\n_legacy_agent02/ subdirectory, per docs/fleetshift/inventory/kubernetes-indexing-refactor/07-phased-implementation-plan.md.\n\nNo content changes, no import fixes, no gofmt. The leading underscore\nexcludes the directory from go build/vet/test. Full directory (including\nthe 4 files that already have an equivalent on main) copied per repo\nowner preference for easy side-by-side diffing.\n\n* Phase 1: platform delete/resync/subtree primitives\n\nAdd the missing delete half of the extension-resource inventory\nwrite contract: DeleteInventoryResources, PruneInventoryCollection,\nand DeleteInventorySubtree on ExtensionResourceRepository (SQLite +\nPostgres), plus application-layer DeleteBatch, ReplaceCollection, and\nDeleteCollection on InventoryReportService. Zero Kubernetes code —\nthis only closes platform gaps 1-3 from the kubernetes-indexing-refactor\ndoc set (docs/fleetshift/inventory/kubernetes-indexing-refactor/03-delete-resync-contract.md)\nso the future indexer has somewhere to report deletes and resync\nprunes.\n\nSource commit for the port plan: 3b2254827f6511602902c3b326cfe31431d417d4\n\n* Phase 2: target lifecycle plumbing and cleaner boundary\n\nAdd a generic, Kubernetes-agnostic TargetOutputHooks port on\nOrchestrationWorkflowSpec (AfterTargetRegistered / BeforeTargetDeleted)\nso orchestration depends on one field instead of raw notifier/cleaner\nregistries. The application TargetOutputHookService implements it,\ncomposing a non-failing TargetRuntimeNotifier with a\ntarget-type-to-TargetIndexedInventoryCleaner registry: an undeclared\ntarget type has no indexed inventory, a declared-but-nil cleaner is a\nwiring error, and a cleaner''s failure blocks target row deletion.\n\nSplit the single CleanupDeliveryData activity into\nPlanDeliveryOutputCleanup -> CleanupTargetIndexedInventory ->\nCleanupDeliveryData so target-owned indexed inventory is always\ncleaned up before the target row is deleted. Add\nTargetInventoryCleanupService.DeleteOwnedInventorySubtree as the\nowner-validated, resource-type-scoped subtree-delete primitive\nconcrete cleaners will call.\n\nNo concrete cleaner is registered yet, so existing delivery-only\nbehavior is unaffected.\n\n* Genericize Kubernetes/cluster vocabulary in new inventory-cleanup code\n\nReplace Kubernetes- and cluster-specific wording in the new\ndelete/resync/subtree comments and test fixtures with\nprovider-agnostic terms, keeping the platform target-type-neutral.\n\n* Phase 3: Kubernetes identity/naming contract\n\nAdd a standalone identity.go for the Kubernetes addon: ObjectResourceName\nbuilds \"clusters/{target}/apiResources/{gvr}/objects/{uid}\" through\ndomain.ParseResourceName, path-encoding every dynamic segment so a\ntarget ID containing \"/\" can''t shift the surrounding path structure.\nTargetObjectSubtree gives target-scoped cleanup its parent name, GVRKey\ncollapses group/version/resource into a tilde-separated key that\nsurvives inside one resource-name segment, and\nObjectLabels/ObjectObservation/ObjectConditions produce the query\nlabels, observation payload, and normalized condition set for a\nwatched object -- including generic per-object metadata\n(deletionTimestamp, ownerReferences) alongside the core identity\nfields.\n\nNo indexer wiring yet -- this only adds the identity contract the\nfuture writer and cleaner will call.\n\n* Phase 4: Kubernetes capability and schema registration\n\nDeclare an InventoryResourceCapability and the generic Object\ninventory schema on the Kubernetes addon descriptor, alongside its\nexisting delivery capability. The addon''s ID now reuses the AddonID\nconstant instead of duplicating the literal service name.\n\nCovers both layers: unit tests pin the schema''s exact field shape\n(including fields the platform never reads back for inventory-only\nschemas), and AddonManager tests prove Enable/Connect accept it,\nregister the inventory type, and correctly skip dynamic API\nactivation.\n\n* Phase 3 fix: rename identity.go to object.go, tighten AddonID ownership\n\nEvery symbol in the file is about the identity of a watched Kubernetes\nobject specifically, not the addon in general, and the package is\nabout to gain a roughly equal amount of delivery-side code alongside\nit -- object.go makes that boundary obvious the way informer.go/\nwriter.go already do, matching the file''s own Object* symbol prefix.\n\nAddonID moves to descriptor.go, its only consumer, and\nObjectResourceType is now built from AddonID instead of repeating the\nservice-name literal, so the two can''t drift apart.\n\n* Phase 5: Kubernetes target inventory cleaner\n\nAdd KubernetesTargetIndexedInventoryCleaner: it ignores non-Kubernetes\ntarget types, and otherwise deletes a terminating target''s Kubernetes\nobject subtree through TargetInventoryCleanupService''s owner-validated\nDeleteOwnedInventorySubtree. It never calls the Kubernetes API, so\ncleanup succeeds with the Kubernetes addon disconnected, the target\ncluster gone, or no local watcher running. The subtree-delete\ndependency is declared as an interface inside the kubernetes package\nrather than imported from application, so this addon package still\nnever depends on the application layer.\n\nUnit tests cover the cleaner''s own dispatch logic (ignored target\ntypes, subtree ref shape, error propagation, empty target ID) against\na fake. A further test composes the real TargetInventoryCleanupService\nand TargetOutputHookService with a real store, seeding rows across\nmultiple GVR collections for one target plus a same-prefix sibling\ntarget via InventoryReportService''s ReplaceCollection, and asserts\ncleanup deletes exactly the target''s subtree.\n\nServer composition -- registering this cleaner and wiring the\nreconciliation controller into serve.go -- is not done here.\n\n* Phase 6: InventoryReporter and no-op edge sink\n\nAdd InventoryReporter as the reusable inventory report boundary for the\nKubernetes indexing core, with LocalInventoryReporter adapting onto\nInventoryReportBackend (ReplaceBatch/DeleteBatch/collection/subtree) so\nthe addon package never imports application. Empty ApplyDelta is a\nnoop (no heartbeat). Also add EdgeSink/NoopEdgeSink, and typed\nTarget/APIResource/Object CollectionID constants used by object naming\nhelpers and Schema.\n\n* Phase 7a: Discovery/filter/informer/edge/schema types\n\nPort discovery, namespace filter, informer, edge computation, and schema\ntype definitions from _legacy_agent02 into the live kubernetes package.\nMove EdgeType/Edge/EdgeSink/NoopEdgeSink from inventory_reporter into\nedge.go, and EventOp/ResourceEvent/ResyncEvent into informer.go. Add\nfull unit coverage for the ported surface (including RunContinuous via\nan injectable reconcile interval).\n\nDisposition:\n- discovery.go(+test), namespace_filter.go(+test), schema.go,\n  informer.go(+test), edge_test.go: ported as-is\n- edge.go: EdgeType/Edge/NodeStore/commonEdges ported; EdgeDelta/EdgeSink/\n  NoopEdgeSink adapted from Phase 6 inventory_reporter into edge.go;\n  unreachable empty-ownerUID guard in commonEdges dropped\n- EventOp/ResourceEvent/ResyncEvent: ported from legacy writer.go into\n  informer.go (writer remains for 7d; must not redeclare)\n- inventory_reporter.go: edge symbols removed (now in edge.go)\n\n* Phase 7b: Extraction contract adaptation\n\nAdapt ExtractObservedResource to emit InventoryObjectReport via\nObjectResourceName/ObjectLabels/ObjectObservation/ObjectConditions\ninstead of domain.InventoryItem. Schema fields and ComputeExtra land\nin observation.extracted; fix typed-nil map/slice leakage from field\ncoercion. Full unit coverage of the extraction surface.\n\nDisposition:\n- ExtractObservedResource: adapted (InventoryObjectReport + error)\n- extractConditions: adapted to extractRawConditions + ObjectConditions\n- extractAnnotations, extractSingleField, collectSlice, coerceNumber,\n  coerceMapString, memoryToBytes, stringFromMap: ported as-is\n- Flat observed keys namespace/generation/deletionTimestamp/\n  controllingOwnerUID: intentionally dropped (covered by\n  ObjectObservation metadata / inventoryNode fields)\n\n* Phase 7c: Default schema hooks\n\nPort DefaultKubernetesSchema and per-kind ComputeExtra/BuildEdges hooks\nfrom _legacy_agent02 as-is. Adapt through-extraction tests for the 7b\nExtractObservedResource signature and expand unit coverage of pod\nstatus, node roles, and edge-builder edge cases.\n\nDisposition:\n- DefaultKubernetesSchema, defaultEntries, computePodStatus,\n  buildPodEdges, buildServiceEdges, matchesSelector, buildPVCEdges,\n  computeNodeRoles: ported as-is\n- schema_hooks_test.go: adapted ExtractObservedResource call sites;\n  coverage expanded beyond the legacy suite\n\n* Phase 7d: Writer, per-target indexer, InventoryReporter wiring\n\nAdapt the writer and indexer onto InventoryReporter and EdgeSink.\nWatch deletes use ObjectResourceName; resync uses ReplaceCollection;\nGVR removal uses DeleteCollection. Drop idle ApplyDelta heartbeats and\ninformer shutdown/LIST stale EventDeletes that duplicated collection\nprune. Wire InformerManager removeCh for reconcile-only GVR removal.\n\nDisposition:\n- edgeKey, EventCh/ResyncCh, batching/dedup/late-delete/edge-diff,\n  retry shape, indexer IndexConfig and start lifecycle: ported as-is\n- EventOp/ResourceEvent/ResyncEvent: already in informer.go from 7a\n- Writer/NewWriter/Run/flush/sendResync: adapted to InventoryReporter,\n  EdgeSink, ObjectResourceName, ReplaceCollection\n- pendingDeletes UID→GVR, RemoveCh/removeGVR, schemaEntry/resourceRef/\n  diffEdges: new for the reporter contract\n- idle empty-ApplyDelta heartbeat: intentionally dropped\n- informer shutdown EventDelete storm and LIST stale EventDeletes:\n  intentionally dropped (ReplaceCollection owns LIST prune; StopAll\n  must not persist cache eviction)\n- indexerDelegate/newIndexerDelegate/start: adapted to reporter,\n  EdgeSink, RemoveCh\n- writer_test: adapted; TestHeartbeat→TestNoIdleHeartbeat;\n  TestMockInventoryWriter_ResyncFunc dropped; coverage expanded\n- indexer_test: new (legacy had no dedicated indexer unit tests)\n\n* Phase 8: in-process index controller, host, and serve wiring.\n\nAdd reconcile/lifecycle control for per-target indexers, DirectInventoryReporter rename, and composition adapters with full unit coverage.\n\n* Phase 9: Delivery agent reconciliation.\n\nKeep main''s stateless delivery Agent separate from indexing; extract applier;\nprove delivery succeeds when the indexer is absent or failing; dispose legacy\nmanager/delivery/applier/agent/descriptor snapshot files.\n\nDisposition: AgentPool.Deliver/Remove dropped (indexing was a delivery\nprerequisite); deliveryDelegate dropped in favor of main Agent; applier\nported to applier.go; combined per-target Agent dropped; descriptor legacy\ncopy removed as duplicate-of-main.\n\n* Clarify kubernetes addon delivery vs inventory organization.\n\nPrefix files by role, rename Agent/Schema for capability, and share cluster connection helpers.\n\n* Phase 10: Test suite reconciliation and hardening.\n\nPort kind-backed inventory e2e onto the in-process host and extension-resource\ninventory model, drop DB edge assertions, and remove the empty legacy snapshot.\n\nDisposition: integration_test.go adapted to KubernetesInProcessIndexHost +\nDirectInventoryReporter + ObjectResourceType; IncomingEdges and edge DB awaits\ndropped; _legacy_agent02/ removed.\n\n* Add inventory composition coverage and split Docker integration tests.\n\nCover stop-before-cleanup, inventory mode, GVR delete/resync prune, serve-style\ncontroller wiring, and orchestration cleanup with the real Kubernetes cleaner.\nGate Docker kind tests behind task test:integration.\n\n* Fix listFailTx stub after domain.Tx gained Queries().\n\n* Apply SQLite busy timeout to every pooled connection\n\nPRAGMA busy_timeout is connection-local. Configuring it through db.Exec only updated whichever pooled connection executed the statement, leaving connections opened later with SQLite''s zero-timeout default. Concurrent controller and workflow database access could therefore fail immediately with SQLITE_BUSY.\n\nConfigure busy_timeout through modernc''s DSN pragmas so every physical connection receives the five-second timeout. Add a file-backed regression test that pins two pooled connections and verifies the setting on both.\n\n* Own Kubernetes index controller lifecycle\n\nThe in-process controller was launched as an untracked goroutine before later addon initialization completed. runServe could return and close the application database while controller and indexer shutdown work was still running.\n\nGive the controller and hosted indexers a shared child context, launch the controller only after all addon connection and recovery work, and cancel and join its tracked done channel before database closure. Add deterministic coverage proving the lifecycle owner waits for controller shutdown.\n\n* Harden in-process indexer shutdown and await descendants\n\nCancel all indexers concurrently, join informers (including CRD) before the writer flush under a shared deadline, bound Kubernetes client requests, and cover the races with dedicated tests plus CI/Task race and kubernetes integration runs.\n\n* Make target termination a durable failing barrier\n\nCompare-and-swap ready to draining, then OnTargetDraining must stop local\nruntime work before indexed-inventory cleanup. Stop failures block cleanup\nand retry instead of racing a still-running indexer.\n\n* Convert inventory writer tests to synctest\n\nReplace wall-clock sleeps with synctest bubbles so batching and flush\ntiming assertions are deterministic.\n\n* Keep indexing REST configs without a global client timeout.\n\nLong-lived watches share BuildTargetRESTConfig; bound Timeout only on short-lived delivery clients.\n\n* Phase A: fold inventory hard-delete into ReplaceInventory IsDelete\n\n* Phase B: route inventory deletes through ReplaceBatch only\n\n* Phase C: Kubernetes mixed replace + per-GVR ReportedUIDs convergence\n\nGate WATCH on LIST write ack; retain/retry failed resyncs; resume from\nbookmark cursor and relist on unsafe watch endings.\n\n* Phase D: drop dead delete/prune surfaces and align tests\n\n* Remove target inventory cleanup path\n\nDrop the cleanup service, Kubernetes cleaner, CleanupTargetIndexedInventory activity, and related wiring/tests. Target deletion no longer removes source-owned indexed inventory.\n\n* Phase A: replace inventory host with IndexProcessManager\n\nAdd EnsureIndexer readiness, generation fencing, and stop-by-TargetID.\n\n* Phase B+B.5: move Kubernetes indexing to producer-owned IndexingRuntime\n\nKind/GCP EnsureIndexer before Delivered and StopIndexer at teardown, with\nstartup replay and IndexerClients DI; remove the store-driven controller.\n\n* Phase C: remove target output hooks and draining TransitionState\n\n* Phase D: align indexing lifecycle tests with producer-owned start\n\nCover EnsureIndexer retry, ReportResult retry, recover-delete StopIndexer,\nno credential retention, replay miss, and Kind docker ensure/stop wiring.\n\n* Fix Kind Remove logger wiring and kubernetes e2e compile breakage\n\nRemove was passing a nil kind logger, which panics under real provider\ndetection; restore the Object type seed helper deleted with cleanup tests.\n\n* minor tweaks and fixes\n\n* Fix Kind test helpers and inventory-only schema activation expectations.\n\nAlign newTestAgent call sites with the ownership helper signature, and\nexpect inventory-only schemas to activate for QueryResources scoping.\n\n* Fix Kind inflight race and fs-- naming in integration tests.\n\nClear inflight before terminal ReportResult so same-ID redelivery is not dropped, and use ownership-encoded kind names in docker/k8s e2e fixtures.\n\n* CodeRabbit fixes: harden indexing review follow-ups and tests.\n\nAddress PR #123 review: race-safe indexer cancel/done, edge flush after\nresync/removal, namespace glob validation, retry/backoff cleanup, and\nrevert the unused delivery cleanup plan split.\n\n* Harden inventory writer generation/resync and reporter guards.\n\nDrop pending work on generation adopt, treat LIST presence separately from extract success, skip NoopEdgeSink edge diffs, and add regression coverage.\n\n* Retry failed edge flushes without blocking resync ACK.\n\nTrack edgeDirty when flushEdges fails after membership advances and retry on the batch ticker so topology can catch up once the sink recovers.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV9bPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG2wQADRA3UnmoqdiHw+KM/xjN5ZB\nYiiZeKVVeECh6K9swCyTcFBRKHYimofswoI2QZd/pzRjsVwCnSbpMGi6/OC/sbra\nE8zvXRZYwRfAxX2s8O7EDczV/S1ln3t8