","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeffrey2423","id":37357913,"login":"jeffrey2423","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MzU3OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commits/188d9e3668eada3ef09347c4dff7b8a2dcfb11db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-24T00:55:41Z","email":"37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeffrey Rios Muñoz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-24T00:55:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(backend): deployment & environments standard (2.6.0) (#18)\n\nAdd an opt-in distributed-architecture doc (arch id `deployment`) covering\nthe laptop->production path: logical-vs-physical database separation,\nexpand-contract migrations as a pre-rollout step, zero-downtime release\nstrategy (rolling/blue-green/canary) with graceful shutdown, health probes\nand feature flags, secrets management (manager + envelope encryption for\nper-customer secrets), three-layer dev/prod parity from one canonical\npackaging artifact, IaC separated from app deploy, and the OSS relicensing\ntrap.\n\nThe doc is decision-aware: a monolith install reads the single-deployable\ntopology, a microservices install reads the distributed material, and\nmultitenancy-only content is gated to arch=multitenancy — so a committed\ninstall never carries guidance for a path the user didn''t pick.\n\nWire `deployment` into bin/cli.js ARCH_DOCS (interactive, --arch, --all),\ndocument it in README and CHANGELOG, and bump to 2.6.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"da96e142b402e5d5392a913365fdbdebe6e689d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/trees/da96e142b402e5d5392a913365fdbdebe6e689d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/commits/188d9e3668eada3ef09347c4dff7b8a2dcfb11db","verification":{"payload":"tree da96e142b402e5d5392a913365fdbdebe6e689d1\nparent f2a96c0a5e8f5b4f7b164f9efd52d2dad1508f98\nauthor Jeffrey Rios Muñoz <37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com> 1782262541 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782262541 -0500\n\nfeat(backend): deployment & environments standard (2.6.0) (#18)\n\nAdd an opt-in distributed-architecture doc (arch id `deployment`) covering\nthe laptop->production path: logical-vs-physical database separation,\nexpand-contract migrations as a pre-rollout step, zero-downtime release\nstrategy (rolling/blue-green/canary) with graceful shutdown, health probes\nand feature flags, secrets management (manager + envelope encryption for\nper-customer secrets), three-layer dev/prod parity from one canonical\npackaging artifact, IaC separated from app deploy, and the OSS relicensing\ntrap.\n\nThe doc is decision-aware: a monolith install reads the single-deployable\ntopology, a microservices install reads the distributed material, and\nmultitenancy-only content is gated to arch=multitenancy — so a committed\ninstall never carries guidance for a path the user didn''t pick.\n\nWire `deployment` into bin/cli.js ARCH_DOCS (interactive, --arch, --all),\ndocument it in README and CHANGELOG, and bump to 2.6.0.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOysNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAtoQAIjfTxjujcrVHi0W854jfScK\nBv8PZsF+9gMyQjWxAom8FP7+TKye42w0kLViqvXvG3oxj4murMQKbOG03tjOMGkO\nDFW+5e+v1g5Ksd8HRUD8zCbHTMnPhp7/Vx9DDMijp76P2cTLlJbi8BTRmHyFK4bt\nk9c94YXD