is-exists section (2.5.1) (#16)\n\n* docs: add \"Why this exists\" — install-time decisions, committed docs\n\nState the package''s core principle in the README: architectural decisions are made once at install time and the installed docs commit to them, so AI agents read one consistent source of truth instead of re-opening settled decisions.\n\n* chore(release): 2.5.1","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNy9PCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIgsQAA+kWtg791rl/mNuWclPI6AP\n39IQP4tY6R2tVPIASaJoE5NNWrEJOoxhi9uc/0Vrdv3RkjTgpXdr7jyYCcxvYVW6\nWiU8LUZtoExz4ZcSAZ5fR7BqmF1jXdcwgUMANTo48L7BfjWfwPskh3BNPNE0NGm/\nX7pPFsY9dYnQLk1hgS0a6bwBFmhgw+K7N+LU2/g+lN1ZyLqx6/Vx1Xwkm++Z/EYR\nJ7R+DpFzTLD5tWfOdD6eQxNB+MM+WsOJRQ/sJNKRR/Mg/D94yu6UkpmkKZcVlfyk\nO72LqISKYdahZu91o7bfFDRXNe2X/hU3fWMPmznXAk51TZf2j6L9EeZizjXPUFvr\nh+TqYZ1NCDTBoPtJEf1XJn+pgr6KJAfjnaLuMuBu4LbPBhVsv7GjW+TjgatIssMd\nKg2Z+HFPM5+0oQw4bpubBb8JDGdUZzGJDwUp8nu7egnsgr+hiW8yixDN6M49y1Hv\nA9IivBEZE2sNd7k7gZpoe3MgDI1PUCpmd5GM5WHjWuCHosq1PDZKfBIKPzrybyd4\nEmILQQz0LMjTEwo6krecY+IyaSK1OZHTq3AWCoDlP9IwdCE06QMzGbgjZx2Wicdd\nFI2Zzrzzgz1i3kUNE5eo7AGPZVRRtGtEGAhmRpNx2w8QTaHnbbop36KF3Plrs49A\ntXINZhSPUKxyhyBGqsdN\n=S05y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-21T00:24:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commit/a7585344dea0ddbdf11368a5a671373e84d68be4","node_id":"C_kwDORXXHc9oAKGE3NTg1MzQ0ZGVhMGRkYmRmMTEzNjhhNWE2NzEzNzNlODRkNjhiZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commit/90916c4a681968738ad1189b0ed76388de8dbde0","sha":"90916c4a681968738ad1189b0ed76388de8dbde0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commits/90916c4a681968738ad1189b0ed76388de8dbde0"}],"sha":"a7585344dea0ddbdf11368a5a671373e84d68be4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commits/a7585344dea0ddbdf11368a5a671373e84d68be4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37357913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeffrey2423","id":37357913,"login":"jeffrey2423","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MzU3OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commits/90916c4a681968738ad1189b0ed76388de8dbde0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-21T00:16:55Z","email":"37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeffrey Rios Muñoz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-21T00:16:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(installer): decision-aware installs — commit docs to the chosen architecture (2.5.0) (#15)\n\n* feat(installer): decision-aware conditional content\n\nAdd a conditional-block engine so the installer commits docs to the architecture chosen at install time — AI agents stop diverging to options the user didn''t pick. Block markers <!-- when:COND --> ... <!-- /when --> and inline end-of-line markers (ANDed) wrap option-specific content; the installer strips content for non-selected paths. Conditions support arch/web/backend/mobile, comma-OR, !=, and nesting. Markers are HTML comments, invisible when rendered; full installs strip the markers and keep everything.\n\n* docs: author meta docs with decision-aware conditional markers\n\nWrap option-specific content in the decision-bearing docs so a committed install carries no guidance for paths not chosen: monolith Step-0/anti-patterns (when:arch=monolith), per-track scaling/backend/selection rows and the microfrontends section (when:web=...), and a track-neutral platform diagram. Document the convention in CONTRIBUTING.\n\n* chore(release): 2.5.0","tree":{"sha":"262e14af6a830306700a9a783203faf3ca129b03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/trees/262e14af6a830306700a9a783203faf3ca129b03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/commits/90916c4a681968738ad1189b0ed76388de8dbde0","verification":{"payload":"tree 262e14af6a830306700a9a783203faf3ca129b03\nparent 9841275ae228b684a963ce89672f96e9e738fd08\nauthor Jeffrey Rios Muñoz <37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com> 1782001015 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782001015 -0500\n\nfeat(installer): decision-aware installs — commit docs to the chosen architecture (2.5.0) (#15)\n\n* feat(installer): decision-aware conditional content\n\nAdd a conditional-block engine so the installer commits docs to the architecture chosen at install time — AI agents stop diverging to options the user didn''t pick. Block markers <!-- when:COND --> ... <!-- /when --> and inline end-of-line markers (ANDed) wrap option-specific content; the installer strips content for non-selected paths. Conditions support arch/web/backend/mobile, comma-OR, !=, and nesting. Markers are HTML comments, invisible when rendered; full installs strip the markers and keep everything.\n\n* docs: author meta docs with decision-aware conditional markers\n\nWrap option-specific content in the decision-bearing docs so a committed install carries no guidance for paths not chosen: monolith Step-0/anti-patterns (when:arch=monolith), per-track scaling/backend/selection rows and the microfrontends section (when:web=...), and a track-neutral platform diagram. Document the convention in CONTRIBUTING.\n\n* chore(release): 2.5.0","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNy13CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWkgQACTyWIdhjXiIDpuAgyeDvC79\nkvULbB8HDK+SiJGTqxadSVcaG6PA3NZtFVTc4l6uvNNroBpQxnBrI3ahAkDoilPw\ncTK3+GC0OZNZz7ziHZpoU6F2ZQl6AyqgGcXA2EkgqmP8HjI+sv5Q99sWjz9NSBYH\nV9wHAop0w2abtZMeViD6pSiwrA70FYm+NhXYtSR5hhZtpofl56qUi0eskG8M9JPd\n37CHbAxOxbJHnd5vauYvo5r6U0rAiOli3EwhJrpcYhgfwFzZ+SFK7gKfJW6dHA7e\nhHF7a2EHPh2OnQ1UuKrJOPkWZ29mK2Inv1y7fh2Y7ydc7ywSR1bEmBwESGyX6BjE\nQCWGRE9I+o6oQMq1Z06JS+nbdDfZ2N1lrqlJk40TQJEgtnOQjK7ozCjcH8aLlfvK\nUxht69xmRfjje3ruC6i6H+yi71ltkU4T/HTmj25qKxxx1Hx7nhJgPuAAJAdzPLjl\nRW19pgZNAaMuTvktwW6yROfWIA9YuAU6XSGE9tY1TADECqPPaxZvspOnDk7m30YK\nGUR79UJAOM3AH6590JfGFfnfMphHDJPqMcxTiZLK59SxxIGM9zPdisBx1yZDM7Fy\nxcO1yup58Bn6H77BWBk75V3zBXhFc2mohPP/A5HKQ9R7pB5TWuZssl+K+z+tFUZ0\n5kVI95rwlQsaLPg7EBfa\n=nXTV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-21T00:16:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commit/90916c4a681968738ad1189b0ed76388de8dbde0","node_id":"C_kwDORXXHc9oAKDkwOTE2YzRhNjgxOTY4NzM4YWQxMTg5YjBlZDc2Mzg4ZGU4ZGJkZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commit/9841275ae228b684a963ce89672f96e9e738fd08","sha":"9841275ae228b684a963ce89672f96e9e738fd08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commits/9841275ae228b684a963ce89672f96e9e738fd08"}],"sha":"90916c4a681968738ad1189b0ed76388de8dbde0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commits/90916c4a681968738ad1189b0ed76388de8dbde0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37357913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeffrey2423","id":37357913,"login":"jeffrey2423","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MzU3OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commits/9841275ae228b684a963ce89672f96e9e738fd08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T23:16:03Z","email":"37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeffrey Rios Muñoz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T23:16:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(installer): clean decision-table pruning, no orphaned refs (closes #12, 2.4.0) (#14)\n\n* fix(installer): prune decision tables cleanly, no orphaned references\n\nA partial install could leave dangling phrasing after pruning — notably the web-track table''s Combined row reading ''both docs above'' once the rows it referenced were removed. The Combined row now links to both tracks it combines so it prunes when either is absent, and the pruner drops section headings left empty after pruning. Documented the self-contained cross-reference convention in CONTRIBUTING. Closes #12.\n\n* chore(release): 2.4.0","tree":{"sha":"911be7f8a6ca2039012a836ff6526a49c918c38c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/trees/911be7f8a6ca2039012a836ff6526a49c918c38c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/commits/9841275ae228b684a963ce89672f96e9e738fd08","verification":{"payload":"tree 911be7f8a6ca2039012a836ff6526a49c918c38c\nparent fe2c99b2b0db48ddd3128fd5c2e21150d9665775\nauthor Jeffrey Rios Muñoz <37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com> 1781997363 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781997363 -0500\n\nfix(installer): clean decision-table pruning, no orphaned refs (closes #12, 2.4.0) (#14)\n\n* fix(installer): prune decision tables cleanly, no orphaned references\n\nA partial install could leave dangling phrasing after pruning — notably the web-track table''s Combined row reading ''both docs above'' once the rows it referenced were removed. The Combined row now links to both tracks it combines so it prunes when either is absent, and the pruner drops section headings left empty after pruning. Documented the self-contained cross-reference convention in CONTRIBUTING. Closes #12.\n\n* chore(release): 2.4.0","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNx8zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArBYQACzh1z1BEEv2nQzZtyMc76mO\n6vwOYOFyvvc7frgslymhreT/fKqI3Q7qa7RVARDXN7JOK0ZsLsJMsYpSysNyDhQg\nh98qevitn8lKTrk01Lf23QJbtS7z62sScnxcyX44ynuKwODDhHPSYMiv9/ADRIF5\nRfqLF/Ozi4oxNhnNLO5Eh6iwUzC6HueK6Ol+5q03Xhy5NUGsZX0n4UGPGu21FCci\nx026oWbJFCIZH/glIIYkQJQeaWkfsHPTzc5bodEjSb/P9q7/iJXPbPFEg3BVq3hc\nJN0TwpbY7MoXr5iP+9tPA8qmfSgLGXTACKICs6gMfPN08dj55RXtJAWhOYcqqrpK\nr1UVGtz8omW0DpN2OF0slS/AuM5VIHmdrWR+mtVv+ouxn418j5HPye2rqm7pQ0CO\nqdeoS24v01VPwp+25nRzxEa0HveyBaJmolp+43gmoCwLt/CrZeHvxsRKVj3bJXjv\n/R9j8gGn17xsqe4uI6ZeftpBctRLXXrZpjaKqr4yJkV0boMZTQqkw9ijDqWF+4D1\nQdMPA+sofzP04qFRS9I6PwVi39ovR78giZDDSYPglvekrpjn1yAWg9JtMaYh0vjx\nBuJ9KGwm+jynRu89WxA6UyZF3GWTw38hMq1swd8rxzPDY2mAeg803QLgNwC5AbhR\nMucZBSP/SIU5p2DtWThX\n=8di2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-20T23:16:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow"