":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37357913?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeffrey2423","id":37357913,"login":"jeffrey2423","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MzU3OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commits/5e599ce700ffb0234c0365ddd8377d7b768c9fb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T21:52:23Z","email":"37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeffrey Rios Muñoz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T21:52:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(architecture): cohesive full-stack doctrine, monolith standard, English docs (2.2.0) (#9)\n\n* feat(architecture): cohesive full-stack doctrine + monolith + platform map\n\nMake the package tell one coherent end-to-end story and remove the\ncontradictions that had crept in across the frontend and backend tracks.\n\nThe organizing principle is the vertical slice: a bounded context is\nowned end-to-end by one team — microfrontend + optional BFF +\nmicroservice(s) — with frontend and backend boundaries aligned on the\nsame seam. A new core/platform-architecture.md is the north star.\n\nMicrofrontend doctrine, reconciled on 2026 evidence and made\nsingle-source in frontend-architecture.md (decision tree + per-track\nbackend implications):\n- Module Federation is the default for homogeneous React.\n- Single-SPA orchestrates mixed frameworks / hard isolation.\n- They are NOT mutually exclusive and can combine.\nThis removes frontend-standards.md''s contradictory \"Single-SPA is the\ndefault for all microfrontends\" rule, which clashed with the track docs,\nthe README and the installer.\n\nAlso:\n- New monolith-standard.md: the modular monolith as a first-class\n  starting point with an explicit path to extract microservices;\n  resolves the dangling monolith reference in the decision map.\n- bff-standard.md: scope a BFF per client type AND per microfrontend\n  slice, owned by the frontend team.\n- Installer: Single-SPA and Module Federation are no longer mutually\n  exclusive — new combined web track (--web=single-spa+mf, aliases mf\n  and microfrontends), need-driven two-step interactive selection, and\n  a selectable `monolith` arch doc.\n- frontend-standards.md fully translated to English (user-facing UI\n  string literals stay Spanish per the language rule); fixed a duplicate\n  section number and a dead vite-config-standard.md link; bumped\n  React 19 / Vite 7 / Zustand 5.\n- README and cross-links updated to match.\n\n* chore(release): 2.2.0","tree":{"sha":"7c634e35a5bfa3fa16b4fff78e4aea0ade6cfdb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/trees/7c634e35a5bfa3fa16b4fff78e4aea0ade6cfdb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/commits/5e599ce700ffb0234c0365ddd8377d7b768c9fb5","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c634e35a5bfa3fa16b4fff78e4aea0ade6cfdb5\nparent 01f711a1efbdbed5846b45e9ee98056958e7f0be\nauthor Jeffrey Rios Muñoz <37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com> 1781992343 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781992343 -0500\n\nfeat(architecture): cohesive full-stack doctrine, monolith standard, English docs (2.2.0) (#9)\n\n* feat(architecture): cohesive full-stack doctrine + monolith + platform map\n\nMake the package tell one coherent end-to-end story and remove the\ncontradictions that had crept in across the frontend and backend tracks.\n\nThe organizing principle is the vertical slice: a bounded context is\nowned end-to-end by one team — microfrontend + optional BFF +\nmicroservice(s) — with frontend and backend boundaries aligned on the\nsame seam. A new core/platform-architecture.md is the north star.\n\nMicrofrontend doctrine, reconciled on 2026 evidence and made\nsingle-source in frontend-architecture.md (decision tree + per-track\nbackend implications):\n- Module Federation is the default for homogeneous React.\n- Single-SPA orchestrates mixed frameworks / hard isolation.\n- They are NOT mutually exclusive and can combine.\nThis removes frontend-standards.md''s contradictory \"Single-SPA is the\ndefault for all microfrontends\" rule, which clashed with the track docs,\nthe README and the installer.\n\nAlso:\n- New monolith-standard.md: the modular monolith as a first-class\n  starting point with an explicit path to extract microservices;\n  resolves the dangling monolith reference in the decision map.\n- bff-standard.md: scope a BFF per client type AND per microfrontend\n  slice, owned by the frontend team.\n- Installer: Single-SPA and Module Federation are no longer mutually\n  exclusive — new combined web track (--web=single-spa+mf, aliases mf\n  and microfrontends), need-driven two-step interactive selection, and\n  a selectable `monolith` arch doc.\n- frontend-standards.md fully translated to English (user-facing UI\n  string literals stay Spanish per the language rule); fixed a duplicate\n  section number and a dead vite-config-standard.md link; bumped\n  React 19 / Vite 7 / Zustand 5.\n- README and cross-links updated to match.\n\n* chore(release): 2.2.0","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNwuXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdYUQAGYpBkouHNrvcOfaSD1igL