MzU3OTEz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commits/dc2caed343d21ba278f3940cd17278eed1c526e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T20:46:05Z","email":"37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeffrey Rios Muñoz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T20:46:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(architecture): BFF standard + distributed-architecture decision map (#7)\n\n* feat(architecture): add BFF standard and distributed-architecture decision map\n\nThe distributed-architecture track had detailed docs but no entry point\ntelling someone what to choose and when, and no doc named the\nBackend-for-Frontend pattern at all. That let three distinct concerns —\nAPI Gateway, Public API Facade, and BFF — get conflated.\n\n- Add choosing-distributed-architecture.md as the decision map (modular\n  monolith vs microservices; gateway vs public facade vs BFF), installed\n  whenever --backend is selected.\n- Add bff-standard.md as an opt-in, selectable arch doc, with explicit\n  boundaries against the gateway, the public facade, and microservices.\n- Clarify in public-api-facade.md that the gateway is foundational\n  infrastructure while the public facade is opt-in (third parties only).\n- Document in frontend-architecture.md where cross-context composition\n  belongs (frontend stitching vs a server-side BFF).\n- Wire the installer: new selectable `bff` arch id.\n\n* chore(release): 2.1.0","tree":{"sha":"d890e478754cb78e0e79fe7c731129953d6462d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/trees/d890e478754cb78e0e79fe7c731129953d6462d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/commits/dc2caed343d21ba278f3940cd17278eed1c526e6","verification":{"payload":"tree d890e478754cb78e0e79fe7c731129953d6462d5\nparent c2705c46fb18a428d2434c1ecbcccf2656c42d6e\nauthor Jeffrey Rios Muñoz <37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com> 1781988365 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781988365 -0500\n\nfeat(architecture): BFF standard + distributed-architecture decision map (#7)\n\n* feat(architecture): add BFF standard and distributed-architecture decision map\n\nThe distributed-architecture track had detailed docs but no entry point\ntelling someone what to choose and when, and no doc named the\nBackend-for-Frontend pattern at all. That let three distinct concerns —\nAPI Gateway, Public API Facade, and BFF — get conflated.\n\n- Add choosing-distributed-architecture.md as the decision map (modular\n  monolith vs microservices; gateway vs public facade vs BFF), installed\n  whenever --backend is selected.\n- Add bff-standard.md as an opt-in, selectable arch doc, with explicit\n  boundaries against the gateway, the public facade, and microservices.\n- Clarify in public-api-facade.md that the gateway is foundational\n  infrastructure while the public facade is opt-in (third parties only).\n- Document in frontend-architecture.md where cross-context composition\n  belongs (frontend stitching vs a server-side BFF).\n- Wire the installer: new selectable `bff` arch id.\n\n* chore(release): 2.1.0","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNvwNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGmUQAI80L0jYNfSjCe3SfBNchdXI\nGpJ4MO60iEioatpfIWGWx6zSSTRX+7Ec7+gKaaHDfrqzmOgrBlzSgXXU6I3ehaDR\niANhhiGQn/sCEDh2mk7JPP/x8h1R1LjwJq02nBEU3FwwSh6e2cFAPMPxs6HD8dj4\ndnk47Hoyybdm28O28c/G5wlHUWvurY0xScSz97wWAbAg4LKbI25dUODbxjDsWeUd\n7KQYMjIN0qxZo4eK