/api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeffrey2423","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/commits/90b8358ff0e1c90490c845baf75147b010d71531/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T01:28:21Z","email":"37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Jeffrey Rios Muñoz"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T01:28:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: v2 — modular, AI-ready, open-source-only standards + interactive installer (#1)\n\nRestructure the flat standards library into independent, selectable packs and\nrewrite the installer so projects pull only the standards they need.\n\nStandards\n- Reorganize standards/ into core / backend / web / mobile packs (git mv preserves history).\n- Split Single-SPA and Module Federation into separate, mutually-exclusive web tracks\n  (plus a plain SPA track); no forced default.\n- Add 15 new docs enriched with verified 2026 practices: clean-architecture-ddd,\n  coding-conventions, testing-strategy, ai-collaboration (AGENTS.md), microservice-anatomy,\n  multitenancy (RLS/PG18), event-driven (outbox/sagas), public-api-facade (OpenAPI 3.1/\n  Standard Webhooks/RFC 9457), shared-vs-owned, web/backend technology-stack, frontend-architecture,\n  Module Federation 2.0 and Single-SPA tracks.\n- Add load_when front-matter to every doc for on-demand loading by AI agents.\n- Enforce an open-source-only policy: exclude commercial/revenue-gated libs\n  (MediatR, MassTransit, AutoMapper, QuestPDF) in favor of Wolverine, Mapperly, PdfSharp/MigraDoc.\n\nInstaller (v2.0.0)\n- Interactive selection via @clack/prompts + non-interactive flags (--backend, --web=, --mobile=, --arch=, --all, --yes).\n- Generate coding-standards/INDEX.md listing active standards with triggers + precedence.\n- Idempotent upgrades: manifest-tracked cleanup + v1 flat-layout migration + empty-dir pruning;\n  never touches the user''s own files.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a8dc40f93258303974e33093f043428467d1245","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/trees/6a8dc40f93258303974e33093f043428467d1245"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeffrey2423/coding-standards/git/commits/90b8358ff0e1c90490c845baf75147b010d71531","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a8dc40f93258303974e33093f043428467d1245\nparent 841e9125f7ff51e49c433768463728c360d01fff\nauthor Jeffrey Rios Muñoz <37357913+jeffrey2423@users.noreply.github.com> 1781918901 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781918901 -0500\n\nfeat: v2 — modular, AI-ready, open-source-only standards + interactive installer (#1)\n\nRestructure the flat standards library into independent, selectable packs and\nrewrite the installer so projects pull only the standards they need.\n\nStandards\n- Reorganize standards/ into core / backend / web / mobile packs (git mv preserves history).\n- Split Single-SPA and Module Federation into separate, mutually-exclusive web tracks\n  (plus a plain SPA track); no forced default.\n- Add 15 new docs enriched with verified 2026 practices: clean-architecture-ddd,\n  coding-conventions, testing-strategy, ai-collaboration (AGENTS.md), microservice-anatomy,\n  multitenancy (RLS/PG18), event-driven (outbox/sagas), public-api-facade (OpenAPI 3.1/\n  Standard Webhooks/RFC 9457), shared-vs-owned, web/backend technology-stack, frontend-architecture,\n  Module Federation 2.0 and Single-SPA tracks.\n- Add load_when front-matter to every doc for on-demand loading by AI agents.\n- Enforce an open-source-only policy: exclude commercial/revenue-gated libs\n  (MediatR, MassTransit, AutoMapper, QuestPDF) in favor of Wolverine, Mapperly, PdfSharp/MigraDoc.\n\nInstaller (v2.0.0)\n- Interactive selection via @clack/prompts + non-interactive flags (--backend, --web=, --mobile=, --arch=, --all, --yes).\n- Generate coding-standards/INDEX.md listing active standards with triggers + precedence.\n- Idempotent upgrades: manifest-tracked cleanup + v1 flat-layout migration + empty-dir pruning;\n  never touches the user''s own files.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNey1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA49UQAHGo4aYt/WaUrsM2x1f66mwl\nzAyOSlUO3QTIr56IzqTe28Dukalrbeqz1XIzzDKbWszEVkEjqZXDo4c5ZyMvlagF\nYV9f6a9cRARSAUKo7EgmUGSiKA/N+jhJshwDC7bi1bvReMuClgYIIBjL40d7G6ym\n0duO9I+LaGYr+IwWeB/ijcIO+xKh4nm17U1NRN/K+AUZfkuebnFqnUznuPXbvgtx\ngpx0/fLjnj8mS1cZI48kb1oLUGoiKYrmnI3Pzdt6UzdEhwTTCX80smxMXx+GVxxE\nsAJu6CbMd8B/Ay4V23hn35bM1oue/hxRS2m3ieOnQ2FCsTK0nQ4GqXlNquOuk3t5\nNpTm6s434iHmbunWgNTTABHnNqDj8Hy1gupFfp5Sbafb3GZKFYyyyfz0nDmTsgeM\nuHfRmzmzkFH9m4yNzAg/cmKzw4PPPvsBqsPUiXqCwNATG/egU1db6NwOJfTuhrWW\nBBw06yxz6BXzKFyl8a2Be3lMKQ25FoImkCX6JisrXH+6hb0DAdP2GSPnBSVVVgYF\njoS0kBysiPBBc2TKBMT2ZVpjN6PG2c2AvbFefi/Y8PhPWbDT/ChQ7EMVSsBtBqIK\nSlfzM8hQZdENX6vcIGppNb+l5MkOxxXZGFpzHdROpahaxfCi+DT4nZJ3bll1oINZ\nY3tdwUr3VF7wUKQVURWV\n=aZ/h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-20T01:28:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":