26-09-29T12:59:58Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T21:57:25.720Z","repositoryId":1165371200,"sha":"ca3a5e9b523905697b52b8f2adf39f152c524411"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"james-elicx","providerType":"User"},"email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-29T12:57:16Z","committedDate":"2026-09-29T12:57:16Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T21:57:25.720Z","repositoryId":1165371200,"sha":"54f0afefd556fb536a513fb08384e406292626e0"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T21:57:25.720Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111243485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedElBanna80","id":111243485,"login":"AhmedElBanna80","node_id":"U_kgDOBqFw3Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/fef1e43ef8feb099099b40b570e34da92de3d1de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:02:24Z","email":"111243485+AhmedElBanna80@users.noreply.github.com","name":"AhmedElBanna80"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T13:02:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cache): accept a class as the cache adapter''s default export and reject non-callable exports with a clear error (#3480)\n\n* fix(cache): accept a class as the cache adapter''s default export and reject non-callable exports with a clear error\n\n* fix(cache): construct adapter exports by [[Construct]] and validate the adapter shape\n\nReplace the Function.prototype.toString class check with a language-level\nconstructor test: a default export with [[Construct]] (native, transpiled,\nbound or Proxy-wrapped classes and any `function`) is invoked with `new`;\narrow functions and methods are called. A `function` factory that returns\nan object yields the same object under `new`, so existing factories are\nunchanged.\n\nThe produced value must be a synchronous adapter object with the slot''s\nrequired methods (data: get/set/revalidateTag; CDN: also\nbuildResponseHeaders). Non-function exports, Promises and wrong shapes throw\nan error naming the slot and what is wrong; the registrar logs it and keeps\nthe default handler.\n\nAdd an app-basic dev-server test that configures a class as cache.data and\nobserves the instance serving unstable_cache, plus unit tests for the\ndetection edge cases and the built-in Cloudflare factories.\n\n* test(cache): move the class adapter fixture test into the app-basic dev-server suite\n\nKeeps the integration file set unchanged, so the CI shard plan stays as on\nmain.\n\n* fix(cache): keep plain-call semantics for function factories and validate CDN ownership\n\n- Invoke only classes with `new`: a non-writable `prototype` (class\n  syntax, Babel) or one carrying members besides `constructor`\n  (down-levelled classes). Other functions, including bound ones, are\n  called, so `this`, `new.target` and bound receivers behave as before.\n- Probe [[Construct]] through a no-op construct Proxy so the check never\n  reads properties from the configured export.\n- Require a boolean ownsBackgroundRevalidation on CDN adapters, which ISR\n  regeneration reads.\n\n* fix(cache): recognise down-levelled subclasses as class adapter exports\n\nA TypeScript ES5 subclass''s own prototype holds only `constructor` and\ninherits every method from the base class. Treat a prototype that inherits\nfrom anything deeper than the realm''s root object as a class.\n\n* docs(cache): document that fields-only ES5 classes need a factory export\n\nAn ES5-compiled class whose adapter methods are all instance fields has a\nprototype holding only `constructor`, the same shape as a `function`\nfactory. Document the `(args) => new Adapter(args)` export for it and\ncover the case in the unit tests.\n\n* fix(cache): construct only class syntax and call every other adapter export\n\nPrototype heuristics misclassified ordinary factories (a frozen function\nhas a non-writable prototype; prototype metadata looks like methods), which\nchanged their `this`/`new.target` semantics. Recognise class syntax only,\nfrom the source text Function.prototype.toString returns for it, and call\nevery other function. Constructors that are not class syntax (ES5-compiled,\nbound or Proxy-wrapped classes) export `(args) => new Adapter(args)`.\n\n* fix(cache): accept callable adapters that have the required members\n\nCacheHandler and CdnCacheAdapter are structural contracts, and the\nregistrar previously stored any factory result unchanged. Let functions\nthrough to member validation; keep the Promise check.\n\n* fix(cache): detect a Promise result by its brand, not a then member\n\n* fix(cache): reject a Promise subclass whose species lookup throws\n\n* fix(cache): recognise another realm''s Promise when its species lookup throws\n\n* fix(cache): judge a Promise result by its brand only and handle the derived promise\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"6d9354907a6da7e6aabe63071964767743496e5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/6d9354907a6da7e6aabe63071964767743496e5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/fef1e43ef8feb099099b40b570e34da92de3d1de","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d9354907a6da7e6aabe63071964767743496e5e\nparent 4b58dac7496fc1f57b263a707aec4c46378051fe\nauthor AhmedElBanna80 <111243485+AhmedElBanna80@users.noreply.github.com> 1791464544 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791464544 +0100\n\nfix(cache): accept a class as the cache adapter''s default export and reject non-callable exports with a clear error (#3480)\n\n* fix(cache): accept a class as the cache adapter''s default export and reject non-callable exports with a clear error\n\n* fix(cache): construct adapter exports by [[Construct]] and validate the adapter shape\n\nReplace the Function.prototype.toString class check with a language-level\nconstructor test: a default export with [[Construct]] (native, transpiled,\nbound or Proxy-wrapped classes and any `function`) is invoked with `new`;\narrow functions and methods are called. A `function` factory that returns\nan object yields the same object under `new`, so existing factories are\nunchanged.\n\nThe produced value must be a synchronous adapter object with the slot''s\nrequired methods (data: get/set/revalidateTag; CDN: also\nbuildResponseHeaders). Non-function exports, Promises and wrong shapes throw\nan error naming the slot and what is wrong; the registrar logs it and keeps\nthe default handler.\n\nAdd an app-basic dev-server test that configures a class as cache.data and\nobserves the instance serving unstable_cache, plus unit tests for the\ndetection edge cases and the built-in Cloudflare factories.\n\n* test(cache): move the class adapter fixture test into the app-basic dev-server suite\n\nKeeps the integration file set unchanged, so the CI shard plan stays as on\nmain.\n\n* fix(cache): keep plain-call semantics for function factories and validate CDN ownership\n\n- Invoke only classes with `new`: a non-writable `prototype` (class\n  syntax, Babel) or one carrying members besides `constructor`\n  (down-levelled classes). Other functions, including bound ones, are\n  called, so `this`, `new.target` and bound receivers behave as before.\n- Probe [[Construct]] through a no-op construct Proxy so the check never\n  reads properties from the configured export.\n- Require a boolean ownsBackgroundRevalidation on CDN adapters, which ISR\n  regeneration reads.\n\n* fix(cache): recognise down-levelled subclasses as class adapter exports\n\nA TypeScript ES5 subclass''s own prototype holds only `constructor` and\ninherits every method from the base class. Treat a prototype that inherits\nfrom anything deeper than the realm''s root object as a class.\n\n* docs(cache): document that fields-only ES5 classes need a factory export\n\nAn ES5-compiled class whose adapter methods are all instance fields has a\nprototype holding only `constructor`, the same shape as a `function`\nfactory. Document the `(args) => new Adapter(args)` export for it and\ncover the case in the unit tests.\n\n* fix(cache): construct only class syntax and call every other adapter export\n\nPrototype heuristics misclassified ordinary factories (a frozen function\nhas a non-writable prototype; prototype metadata looks like methods), which\nchanged their `this`/`new.target` semantics. Recognise class syntax only,\nfrom the source text Function.prototype.toString returns for it, and call\nevery other function. Constructors that are not class syntax (ES5-compiled,\nbound or Proxy-wrapped classes) export `(args) => new Adapter(args)`.\n\n* fix(cache): accept callable adapters that have the required members\n\nCacheHandler and CdnCacheAdapter are structural contracts, and the\nregistrar previously stored any factory result unchanged. Let functions\nthrough to member validation; keep the Promise check.\n\n* fix(cache): detect a Promise result by its brand, not a then member\n\n* fix(cache): reject a Promise subclass whose species lookup throws\n\n* fix(cache): recognise another realm''s Promise when its species lookup throws\n\n* fix(cache): judge a Promise result by its brand only and handle the derived promise\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx5RgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA63EQADkErC8uGO6wXLdTCbtywIAM\nC9zBjC9EYtivHX25NN+6jxuWDFhTzwf5FgsPDMlUcqHmP1F0H+h50FphyuhF1Cc9\nPrMrCMRuBlTgUO82+BUMrO5iMFF0rnQ5ng2NAVtw0zb1CRjeQIxUqyY6K6yN9gUt\nRxVQWh5S6k4qhf+qj2IQJdncChb/9fAixi7kCz2oFe6ySHo0JkWqrrGnieIbYvvg\npEuWMIgje2g8o/QGZm9Ky9iYfLW3i3GrYgIZ0vsXOft4HNw8EuRmcS4F6AesPtQ/\nf8MsBpWqOSRrQQ0codwHAYK6oGgZobu3Id9xLvVWIlld38Y6OAeSkYogBSHxYsE/\ngVCo+JgNPOMi/1KwK4PGshlVn3S3WOHQYeJwsZX3/HUBZ1cddBFyH0NsTguUi3h3\nqcn1/7CTbwQ/DSfG4WRvxEIjeYgDp8LzRpTvlKGxVy9HzqicKDiz+L1Iw0/oRwne\noQqebnwRmLoyVFPbl3chNEi5/yNJfONzHEa4TK2rE7ZffXkQ+3oQsedE1cIeT7lh\n40L6/iiSqovuC/kFlVGQxkJGtg74KOyeXhmLU54lj/XJvuHT+1lYnFzvQ26XVv4d\nCQRg8/luYpeKBhGY5w/PShC8vdZ51uDMjYIKAWUOH5roseRtTNT0Hw7dKkapj9px\n+vG3VgJI2Vz6vkk2V9Fp\n=AnGz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T13:02:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/fef1e43ef8feb099099b40b570e34da92de3d1de","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGZlZjFlNDNlZjhmZWIwOTkwOTliNDBiNTcwZTM0ZGE5MmRlM2QxZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/4b58dac7496fc1f57b263a707aec4c46378051fe","sha":"4b58dac7496fc1f57b263a707aec4c46378051fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/4b58dac7496fc1f57b263a707aec4c46378051fe"}],"sha":"fef1e43ef8feb099099b40b570e34da92de3d1de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/fef1e43ef8feb099099b40b570e34da92de3d1de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/4b58dac7496fc1f57b263a707aec4c46378051fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:40:17Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T11:40:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(fonts): ignore font caches written before the path-free format (#3770)\n\n#3530 kept the cached stylesheet''s name, style.css, while changing its\ncontents to token-form url()s. A .vinext/ kept across an upgrade still\nholds the old file with the writing checkout''s absolute paths; it was\nread as current, so those paths reached the bundle and every web font\n404''d until .vinext/fonts/ was deleted.\n\nName the cached stylesheet style-q7f3kd.css so an old style.css is never\nread: the font is fetched once more, the token-form file is written, and\nthe right font loads.","tree":{"sha":"4cb78c17122395a123d45ba89f5ce7a39d61c6af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/4cb78c17122395a123d45ba89f5ce7a39d61c6af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/4b58dac7496fc1f57b263a707aec4c46378051fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 4cb78c17122395a123d45ba89f5ce7a39d61c6af\nparent 48b3f33e7403c7e0b3320334f4cebb817defa5d2\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791459617 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791459617 +0100\n\nfix(fonts): ignore font caches written before the path-free format (#3770)\n\n#3530 kept the cached stylesheet''s name, style.css, while changing its\ncontents to token-form url()s. A .vinext/ kept across an upgrade still\nholds the old file with the writing checkout''s absolute paths; it was\nread as current, so those paths reached the bundle and every web font\n404''d until .vinext/fonts/ was deleted.\n\nName the cached stylesheet style-q7f3kd.css so an old style.css is never\nread: the font is fetched once more, the token-form file is written, and\nthe right font loads.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx4EhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7bIQACimPJeQxzo015C5Je3jtzWC\nmGAxIOUQQc6PRyqQFCrCo4O/LDsR8FqbcWF8DmWwk+ux4amFr/Lq+NDmyz/tUd5h\nr/Bt7ff+1/vibEK3hZPduVeLkIxDZ85eUG4VJSji+KSz6xNGr6d6gj0IokK1Lks8\nVS/X84fD1i04xHBHCNwNoB4Jgfd0ACh97rdZ