are/vinext/commits/329b1810c1d548b2c2c381cd43cfd64429fa22cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/602579a4851288eb6728a58e2e9888fe630b9da8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:51:16Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:51:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): follow redirect() from a prefetched Link navigation (#3749)\n\n* fix(app-router): follow redirect() from a prefetched Link navigation\n\nThe prefetch snapshot dropped the X-Vinext-Rsc-Redirect(-Type) headers, so\na navigation that consumed a prefetched redirect response decoded the\nredirect payload as a page, hit React error #441, and hard-reloaded.\nKeep both headers in CachedRscResponse and restore them on replay.\n\nReplaying redirects makes their client lifetime matter: a streamed RSC\nredirect from a known-dynamic render (including a layout that reads a\ndynamic API inside the isolated layout probe, seen through the render\nlatch) now carries X-Vinext-Dynamic-Stale-Time, so an auto prefetch of a\ndynamic redirect is not reused past staleTimes.dynamic.\n\nFixes #3745\n\n* fix(app-router): forward the route dynamic stale time to dispatch-level cache policy\n\nA generated-param miss renders the not-found boundary, which can answer an\nRSC request with a streamed redirect. Its cache policy now carries the\nroute''s dynamicStaleTimeSeconds so that redirect is bounded by the page''s\nown stale time instead of the global staleTimes.dynamic.\n\n* test(app-router): cover prefetched layout redirects; drop the unneeded latch check\n\nA page''s redirect() now streams inside its Flight payload, so only\nearly-answered redirects (layout probe, boundaries) carry the\nX-Vinext-Rsc-Redirect side channel. Add layout-redirect and\nlayout-guard-full variants that replay a prefetched side-channel redirect,\nand drive the stale-time unit test through the real layout probe, whose\ndynamic usage already classifies the response, making the render-latch\nfallback unnecessary.\n\n* test(app-router): tighten the known-dynamic redirect stamp cases\n\n* test(app-router): note hover prefetch handoff in the refetch cases","tree":{"sha":"c7392dde0cabb1e7684e4414bc335b3d562c8912","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/c7392dde0cabb1e7684e4414bc335b3d562c8912"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/602579a4851288eb6728a58e2e9888fe630b9da8","verification":{"payload":"tree c7392dde0cabb1e7684e4414bc335b3d562c8912\nparent e5b595e012382aa70eb8299e21b78e3896f02e4b\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791453076 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791453076 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): follow redirect() from a prefetched Link navigation (#3749)\n\n* fix(app-router): follow redirect() from a prefetched Link navigation\n\nThe prefetch snapshot dropped the X-Vinext-Rsc-Redirect(-Type) headers, so\na navigation that consumed a prefetched redirect response decoded the\nredirect payload as a page, hit React error #441, and hard-reloaded.\nKeep both headers in CachedRscResponse and restore them on replay.\n\nReplaying redirects makes their client lifetime matter: a streamed RSC\nredirect from a known-dynamic render (including a layout that reads a\ndynamic API inside the isolated layout probe, seen through the render\nlatch) now carries X-Vinext-Dynamic-Stale-Time, so an auto prefetch of a\ndynamic redirect is not reused past staleTimes.dynamic.\n\nFixes #3745\n\n* fix(app-router): forward the route dynamic stale time to dispatch-level cache policy\n\nA generated-param miss renders the not-found boundary, which can answer an\nRSC request with a streamed redirect. Its cache policy now carries the\nroute''s dynamicStaleTimeSeconds so that redirect is bounded by the page''s\nown stale time instead of the global staleTimes.dynamic.\n\n* test(app-router): cover prefetched layout redirects; drop the unneeded latch check\n\nA page''s redirect() now streams inside its Flight payload, so only\nearly-answered redirects (layout probe, boundaries) carry the\nX-Vinext-Rsc-Redirect side channel. Add layout-redirect and\nlayout-guard-full variants that replay a prefetched side-channel redirect,\nand drive the stale-time unit test through the real layout probe, whose\ndynamic usage already classifies the response, making the render-latch\nfallback unnecessary.\n\n* test(app-router): tighten the known-dynamic redirect stamp cases\n\n* test(app-router): note hover prefetch handoff in the refetch cases","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx2eUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZmsQAK2jagr9ZxMwcSH1bDulDbpK\nbr2x3zXCxH+hr+sfV2x+OKiGOGh+fqmbyHoz7I4y91wjfS56Eg6Ry54xYl4of7mT\nmcUHiZJDBy2CLtF9F9Vt42qX14ZhukEqz+6T6xsZU9/Y/I+5UvPKeqj+Cnn2haxH\n/6/cUsBbxI4y0Ff8iQvMKgiunbZqF9wWk2FnZd/fo7DDD2Nh7up5PMWbKSN8RCaY\niNKzZX1wK1wisfCH7H2j8TkRK+jV75sQ/UyAd7N+KoBrULrxDl+mG+y1etjSQOam\n2UhhQj8hxgDc0QlVxWARS0Mo3stS06hj1wmplnsilpeZlwe6glIxbPV/x1A004py\nq0Y14/WS/RiTNFWDoClsmI2yvSK4GE+QulJeFeuora9VIbUAGoLNWAqQhpVC+3+P\nBTfKyKVzLXhrFJQ6zuWC/VCn+54AnhHWiq4g4uHZJZ6stq4O040m0Fw0EAflAzYv\nqV0K/o/Ce9FyZNDVaa7SI99KVnOd/7muvviv2ELDOLd9zt0grP5b8jdsIym1NdkM\nP6XSHIL1rdE68I3fKYZAkKhBvr9W93cJA3ujZ/BJazEaTaUsLO1TTxUrGqMvyRh9\nall4kmmFRdFC1h1ZNaE4vqoch/jzA4TUEpcDOfqjKR2D+f7k5+e/C2clNRlZWnlM\nuuQU8Qf3WOIXMQTrxHjm\n=wp6C\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T09:51:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/602579a4851288eb6728a58e2e9888fe630b9da8","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDYwMjU3OWE0ODUxMjg4ZWI2NzI4YTU4ZTJlOTg4OGZlNjMwYjlkYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/e5b595e012382aa70eb8299e21b78e3896f02e4b","sha":"e5b595e012382aa70eb8299e21b78e3896f02e4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/e5b595e012382aa70eb8299e21b78e3896f02e4b"}],"sha":"602579a4851288eb6728a58e2e9888fe630b9da8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/602579a4851288eb6728a58e2e9888fe630b9da8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141031946?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adnan-Husayn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adnan-Husayn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adnan-Husayn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adnan-Husayn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Adnan-Husayn","id":141031946,"login":"Adnan-Husayn","node_id":"U_kgDOCGf6Cg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adnan-Husayn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adnan-Husayn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adnan-Husayn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adnan-Husayn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adnan-Husayn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Adnan-Husayn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/e5b595e012382aa70eb8299e21b78e3896f02e4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:37:45Z","email":"141031946+Adnan-Husayn@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Adnan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:37:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): compress RSC responses in the production server (#3732)\n\n* fix(server): compress RSC responses in the production server\n\n* fix(server): match Next.js compression rules in the production server\n\nPort the response filter of the compression middleware that next start\ninstalls (next/dist/compiled/compression):\n\n- compressible content types follow compressible()/mime-db, which covers\n  text/x-component through the text/* rule\n- Cache-Control: no-transform skips compression and Vary\n- Vary: Accept-Encoding is added to every other compressible response,\n  including empty, HEAD, small and already-encoded ones\n- a known length under 1 KiB is not compressed; streamed bodies are\n- HEAD responses and bodies that already carry a Content-Encoding are\n  sent as is\n- next.config compress: false turns compression off\n\n* fix(server): honor compress in function-form config defaults and static Vary\n\n- pass compress: true in the defaultConfig given to function-form\n  next.config, as Next.js does\n- drop the cached Vary: Accept-Encoding from precompressed static assets\n  when compression is disabled\n\n* fix(server): read compress from vinext-server.json for every entry shape\n\nWorker-style dist/server/index.js facades do not re-export the RSC entry''s\nnamed exports, so the embedded __compress was lost and vinext start\nre-enabled compression. Record next.config compress in vinext-server.json,\nwhich the Node server already reads for both routers and all entry shapes.\n\n* fix(server): apply the compression rules to the static slow path and Pages serverDir\n\n- the uncached static path now uses resolveResponseCompression with the\n  file size and effective headers (threshold, no-transform, HEAD)\n- the Pages Router server reads vinext-server.json from serverDir, like\n  the App Router server\n\n* fix(server): honor Cache-Control no-transform for precompressed static variants\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"434fc717a85293c00b2c30abfe7fe04abcfcdf37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/434fc717a85293c00b2c30abfe7fe04abcfcdf37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/e5b595e012382aa70eb8299e21b78e3896f02e4b","verification":{"payload":"tree 434fc717a85293c00b2c30abfe7fe04abcfcdf37\nparent f7f59df6ec73636905a6f9c7d3454c37a9f57b14\nauthor Adnan <141031946+Adnan-Husayn@users.noreply.github.com> 1791452265 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791452265 +0100\n\nfix(server): compress RSC responses in the production server (#3732)\n\n* fix(server): compress RSC responses in the production server\n\n* fix(server): match Next.js compression rules in the production server\n\nPort the response filter of the compression middleware that next start\ninstalls (next/dist/compiled/compression):\n\n- compressible content types follow compressible()/mime-db, which covers\n  text/x-component through the text/* rule\n- Cache-Control: no-transform skips compression and Vary\n- Vary: Accept-Encoding is added to every other compressible response,\n  including empty, HEAD, small and already-encoded ones\n- a known length under 1 KiB is not compressed; streamed bodies are\n- HEAD responses and bodies that already carry a Content-Encoding are\n  sent as is\n- next.config compress: false turns compression off\n\n* fix(server): honor compress in function-form config defaults and static Vary\n\n- pass compress: true in the defaultConfig given to function-form\n  next.config, as Next.js does\n- drop the cached Vary: Accept-Encoding from precompressed static assets\n  when compression is disabled\n\n* fix(server): read compress from vinext-server.json for every entry shape\n\nWorker-style dist/server/index.js facades do not re-export the RSC entry''s\nnamed exports, so the embedded __compress was lost and vinext start\nre-enabled compression. Record next.config compress in vinext-server.json,\nwhich the Node server already reads for both routers and all entry shapes.\n\n* fix(server): apply the compression rules to the static slow path and Pages serverDir\n\n- the uncached static path now uses resolveResponseCompression with the\n  file size and effective headers (threshold, no-transform, HEAD)\n- the Pages Router server reads vinext-server.json from serverDir, like\n  the App Router server\n\n* fix(server): honor Cache-Control no-transform for precompressed static variants\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx2RpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2OQQAGmTCzpt0/ki9vMy71Nnjeax\nBBJo+5yv86b7LQB9Rr4POcirw5PG36FCJU8MJWxDcrfVOmasEyvptWxr60decYNx\n2Z+/DGYXsQ0nuJ+Z7kp67SfFv5i8r3dtLWRgWYKVY4DZWQTxYUbyTkcKdcdvp4GD\nBL9S/rsJS8uRtHDWsDDWTWaK8ivxJynmQczQomZeC+n0YshHSY+oR0VMJP/I7LS1\nsdejOseaZsF6mHnqt9SQVElWG3vquSHzz1eSD/kYp3FyXDgn/eLo3cvqitUobVnR\nX4Z0tmOgVSz1AIPI6JA/FHpzcC53eSeP2Pnah+f669W4JF/njRODykshZbg7hpdK\n1T0kfvGzqdRrHER3SKwLcT+FHl3cJjf8svHkkslhfYcerdVF0T9wWxLgS1PG41Da\nL89ahRUJ9Gq+UXimkEN7e48ovEo6jWJ+6AUzC146iw8sA073kkAJq4YysT+DrgXR\nQxQWVkmhKTHRrUqeTvE0+IHkKZSnvxRWJLuUueDCxUvq+WPSfcT3v39O+fpUUd0C\nYQDFP3s1mKNjO/6WhrPI7azTxuw00w3pHmo0GD6Xo1YzkGoq+DbwNpXuWNuyD5I6\nT5cYixOMvui4DwGyXmIL74nEUMGu5trddIit1uRMpqO2Oc8beI2CP2e4UzaV0eGu\nb1+i+GcXWKzF3QaHGmyn\n=nfTA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T09:37:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/e5b595e012382aa70eb8299e21b78e3896f02e4b","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGU1YjU5NWUwMTIzODJhYTcwZWI4Mjk5ZTIxYjc4ZTM4OTZmMDJlNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/f7f59df6ec73636905a6f9c7d3454c37a9f57b14","sha":"f7f59df6ec73636905a6f9c7d3454c37a9f57b14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f7f59df6ec73636905a6f9c7d3454c37a9f57b14"}],"sha":"e5b595e012382aa70eb8299e21b78e3896f02e4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/e5b595e012382aa70eb8299e21b78e3896f02e4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68327188?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sppidy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sppidy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sppidy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sppidy/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sppidy","id":68327188,"login":"sppidy","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MzI3MTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sppidy/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sppidy/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sppidy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sppidy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sppidy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sppidy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f7f59df6ec73636905a6f9c7d3454c37a9f57b14/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:31:49Z","email":"rshouriesh@gmail.com","name":"Ramshouriesh"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:31:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(headers): stop completed connection probes leaking their caller''s async context (#3731)\n\n* fix(headers): stop completed connection probes leaking their caller''s async context\n\nAsync resources created inside a connection probe keep the probe''s scope\nstate, and through it the probe, alive after runWithConnectionProbe\nreturns. The probe still referenced two promises whose reactions capture\nthe caller''s async context:\n\n- `interrupted` only resolves when the probe is interrupted, so a probe\n  that completes leaves it pending forever with Promise.race''s reaction on\n  it;\n- `pending`, which code that `connection()` suspended waits on.\n\nOn workerd every async context store value is held by a strong handle, so\nthe resulting cycle (store -> probe -> promise -> reaction -> async context\nframe -> store) is never collected, and each request''s context, with its\nRequest, Headers and streams, stays in the isolate. In a production App\nRouter app on workerd this kept ~20 KB per request until V8 aborted with\n\"Ineffective mark-compacts near heap limit\" after about a day.\n\nThe probe''s `finally` now settles `interrupted` (the race is already\ndecided there) and drops `pending` (an inactive probe never hands it out\nagain).\n\n* fix(headers): give each suspended connection() its own hanging promise\n\nThe probe no longer keeps the promise that connection() suspends on, so it\ncannot hold the suspended code''s async context after the probe returns.\nThis replaces swapping in a shared never-settling promise, which relied on\nnothing ever awaiting it again.\n\n* test(headers): prove connection probes release requests on workerd\n\nBuilds cf-app-basic for the Workers runtime, renders a page that calls\nconnection() as HTML and RSC, forces a GC through the inspector and checks\nthe handled requests were collected.\n\n* test(headers): fail fast when the inspector socket errors or closes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"9352a068908a78863f3463993eeb8d300e1d1163","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/9352a068908a78863f3463993eeb8d300e1d1163"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/f7f59df6ec73636905a6f9c7d3454c37a9f57b14","verification":{"payload":"tree 9352a068908a78863f3463993eeb8d300e1d1163\nparent 74c0c572e779d00274877ee268d0ae367c849731\nauthor Ramshouriesh <rshouriesh@gmail.com> 1791451909 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791451909 +0000\n\nfix(headers): stop completed connection probes leaking their caller''s async context (#3731)\n\n* fix(headers): stop completed connection probes leaking their caller''s async context\n\nAsync resources created inside a connection probe keep the probe''s scope\nstate, and through it the probe, alive after runWithConnectionProbe\nreturns. The probe still referenced two promises whose reactions capture\nthe caller''s async context:\n\n- `interrupted` only resolves when the probe is interrupted, so a probe\n  that completes leaves it pending forever with Promise.race''s reaction on\n  it;\n- `pending`, which code that `connection()` suspended waits on.\n\nOn workerd every async context store value is held by a strong handle, so\nthe resulting cycle (store -> probe -> promise -> reaction -> async context\nframe -> store) is never collected, and each request''s context, with its\nRequest, Headers and streams, stays in the isolate. In a production App\nRouter app on workerd this kept ~20 KB per request until V8 aborted with\n\"Ineffective mark-compacts near heap limit\" after about a day.\n\nThe probe''s `finally` now settles `interrupted` (the race is already\ndecided there) and drops `pending` (an inactive probe never hands it out\nagain).\n\n* fix(headers): give each suspended connection() its own hanging promise\n\nThe probe no longer keeps the promise that connection() suspends on, so it\ncannot hold the suspended code''s async context after the probe returns.\nThis replaces swapping in a shared never-settling promise, which relied on\nnothing ever awaiting it again.\n\n* test(headers): prove connection probes release requests on workerd\n\nBuilds cf-app-basic for the Workers runtime, renders a page that calls\nconnection() as HTML and RSC, forces a GC through the inspector and checks\nthe handled requests were collected.\n\n* test(headers): fail fast when the inspector socket errors or closes\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx2MFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnDsQACfisqeNlzbG2hz6n2KrWGAC\n47nLOmbm8uAE+jNDNAFilnYw8juze4qO1fa88yoGq3pJTpRTjO31Gup7fU1Bx8hq\nR5vAjkBQF7ScqMSvVk3npOooZ3RrVkTCyvB5KiLYoRbsn+yYgNQ4ZcWkqWHUp4Ii\nATwQI9JM8ssqoocqksdar0Lk+JVrjZPlXtZiCBZsVv2jXlWDjUcZmUsxopBjAqZD\nAsVQcX7OuQeEscDvSU/SHvvpG7o+N20l/ZN3P/tYz7WHUvqq5gz1dZWmMfVwTzUt\nVijhujaLvdWUp14uIfJB+bTLXKtJ2CO/wJIAQxG6hlWddjJAG+y9e/zGnPAbrhXp\nciyL2nlTpoEfmdIwFG5zaQgwgc6CyaD0j9gvTANnjJKDr7H3nQr+Ba8ZpS00dSVX\nuRD5q0iiGSaGAIEcmsgxtYy955NguVU9wDAL5i+OzCQsYm1xdgsG0MHSTyUQeLIa\nGDB75q/m4NqAbuDqY3HQQ8G2DYv5ywjmHSBJNXjAZBBXJxnjjtEDWe2csVHp1OCl\nQgE54Xq9CeTq1xZjKTqsiW7fktY3LCROZ667LZDVAS+kW2S9ijiGGelimql9slaB\nDo+zq5Wi6j/LUhHbC6PPKbriSkfL56x2Iz1mkc+XBs1BUcG4kRjlCUWFyAwBHT9k\nnQrmJScGpbRy2ixhym3l\n=KWIE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T09:31:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/f7f59df6ec73636905a6f9c7d3454c37a9f57b14","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGY3ZjU5ZGY2ZWM3MzYzNjkwNWE2ZjljN2QzNDU0YzM3YTlmNTdiMTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/74c0c572e779d00274877ee268d0ae367c849731","sha":"74c0c572e779d00274877ee268d0ae367c849731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/74c0c572e779d00274877ee268d0ae367c849731"}],"sha":"f7f59df6ec73636905a6f9c7d3454c37a9f57b14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f7f59df6ec73636905a6f9c7d3454c37a9f57b14"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2810237?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiscs/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiscs/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiscs/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiscs/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Tiscs","id":2810237,"login":"Tiscs","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MTAyMzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiscs/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiscs/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiscs/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiscs/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiscs/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tiscs","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/74c0c572e779d00274877ee268d0ae367c849731/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:31:31Z","email":"tiscs@live.com","name":"Galen Suen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T09:31:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): propagate client disconnects to request signals (#3692)\n\n* fix(server): propagate client disconnects to request signals\n\n* fix(server): match Next.js ResponseAborted signal and cover disconnects in fixtures\n\nPort signalFromNodeResponse exactly (ResponseAborted reason, response\nerror for already-errored responses), give dev Pages edge API routes the\nsame response-lifetime signal as production, and replace the synthetic\nserver test with app-basic/pages-basic fixture probes covering App Router\nprod/dev route handlers and Pages Router prod/dev edge API routes and\nmiddleware, including a negative completed-request case.\n\n* chore(server): keep ResponseAbortedName module-private\n\n* fix(server): keep disconnect signals through middleware overrides and stop work on disconnect\n\n- preserve request.signal when middleware request-header overrides\n  rebuild the request (Pages pipeline and App external rewrite proxy)\n- abort external rewrite upstream fetches on client disconnect, without\n  logging a proxy error, while keeping the 30s timeout\n- cancel dev edge API and Pages production response bodies once the\n  client has gone instead of reading stalled streams forever\n- cover overrides, body cancellation and external rewrites in the\n  app-basic/pages-basic fixture tests\n\n* fix(dev): cancel Pages middleware response bodies when the client disconnects\n\nwriteWebResponseToNodeRes piped with .pipe() and waited only for the\nsource''s end, so a stalled middleware body outlived a disconnect. Use\npipeline(), which destroys the body on premature close, and cover a\nstreamed middleware response in the fixture tests.\n\n* fix(dev): discard Pages middleware responses produced after a disconnect\n\nIf the client left while middleware ran, writeWebResponseToNodeRes\nhanded a destroyed response to pipeline(), which cannot pipe and left\nthe body locked and uncancelled. Cancel the body up front instead.\n\nMake the fixture probes stricter: warm each route before the readiness\npoll, record whether the hang probe timed out rather than seeing the\nabort, and return a streamed body after the abort that the server must\ncancel.\n\n* fix(server): omit the body of requests that are already aborted\n\nMatch Next.js NextRequestAdapter: when the response signal is already\naborted, do not attach the Node request stream, whose terminal events\nmay have fired before the reader subscribes.\n\n* test(server): cover client disconnects during an incomplete upload\n\n* test(server): cover external rewrites with middleware request headers on disconnect\n\n* fix(dev): only treat a premature close as a disconnect when the client closed first\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"a037bd367260c5afc47345071d06570ae4bfc1d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/a037bd367260c5afc47345071d06570ae4bfc1d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/74c0c572e779d00274877ee268d0ae367c849731","verification":{"payload":"tree a037bd367260c5afc47345071d06570ae4bfc1d3\nparent 4216f6127e4799a07e4b5ace8e52cf409e491470\nauthor Galen Suen <tiscs@live.com> 1791451891 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791451891 +0000\n\nfix(server): propagate client disconnects to request signals (#3692)\n\n* fix(server): propagate client disconnects to request signals\n\n* fix(server): match Next.js ResponseAborted signal and cover disconnects in fixtures\n\nPort signalFromNodeResponse exactly (ResponseAborted reason, response\nerror for already-errored responses), give dev Pages edge API routes the\nsame response-lifetime signal as production, and replace the synthetic\nserver test with app-basic/pages-basic fixture probes covering App Router\nprod/dev route handlers and Pages Router prod/dev edge API routes and\nmiddleware, including a negative completed-request case.\n\n* chore(server): keep ResponseAbortedName module-private\n\n* fix(server): keep disconnect signals through middleware overrides and stop work on disconnect\n\n- preserve request.signal when middleware request-header overrides\n  rebuild the request (Pages pipeline and App external rewrite proxy)\n- abort external rewrite upstream fetches on client disconnect, without\n  logging a proxy error, while keeping the 30s timeout\n- cancel dev edge API and Pages production response bodies once the\n  client has gone instead of reading stalled streams forever\n- cover overrides, body cancellation and external rewrites in the\n  app-basic/pages-basic fixture tests\n\n* fix(dev): cancel Pages middleware response bodies when the client disconnects\n\nwriteWebResponseToNodeRes piped with .pipe() and waited only for the\nsource''s end, so a stalled middleware body outlived a disconnect. Use\npipeline(), which destroys the body on premature close, and cover a\nstreamed middleware response in the fixture tests.\n\n* fix(dev): discard Pages middleware responses produced after a disconnect\n\nIf the client left while middleware ran, writeWebResponseToNodeRes\nhanded a destroyed response to pipeline(), which cannot pipe and left\nthe body locked and uncancelled. Cancel the body up front instead.\n\nMake the fixture probes stricter: warm each route before the readiness\npoll, record whether the hang probe timed out rather than seeing the\nabort, and return a streamed body after the abort that the server must\ncancel.\n\n* fix(server): omit the body of requests that are already aborted\n\nMatch Next.js NextRequestAdapter: when the response signal is already\naborted, do not attach the Node request stream, whose terminal events\nmay have fired before the reader subscribes.\n\n* test(server): cover client disconnects during an incomplete upload\n\n* test(server): cover external rewrites with middleware request headers on disconnect\n\n* fix(dev): only treat a premature close as a disconnect when the client closed first\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx2LzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgJsQAF4lvCEKh48UjGkwiaRQ6Go8\nX3pmZfFn1bdx9FpLmMNa8XImNOAFgvFlTlGzEh1sMZybHr/VEf0dyyc+PnDmF53Q\nBbsHRLj92WWP1r/FBA+DUQ5u6BwvgalgMVSw2QOrV4AcSNATPuvDFtv83fwrQ8KV\nISEwTsmBzSeL+YIiQN