cf409e491470"}],"sha":"74c0c572e779d00274877ee268d0ae367c849731","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/74c0c572e779d00274877ee268d0ae367c849731"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146103794?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SisyphusZheng/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SisyphusZheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SisyphusZheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SisyphusZheng/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/SisyphusZheng","id":146103794,"login":"SisyphusZheng","node_id":"U_kgDOCLVd8g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SisyphusZheng/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SisyphusZheng/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SisyphusZheng/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SisyphusZheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SisyphusZheng/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SisyphusZheng","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/4216f6127e4799a07e4b5ace8e52cf409e491470/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:39:23Z","email":"freemanzheng@hotmail.com","name":"Zhi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:39:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(middleware): accept variable-length alternation branches in matcher safety analysis (#3663)\n\n* fix(middleware): accept variable-length alternation branches in matcher safety analysis\n\nambiguousExpansionFactor() treated an alternation whose language is\nnon-finite (any branch carries a variable-length quantifier) the same as\na budget-exceeded analysis, returning the max-expansions sentinel. The\nsame quantifier outside an alternation (variable `repeat`) already\nreturns factor 1, so the guard rejected safe, commonly recommended\nmatchers — e.g. the static-asset exclusion matcher from\nsupabase/supabase examples (html?, jpe?g, woff2?), which fails\nproduction builds with ''ambiguous sequence expansion''.\n\nSplit the conditions: budget-exceeded still fails closed; a non-finite\nlanguage returns 1, matching the variable-repeat treatment. Ambiguity\nunder repetition remains caught by the dedicated nested/overlapping/\nambiguous-alternative checks.\n\n* fix(middleware): count bounded optional matcher branches as finite words\n\nTreating every non-finite alternation as factor 1 re-admitted catastrophic\nsequences such as (?:a|aa?) x26 and (?:a*|b) x8. Restore the fail-closed\nalternation rule and instead expand bounded repeats (x?, x{m,n}) into their\nfinite word language, so html?/jpe?g/woff2? branches are counted as match\npaths by the existing ambiguous-expansion budget.\n\nCover Clerk''s static-asset exclusion matcher in the middleware-matcher-auth\nfixture across dev, Node prod and Workers, and add ReDoS canaries for the\noptional and unbounded alternation sequences.\n\n* fix(middleware): keep wildcard and literal dots apart in matcher safety trie\n\nThe literal \\. and wildcard . symbols shared the trie key \".\", so the\nwildcard reused the literal edge without an overlap check and alternations\nlike (?:\\.x|.y|ay)+ were treated as prefix-free. Namespace opaque symbol\nkeys. Also reject out-of-order bounded ranges such as {2,1} before word\nexpansion so an outer finite repeat cannot spin to its declared maximum.\n\n* fix(middleware): fail closed on named backreferences in matcher safety analysis\n\nModel \\k<name> as an unanalysable backreference like \\1 instead of the\nopaque \\k plus literal <name> text, and short-circuit exact repeats whose\nchild has a single match path so huge counts cannot stall analysis.\n\n* fix(middleware): parse control escapes as one atom in matcher safety analysis\n\nECMAScript reads \\cA as a single control character and a bare \\c as a\nliteral backslash followed by c. Model both exactly instead of an opaque\n\\c atom, so bounded expansion cannot split \\cA? into \\c and A?.\n\n* fix(middleware): compare suffixes under overlapping trie edges in matcher safety analysis\n\nExplore overlapping first symbols instead of rejecting them outright, so\n(?:\\.x|.y)+ stays accepted after namespacing the wildcard key. Treat\n\\k<name> as a backreference only when the compiled matcher declares a\nnamed group; middleware checks every token since they share one RegExp.\n\n* fix(middleware): skip escapes and classes when detecting named groups\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"0154e620b52359d93002755bebd35f2c721e57b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/0154e620b52359d93002755bebd35f2c721e57b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/4216f6127e4799a07e4b5ace8e52cf409e491470","verification":{"payload":"tree 0154e620b52359d93002755bebd35f2c721e57b2\nparent 7f10e38df99f59b89bc78204ee380105aa0ab0ff\nauthor Zhi <freemanzheng@hotmail.com> 1791416363 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791416363 +0100\n\nfix(middleware): accept variable-length alternation branches in matcher safety analysis (#3663)\n\n* fix(middleware): accept variable-length alternation branches in matcher safety analysis\n\nambiguousExpansionFactor() treated an alternation whose language is\nnon-finite (any branch carries a variable-length quantifier) the same as\na budget-exceeded analysis, returning the max-expansions sentinel. The\nsame quantifier outside an alternation (variable `repeat`) already\nreturns factor 1, so the guard rejected safe, commonly recommended\nmatchers — e.g. the static-asset exclusion matcher from\nsupabase/supabase examples (html?, jpe?g, woff2?), which fails\nproduction builds with ''ambiguous sequence expansion''.\n\nSplit the conditions: budget-exceeded still fails closed; a non-finite\nlanguage returns 1, matching the variable-repeat treatment. Ambiguity\nunder repetition remains caught by the dedicated nested/overlapping/\nambiguous-alternative checks.\n\n* fix(middleware): count bounded optional matcher branches as finite words\n\nTreating every non-finite alternation as factor 1 re-admitted catastrophic\nsequences such as (?:a|aa?) x26 and (?:a*|b) x8. Restore the fail-closed\nalternation rule and instead expand bounded repeats (x?, x{m,n}) into their\nfinite word language, so html?/jpe?g/woff2? branches are counted as match\npaths by the existing ambiguous-expansion budget.\n\nCover Clerk''s static-asset exclusion matcher in the middleware-matcher-auth\nfixture across dev, Node prod and Workers, and add ReDoS canaries for the\noptional and unbounded alternation sequences.\n\n* fix(middleware): keep wildcard and literal dots apart in matcher safety trie\n\nThe literal \\. and wildcard . symbols shared the trie key \".\", so the\nwildcard reused the literal edge without an overlap check and alternations\nlike (?:\\.x|.y|ay)+ were treated as prefix-free. Namespace opaque symbol\nkeys. Also reject out-of-order bounded ranges such as {2,1} before word\nexpansion so an outer finite repeat cannot spin to its declared maximum.\n\n* fix(middleware): fail closed on named backreferences in matcher safety analysis\n\nModel \\k<name> as an unanalysable backreference like \\1 instead of the\nopaque \\k plus literal <name> text, and short-circuit exact repeats whose\nchild has a single match path so huge counts cannot stall analysis.\n\n* fix(middleware): parse control escapes as one atom in matcher safety analysis\n\nECMAScript reads \\cA as a single control character and a bare \\c as a\nliteral backslash followed by c. Model both exactly instead of an opaque\n\\c atom, so bounded expansion cannot split \\cA? into \\c and A?.\n\n* fix(middleware): compare suffixes under overlapping trie edges in matcher safety analysis\n\nExplore overlapping first symbols instead of rejecting them outright, so\n(?:\\.x|.y)+ stays accepted after namespacing the wildcard key. Treat\n\\k<name> as a backreference only when the compiled matcher declares a\nnamed group; middleware checks every token since they share one RegExp.\n\n* fix(middleware): skip escapes and classes when detecting named groups\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxtgrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPQwQAInGKkRh4YwDNFoGmGXJR065\n1KuSiK3tevNgYzV38MU93vuXDBp/JdHaLVIE+gfwSXH+Dwuk2XaFgzgeXqDm8BAU\nUEZTzUOCsslOpaxyPdqm+qoTbpxjEn4QJRAzaeKEWaF5zrwJYHb+3J1tZ1bFcc8t\nS1nQxqZ7sKmHVafG+XLhbHKhpgEOAmsDYCMCyGKOPBvQNzPXuzIo3yuIvh9rhf0X\naOOnLO2Why33Gn51cLDd7Q9XEH5nuthzoyZzd2c6zSByhAll5GouLrmzMAGEAswf\nDVLqb10j5TKHzfNTkEUKpUTuhmAjHhnlo812IW7XS6skkiLMY2nYRo1PV36/l0Ah\n83HvogrINXwleRbf09YO7KTbK8oPkE23ZOkJW80moLaHrq/ChI5rP53KrUxMF+yL\n5/TFRJ7IEVIOXRuborCQrSx0XRYn9d2/+RtVwkX0mxg9UtKYqOTs4W/V1Gz233n6\nY4kScFS6JlhdjeXpAdgHWbEikNhXW2ZvKj1XBwbUrjChWdhURiMORBzFLpWfNd7r\nCppYBb3Dsz3m51uk0da33/5bcme8XJtmRFTkGS9Y0mCaQxL2+npv65+VdBMOzqot\nMLcjoSJcmA39uRoh1tuZUeXEHoV5rpX0APfxgriNnIWnjf37ayRDM8qsJpUGVKTJ\nZoIhBd2r00vmo5kv7/iB\n=wZRb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T23:39:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/4216f6127e4799a07e4b5ace8e52cf409e491470","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDQyMTZmNjEyN2U0Nzk5YTA3ZTRiNWFjZThlNTJjZjQwOWU0OTE0NzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/7f10e38df99f59b89bc78204ee380105aa0ab0ff","sha":"7f10e38df99f59b89bc78204ee380105aa0ab0ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/7f10e38df99f59b89bc78204ee380105aa0ab0ff"}],"sha":"4216f6127e4799a07e4b5ace8e52cf409e491470","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/4216f6127e4799a07e4b5ace8e52cf409e491470"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111243485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedElBanna80","id":111243485,"login":"AhmedElBanna80","node_id":"U_kgDOBqFw3Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/7f10e38df99f59b89bc78204ee380105aa0ab0ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:35:31Z","email":"111243485+AhmedElBanna80@users.noreply.github.com","name":"AhmedElBanna80"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:35:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(server): redirect repeated slashes and backslashes like Next.js (#3684)\n\n* fix(server): a bare double slash is not an open-redirect shape\n\nisOpenRedirectShaped() rejected ANY pathname starting with // (or its\nbackslash/percent-encoded equivalents) as a protocol-relative\nopen-redirect shape, including a bare \"//\" with nothing after it.\nBut a redirect target needs something host-like after the double\nslash to be dangerous — \"//\" alone has no host segment, and Next.js\nserves it as the index route, not a 404.\n\nRewrite the check to look at what, if anything, follows the detected\ndouble-slash/backslash/percent-encoded prefix, and only flag the\nshape when that remainder is non-empty. The real attack shapes\n(//evil.com, /%2F/evil.com, ...) are unaffected.\n\nExtends the existing isOpenRedirectShaped unit tests in\ntests/request-pipeline.test.ts with the bare-double-slash cases\n(ported from Next.js''s test/e2e/hydration, which browses \"//\" and\nexpects it to hydrate like \"/\").\n\n* fix(server): redirect repeated slashes and backslashes like Next.js\n\nNext.js answers any request whose raw path contains a backslash or a\nrepeated slash with a 308 to the collapsed same-origin path\n(base-server.ts / resolve-routes.ts via normalizeRepeatedSlashes), before\nbasePath handling: `//` -> `/`, `/about//` -> `/about/`, `//evil.com` ->\n`/evil.com`. vinext 404''d the leading forms, served `/foo//bar` directly,\nreturned a 500 for `//` in dev and could crash the App Router Node\nproduction server on paths containing `//`.\n\nPort the redirect into one shared helper and run it at every request\nentry (Node prod App + Pages, dev, Worker App/Pages request stages, the\nRSC request normalizer and the SSR entry), ahead of the existing guard.\nPercent-encoded leading `%2F` / `%5C` keep returning 404, as in Next.js.\n\nRevert the earlier relaxation of `isOpenRedirectShaped` so a bare `//`\nstays open-redirect shaped: a middleware redirect to a same-origin `//`\nURL must never be relativized to `Location: //`.\n\n* fix(dev): run the repeated-slash redirect after the dev origin check\n\nNext.js runs blockCrossSiteDEV before resolveRoutes, so a cross-origin request for a repeated-slash path gets the 403, not the 308. Also document why the Location is serialized through a WHATWG URL (router-server.ts formats the parsed URL) and pin the observed next start results.\n\n* fix(server): match Next.js query and public/_next ordering for repeated-slash redirects\n\nPort normalizeRepeatedSlashes'' query rule exactly (the query is kept only when the first ?-separated part is non-empty, so //??next=1 redirects to /), and run the dev public/_next conflict check after the redirect, as next-dev-server.ts does after resolveRoutes.\n\n* docs(server): note the Worker ingress limits of the repeated-slash redirect\n\nWorkers only see request.url after WHATWG parsing (backslashes already turned into slashes), and Cloudflare''s asset layer answers repeated-slash requests for existing assets before the Worker runs.\n\n* fix(server): 404 repeated-slash paths whose collapsed form is still encoded-slash shaped\n\ngetRepeatedSlashRedirect now returns a typed 308/404 result so a path like /.//%2Fevil.com, which collapses to /%2Fevil.com, gets a 404 at every entry instead of falling through to routing. One sendRepeatedSlashRedirect helper serves the Node entries (dev and vinext start). Tighten the middleware redirect assertions to the exact Location.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"c4e4f94541400714d7b1cc722fb937dc9110018d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/c4e4f94541400714d7b1cc722fb937dc9110018d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/7f10e38df99f59b89bc78204ee380105aa0ab0ff","verification":{"payload":"tree c4e4f94541400714d7b1cc722fb937dc9110018d\nparent 5f0629e10d73bf2f913e08b683df73988bd54fa3\nauthor AhmedElBanna80 <111243485+AhmedElBanna80@users.noreply.github.com> 1791416131 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791416131 +0100\n\nfix(server): redirect repeated slashes and backslashes like Next.js (#3684)\n\n* fix(server): a bare double slash is not an open-redirect shape\n\nisOpenRedirectShaped() rejected ANY pathname starting with // (or its\nbackslash/percent-encoded equivalents) as a protocol-relative\nopen-redirect shape, including a bare \"//\" with nothing after it.\nBut a redirect target needs something host-like after the double\nslash to be dangerous — \"//\" alone has no host segment, and Next.js\nserves it as the index route, not a 404.\n\nRewrite the check to look at what, if anything, follows the detected\ndouble-slash/backslash/percent-encoded prefix, and only flag the\nshape when that remainder is non-empty. The real attack shapes\n(//evil.com, /%2F/evil.com, ...) are unaffected.\n\nExtends the existing isOpenRedirectShaped unit tests in\ntests/request-pipeline.test.ts with the bare-double-slash cases\n(ported from Next.js''s test/e2e/hydration, which browses \"//\" and\nexpects it to hydrate like \"/\").\n\n* fix(server): redirect repeated slashes and backslashes like Next.js\n\nNext.js answers any request whose raw path contains a backslash or a\nrepeated slash with a 308 to the collapsed same-origin path\n(base-server.ts / resolve-routes.ts via normalizeRepeatedSlashes), before\nbasePath handling: `//` -> `/`, `/about//` -> `/about/`, `//evil.com` ->\n`/evil.com`. vinext 404''d the leading forms, served `/foo//bar` directly,\nreturned a 500 for `//` in dev and could crash the App Router Node\nproduction server on paths containing `//`.\n\nPort the redirect into one shared helper and run it at every request\nentry (Node prod App + Pages, dev, Worker App/Pages request stages, the\nRSC request normalizer and the SSR entry), ahead of the existing guard.\nPercent-encoded leading `%2F` / `%5C` keep returning 404, as in Next.js.\n\nRevert the earlier relaxation of `isOpenRedirectShaped` so a bare `//`\nstays open-redirect shaped: a middleware redirect to a same-origin `//`\nURL must never be relativized to `Location: //`.\n\n* fix(dev): run the repeated-slash redirect after the dev origin check\n\nNext.js runs blockCrossSiteDEV before resolveRoutes, so a cross-origin request for a repeated-slash path gets the 403, not the 308. Also document why the Location is serialized through a WHATWG URL (router-server.ts formats the parsed URL) and pin the observed next start results.\n\n* fix(server): match Next.js query and public/_next ordering for repeated-slash redirects\n\nPort normalizeRepeatedSlashes'' query rule exactly (the query is kept only when the first ?-separated part is non-empty, so //??next=1 redirects to /), and run the dev public/_next conflict check after the redirect, as next-dev-server.ts does after resolveRoutes.\n\n* docs(server): note the Worker ingress limits of the repeated-slash redirect\n\nWorkers only see request.url after WHATWG parsing (backslashes already turned into slashes), and Cloudflare''s asset layer answers repeated-slash requests for existing assets before the Worker runs.\n\n* fix(server): 404 repeated-slash paths whose collapsed form is still encoded-slash shaped\n\ngetRepeatedSlashRedirect now returns a typed 308/404 result so a path like /.//%2Fevil.com, which collapses to /%2Fevil.com, gets a 404 at every entry instead of falling through to routing. One sendRepeatedSlashRedirect helper serves the Node entries (dev and vinext start). Tighten the middleware redirect assertions to the exact Location.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxtdDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABe0QABSnsTm3CRM4/rUe2TyFGaR0\nciHJXFjX+v/lPXltOxoXZXc7Fcts5pyyaHr+uolSGCzybBAJu6TG4rLJveDZI75k\nUK7de98yIQUJxKCar0EgwxunV1UGlIjrxb1Jh55VZN/KWRpdsc48+LqgnbItSO+V\nLaOT00IItmqxbv0wTW6JTtefkP3XNHsHxNi9YyhxbyRvwPr68EnAfjUdZuDd4LC0\nsZyFvB6U+JHL+5F6d6vN3rWP9BhL5mnBxYyFbRPqL9YajislwRPGO32wIgJ6YzRP\nWxHOSQDRg7pqzjtmPnGTGj5E/WrihERv5GWB+EI9+z8zoE+zBg6QJw0ki96KQVmB\nBzHradtbUl4BHOl0ZWI/X16HImUktFJ5a7SnrJsfpSNTLlLOrXhQ7vaxtfxQkUaG\n/qADabuJTXvC5y461vBKQVRgIw5/4bb0fT0ZfaVKBvgS3bOMI9ABfILBwCgyMZnz\n0gkEErf2TtmXarswrup7CDNfcq3GIrxggbKXcFRg2WFnrLJXECWux1ZL8jh9tslc\n3Wa5OvPBd0DyYurQg1d/nU5xSQ4x/wfQzCxWKfMGPVEr9U3b3Pm17p3UqcoUqdIE\n3Dors3iA9qD4bli+ipSGFVAKGBXlDRhL7v+w/gpkoYG57axZAeF7IzXpOm3EdaHp\nfKewlQ4uG/MKL7uVLvHU\n=8Q/S\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T23:35:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/7f10e38df99f59b89bc78204ee380105aa0ab0ff","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDdmMTBlMzhkZjk5ZjU5Yjg5YmM3ODIwNGVlMzgwMTA1YWEwYWIwZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/5f0629e10d73bf2f913e08b683df73988bd54fa3","sha":"5f0629e10d73bf2f913e08b683df73988bd54fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/5f0629e10d73bf2f913e08b683df73988bd54fa3"}],"sha":"7f10e38df99f59b89bc78204ee380105aa0ab0ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/7f10e38df99f59b89bc78204ee380105aa0ab0ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44969538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arif-js/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arif-js/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arif-js/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arif-js/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arif-js","id":44969538,"login":"arif-js","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTY5NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arif-js/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arif-js/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arif-js/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arif-js/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arif-js/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arif-js","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/5f0629e10d73bf2f913e08b683df73988bd54fa3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:32:02Z","email":"44969538+arif-js@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Arif"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:32:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test(standalone): cover workspace-pinned react and nested dependency versions (#3576)\n\n* fix(build): prefer the app root''s package version in standalone output\n\n`copyPackageAndRuntimeDeps` walks the dependency graph and keeps a single copy\nper package name at the top level of `standalone/node_modules`, taking the copy\nfrom whichever dependent reaches the package first. In a workspace where a\ndependency pins a different version than the app root, the dependency''s copy won\nthe slot and the root-resolved version was never copied. Every page then failed\nat runtime with an \"Incompatible React versions\" error.\n\nResolve each package from the app root first, falling back to the dependent''s\nresolver only when the root cannot resolve it. The walk still keeps one\ntop-level copy per package, so the app''s own version can no longer be shadowed\nby a dependency.\n\nCloses #3443\n\nCo-authored-by: CommandCodeBot <noreply@commandcode.ai>\n\n* revert(build): drop root-first package resolution in standalone output\n\nThis reverts commit 5177eb20391cd38858c4e7ec2aaad34e09020efb.\n\nResolving every package from the app root first copies the root version\nof a dependency even when a server-external package needs a different,\nnested version of it, which crashes the standalone server. The #3443\nReact scenario already works without this change, because Node builds\nalways mark react/react-dom SSR-external and the copier seeds them from\nthe app root.\n\n* test(standalone): cover workspace-pinned react and nested dependency versions\n\nBuild the standalone-output fixture inside a monorepo layout and run\ndist/standalone/server.js from an isolated directory:\n\n- A workspace package pins its own react@19.2.5 in nested node_modules\n  (#3443). The standalone output must ship the app root''s react and render.\n- The app root installs dep-x@1 (never imported on the server), while a\n  server-external workspace package needs its nested dep-x@2. The\n  standalone server must give that package dep-x@2 and render.\n\n* test(standalone): bound the build subprocess and assert how ws-ui ships\n\n* test(standalone): bound each readiness probe\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: CommandCodeBot <noreply@commandcode.ai>\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"83df2ba345c17b82b1ee42863affca4a257ed5f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/83df2ba345c17b82b1ee42863affca4a257ed5f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/5f0629e10d73bf2f913e08b683df73988bd54fa3","verification":{"payload":"tree 83df2ba345c17b82b1ee42863affca4a257ed5f5\nparent c1f02066de923e1772e6eaaec1da0935be7667cc\nauthor Arif <44969538+arif-js@users.noreply.github.com> 1791415922 +0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791415922 +0100\n\ntest(standalone): cover workspace-pinned react and nested dependency versions (#3576)\n\n* fix(build): prefer the app root''s package version in standalone output\n\n`copyPackageAndRuntimeDeps` walks the dependency graph and keeps a single copy\nper package name at the top level of `standalone/node_modules`, taking the copy\nfrom whichever dependent reaches the package first. In a workspace where a\ndependency pins a different version than the app root, the dependency''s copy won\nthe slot and the root-resolved version was never copied. Every page then failed\nat runtime with an \"Incompatible React versions\" error.\n\nResolve each package from the app root first, falling back to the dependent''s\nresolver only when the root cannot resolve it. The walk still keeps one\ntop-level copy per package, so the app''s own version can no longer be shadowed\nby a dependency.\n\nCloses #3443\n\nCo-authored-by: CommandCodeBot <noreply@commandcode.ai>\n\n* revert(build): drop root-first package resolution in standalone output\n\nThis reverts commit 5177eb20391cd38858c4e7ec2aaad34e09020efb.\n\nResolving every package from the app root first copies the root version\nof a dependency even when a server-external package needs a different,\nnested version of it, which crashes the standalone server. The #3443\nReact scenario already works without this change, because Node builds\nalways mark react/react-dom SSR-external and the copier seeds them from\nthe app root.\n\n* test(standalone): cover workspace-pinned react and nested dependency versions\n\nBuild the standalone-output fixture inside a monorepo layout and run\ndist/standalone/server.js from an isolated directory:\n\n- A workspace package pins its own react@19.2.5 in nested node_modules\n  (#3443). The standalone output must ship the app root''s react and render.\n- The app root installs dep-x@1 (never imported on the server), while a\n  server-external workspace package needs its nested dep-x@2. The\n  standalone server must give that package dep-x@2 and render.\n\n* test(standalone): bound the build subprocess and assert how ws-ui ships\n\n* test(standalone): bound each readiness probe\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: CommandCodeBot <noreply@commandcode.ai>\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxtZyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbowQAK2SKiWvjq6tJwbB3PzwdgRX\nQ2ZyyrlUl4mkSWnIvTb6SaI+jPDZz9qp3U+MTkFPntUg2l1rmosDEjlfWkyiMCHe\n/cm4n+Sfe+5oLLbcnqMUVt2dznvDBU7A39BXbvti+EV0+EYQ7Ozf0DVqtvRaoZ+1\ndVxkRCm/h6VknGvWH9mhZx4Upx/jKlCU2JD21nQcjU6possU6JcALkwtt5YG+W5l\nmc8FTzg69uR2ds8rPtAK9E2wpSRUGkiwgyC8/i3idIBFVjbTtrdkswFspdfxsUQ0\nPI+LnGUjggMOknv9GiuwYKinqqNE2DqL7PAj6jHA7ibDS/IDLPle6J5vUJHLP5mx\nh7nY+/tAVj5wCAiGmkd++cW8SNCcqUGEF0t+KLryJJMTRXhdwyP1xN5/pUtRbf2I\n3ud2jm+wrdm3hHYu3tHjR3RUzOiTqD7Cr9S+xMCqVboWyo/5+eBhqCkhWmQR87wZ\nHxKqO2DTkIXCvysddjr2U1l4TrK0cKUH8FqYB9WbCtAKflImsbaiHtqoHbkkjmLO\nPWGoQAiAzVPM/K7NqheX0Yk0575a+GeVdaBKceUf3WhkBLn7HEja9YEAcsQ/jObi\nkWxZUczwU7MJ63tXO0Z839ZiLz9gwLHOyofPkOZg31+Q8i+FHT3+lwoOYwJ+wdxi\nj/QtnblrnJh8tStWoP9R\n=N9RI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T23:32:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/5f0629e10d73bf2f913e08b683df73988bd54fa3","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDVmMDYyOWUxMGQ3M2JmMmY5MTNlMDhiNjgzZGY3Mzk4OGJkNTRmYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/c1f02066de923e1772e6eaaec1da0935be7667cc","sha":"c1f02066de923e1772e6eaaec1da0935be7667cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/c1f02066de923e1772e6eaaec1da0935be7667cc"}],"sha":"5f0629e10d73bf2f913e08b683df73988bd54fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/5f0629e10d73bf2f913e08b683df73988bd54fa3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190122957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reginaldalfret/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reginaldalfret/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reginaldalfret/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reginaldalfret/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/reginaldalfret","id":190122957,"login":"reginaldalfret","node_id":"U_kgDOC1ULzQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reginaldalfret/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reginaldalfret/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reginaldalfret/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reginaldalfret/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reginaldalfret/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reginaldalfret","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/c1f02066de923e1772e6eaaec1da0935be7667cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:29:24Z","email":"reginaldalfret@gmail.com","name":"Reginald Alfret V"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:29:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(standalone): document startProdServer for custom and compiled entries (#3469)\n\n* fix(standalone): allow VINEXT_OUT_DIR to override output directory\n\nResolves #3445\n\nWhen standalone server.js is compiled into a single executable (e.g. with bun build --compile), import.meta.dirname is resolved at compile time to the build host path, preventing relocation.\n\nAllow overriding outDir via process.env.VINEXT_OUT_DIR with fallback to join(import.meta.dirname, ''dist'').\n\n* revert(standalone): drop VINEXT_OUT_DIR override in favour of documenting startProdServer\n\n* docs(standalone): document startProdServer for custom and compiled entries\n\n* docs(standalone): keep the compiled entry outside the regenerated dist/standalone\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"c85b26938efdc58006e57a66549c978d23b87eb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/c85b26938efdc58006e57a66549c978d23b87eb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/c1f02066de923e1772e6eaaec1da0935be7667cc","verification":{"payload":"tree c85b26938efdc58006e57a66549c978d23b87eb4\nparent d06c5baa849f090d2e60b8d5afcf155d0d169103\nauthor Reginald Alfret V <reginaldalfret@gmail.com> 1791415764 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791415764 +0100\n\ndocs(standalone): document startProdServer for custom and compiled entries (#3469)\n\n* fix(standalone): allow VINEXT_OUT_DIR to override output directory\n\nResolves #3445\n\nWhen standalone server.js is compiled into a single executable (e.g. with bun build --compile), import.meta.dirname is resolved at compile time to the build host path, preventing relocation.\n\nAllow overriding outDir via process.env.VINEXT_OUT_DIR with fallback to join(import.meta.dirname, ''dist'').\n\n* revert(standalone): drop VINEXT_OUT_DIR override in favour of documenting startProdServer\n\n* docs(standalone): document startProdServer for custom and compiled entries\n\n* docs(standalone): keep the compiled entry outside the regenerated dist/standalone\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxtXUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2ocQAJZauPkS5ckxnDX+OJ2dcSi1\nrO+KtMM+hdfCw8BhCYSE2jCwsFCGQwCgiTrsssXR2dAoA+kUiOERefT81dIkRBQA\nrISkW222M/JeHLuq6dI/RcyHUy+RVrfi398+6PaD2koIhZKg4Uqy4I0O0PBKTamE\nnUbqeV2+0RMgpSXs9ivg3I7gWRuSn5Hd7+dkD9udTfaxxow1WhUhiMvbCtVa0krs\nHcLS417++eDKg/uGTIciypOyN5Q37UlNfrQ9OP0CMnw9wd3BT/WzquktjAgA9ntk\nxBV0w8QZO+N1Kv3k3SZR3dhACx30PpxLP5zx/CdiIoLSC275eqA+04d345+oceH8\nS+BS6J65IjSY3M4kHnzqJ+qvJUIEREynHaf4PulhK6PZmULW9CbDvZYZgRwK94r7\neUoIDzd3Jfo2GsLdS7fkeXHuniFpFAsYA8gA1kSNwH+TolA/2m1bbIpNxmTBIwke\n/qSFUYYDgzQy95+mdyJcgEr9zxhdoOTRBgzXr/E9h6BaH0jHxiTrfRtRocW+XqVf\nyouZXKAYSAChqSFakHJluRvstIhHsKZXI/GypflDB38E3Cld7bK2bf5rgYQanM/w\nkSyBLPBwElw683vDjb4WOn/qfSTbyjF0jlIEwTCPW220Ui/zbHtnYrFwx2crN6B3\nAnqHYzx9x+ySfqbf1ksI\n=xteF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T23:29:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/c1f02066de923e1772e6eaaec1da0935be7667cc","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGMxZjAyMDY2ZGU5MjNlMTc3MmU2ZWFhZWMxZGEwOTM1YmU3NjY3Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/d06c5baa849f090d2e60b8d5afcf155d0d169103","sha":"d06c5baa849f090d2e60b8d5afcf155d0d169103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/d06c5baa849f090d2e60b8d5afcf155d0d169103"}],"sha":"c1f02066de923e1772e6eaaec1da0935be7667cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/c1f02066de923e1772e6eaaec1da0935be7667cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/d06c5baa849f090d2e60b8d5afcf155d0d169103/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:24:44Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T23:24:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cloudflare): keep KV entries until their expire (#3735)\n\nThe KV data adapter wrote every entry with the configured ttlSeconds (30\ndays by default), even when the entry''s expire was longer. A\ncacheLife(\"max\") entry goes stale after 30 days but stays servable as\nstale for a year, so KV deleted it the moment it went stale, and the\nbackground re-render missed instead of reading the stale value.\n\nAn entry whose finite expire outlasts ttlSeconds now gets that expire as\nits KV expirationTtl, rounded up and kept within KV''s range. Shorter or\nmissing expires keep ttlSeconds.","tree":{"sha":"7a297987ab31d34b64c92f0001ce18435c932663","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/7a297987ab31d34b64c92f0001ce18435c932663"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/d06c5baa849f090d2e60b8d5afcf155d0d169103","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a297987ab31d34b64c92f0001ce18435c932663\nparent 82458b4252f66ebd6fae0f7b0ad026a8e7c5718b\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791415484 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791415484 +0100\n\nfix(cloudflare): keep KV entries until their expire (#3735)\n\nThe KV data adapter wrote every entry with the configured ttlSeconds (30\ndays by default), even when the entry''s expire was longer. A\ncacheLife(\"max\") entry goes stale after 30 days but stays servable as\nstale for a year, so KV deleted it the moment it went stale, and the\nbackground re-render missed instead of reading the stale value.\n\nAn entry whose finite expire outlasts ttlSeconds now gets that expire as\nits KV expirationTtl, rounded up and kept within KV''s range. Shorter or\nmissing expires keep ttlSeconds.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxtS8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdOwQAK6xJzgKa1xdHhoODcLATrX4\nnjIArVHSRsxZ3oULMaDJrrSVv5tCbefMBp1cyb4PdWNqgtqpTi9sfg3BZUUGCyk+\nZjaB5GjVb5x3wTrlxM1rHv76IRbmIFmwxVcBB5X6dTyQ4/x+cVyV86O+7iWlt4Wh\nvuCciNKA6y3hFGAbh/N9uq1Y3nxc07LZOsg/L9Dmg67+tNnWkZfwj6t8ct7w7QHT\nHzBn60+nyz/wYFDnNazwZbN/567oyOk2e+gJTWyGieKHr0hIcltMek11PZgfOUF/\nGLPXjaac5ItGD0vu9+zl1iwHtr+jlyW+EQXZM0S/hjfcSvITbndXvqZK0WgG6JBq\nyrwLCFZcsrJHmdAE1gTbvIGNJFeSRrL3TPrcNSkzUcEGf8k6sIvoHyadm5/Lldz2\nSDyieWw+1ez5T3hcQoNOmoFaxqunhp7Cs+EeXm25mFRqj3OVl8/E67DNb4MdZeSk\nsjvU4tMgpOdLWu29Pe58zMZSpYu+1tKjwHreKoVwMFjEhWwLLZQKPLDsA6VLVpAt\nwtSOGfu+awnjVTLoY5+T9k/2YY/Ib0cWGft3sSwCgjG9d9N971nvCEwhLYkwG8Qw\nIGDjwSwRNHzhJnSn78+IxLkZ5TksxdIaiB8BuP8zDHHz+WVNgQvryDBd0dXvrwxN\nLIin0yPQAV3CkYgo1JFN\n=8xaE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T23:24:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/d06c5baa849f090d2e60b8d5afcf155d0d169103","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGQwNmM1YmFhODQ5ZjA5MGQyZTYwYjhkNWFmY2YxNTVkMGQxNjkxMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/82458b4252f66ebd6fae0f7b0ad026a8e7c5718b","sha":"82458b4252f66ebd6fae0f7b0ad026a8e7c5718b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/82458b4252f66ebd6fae0f7b0ad026a8e7c5718b"}],"sha":"d06c5baa849f090d2e60b8d5afcf155d0d169103","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/d06c5baa849f090d2e60b8d5afcf155d0d169103"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/82458b4252f66ebd6fae0f7b0ad026a8e7c5718b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:54:09Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:54:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): authorize an interception source as a direct request to it (#3654)\n\n* fix(app-router): authorize an interception source as a direct request to it\n\nMatch the claimed interception source on its raw segments, as a direct\nrequest is matched, and run the source authorization steps a direct\nrequest to it takes. Next.js matches static segments against the raw path\nand keeps dynamic params encoded as they appear in the URL.\n\n- findIntercept matches the source like matchRequestRoute; source params\n  stay raw-encoded (`caf%C3%A9`, `%2561`, `a%2Fb`, `100%25`).\n- Source middleware sees the raw context in its request URL, with basePath\n  concatenated so a `/docs/...` context keeps its leading segment.\n- The context must already be URL-parser output, so raw matching cannot\n  reach a route no request URL does.\n- Trailing-slash canonicalization, config redirects and beforeFiles rewrites\n  apply to the source; a beforeFiles rewrite re-resolves it like a\n  middleware rewrite.\n- A slot-owner fallback, or a source a late rewrite reaches without\n  authorization, renders the target directly instead of intercepting.\n- The equal-route skip also requires equal params.\n- The ISR source variant keys on the raw context.\n- The client sends its decoded matched pathname only when it reads the\n  same raw.\n\n* fix(app-router): re-encode a matched interception source and refresh its rewrite host\n\n* test(app-router): type the host rewrite condition\n\n* fix(app-router): re-encode any matched interception source that round-trips\n\n* fix(app-router): refuse an ambiguous matched interception source\n\n* test(app-router): cover an escaped-ASCII interception source like Next.js\n\nNext.js renders `/tags/%61` with tag \"a\" and sends `Next-Url: /en/tags/a`,\nsince it builds the header from the router tree''s canonical params. The\nmatched-pathname fallback already sends the same; cover it in the client,\nthe locale-rewrite integration and e2e, and say so in the helper.\n\n* refactor(app-router): stop exporting the interception proof normalizer\n\nThe ISR cache key no longer goes through it, so it is only used inside its\nmodule.","tree":{"sha":"e612ab9f4d531824b5fa6fd97fc12c42eccb2040","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/e612ab9f4d531824b5fa6fd97fc12c42eccb2040"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/82458b4252f66ebd6fae0f7b0ad026a8e7c5718b","verification":{"payload":"tree e612ab9f4d531824b5fa6fd97fc12c42eccb2040\nparent 343583c8c7b06ff0e66177d106934c1c7427e5fe\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791388449 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791388449 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): authorize an interception source as a direct request to it (#3654)\n\n* fix(app-router): authorize an interception source as a direct request to it\n\nMatch the claimed interception source on its raw segments, as a direct\nrequest is matched, and run the source authorization steps a direct\nrequest to it takes. Next.js matches static segments against the raw path\nand keeps dynamic params encoded as they appear in the URL.\n\n- findIntercept matches the source like matchRequestRoute; source params\n  stay raw-encoded (`caf%C3%A9`, `%2561`, `a%2Fb`, `100%25`).\n- Source middleware sees the raw context in its request URL, with basePath\n  concatenated so a `/docs/...` context keeps its leading segment.\n- The context must already be URL-parser output, so raw matching cannot\n  reach a route no request URL does.\n- Trailing-slash canonicalization, config redirects and beforeFiles rewrites\n  apply to the source; a beforeFiles rewrite re-resolves it like a\n  middleware rewrite.\n- A slot-owner fallback, or a source a late rewrite reaches without\n  authorization, renders the target directly instead of intercepting.\n- The equal-route skip also requires equal params.\n- The ISR source variant keys on the raw context.\n- The client sends its decoded matched pathname only when it reads the\n  same raw.\n\n* fix(app-router): re-encode a matched interception source and refresh its rewrite host\n\n* test(app-router): type the host rewrite condition\n\n* fix(app-router): re-encode any matched interception source that round-trips\n\n* fix(app-router): refuse an ambiguous matched interception source\n\n* test(app-router): cover an escaped-ASCII interception source like Next.js\n\nNext.js renders `/tags/%61` with tag \"a\" and sends `Next-Url: /en/tags/a`,\nsince it builds the header from the router tree''s canonical params. The\nmatched-pathname fallback already sends the same; cover it in the client,\nthe locale-rewrite integration and e2e, and say so in the helper.\n\n* refactor(app-router): stop exporting the interception proof normalizer\n\nThe ISR cache key no longer goes through it, so it is only used inside its\nmodule.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxmshCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATGsQAFiw2F57JwSDIpbVrW+6arUU\n0OYr5tMYjf2xpDScCRrJCymIIVJ2L5fXy03s/Imx8KSLNgIA+yJn7VJmmWFUZCob\njPN+VdFRjAMsZa7jz+29ynONX9GbgNlUxZSqX2+ZE4rRNBBxOZ48RtBGf+Ik4hf3\nYcufFjEEGtyBLGr4EyhZfB6H8oqiBoPgJ43dWa0VbZNXHqNY3G0yVgQl7lYFyMO5\ngaLeNsgIhNb1OZx1+2YP6cuMNuDdfk42n5x6vihW5W5PNCWI3XRGi96ukvBhfd6q\naSM3ecQsL6et9DL6HkiUNoVWhmVvylEwvyHxvqZKyMAPPhF5tyDnzHHj8vC4eNRA\nVIVoTIQEedfRWHC8iNnLqKJuKHTXrHiEYCy6zv85SoZY4fomlzijAWZ38IQNhDS8\nDCyUANmUKNd5Rm573m+0c16ZzXrVOBJAghFnaQjif00BDMkB6wnkWtI0OexSKcPF\nT/jguny7rCTV6DbmODHyHUC3DKiEluTnGyF3SL5Ou/AesoxhYP84562IDY4+k08T\n62g2G7KIE0CeM1VOe2Ng+9Ul+4U2FINPFSiBra2pODREwR1nv6nRXFmUsvuuQZLr\nPXOq6LlPBzDy+FMucXeub5vRhzOaz+qsDQn+bJSRzVl29cJaLhBY/L0bCkD9e22t\nltMTzo+Nfky7fn9vsaBv\n=JBUO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T15:54:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/82458b4252f66ebd6fae0f7b0ad026a8e7c5718b","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDgyNDU4YjQyNTJmNjZlYmQ2ZmFlMGY3YjBhZDAyNmE4ZTdjNTcxOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/343583c8c7b06ff0e66177d106934c1c7427e5fe","sha":"343583c8c7b06ff0e66177d106934c1c7427e5fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/343583c8c7b06ff0e66177d106934c1c7427e5fe"}],"sha":"82458b4252f66ebd6fae0f7b0ad026a8e7c5718b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/82458b4252f66ebd6fae0f7b0ad026a8e7c5718b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/343583c8c7b06ff0e66177d106934c1c7427e5fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:54:09Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T15:54:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): resolve an interception source through its proxy rewrite (#3648)\n\n* fix(app-router): resolve an interception source through its proxy rewrite\n\nWith an unprefixed default locale, a proxy rewrites /feed to /en/feed.\nThe client sends /feed as the interception context, and the route matcher\nresolves it before the rewrite to /[locale] itself with locale \"feed\".\nThe source authorization pass then saw the rewrite reach /[locale]/feed,\na different route, and returned 404, so the client fell back to a full\npage load instead of opening the intercepted route.\n\nWhen the source middleware rewrite resolves to another route, resolve the\ninterception again from the rewritten source, which this middleware run\nproduced and so authorized. Rewrites to a route outside the interception\nand query-only rewrites still fail closed. Pages are dispatched with the\nresolved source, so the rendered source tree and the interception proof\nname /en/feed, which the client needs to keep the source mounted.\n\nExtends Next.js test/e2e/app-dir/interception-dynamic-segment-middleware/,\nwhich only navigates from the locale root.\n\n* refactor(app-router): let the existing check gate the re-resolved source\n\nThe re-resolution only proposes the source the rewrite reaches. The check\nthat follows already requires its exact route, params and query, so the\nextra guards before it were redundant.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep a rewritten interception source encoded once\n\nThe source middleware''s rewritten pathname is a URL pathname, so it is\nalready percent-encoded like the raw interception context. Encoding it\nagain made the matcher see literal escapes, so a source with an encoded\nstatic segment failed closed and an encoded dynamic segment produced a\nproof the client could not match. Pass it through unchanged, and compare\nthe rewritten route''s canonical params against the canonical form of the\ndecoded interception source params.\n\n* fix(app-router): hold a rewritten interception source to the header contract\n\nThe re-resolved source becomes the interception context the client sends\nback on refresh and actions. Adopt it only when it passes the same\nvalidation as the raw header, so a non-canonical rewrite such as\n/en//feed keeps the raw match and fails closed instead of producing a\ncontext the next request rejects.\n\n* fix(app-router): apply the full header contract to a rewritten source\n\nA rewritten interception source is sent back by the client as its context\nheader, so it must also pass the inbound normalization (length cap,\nwhitespace, null bytes). Otherwise middleware could expand a short source\npast the 1,024-character cap: the server would adopt it, and the client''s\nnext request would drop it.\n\n* fix(app-router): encode decoded interception params without decoding again\n\nThe interception matcher returns source params decoded exactly once, so\ncanonicalizing them decoded them a second time: a rewritten source of\n/en/tags/%2561 compared %2561 from matchRoute against a, and failed closed.\nPercent-encode the decoded values directly, including catch-all parts.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep a __proto__ param when encoding interception params\n\nBuild the encoded record with a null prototype like the matcher''s own\nparam records, so a [__proto__] segment becomes an own key instead of\nhitting Object.prototype.__proto__ and failing the exact comparison.\n\n* test(app-router): drop the double-encoded source case the client rejects\n\n* test(app-router): cover a Server Action from a rewritten interception source\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Brendan Dash <me@aiwan.run>","tree":{"sha":"429ba5eec7eff6dd85b7eeeb507eb59826041ea7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/429ba5eec7eff6dd85b7eeeb507eb59826041ea7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/343583c8c7b06ff0e66177d106934c1c7427e5fe","verification":{"payload":"tree 429ba5eec7eff6dd85b7eeeb507eb59826041ea7\nparent 7fe4bf37d554c1531070bff51cb43962c0d99f04\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791388449 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791388449 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): resolve an interception source through its proxy rewrite (#3648)\n\n* fix(app-router): resolve an interception source through its proxy rewrite\n\nWith an unprefixed default locale, a proxy rewrites /feed to /en/feed.\nThe client sends /feed as the interception context, and the route matcher\nresolves it before the rewrite to /[locale] itself with locale \"feed\".\nThe source authorization pass then saw the rewrite reach /[locale]/feed,\na different route, and returned 404, so the client fell back to a full\npage load instead of opening the intercepted route.\n\nWhen the source middleware rewrite resolves to another route, resolve the\ninterception again from the rewritten source, which this middleware run\nproduced and so authorized. Rewrites to a route outside the interception\nand query-only rewrites still fail closed. Pages are dispatched with the\nresolved source, so the rendered source tree and the interception proof\nname /en/feed, which the client needs to keep the source mounted.\n\nExtends Next.js test/e2e/app-dir/interception-dynamic-segment-middleware/,\nwhich only navigates from the locale root.\n\n* refactor(app-router): let the existing check gate the re-resolved source\n\nThe re-resolution only proposes the source the rewrite reaches. The check\nthat follows already requires its exact route, params and query, so the\nextra guards before it were redundant.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep a rewritten interception source encoded once\n\nThe source middleware''s rewritten pathname is a URL pathname, so it is\nalready percent-encoded like the raw interception context. Encoding it\nagain made the matcher see literal escapes, so a source with an encoded\nstatic segment failed closed and an encoded dynamic segment produced a\nproof the client could not match. Pass it through unchanged, and compare\nthe rewritten route''s canonical params against the canonical form of the\ndecoded interception source params.\n\n* fix(app-router): hold a rewritten interception source to the header contract\n\nThe re-resolved source becomes the interception context the client sends\nback on refresh and actions. Adopt it only when it passes the same\nvalidation as the raw header, so a non-canonical rewrite such as\n/en//feed keeps the raw match and fails closed instead of producing a\ncontext the next request rejects.\n\n* fix(app-router): apply the full header contract to a rewritten source\n\nA rewritten interception source is sent back by the client as its context\nheader, so it must also pass the inbound normalization (length cap,\nwhitespace, null bytes). Otherwise middleware could expand a short source\npast the 1,024-character cap: the server would adopt it, and the client''s\nnext request would drop it.\n\n* fix(app-router): encode decoded interception params without decoding again\n\nThe interception matcher returns source params decoded exactly once, so\ncanonicalizing them decoded them a second time: a rewritten source of\n/en/tags/%2561 compared %2561 from matchRoute against a, and failed closed.\nPercent-encode the decoded values directly, including catch-all parts.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep a __proto__ param when encoding interception params\n\nBuild the encoded record with a null prototype like the matcher''s own\nparam records, so a [__proto__] segment becomes an own key instead of\nhitting Object.prototype.__proto__ and failing the exact comparison.\n\n* test(app-router): drop the double-encoded source case the client rejects\n\n* test(app-router): cover a Server Action from a rewritten interception source\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Brendan Dash <me@aiwan.run>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxmshCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkBQQABMQgbQBAAElRsjxYEFCm58a\n8TJ5kTwFp0A4uOblovlPYCdcSpnSgiA7Hfcl/WRcxAM83AAPfjkJUJ9hVgunDEK/\nGw2zdDis/TCfHPqb075P1VhqhdK7tao2h5aK9kKX+4bAH5Irq1VKPT1vptDuYC/H\nnvGQpdRZvoXJ+gz/A2Q49JQ1HioYxNFujcWw8ekqBGJ8lkcDurHANuz0O9BLuJH2\ncE1WRHlVoKJe7yQyClv1DREdYwIzCm/JWi5idzvr3PCc1S+2d2aoRgy/R0cV6mhn\nfg7zbCBvJp7jACaP+nkNvE95XvVc1QLQt82lqmEsv/kt75F8ln5XJ4WbgwbD0/k9\n5HScCemtTxNCscjAjZzqYs9MIyyGYHWEwgcodmDC7fk7eeczxj+EF2b1ck3RwQpU\nMwrS3Y1yKm+lTjjjiUM/Vio4eHalb35V3bvFdq56I+OFbbVqNcprUgVQJXrvt+Ce\nw0OAylV9RT1IF1i3ekdgqW1mgcL7KjDLxS/s8IQeazIbsrXp6w50JvZNuoOQjhmM\nNJSGJiv2UaDEmNeV33m05pVpEvGMKdgyDSYI6qu06DVDbbDRo9Sdygazt+ayUCof\ntuywA5SvdpkGqLTVCB03QTuYs+eIMXaX7lTgWzsISPxDwfUsMl8JF2nhgfqxNM4P\nL7AnHeuyvCb6PdhTkBAa\n=nRKJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T15:54:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/343583c8c7b06ff0e66177d106934c1c7427e5fe","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDM0MzU4M2M4YzdiMDZmZjBlNjYxNzdkMTA2OTM0YzFjNzQyN2U1ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/7fe4bf37d554c1531070bff51cb43962c0d99f04","sha":"7fe4bf37d554c1531070bff51cb43962c0d99f04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/7fe4bf37d554c1531070bff51cb43962c0d99f04"}],"sha":"343583c8c7b06ff0e66177d106934c1c7427e5fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/343583c8c7b06ff0e66177d106934c1c7427e5fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/7fe4bf37d554c1531070bff51cb43962c0d99f04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:31:12Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T12:31:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): upgrade vite-plus to 1.1.0 (#3748)\n\n* chore(deps): upgrade vite-plus to 1.1.0\n\nBumps vite-plus and the vite-plus-core vite alias from 0.3.2 to 1.1.0\nacross the workspace catalog, along with vitest and\n@vitest/coverage-istanbul 5.0.3 to match the vitest version vite-plus\n1.1.0 bundles. Reformats apps/web globals.css for the new oxfmt.\n\n* fix: adapt CI to vite-plus 1.1.0\n\nvite-plus no longer ships an oxlint bin, so knip now treats the oxlint\nthat `vinext lint` invokes as a consumer-project binary, like eslint.\n\nVitest 5 clears mocks between tests by default, so the prerender\nCloudflare loader test captures the once-per-process register() call\nbefore any test runs.\n\n* fix(dev): stop Vite from watching the filesystem root for /?query pages\n\nVite 8.3.3 (vitejs/vite#23653) strips the query before mapping the\ntransformIndexHtml URL to a file, so `/?q` now resolves to the project\nroot directory. Because that directory exists and the query hides the\ntrailing slash, Vite treats `/?q` as a real file and gives each inline\n<style> proxy module the file `/`, then calls watcher.add(\"/\"). On\nLinux chokidar crawls the whole filesystem with one fs.watch per file,\nwhich ran the Pages _document integration tests out of memory.\n\nThe query has no meaning for the HTML transform, so the Pages dev server\nnow passes the bare path, which keeps Vite''s virtual proxy modules.\n\n* ci: point vitest 5 merge-reports at the downloaded shard blobs\n\nVitest 5 reads --merge-reports from .vitest/blob by default, but the\nintegration shards upload and the report job downloads their blobs into\n.vitest-reports.","tree":{"sha":"99e6c2fd4124ddcb362b9b10347dc250c008a13f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/99e6c2fd4124ddcb362b9b10347dc250c008a13f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/7fe4bf37d554c1531070bff51cb43962c0d99f04","verification":{"payload":"tree 99e6c2fd4124ddcb362b9b10347dc250c008a13f\nparent c1eee7f83152c969c34d9fec3c54804b2f223afb\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791376272 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791376272 +0100\n\nchore(deps): upgrade vite-plus to 1.1.0 (#3748)\n\n* chore(deps): upgrade vite-plus to 1.1.0\n\nBumps vite-plus and the vite-plus-core vite alias from 0.3.2 to 1.1.0\nacross the workspace catalog, along with vitest and\n@vitest/coverage-istanbul 5.0.3 to match the vitest version vite-plus\n1.1.0 bundles. Reformats apps/web globals.css for the new oxfmt.\n\n* fix: adapt CI to vite-plus 1.1.0\n\nvite-plus no longer ships an oxlint bin, so knip now treats the oxlint\nthat `vinext lint` invokes as a consumer-project binary, like eslint.\n\nVitest 5 clears mocks between tests by default, so the prerender\nCloudflare loader test captures the once-per-process register() call\nbefore any test runs.\n\n* fix(dev): stop Vite from watching the filesystem root for /?query pages\n\nVite 8.3.3 (vitejs/vite#23653) strips the query before mapping the\ntransformIndexHtml URL to a file, so `/?q` now resolves to the project\nroot directory. Because that directory exists and the query hides the\ntrailing slash, Vite treats `/?q` as a real file and gives each inline\n<style> proxy module the file `/`, then calls watcher.add(\"/\"). On\nLinux chokidar crawls the whole filesystem with one fs.watch per file,\nwhich ran the Pages _document integration tests out of memory.\n\nThe query has no meaning for the HTML transform, so the Pages dev server\nnow passes the bare path, which keeps Vite''s virtual proxy modules.\n\n* ci: point vitest 5 merge-reports at the downloaded shard blobs\n\nVitest 5 reads --merge-reports from .vitest/blob by default, but the\nintegration shards upload and the report job downloads their blobs into\n.vitest-reports.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxjuQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT/gQADSV0bhqq2LcNmEl0BzP7bRu\nt3PcotE5ZFo5QP8A5LtDCe++i+udgyoeXug2mqrMiY7+TgdfaD/XWtk+m7/mdJNm\ntUppl9zRqPH13zQb4mJZ