render Response Store and Workers Cache regenerations and warm-ups whole (#3737)\n\n* feat(app-router): render a page whole when the adapter asks, with its metadata in <head>\n\nA renderWholeDocument response-stage option makes an App page document wait for\nallReady before its first byte, with streamed metadata in <head>, as a core\nbackground regeneration and Next.js''s static renders do.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): render Response Store and Workers Cache regenerations and warm-ups whole\n\nNo client waits on these renders, so they store the document Next.js stores, with\ngenerated metadata in <head>:\n- Response Store regeneration and warm-up set renderWholeDocument.\n- Workers Cache gives a cacheable App page document a Last-Modified validator, so\n  it revalidates conditionally, and renders a warm-up or a conditional request whole.","tree":{"sha":"2cdb544406f6a44b01ac501961a9c98403371007","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/2cdb544406f6a44b01ac501961a9c98403371007"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/d6410f39dfa1af7b897fb84d799141e5efa14d5a","verification":{"payload":"tree 2cdb544406f6a44b01ac501961a9c98403371007\nparent f18b653cdfdaf06f0aa1ca7acf31e6d55162230c\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361746 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361746 +0100\n\nfix(cloudflare): render Response Store and Workers Cache regenerations and warm-ups whole (#3737)\n\n* feat(app-router): render a page whole when the adapter asks, with its metadata in <head>\n\nA renderWholeDocument response-stage option makes an App page document wait for\nallReady before its first byte, with streamed metadata in <head>, as a core\nbackground regeneration and Next.js''s static renders do.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): render Response Store and Workers Cache regenerations and warm-ups whole\n\nNo client waits on these renders, so they store the document Next.js stores, with\ngenerated metadata in <head>:\n- Response Store regeneration and warm-up set renderWholeDocument.\n- Workers Cache gives a cacheable App page document a Last-Modified validator, so\n  it revalidates conditionally, and renders a warm-up or a conditional request whole.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA09oQAD81krYbFaD66Rd2TcXMEg5Q\nXNdyq3ozGEYdCBJyaYKqyJgN4tY6H6bj2f4bFP3Y51vcEsll8/KXsdvOcEpxk4P1\n8W5UVAw7Lkc4MGrFlfx1U2xYrN0xT9t5uhnEaziqzjzL+kGQVIoRlx3C1eo12m7o\nKpSX/axBdVTtcFAY+Uk9gZwTd/+4VrgKTbnVr7tqMhFFrSgqPoRaEmxzCtcHptpQ\n4rh2cbRPNEqaoaMxBOaKPVVQD/M4c7YmOhv3CIE9tGLOZbpRysV8vAN1XsVgbN9R\nXTh1TP80xVJslLxx/omF+LY53Nz9BC0OR/4JpVxmHaK6dL3+JF3b5ZzXDGhbY8EZ\npkFiSRkyHO8c4nFR0yg+BnMN5n55GHvC4QhShc/w2l90p1RGW3DbWlt6AlTDff/j\nuuhQI9i9ZCDhikRaLzMAwIeiqkgnON31PwEmWqmyL58HRyLFR1OJdSmgQlWl4PZg\n2yf65lCVBj39Es9/AROr5ZLF9ovPDsvF2fPsUYz8llv1mwUcZ92Nz6ErKDvYWu7G\n8/4Vg7szs2Y3DzUl6xzuf2/l6vyMn+jphn+4x1O2YR81H/gDh5674wC+ZrD+Bx5p\nvFp7Srr4ZfC1Lnh6QjhEDwm0QKHcl12xxBmEreCvljoKuCxwh1FwpiTivCTZzG2p\nj7RlwXR5UPUf9aFFMsqA\n=owzN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:29:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/d6410f39dfa1af7b897fb84d799141e5efa14d5a","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGQ2NDEwZjM5ZGZhMWFmN2I4OTdmYjg0ZDc5OTE0MWU1ZWZhMTRkNWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/f18b653cdfdaf06f0aa1ca7acf31e6d55162230c","sha":"f18b653cdfdaf06f0aa1ca7acf31e6d55162230c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f18b653cdfdaf06f0aa1ca7acf31e6d55162230c"}],"sha":"d6410f39dfa1af7b897fb84d799141e5efa14d5a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/d6410f39dfa1af7b897fb84d799141e5efa14d5a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f18b653cdfdaf06f0aa1ca7acf31e6d55162230c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:05Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): restore streamed metadata and the __next_f mirror for the stack''s deploy-suite regressions (#3736)\n\n* fix(app-router): stream generated metadata in request renders, as before #3714\n\nOnly a background regeneration, which vinext already renders whole, waits for\nstreamed metadata in <head>. A request render that may be stored streams it into\n<body> again, which the Next.js metadata-streaming suites expect for live renders.\n\n* fix(app-router): mirror self.__next_f in a document that streams a caught special error\n\nSince #3711, a special error that a boundary caught streams as the page''s 200\ndocument instead of the boundary''s document, which carried Next.js''s inline\nFlight transport. Start the mirror at the first flush after the render captures\na special error, replaying the chunks already embedded.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep the embedded Flight chunks for a late __next_f mirror\n\nCache capture''s getRawBuffer() clears the raw chunks once the stream completes,\nso a mirror that starts after it replayed empty chunks. Keep the decoded chunks\nalready embedded apart, until the mirror starts or the stream finalizes.\n\n* perf(app-router): replay a late __next_f mirror from the raw chunks\n\nInstead of keeping a second decoded copy of the payload, hold the raw chunks\nuntil a mirror that may start late can''t, then release them as before.\n\n* fix(app-router): mirror self.__next_f in a regenerated document with a caught special error\n\nCore ISR regeneration stores the same 200 document, with the digest, that a\nrequest render streams, so it takes the same mirror predicate.","tree":{"sha":"a073a7031acceeee7922b688001e7ea9f2e69476","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/a073a7031acceeee7922b688001e7ea9f2e69476"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/f18b653cdfdaf06f0aa1ca7acf31e6d55162230c","verification":{"payload":"tree a073a7031acceeee7922b688001e7ea9f2e69476\nparent b4b525d223778228d12d0a3d8e4d6193cb27966b\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361745 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361745 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): restore streamed metadata and the __next_f mirror for the stack''s deploy-suite regressions (#3736)\n\n* fix(app-router): stream generated metadata in request renders, as before #3714\n\nOnly a background regeneration, which vinext already renders whole, waits for\nstreamed metadata in <head>. A request render that may be stored streams it into\n<body> again, which the Next.js metadata-streaming suites expect for live renders.\n\n* fix(app-router): mirror self.__next_f in a document that streams a caught special error\n\nSince #3711, a special error that a boundary caught streams as the page''s 200\ndocument instead of the boundary''s document, which carried Next.js''s inline\nFlight transport. Start the mirror at the first flush after the render captures\na special error, replaying the chunks already embedded.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep the embedded Flight chunks for a late __next_f mirror\n\nCache capture''s getRawBuffer() clears the raw chunks once the stream completes,\nso a mirror that starts after it replayed empty chunks. Keep the decoded chunks\nalready embedded apart, until the mirror starts or the stream finalizes.\n\n* perf(app-router): replay a late __next_f mirror from the raw chunks\n\nInstead of keeping a second decoded copy of the payload, hold the raw chunks\nuntil a mirror that may start late can''t, then release them as before.\n\n* fix(app-router): mirror self.__next_f in a regenerated document with a caught special error\n\nCore ISR regeneration stores the same 200 document, with the digest, that a\nrequest render streams, so it takes the same mirror predicate.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAamMQAF2kftVfbUKppCX09FRf3fVj\nxOg9Se8Eu05GXUBhfKmH3c0BI5vXs3oBZJsZEpSc8L4mVViXJ8GY3DneqjIOjw8V\n3kHA0QWvTlhD4D4+d8HS7XzDSJWnEqKzUElTkoEW6RE5nH2KdJNTthULjNtjSUh