223778228d12d0a3d8e4d6193cb27966b"}],"sha":"f18b653cdfdaf06f0aa1ca7acf31e6d55162230c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f18b653cdfdaf06f0aa1ca7acf31e6d55162230c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/b4b525d223778228d12d0a3d8e4d6193cb27966b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:05Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(prerender): write a page''s special error that escapes the shell with its status (#3716)\n\n* feat(prerender): write a page''s special error that escapes the shell with its status\n\nAs in Next.js''s build, a prerendered page whose notFound(), forbidden(),\nunauthorized() or redirect() rejects the shell is written with its status,\nand a redirect with its location: the special-error document beside the\npage''s RSC payload, which carries the digest. A prerender-only header marks\nthe response as the page''s own special error, so any other non-2xx still\nfails the route, and a render that turns dynamic is still skipped.\n\nThe page''s payload comes from an RSC request, which now carries its\ncache-busting `_rsc` param, since the document embeds its boundary''s payload.\nMemory seeding and the Workers Static Assets adapter keep the status on both\nentries, and the location on the RSC entry too, as runtime ISR stores them.\nCDN warmup accepts an admitted 401 or 403 as a warmed terminal response, as\nit does a 404. Speculative prerenders and export mode are unchanged.\n\n* fix(prerender): trust only vinext''s special-error marker and the redirect''s own location\n\nMiddleware and config headers can no longer set the prerender special-error\nmarker, and the marker now carries the redirect''s stored location, which is the\nonly location the build persists.\n\n* fix(prerender): mark a page''s special error only from the prerender server''s ctx\n\nThe render records the special error on the prerender server''s execution\ncontext instead of setting a response header, so a middleware short-circuit,\nroute handler or external rewrite can''t mark its own 401/403/404. The prerender\nserver drops any marker the response carries and sets the recorded one when the\nstatus matches; this replaces the merge-point filters.\n\nA boundary''s tags and cacheLife are read once its document has rendered, and a\nredirect to an empty location keeps it in the manifest.\n\n* fix(prerender): mark the special error after the public-file signal is served\n\nReconstructing the response dropped the public-file signal, so the prerender\nserver now marks only the response it streams, and a public file''s headers\nnever carry the marker.","tree":{"sha":"dbe4ea20c9db53acb1430beed5ab796a6df4bda5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/dbe4ea20c9db53acb1430beed5ab796a6df4bda5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/b4b525d223778228d12d0a3d8e4d6193cb27966b","verification":{"payload":"tree dbe4ea20c9db53acb1430beed5ab796a6df4bda5\nparent 2ec4a7f83477c401ef0d8c7cf6e06a310743bc27\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361745 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361745 +0100\n\nfeat(prerender): write a page''s special error that escapes the shell with its status (#3716)\n\n* feat(prerender): write a page''s special error that escapes the shell with its status\n\nAs in Next.js''s build, a prerendered page whose notFound(), forbidden(),\nunauthorized() or redirect() rejects the shell is written with its status,\nand a redirect with its location: the special-error document beside the\npage''s RSC payload, which carries the digest. A prerender-only header marks\nthe response as the page''s own special error, so any other non-2xx still\nfails the route, and a render that turns dynamic is still skipped.\n\nThe page''s payload comes from an RSC request, which now carries its\ncache-busting `_rsc` param, since the document embeds its boundary''s payload.\nMemory seeding and the Workers Static Assets adapter keep the status on both\nentries, and the location on the RSC entry too, as runtime ISR stores them.\nCDN warmup accepts an admitted 401 or 403 as a warmed terminal response, as\nit does a 404. Speculative prerenders and export mode are unchanged.\n\n* fix(prerender): trust only vinext''s special-error marker and the redirect''s own location\n\nMiddleware and config headers can no longer set the prerender special-error\nmarker, and the marker now carries the redirect''s stored location, which is the\nonly location the build persists.\n\n* fix(prerender): mark a page''s special error only from the prerender server''s ctx\n\nThe render records the special error on the prerender server''s execution\ncontext instead of setting a response header, so a middleware short-circuit,\nroute handler or external rewrite can''t mark its own 401/403/404. The prerender\nserver drops any marker the response carries and sets the recorded one when the\nstatus matches; this replaces the merge-point filters.\n\nA boundary''s tags and cacheLife are read once its document has rendered, and a\nredirect to an empty location keeps it in the manifest.\n\n* fix(prerender): mark the special error after the public-file signal is served\n\nReconstructing the response dropped the public-file signal, so the prerender\nserver now marks only the response it streams, and a public file''s headers\nnever carry the marker.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANHIQACYojkkEihOoy/iEFjdxke9e\nd5hQbtsT5hCjmgM2NJRLGYNFPxAXS2U2TIpfCJM4CpIQssc5F9SIyV+3E45KjBlK\n5yryocsbpa7wYcK+Fqne6HcOvl93m+tdT+sF/WWlTD93BQ/iKw01HXsg65KmpyOn\ngBTFmIkt5gKUQGNqkFUqldcPMO2ys5nO1nRUJCU+t/oeH0Xz713S1LkE06ont+C3\n970PU96/lkv03EzyCP8Y7o1PT72CUeysJrpv83N2QdPjHhpV11hBNuhtSMNHGHeJ\nIc6Vo/IoWMpw4W3qc4iaW93nz8fqglqFd5doP5vVPtXTcyG1swTB6L3W1DZEVzKu\n1GvIeW2ra3nBvWsk6HsY+1f7tlPl3apoQoiyhHBPVlRkCrUqRTYbqc+CtSbbpHuu\nK6itEUcxDY6uczRO0FBX0fj3zmgekll4BYviG31enF2jwmcOHmGfhppcmU8PS2UD\nJN0zoo+Zjnjd/308N9nnaxRSWA15+ox85SiWuV5ba9Np3QZLnXKuf2FT/OMIHuqo\nr0HPJ0NOew84aQVAKLTWG/Av3+9qMPkyIxCqIILNfqyfVt+zTi5BZKgsunds0o5y\nXJ7jGZLnYAJgH+TpgvnLj6Tae/QeTrZximPsnR0FBVsXOGHlpEgQ54qjm9U6A30A\nl4ziEZiyT176M2oVusU0\n=LSOr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:29:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/b4b525d223778228d12d0a3d8e4d6193cb27966b","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGI0YjUyNWQyMjM3NzgyMjhkMTJkMGEzZDhlNGQ2MTkzY2IyNzk2NmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/2ec4a7f83477c401ef0d8c7cf6e06a310743bc27","sha":"2ec4a7f83477c401ef0d8c7cf6e06a310743bc27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/2ec4a7f83477c401ef0d8c7cf6e06a310743bc27"}],"sha":"b4b525d223778228d12d0a3d8e4d6193cb27966b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/b4b525d223778228d12d0a3d8e4d6193cb27966b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/2ec4a7f83477c401ef0d8c7cf6e06a310743bc27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:04Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): put generated metadata in <head> of a page that may be stored, as Next.js does (#3714)\n\n* fix(app-router): wait for generated metadata in <head> of a page that may be stored\n\nNext.js renders a static or ISR page whole before serving it, so the\nmetadata it streams is ready before the document flushes and React puts it\nin <head>, on a miss and on a regeneration, for every user agent. vinext\nstreamed it into <body> on a cache candidate''s miss and on a regeneration a\nnormal user agent triggered, so the stored document kept the title and\ncanonical tags in <body>.\n\nA render that may be stored, and every regeneration, now waits for\ngenerated metadata in <head>. It still streams it as the triggering request\ndoes otherwise: generateMetadata()''s special error is left out of the head\nand rethrown by the suspended outlet inside the route''s boundaries, so it\ndoesn''t break the shell, and the stored status stays the same.\n\n* fix(app-router): place an intercepted or mounted-slot render''s metadata as its own storage decides\n\nAn intercepted RSC response renders the source route, so the source''s own\nstatic eligibility, dynamic config and revalidate value, under the request''s\nstorage gates, decide whether it may be stored, and so whether its streamed\nmetadata waits in <head>. A mounted-slot RSC request is never read from or\nwritten to the cache, so it keeps streaming metadata as the request does.\n\n* fix(app-router): stream metadata for an RSC request that may skip transport\n\nAn RSC request whose client-reuse manifest may enable skip transport gets a\nper-client response that is never stored, but whether it does is decided\nonly once the page''s elements are built. Like a mounted-slot request, it\nkeeps streaming its generated metadata instead of waiting for it in <head>.\n\nThe regeneration e2e test now requires the polled document''s timestamp to\nexist and differ from the stored one: Playwright''s expect.not.stringMatching\nalso matches a missing timestamp.","tree":{"sha":"58d1db8163e59524a00500bb840fa58b075276f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/58d1db8163e59524a00500bb840fa58b075276f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/2ec4a7f83477c401ef0d8c7cf6e06a310743bc27","verification":{"payload":"tree 58d1db8163e59524a00500bb840fa58b075276f2\nparent 734549f180945de4c91add47dde88c09a79fa1d8\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361744 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361744 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): put generated metadata in <head> of a page that may be stored, as Next.js does (#3714)\n\n* fix(app-router): wait for generated metadata in <head> of a page that may be stored\n\nNext.js renders a static or ISR page whole before serving it, so the\nmetadata it streams is ready before the document flushes and React puts it\nin <head>, on a miss and on a regeneration, for every user agent. vinext\nstreamed it into <body> on a cache candidate''s miss and on a regeneration a\nnormal user agent triggered, so the stored document kept the title and\ncanonical tags in <body>.\n\nA render that may be stored, and every regeneration, now waits for\ngenerated metadata in <head>. It still streams it as the triggering request\ndoes otherwise: generateMetadata()''s special error is left out of the head\nand rethrown by the suspended outlet inside the route''s boundaries, so it\ndoesn''t break the shell, and the stored status stays the same.\n\n* fix(app-router): place an intercepted or mounted-slot render''s metadata as its own storage decides\n\nAn intercepted RSC response renders the source route, so the source''s own\nstatic eligibility, dynamic config and revalidate value, under the request''s\nstorage gates, decide whether it may be stored, and so whether its streamed\nmetadata waits in <head>. A mounted-slot RSC request is never read from or\nwritten to the cache, so it keeps streaming metadata as the request does.\n\n* fix(app-router): stream metadata for an RSC request that may skip transport\n\nAn RSC request whose client-reuse manifest may enable skip transport gets a\nper-client response that is never stored, but whether it does is decided\nonly once the page''s elements are built. Like a mounted-slot request, it\nkeeps streaming its generated metadata instead of waiting for it in <head>.\n\nThe regeneration e2e test now requires the polled document''s timestamp to\nexist and differ from the stored one: Playwright''s expect.not.stringMatching\nalso matches a missing timestamp.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2r8QAJ3kNIsHmducjxsVjDgKEaAQ\nDTFKVnoPGknZbdn0hKLNnmj3084zd2czlupsMLKmezi2O7XxIKPj4ADnquPC/TCH\n4wmvB2k/9vrzsn4Pyzro+JZBldE0Oj4GiMJd8Tq9+GsJs1oTZr6WOGFuqNApyjog\nW26j1uHeZwH/8aRBOoyc3tlFjU1bVrkaCVZey+zsyk90DlJqG3kvbN/asQybpsFI\no3r9j+0dmUB4NBwgO4rmPDGbmSkgnBDywl6o8F/Sg8r/azzrO/ubafF5/KNdsyCG\nzcp7hXVUjKHYpb3KhDrYXYJy/qh08UnaPg+ulI7I4YoRxfHh+QUB2zQuFQEc5QNx\nYpr8qR1xrL+1E2hKTAAHVBNYjMjx8WYFAXhAf6neZJZ4TR5456YNCch4p/3V4WT6\nc+D2IieURCuZ1il8/X9DyAPv9GcqFm84+q5Y61GENfuBnKPKfVzWLDJak+FyJpvO\np4epK6/GY4gTLdQr7JOVCFzkroo+wNENjrcTH+6i7QmbcW2H3tK4W0mm1vkc8i5C\naDupUJ71vQph7cb6606f9O+6vOLHHXtnW4tDxnKEb9yUoJneyTdo1GW2YOGD5/U4\n3B+sI1DPehrHUyQJsskhb1oj6ZCOoCRguJW4PsNiKu2zTXVCGyGk9HZL/yrgXMNi\nzswYc5qXVbh5FYHWehMt\n=oc1r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:29:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/2ec4a7f83477c401ef0d8c7cf6e06a310743bc27","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDJlYzRhN2Y4MzQ3N2M0MDFlZjBkOGM3Y2Y2ZTA2YTMxMDc0M2JjMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/734549f180945de4c91add47dde88c09a79fa1d8","sha":"734549f180945de4c91add47dde88c09a79fa1d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/734549f180945de4c91add47dde88c09a79fa1d8"}],"sha":"2ec4a7f83477c401ef0d8c7cf6e06a310743bc27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/2ec4a7f83477c401ef0d8c7cf6e06a310743bc27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/734549f180945de4c91add47dde88c09a79fa1d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:04Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): stream a special error a Suspense boundary caught as a 200, as Next.js does (#3711)\n\n* fix(app-router): stream a special error a Suspense boundary caught as the page''s 200 document\n\nWhen a Suspense boundary, such as a loading.tsx, caught a page''s\nnotFound(), forbidden(), unauthorized() or redirect(), vinext cancelled the\nstreamed document and served the special error''s 404, 403, 401 or 307\ninstead. Next.js doesn''t: the shell rendered, so the document streams as a\n200 with the digest, which the client''s boundary renders, along with the\nnoindex robots tag or a meta refresh. The same holds in dev, for dynamic\nrenders and for ISR, which stores the render as a 200.\n\n* test(app-router): cover an ISR page whose loading.tsx catches its special error end to end\n\n* fix(app-router): store generateMetadata()''s special error with the status its triggering request gets\n\nNext.js stores an ISR render whose generateMetadata() throws a special\nerror with the status the request that rendered it gets: an html-limited\nbot blocks on metadata, so the error rejects the shell and the 404 or\nredirect is stored for everyone, while other user agents stream metadata\nand store the 200 document with the digest. A regeneration streams metadata\nas the request that triggered it does.\n\nvinext never stored the shell-rejecting case, and a regeneration always\nblocked on metadata, so it failed and kept the previous entry. A miss, an\nRSC-first miss and a regeneration now store it as Next.js does.\n\n* fix(app-router): don''t store generateMetadata()''s special error from an RSC-only render\n\nAn html-limited bot''s RSC request blocks on metadata, so generateMetadata()''s\nspecial error rejects the shell. Next.js stores the 404 or redirect document\nbeside the payload, but an RSC miss or regeneration writes only the RSC entry.\nIts status would sit beside a document that a request streaming metadata\nstores as a 200, so the RSC-only render stores nothing, and a regeneration\nkeeps the previous entry, until a document request stores both.","tree":{"sha":"6b9c72a5102ee43d66b9242778e78794047f21c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/6b9c72a5102ee43d66b9242778e78794047f21c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/734549f180945de4c91add47dde88c09a79fa1d8","verification":{"payload":"tree 6b9c72a5102ee43d66b9242778e78794047f21c7\nparent cee2d40450a945df27191daeab8959b430edd004\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361744 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361744 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): stream a special error a Suspense boundary caught as a 200, as Next.js does (#3711)\n\n* fix(app-router): stream a special error a Suspense boundary caught as the page''s 200 document\n\nWhen a Suspense boundary, such as a loading.tsx, caught a page''s\nnotFound(), forbidden(), unauthorized() or redirect(), vinext cancelled the\nstreamed document and served the special error''s 404, 403, 401 or 307\ninstead. Next.js doesn''t: the shell rendered, so the document streams as a\n200 with the digest, which the client''s boundary renders, along with the\nnoindex robots tag or a meta refresh. The same holds in dev, for dynamic\nrenders and for ISR, which stores the render as a 200.\n\n* test(app-router): cover an ISR page whose loading.tsx catches its special error end to end\n\n* fix(app-router): store generateMetadata()''s special error with the status its triggering request gets\n\nNext.js stores an ISR render whose generateMetadata() throws a special\nerror with the status the request that rendered it gets: an html-limited\nbot blocks on metadata, so the error rejects the shell and the 404 or\nredirect is stored for everyone, while other user agents stream metadata\nand store the 200 document with the digest. A regeneration streams metadata\nas the request that triggered it does.\n\nvinext never stored the shell-rejecting case, and a regeneration always\nblocked on metadata, so it failed and kept the previous entry. A miss, an\nRSC-first miss and a regeneration now store it as Next.js does.\n\n* fix(app-router): don''t store generateMetadata()''s special error from an RSC-only render\n\nAn html-limited bot''s RSC request blocks on metadata, so generateMetadata()''s\nspecial error rejects the shell. Next.js stores the 404 or redirect document\nbeside the payload, but an RSC miss or regeneration writes only the RSC entry.\nIts status would sit beside a document that a request streaming metadata\nstores as a 200, so the RSC-only render stores nothing, and a regeneration\nkeeps the previous entry, until a document request stores both.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADogQAB0X8r1nyqMgA6xQ+F0WJLEn\npg4LpuQHri+XZB4GUV0ZY58DHIEgjKFhFpmcRmCLlqgAl0bJ2H71AEmNeG4kr+uV\nxR/uv1YfV+NAQmzUwQyqNV5exQHYrHg/Nbw2E1LZr5jnUAF7LMvCK2QD3zRpm27G\ntkZzZ/n48XA+YhBvW/5tZF3PG0Al91UKwGRiadGgNQCS1yaygblinnsnXSYxO1hV\nG0aClD53GuuWicQb6nbffYB+rDH4K7eagY3587Zp4ABqjmI5mHyjs5y+gHzyoDoa\ns1bIueomtKZ6eD8mmtquZtTen88jVAhWXO2vr3jpQZ6FKPvbC1574GY1Izc+n9Gn\nZjgduE+pIDqlN/U0SDtzFxQtd/+pbodJl6i+rQwREMcgcPipi23buFc4TCc/vXlK\nZtk5bYWG17NRocwlI7hVBGKKtA3l1w5Xym25jC29Hsc4Tm0aANZROUrQwqd/AA+v\nEveNAodnivevZx6EBp2kcpSiGpQtW5Ht9E76NbcqzLG0okLRrwMC2wtMozWuoj1B\n90BE9FYkHN41YaaH0EjqSvCf9D+BQ5fRo4pgnsD5+DXaJarCnx7zz4porlAT5YBV\nS4odfRb3TQP7EioC5iz++/NsWHHvQbXWAoq77kYtHC4nxkuc1Aw7Fw0iDjQ0WSdx\n/TfNhARAZiTsX/k7NTqM\n=+gqW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:29:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/734549f180945de4c91add47dde88c09a79fa1d8","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDczNDU0OWYxODA5NDVkZTRjOTFhZGQ0N2RkZTg4YzA5YTc5ZmExZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/cee2d40450a945df27191daeab8959b430edd004","sha":"cee2d40450a945df27191daeab8959b430edd004","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/cee2d40450a945df27191daeab8959b430edd004"}],"sha":"734549f180945de4c91add47dde88c09a79fa1d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/734549f180945de4c91add47dde88c09a79fa1d8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/cee2d40450a945df27191daeab8959b430edd004/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:03Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): store an RSC-first ISR render with its real status, and never cache unmatched 404s (#3710)\n\n* fix(app-router): store an RSC-first ISR render with the status its document''s shell gives it\n\nNext.js renders an ISR page''s document beside its RSC payload, so an RSC\nrequest that renders the page first stores the status the shell gives it:\n404, 403 or 401 for a special error that rejects the shell, 307 with its\nlocation for a redirect, and 200 when a Suspense boundary catches it.\nvinext stored every RSC-first render as a 200.\n\nOnce the payload is complete, a render that threw a special error renders\nthe document''s shell from the captured payload to resolve its status.\nServer components don''t run again. Core stores that status. Workers Cache\nand Response Store admission send the completed response with it, an RSC\nredirect as a 200 with its location. A render whose shell another error\nrejects, or generateMetadata()''s special error, isn''t stored.\n\nThe Response Store also stores and serves a page''s 401 and 403 like its\n404, and seeds the RSC entry with its document''s status.\n\n* fix(app-router): never cache an unmatched route''s 404\n\nNext.js sends every 404 of a route it couldn''t match with\n`private, no-cache, no-store, max-age=0, must-revalidate`. vinext sent the\nrendered not-found page, the staged one and the plain fallback without a\nCache-Control header, so a cache could keep them under its own policy.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): send a page''s admitted or seeded special error to a segment prefetch as a 200\n\nWorkers Cache and Response Store admission now send and store an RSC\nrender with the 401, 403 or 404 its special error resolved, and the\nResponse Store seeds a page''s RSC entry with its document''s status. A\nLink''s segment prefetch shares that entry, so it received the 404 and the\nclick loaded the document, where Next.js answers the prefetch with a 200.\n\nBoth mark the status, as a core replay does, so the request stage sends it\nto a segment prefetch as a 200 and strips the marker.\n\n* fix(app-router): render a force-static page''s RSC-first shell as force-static\n\nThe shell pass that resolves an RSC-first render''s status dropped\nforce-static''s exemption, so a client component that read useSearchParams()\nbailed out to client rendering and the render wasn''t stored.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep middleware''s headers over a completed RSC render''s\n\nAdmission applied a completed redirect render''s location over the response\nthat middleware had already merged into, so middleware''s Location lost. As\non a fresh render or an ISR replay, middleware''s headers now win.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep an unmatched route''s never-cache policy over a matching next.config Cache-Control","tree":{"sha":"984c0abeb6719e0a29d935887e616cf453e0bb15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/984c0abeb6719e0a29d935887e616cf453e0bb15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/cee2d40450a945df27191daeab8959b430edd004","verification":{"payload":"tree 984c0abeb6719e0a29d935887e616cf453e0bb15\nparent 85938840cf79e35ed1522bf288623ce96b4ce767\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361743 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361743 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): store an RSC-first ISR render with its real status, and never cache unmatched 404s (#3710)\n\n* fix(app-router): store an RSC-first ISR render with the status its document''s shell gives it\n\nNext.js renders an ISR page''s document beside its RSC payload, so an RSC\nrequest that renders the page first stores the status the shell gives it:\n404, 403 or 401 for a special error that rejects the shell, 307 with its\nlocation for a redirect, and 200 when a Suspense boundary catches it.\nvinext stored every RSC-first render as a 200.\n\nOnce the payload is complete, a render that threw a special error renders\nthe document''s shell from the captured payload to resolve its status.\nServer components don''t run again. Core stores that status. Workers Cache\nand Response Store admission send the completed response with it, an RSC\nredirect as a 200 with its location. A render whose shell another error\nrejects, or generateMetadata()''s special error, isn''t stored.\n\nThe Response Store also stores and serves a page''s 401 and 403 like its\n404, and seeds the RSC entry with its document''s status.\n\n* fix(app-router): never cache an unmatched route''s 404\n\nNext.js sends every 404 of a route it couldn''t match with\n`private, no-cache, no-store, max-age=0, must-revalidate`. vinext sent the\nrendered not-found page, the staged one and the plain fallback without a\nCache-Control header, so a cache could keep them under its own policy.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): send a page''s admitted or seeded special error to a segment prefetch as a 200\n\nWorkers Cache and Response Store admission now send and store an RSC\nrender with the 401, 403 or 404 its special error resolved, and the\nResponse Store seeds a page''s RSC entry with its document''s status. A\nLink''s segment prefetch shares that entry, so it received the 404 and the\nclick loaded the document, where Next.js answers the prefetch with a 200.\n\nBoth mark the status, as a core replay does, so the request stage sends it\nto a segment prefetch as a 200 and strips the marker.\n\n* fix(app-router): render a force-static page''s RSC-first shell as force-static\n\nThe shell pass that resolves an RSC-first render''s status dropped\nforce-static''s exemption, so a client component that read useSearchParams()\nbailed out to client rendering and the render wasn''t stored.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep middleware''s headers over a completed RSC render''s\n\nAdmission applied a completed redirect render''s location over the response\nthat middleware had already merged into, so middleware''s Location lost. As\non a fresh render or an ISR replay, middleware''s headers now win.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep an unmatched route''s never-cache policy over a matching next.config Cache-Control","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlw8QAHdkBPVHHNt4lHXUZf0ZgDZX\n2Re2iHc8SJX+z23kHUxbstS6nMj78x3ySl3a6APrsQyxuaoTGCOrKFjIC/WElOvG\nGS1oHOyTZYqw4cBPYn3YaoAs6g86pOaBm9Ja07IeHL2k8bNrQQAId4E0snFFFIn1\nW2iHz0bVr7Uk6pSCxCQ3KZUWSlL+mgMHUbRwPJqqoWalvgLbUlqXKTRB4k33qkeQ\nfr9nDNM2tFS2C1xtkJaM7npjZg2pT6+DpGi8tc54pBDVM1p3+N/O8Y1XGqF3uV1J\npQQapCcftTgqnCFBmT93M61YI7W5GuPyn1jNaR8sviL7aLpkyh9wayXB8vEv1dsC\nffSqm90y9nQyxB0DxvyGXwb2pE4Dd7C7bq5S4ST2H3fLLINhsI0drhzYv3jV+4rK\njgf64ZfWZJygj2v/zKE7h1n0Vb4qK/6j5N6U9ybUt1TNhQe2AM2iSJF+FQAj59qw\nfTt4m4+nl4Tl3mI2yU+1yQfOWkKztpyTHkGKGE/Uoq1dJoZJE4s8R5O5fewxP70a\nJryTGmi+Fp+OfrJZGh7XkK/Y3VfFRllWSsFhBrJ6/EzxDJBytAIQdBHyYoJIaFv5\n49v5VkihxXirapyrZe4x1ZNy80ecyrbjOMI+TgO14b4/k65ZZkiXHeMw+kwKKdxB\nH/zARb9D6ffWFcKMGZun\n=7gFt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:29:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/cee2d40450a945df27191daeab8959b430edd004","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGNlZTJkNDA0NTBhOTQ1ZGYyNzE5MWRhZWFiODk1OWI0MzBlZGQwMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/85938840cf79e35ed1522bf288623ce96b4ce767","sha":"85938840cf79e35ed1522bf288623ce96b4ce767","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/85938840cf79e35ed1522bf288623ce96b4ce767"}],"sha":"cee2d40450a945df27191daeab8959b430edd004","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/cee2d40450a945df27191daeab8959b430edd004"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/85938840cf79e35ed1522bf288623ce96b4ce767/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:03Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cloudflare): send no-store while Response Store admission is pending (#3708)\n\nA MISS the Response Store may still admit can find a late dynamic API, and\na dynamic render is no-store in Next.js. Use the same pending policy the\nframework sends when it caches the response itself.","tree":{"sha":"01c70563411885b2b9979e710c1374f8b7ce0ab5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/01c70563411885b2b9979e710c1374f8b7ce0ab5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/85938840cf79e35ed1522bf288623ce96b4ce767","verification":{"payload":"tree 01c70563411885b2b9979e710c1374f8b7ce0ab5\nparent 6264a2d75653b1fed7fced148b3937796c88ba25\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361743 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361743 +0100\n\nfix(cloudflare): send no-store while Response Store admission is pending (#3708)\n\nA MISS the Response Store may still admit can find a late dynamic API, and\na dynamic render is no-store in Next.js. Use the same pending policy the\nframework sends when it caches the response itself.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SI