_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/6264a2d75653b1fed7fced148b3937796c88ba25","sha":"6264a2d75653b1fed7fced148b3937796c88ba25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/6264a2d75653b1fed7fced148b3937796c88ba25"}],"sha":"85938840cf79e35ed1522bf288623ce96b4ce767","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/85938840cf79e35ed1522bf288623ce96b4ce767"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/6264a2d75653b1fed7fced148b3937796c88ba25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:02Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): keep a shallow history write made after the optimistic shell commits (#3706)\n\n* fix(app-router): keep a shallow history write made after the optimistic shell commits\n\nA raw pushState/replaceState after a navigation''s optimistic shell is\nvisible no longer overwrites the shallow URL when the authoritative\nresponse lands. As in Next.js, the shell commit counts as the navigation''s\ncommit: the content still fills in, the navigation''s own URL write is\nretired, URL hooks read the shallow URL throughout, and every history\nentry that remembered the shell restores the completed tree.\n\n* fix(app-router): match a retired navigation URL by its full href, only until the navigation finalizes\n\nA redirect that only adds a hash renders the same pathname and search, so it\nmatched the retired shell URL and kept the shallow URL instead of applying\nthe hash. And server action redirects reuse the navigation id without\nbeginNavigation(), so a stale retired URL could keep the shallow URL on a\nlater action redirect back to the shell''s path.","tree":{"sha":"0101c6a571bd73e289cc1fdf998bc0c56341dad1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/0101c6a571bd73e289cc1fdf998bc0c56341dad1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/6264a2d75653b1fed7fced148b3937796c88ba25","verification":{"payload":"tree 0101c6a571bd73e289cc1fdf998bc0c56341dad1\nparent 3ce5cc3e31b24bb51c9fedee7483d4426b5317b7\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361742 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361742 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): keep a shallow history write made after the optimistic shell commits (#3706)\n\n* fix(app-router): keep a shallow history write made after the optimistic shell commits\n\nA raw pushState/replaceState after a navigation''s optimistic shell is\nvisible no longer overwrites the shallow URL when the authoritative\nresponse lands. As in Next.js, the shell commit counts as the navigation''s\ncommit: the content still fills in, the navigation''s own URL write is\nretired, URL hooks read the shallow URL throughout, and every history\nentry that remembered the shell restores the completed tree.\n\n* fix(app-router): match a retired navigation URL by its full href, only until the navigation finalizes\n\nA redirect that only adds a hash renders the same pathname and search, so it\nmatched the retired shell URL and kept the shallow URL instead of applying\nthe hash. And server action redirects reuse the navigation id without\nbeginNavigation(), so a stale retired URL could keep the shallow URL on a\nlater action redirect back to the shell''s path.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsOcQACwKZYwwANYfBT3zQnzb93NS\n63fVcFrL72wWEHGLFeh0ZMSTyRn7Uo2niFLngCw+m+QjnSEwwAokrFDcnobDcyHr\npORDiTP0W+oqtG3Y2qg8lqhYSIBPXFqNV4Zc10m83SNPCOIIXrfhczpSO0yaRKAi\nRTIg2ZiJMAbRVLpCYI4nWpQ/M8xUy5EqhIWlNwO69Gy0ZPF8kff+hOWLU1cIviGr\nHt5dWYQGBTJXdmCN7c//+ezhbVOZ9KJZchI2v9tj1d+oPTNcBDItdfwWe6fwnJwl\nZRQ+WfVlacpOVYdaV57Hx5NRZhge+htDTUd4ZuhWJpq2KlnbJhcyEEA+s1gQ7GEk\nbwFVAT+pCWQ+AbA6jwZ8Ba/tP/HN9l6EbZrJZf4Lxya/TB5DXEwQIT9Y5k3b9M/5\n12yEDhrxxOvGsQzzapTDlT7IOCk+x4AG3mmM+jLPdupH2ZreufgCZGQieNZHJk0R\n/wqzc7mmrYe5dFGkJ3avjkCvOswHSvrT7lxPOAsYq4SrkTsixTfxxeUeKtc/POct\n4QuI/s+OFIE+AEMIlgqFtZBQgUrFcWtkbYXAGsKWZakyNz/OMfib0EIvkh6iYElO\nfaTmWhupeDAQ8cfWMg8TIux3CqKCT0pCH6VMqIZxuakLyfuNu25EE0Tv5Qla7TQN\nmkLYmpJ6q5Jo31zE/02J\n=mrIY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:29:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/6264a2d75653b1fed7fced148b3937796c88ba25","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDYyNjRhMmQ3NTY1M2IxZmVkN2ZjZWQxNDhiMzkzNzc5NmM4OGJhMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/3ce5cc3e31b24bb51c9fedee7483d4426b5317b7","sha":"3ce5cc3e31b24bb51c9fedee7483d4426b5317b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/3ce5cc3e31b24bb51c9fedee7483d4426b5317b7"}],"sha":"6264a2d75653b1fed7fced148b3937796c88ba25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/6264a2d75653b1fed7fced148b3937796c88ba25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/3ce5cc3e31b24bb51c9fedee7483d4426b5317b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:02Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): store a page''s special-error render in the ISR cache (#3702)\n\n* fix(app-router): store a page''s special error that escapes the shell in the ISR cache\n\n* test(app-router): cover ISR HITs for a page''s notFound() and redirect() document end to end\n\n* fix(app-router): replay a stored special-error status over middleware''s, and as a 200 on a PPR RSC hit\n\nA stored 3xx/401/403/404 is the page''s own status, which middleware can''t\noverride on a fresh render either. With PPR, Next.js sends every RSC hit as\na 200 (`cachedData.status && (!isRSCRequest || !isRoutePPREnabled)`), so\nthe route''s PPR state now reaches the cached response builder.\n\n* fix(app-router): store a page''s special error only from its finished render, without the request''s query\n\n- The special-error document renders as a cache candidate, so a miss with a\n  query no longer stores that query in the document''s head.\n- A miss and a regeneration let the page''s Flight render finish while the\n  request context is alive, before the special-error response clears it, so\n  a late dynamic API use prevents the store and late fetch tags and cacheLife\n  reach it.\n- A skipped write still sends the render''s cache policy, a redirect(\"\")\n  keeps its empty location, and a response the boundary replaced isn''t\n  stored.\n- generateMetadata()''s special error isn''t stored: Next.js stores it with\n  the status its triggering request''s metadata streaming gives it, which a\n  regeneration, always blocking on metadata, can''t reproduce.\n- An intercepted RSC regeneration stores its special error, and an HTML\n  regeneration keeps the document''s own Link header.\n\n* fix(app-router): store a special error''s own Link and location, never middleware''s\n\n- Link provenance now records the renderer''s own value, so a miss and a\n  regeneration store exactly that part when middleware also sets a Link,\n  instead of dropping it.\n- A stored redirect keeps the location from its digest, basePath-adjusted,\n  not the response header middleware may have replaced for that request.\n- Replay applies the stored headers before the request''s middleware\n  headers, as a fresh special-error response does, so a middleware\n  Location replaces the stored one rather than joining it.\n- The lifecycle''s special-error render options type is no longer exported.\n\n* fix(app-router): recognise generateMetadata()''s special error after the shell rejects\n\nThe SSR shell rejects with its own copy of the error, decoded from the\nFlight digest, which loses the server-side generateMetadata() marker. So\nneither a miss nor a regeneration recognised it, and both stored the 404:\nan html-limited bot''s miss, and every regeneration, which blocks on\nmetadata. The RSC error tracker now keeps the special errors the render\nthrew by digest, and the shell''s error is generateMetadata()''s when only\ngenerateMetadata() threw that digest.\n\n* fix(app-router): send a Link''s segment prefetch of a stored notFound() page as a 200\n\nA page''s stored notFound(), forbidden() or unauthorized() is replayed with\nits status, so a Link''s prefetch of the page failed and the click loaded\nthe document. Next.js answers a Link''s segment prefetches of such a page\nwith 200s, so its router renders the page''s fallback without a reload. An\nRSC request with a segment prefetch header now receives the stored entry\nas a 200. A navigation without that prefetch, a full prefetch and a route\nthat doesn''t exist still receive their 404 and load the document, as in\nNext.js.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep the request context for the page''s render after generateMetadata()''s special error\n\nThe page''s Flight render goes on after generateMetadata()''s special error\nrejects the shell. Skipping the wait for it let the special-error response\nclear the request context while a sibling server component could still read\nheaders() or cookies(). Wait for that render as for the page''s own special\nerror. Its result still isn''t stored.\n\n* fix(app-router): never treat a special error a client component threw during SSR as generateMetadata()''s\n\nA shell rejected by a client component''s notFound() during SSR has the same\ndigest as generateMetadata()''s 404 from the RSC render, so when both threw,\nthe page''s 404 was taken for generateMetadata()''s and not stored. The\nnavigation functions now mark the errors they throw. React decodes an RSC\nrender''s error into a new Error without that marker, so a marked shell error\nwas thrown during SSR, where generateMetadata() never runs, and is the\npage''s.\n\n* fix(app-router): send a stored special error to a segment prefetch as a 200 behind a shared response stage\n\nWorkers Cache and the Response Store give a Link''s segment prefetch the\nnavigation''s cache identity, so the page''s dispatch never sees the\nprefetch header. A core entry a bypassed render stored, such as an\non-demand revalidation''s, was replayed to that prefetch as a 404, and the\nclick loaded the document.\n\nThe RSC replay of a stored 401, 403 or 404 now carries an internal marker\ninstead, and the request stage, which still sees the request''s headers,\nsends a marked response to a segment prefetch as a 200 and to anything\nelse with its status. It always strips the marker. Any other 404, such as\na dynamicParams = false miss, stays a 404, as in Next.js.\n\n* fix(app-router): treat only a prefetch''s segment header as a segment prefetch\n\nNext.js reads Next-Router-Segment-Prefetch only on a request that also\nsends Next-Router-Prefetch: 1, as vinext''s own classifiers and client do.\nA stored special error''s status now becomes a 200 only for such a\nrequest; a segment header alone keeps the 401, 403 or 404.\n\n* fix(app-router): carry a stored special error''s status in its marker and reserve the marker\n\nThe shared response stage applies a middleware status before the request\nstage reads the marker, so a navigation now gets the stored 401, 403 or 404\nback from the marker, as on a single-stage render. Middleware and config\nheaders can no longer set the marker, and a marker without a special\nerror''s status is ignored.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): seed a warmed page''s RSC entry with its document''s status and special-error marker","tree":{"sha":"5ce898be394438ea947808c9b0af1c6804b2ea91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/5ce898be394438ea947808c9b0af1c6804b2ea91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/3ce5cc3e31b24bb51c9fedee7483d4426b5317b7","verification":{"payload":"tree 5ce898be394438ea947808c9b0af1c6804b2ea91\nparent 1e36a808a74bedbf2ac47503c318032adec35efe\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361742 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361742 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): store a page''s special-error render in the ISR cache (#3702)\n\n* fix(app-router): store a page''s special error that escapes the shell in the ISR cache\n\n* test(app-router): cover ISR HITs for a page''s notFound() and redirect() document end to end\n\n* fix(app-router): replay a stored special-error status over middleware''s, and as a 200 on a PPR RSC hit\n\nA stored 3xx/401/403/404 is the page''s own status, which middleware can''t\noverride on a fresh render either. With PPR, Next.js sends every RSC hit as\na 200 (`cachedData.status && (!isRSCRequest || !isRoutePPREnabled)`), so\nthe route''s PPR state now reaches the cached response builder.\n\n* fix(app-router): store a page''s special error only from its finished render, without the request''s query\n\n- The special-error document renders as a cache candidate, so a miss with a\n  query no longer stores that query in the document''s head.\n- A miss and a regeneration let the page''s Flight render finish while the\n  request context is alive, before the special-error response clears it, so\n  a late dynamic API use prevents the store and late fetch tags and cacheLife\n  reach it.\n- A skipped write still sends the render''s cache policy, a redirect(\"\")\n  keeps its empty location, and a response the boundary replaced isn''t\n  stored.\n- generateMetadata()''s special error isn''t stored: Next.js stores it with\n  the status its triggering request''s metadata streaming gives it, which a\n  regeneration, always blocking on metadata, can''t reproduce.\n- An intercepted RSC regeneration stores its special error, and an HTML\n  regeneration keeps the document''s own Link header.\n\n* fix(app-router): store a special error''s own Link and location, never middleware''s\n\n- Link provenance now records the renderer''s own value, so a miss and a\n  regeneration store exactly that part when middleware also sets a Link,\n  instead of dropping it.\n- A stored redirect keeps the location from its digest, basePath-adjusted,\n  not the response header middleware may have replaced for that request.\n- Replay applies the stored headers before the request''s middleware\n  headers, as a fresh special-error response does, so a middleware\n  Location replaces the stored one rather than joining it.\n- The lifecycle''s special-error render options type is no longer exported.\n\n* fix(app-router): recognise generateMetadata()''s special error after the shell rejects\n\nThe SSR shell rejects with its own copy of the error, decoded from the\nFlight digest, which loses the server-side generateMetadata() marker. So\nneither a miss nor a regeneration recognised it, and both stored the 404:\nan html-limited bot''s miss, and every regeneration, which blocks on\nmetadata. The RSC error tracker now keeps the special errors the render\nthrew by digest, and the shell''s error is generateMetadata()''s when only\ngenerateMetadata() threw that digest.\n\n* fix(app-router): send a Link''s segment prefetch of a stored notFound() page as a 200\n\nA page''s stored notFound(), forbidden() or unauthorized() is replayed with\nits status, so a Link''s prefetch of the page failed and the click loaded\nthe document. Next.js answers a Link''s segment prefetches of such a page\nwith 200s, so its router renders the page''s fallback without a reload. An\nRSC request with a segment prefetch header now receives the stored entry\nas a 200. A navigation without that prefetch, a full prefetch and a route\nthat doesn''t exist still receive their 404 and load the document, as in\nNext.js.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep the request context for the page''s render after generateMetadata()''s special error\n\nThe page''s Flight render goes on after generateMetadata()''s special error\nrejects the shell. Skipping the wait for it let the special-error response\nclear the request context while a sibling server component could still read\nheaders() or cookies(). Wait for that render as for the page''s own special\nerror. Its result still isn''t stored.\n\n* fix(app-router): never treat a special error a client component threw during SSR as generateMetadata()''s\n\nA shell rejected by a client component''s notFound() during SSR has the same\ndigest as generateMetadata()''s 404 from the RSC render, so when both threw,\nthe page''s 404 was taken for generateMetadata()''s and not stored. The\nnavigation functions now mark the errors they throw. React decodes an RSC\nrender''s error into a new Error without that marker, so a marked shell error\nwas thrown during SSR, where generateMetadata() never runs, and is the\npage''s.\n\n* fix(app-router): send a stored special error to a segment prefetch as a 200 behind a shared response stage\n\nWorkers Cache and the Response Store give a Link''s segment prefetch the\nnavigation''s cache identity, so the page''s dispatch never sees the\nprefetch header. A core entry a bypassed render stored, such as an\non-demand revalidation''s, was replayed to that prefetch as a 404, and the\nclick loaded the document.\n\nThe RSC replay of a stored 401, 403 or 404 now carries an internal marker\ninstead, and the request stage, which still sees the request''s headers,\nsends a marked response to a segment prefetch as a 200 and to anything\nelse with its status. It always strips the marker. Any other 404, such as\na dynamicParams = false miss, stays a 404, as in Next.js.\n\n* fix(app-router): treat only a prefetch''s segment header as a segment prefetch\n\nNext.js reads Next-Router-Segment-Prefetch only on a request that also\nsends Next-Router-Prefetch: 1, as vinext''s own classifiers and client do.\nA stored special error''s status now becomes a 200 only for such a\nrequest; a segment header alone keeps the 401, 403 or 404.\n\n* fix(app-router): carry a stored special error''s status in its marker and reserve the marker\n\nThe shared response stage applies a middleware status before the request\nstage reads the marker, so a navigation now gets the stored 401, 403 or 404\nback from the marker, as on a single-stage render. Middleware and config\nheaders can no longer set the marker, and a marker without a special\nerror''s status is ignored.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): seed a warmed page''s RSC entry with its document''s status and special-error marker","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyEQQAKf00NDBcHoMOmANoYwa1+KQ\n9vm910Qcfl4TjkvQw24vscJ47e97Y8/uJSLdZiAL0Y0EKoqM6Rv7tqTlgxRV+Yvu\n4I2WZ48ze/pua4knXuvqG4j1nE3ihkQuOoaXYFp8uFkbE7xLZ4cPbkSZUUfsDt54\naR/FOXxQYwN6Jr9kqd8Ebwy5nlLuCjSjs6wrbM9ssIgQAD3VkaHlRey+JNL2cf+7\nIZldkaVfqbD3thfN5oacbJCyBj3GdU3Pduh0E4EOp8TPHu+acOYcC/tv7fehVlUG\nOYXA+X9Qfjzk6N6fl1fhUuiMXXADYqSHQ2UT6aB/KUYwq07nTA1Uz+h6CL0Sblaw\n+hdOeBKY6l3tTrilfvftgNEEoqbwqNVBTL2CGCXYAD87ELB6+g9IVXTD9hKeeCp1\n5Z9DMr6e5uX1iH00zrJ8KMKQm2gDRb2jjQqpAE2eFiWXhAQXwNhdk/aC9RkE1VTI\ns/vI5rnS5jGc/00VXeHhvOxt6VUYoXb2E5RmbdGk7zK714Xj8Smjcc0/S2FOevE6\nW4t7K77E1+jNj/Pk8wblSV8Umk6kH4e1NKaOkJifCiXPcpDE1gRKVB63xsmWajH7\nLsYRYmKuCIYOekxkgiwuUB2yAxmcsoxhZMcFjHuCXPYJnWa1xGRFKJCoOKdh9AvH\nqcEyR0TZDZFMs0NM/SjH\n=hF0B\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:29:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/3ce5cc3e31b24bb51c9fedee7483d4426b5317b7","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDNjZTVjYzNlMzFiMjRiYjUxYzlmZWRlZTc0ODNkNDQyNmI1MzE3Yjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/1e36a808a74bedbf2ac47503c318032adec35efe","sha":"1e36a808a74bedbf2ac47503c318032adec35efe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/1e36a808a74bedbf2ac47503c318032adec35efe"}],"sha":"3ce5cc3e31b24bb51c9fedee7483d4426b5317b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/3ce5cc3e31b24bb51c9fedee7483d4426b5317b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/1e36a808a74bedbf2ac47503c318032adec35efe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:01Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): stop refetching a page that redirects to itself; remove the leftover page probe (#3701)\n\n* fix(app-router): stop refetching a page that redirects to itself\n\nA page''s redirect() reaches the client in its RSC payload, and following\none that targets the current URL re-renders the same redirect forever.\nLoad the URL as a document instead, as vinext does for a streamed redirect\nto the current URL, so the browser stops the server''s redirect loop.\n\n* refactor(app-router): remove the page probe from the build-error path\n\nSince metadata resolves inside the Flight render, building the page\nelement no longer throws a metadata error, so probing the page to prefer\nits own special error has nothing left to arbitrate. Remove the probe\nand the helpers that only it used.\n\n* fix(app-router): stop following a segment redirect() to the current URL\n\nReloading the document still looped for a self-redirect below loading.js,\nand a hash on the current URL defeated the check. Only page and slot\nboundaries apply the guard, since they render inside the committed route.\n\n* test: update entry and probe tests for the removed page probe\n\n* fix(app-router): compare the hash exactly when detecting a self-redirect\n\nThe navigation planner refreshes the page for the exact current URL, hash\nincluded, and scrolls for any hash change, including removing it.","tree":{"sha":"ba42b7837667f26a076eccf524b188681ab1981f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/ba42b7837667f26a076eccf524b188681ab1981f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/1e36a808a74bedbf2ac47503c318032adec35efe","verification":{"payload":"tree ba42b7837667f26a076eccf524b188681ab1981f\nparent a25516592038e7a997d656c331b53c7c49ab2cea\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361741 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361741 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): stop refetching a page that redirects to itself; remove the leftover page probe (#3701)\n\n* fix(app-router): stop refetching a page that redirects to itself\n\nA page''s redirect() reaches the client in its RSC payload, and following\none that targets the current URL re-renders the same redirect forever.\nLoad the URL as a document instead, as vinext does for a streamed redirect\nto the current URL, so the browser stops the server''s redirect loop.\n\n* refactor(app-router): remove the page probe from the build-error path\n\nSince metadata resolves inside the Flight render, building the page\nelement no longer throws a metadata error, so probing the page to prefer\nits own special error has nothing left to arbitrate. Remove the probe\nand the helpers that only it used.\n\n* fix(app-router): stop following a segment redirect() to the current URL\n\nReloading the document still looped for a self-redirect below loading.js,\nand a hash on the current URL defeated the check. Only page and slot\nboundaries apply the guard, since they render inside the committed route.\n\n* test: update entry and probe tests for the removed page probe\n\n* fix(app-router): compare the hash exactly when detecting a self-redirect\n\nThe navigation planner refreshes the page for the exact current URL, hash\nincluded, and scrolls for any hash change, including removing it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB+QQAAF1IAfrsRP7O7HkNnLWpIZX\noqIXjuJCUFcEud6M6ncNPJnvmTOsVGKZbBDd4Ic2QF6v78tImYaki55Q8rKHu+Dk\nAwBEjnEphFPp13nOK/+UyjXJpEnwyw2F8xzQnOveHcrlYchjKrca2hi2FYbrbB/X\ngOhGujklCgzDWH8dE+q2YDXtGKU+Vm0cSYxtlAIVo37Ub/mD1XFe6vpPU5XqNOhx\nV0LL9JpRygpAHu2zlKlocoxXa5PnINIHNnIsuFn2NPltwjkXPOTCguV+lMG3y78B\ncF4RfC4+4xRWc/60DguozBlAhoHwPgFjYLhWJSTBjmEKhCWiVZRgW2I2Xj+zrjwJ\nu7OApOALi8vdhP8jCHRlJ4dSDsf0maEPks47pTTmmYS+bYY99XRY+wCjrwBhOfvy\nTXxXvGycF8ts9s0zvlpjVyFQDo1Jv9fQTH5Y/2qgHW8E4f5kUFfJzY8AjTjF61vp\nRIVIwy6xiWR8VMcKfBWGydM80vBnQZkCUteyFzBPjFsiek6q1PC6pRJU5rbicKRl\nNUbi9kZiVxGpOOxJirWw8dVxv2dWPjuagGrNILNgkkn0jIekryH2xiE7tv9n9S4E\ns57M5c1bnA/BB1v3Hatqt/5y9Bdp6GLYYqPAqgAQ/aTvfrCMG2U8SUVdNS865RvO\nvJSkLTY2cmVEH5xqWZEd\n=v1PK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:29:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/1e36a808a74bedbf2ac47503c318032adec35efe","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDFlMzZhODA4YTc0YmVkYmYyYWM0NzUwM2MzMTgwMzJhZGVjMzVlZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/a25516592038e7a997d656c331b53c7c49ab2cea","sha":"a25516592038e7a997d656c331b53c7c49ab2cea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/a25516592038e7a997d656c331b53c7c49ab2cea"}],"sha":"1e36a808a74bedbf2ac47503c318032adec35efe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/1e36a808a74bedbf2ac47503c318032adec35efe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/a25516592038e7a997d656c331b53c7c49ab2cea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:01Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(app-router): stop probing the page before RSC renders (#3699)\n\n* perf(app-router): stop probing the page before RSC renders\n\n#2226 removed the pre-render page probe for HTML requests. RSC requests\nstill ran the page, and awaited it, once outside React before rendering\nit again, so every client navigation paid for the page twice.\n\nRemove the RSC page probe. As in Next.js, a page''s redirect() and\nnotFound() now reach a client navigation as a digest in the Flight\npayload, which the client router already handles. Such a payload replaces\nthe page, so it is still not stored in the ISR cache unless a loading\nboundary streams it inside the page, as before.\n\n* fix(app-router): store a page''s redirect() or notFound() RSC render as Next.js does\n\nNext.js stores these renders in the ISR cache. Drop the guard that kept\nthem out, which also skipped renders whose special error came from below\nthe page, and stale probe comments.\n\n* test(app-router): expect a matched page''s notFound() in the RSC flight\n\nWithout the RSC page probe, /gated''s notFound() and its not-found\nboundary, including the boundary''s redirect(), travel in the Flight\npayload instead of a 404 boundary render.\n\n* fix(app-router): reset a page''s RedirectBoundary when the route changes\n\nA page''s redirect() now reaches the client in the RSC payload, as in\nNext.js, so the navigation to the page commits before the redirect runs.\nA javascript: redirect is refused by the router and never resets the\nshared page RedirectBoundary, leaving the next route blank. Next.js mounts\na boundary per segment; reset this one on the route reset key instead.\n\n* test(app-router): expect a page''s notFound() digest in dev RSC responses\n\nNext.js dev streams a page''s notFound() as a digest in a 200 flight.\n\n* fix(app-router): catch a slot page''s redirect() inside the slot\n\nSlot pages were probed before RSC renders, so their redirect() never\nreached the client. It now arrives in the payload; give each slot page a\nRedirectBoundary, as Next.js does per segment, so the route''s layouts stay\nmounted while the router follows it.\n\n* fix(app-router): discard a pending navigation on raw pushState/replaceState\n\nRSC responses now stream before the page finishes rendering, so a link\nnavigation can still be suspended in React when the app calls\nhistory.pushState for shallow routing. The navigation then committed over\nthe shallow URL later, and hooks kept reading its render snapshot instead\nof the new search params. Next.js dispatches ACTION_RESTORE for these\nwrites, which discards the pending navigation and keeps the current tree.\nDo the same: retire the navigation id, release its render snapshots,\nsettle its commit as no-commit, and restore the committed tree in a\ntransition so React drops the suspended one.\n\n* fix(app-router): narrow when raw history writes discard a navigation\n\nFollow-ups to discarding a pending navigation on raw pushState/replaceState:\n\n- Only discard when the write has a URL, as Next.js only dispatches\n  ACTION_RESTORE then. A state-only write keeps the navigation.\n- Clear the discarded navigation''s scroll intent, so the post-navigation\n  scroll fallback does not scroll to its hash or to the top of the page.\n- Stop discarding once a render of the navigation starts committing, and\n  write a committing navigation''s URL before any history write. Next.js\n  writes it from an insertion effect, so a destination layout effect''s\n  relative replaceState lands on the destination entry instead of being\n  overwritten by the navigation''s own URL update.","tree":{"sha":"9e984ce7d94a6369af1060ace9ab75283e2a1de0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/9e984ce7d94a6369af1060ace9ab75283e2a1de0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/a25516592038e7a997d656c331b53c7c49ab2cea","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e984ce7d94a6369af1060ace9ab75283e2a1de0\nparent fa7e8616e425e77b271525da1441c07bdfcf5d0c\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361741 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361741 +0100\n\nperf(app-router): stop probing the page before RSC renders (#3699)\n\n* perf(app-router): stop probing the page before RSC renders\n\n#2226 removed the pre-render page probe for HTML requests. RSC requests\nstill ran the page, and awaited it, once outside React before rendering\nit again, so every client navigation paid for the page twice.\n\nRemove the RSC page probe. As in Next.js, a page''s redirect() and\nnotFound() now reach a client navigation as a digest in the Flight\npayload, which the client router already handles. Such a payload replaces\nthe page, so it is still not stored in the ISR cache unless a loading\nboundary streams it inside the page, as before.\n\n* fix(app-router): store a page''s redirect() or notFound() RSC render as Next.js does\n\nNext.js stores these renders in the ISR cache. Drop the guard that kept\nthem out, which also skipped renders whose special error came from below\nthe page, and stale probe comments.\n\n* test(app-router): expect a matched page''s notFound() in the RSC flight\n\nWithout the RSC page probe, /gated''s notFound() and its not-found\nboundary, including the boundary''s redirect(), travel in the Flight\npayload instead of a 404 boundary render.\n\n* fix(app-router): reset a page''s RedirectBoundary when the route changes\n\nA page''s redirect() now reaches the client in the RSC payload, as in\nNext.js, so the navigation to the page commits before the redirect runs.\nA javascript: redirect is refused by the router and never resets the\nshared page RedirectBoundary, leaving the next route blank. Next.js mounts\na boundary per segment; reset this one on the route reset key instead.\n\n* test(app-router): expect a page''s notFound() digest in dev RSC responses\n\nNext.js dev streams a page''s notFound() as a digest in a 200 flight.\n\n* fix(app-router): catch a slot page''s redirect() inside the slot\n\nSlot pages were probed before RSC renders, so their redirect() never\nreached the client. It now arrives in the payload; give each slot page a\nRedirectBoundary, as Next.js does per segment, so the route''s layouts stay\nmounted while the router follows it.\n\n* fix(app-router): discard a pending navigation on raw pushState/replaceState\n\nRSC responses now stream before the page finishes rendering, so a link\nnavigation can still be suspended in React when the app calls\nhistory.pushState for shallow routing. The navigation then committed over\nthe shallow URL later, and hooks kept reading its render snapshot instead\nof the new search params. Next.js dispatches ACTION_RESTORE for these\nwrites, which discards the pending navigation and keeps the current tree.\nDo the same: retire the navigation id, release its render snapshots,\nsettle its commit as no-commit, and restore the committed tree in a\ntransition so React drops the suspended one.\n\n* fix(app-router): narrow when raw history writes discard a navigation\n\nFollow-ups to discarding a pending navigation on raw pushState/replaceState:\n\n- Only discard when the write has a URL, as Next.js only dispatches\n  ACTION_RESTORE then. A state-only write keeps the navigation.\n- Clear the discarded navigation''s scroll intent, so the post-navigation\n  scroll fallback does not scroll to its hash or to the top of the page.\n- Stop discarding once a render of the navigation starts committing, and\n  write a committing navigation''s URL before any history write. Next.js\n  writes it from an insertion effect, so a destination layout effect''s\n  relative replaceState lands on the destination entry instead of being\n  overwritten by the navigation''s own URL update.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbbsQAELLkT1bYJIEuKnHgIEXjcs8\nFrmHtP1mqhhPrLan/uidiyXwA5pG6GTUWiv8W5qEpKJ3h9QgQYGdt5MG4B1J5W/R\nHDzlmvuhPHsrsPlsRXOhX7g8+sZyhcJ+75h/VaSEGs+ob3sS0ZYG1Qp7neDlKdye\n76pGGz/neB5IFgT2TZjfxhc6OoY9sFBKWVePgSQTmFHhm46rh2/roS9F2RGcP/5A\nxj44MDqDiL2I6b+ZYl6A7B1e1uy5yzApIAd8AcCOfhp6CW1FV3lJtP13DVHz47e4\nSov9CHLDRuymOGAV83Tw8xVo9vJw22nD0JBc5jJT2IOr67XewKicQixxk28v6VH+\nwUC7FRhas1QgyaY8v5mhF+r3MjfwzAD8ZP18u/vlqryA4UtrpgGGSqPLDwixRdSM\ntZmvlUzoShPyF0akERBxv/xBl3cjWge8xzOdYp/TqLC2GXZm40ToLemq21iMufbd\niY8PKeTnATRt/0LUCqQ3H0VKpCE3k70AzBgyTBt0kAbgGTBgflHugegqjNrQ4OUX\nLe9TBWYh6y/vIRzY279zlknOEIck4UHIVblXhI99d7zSYC1ldjSz0I6HB6nc8/Yb\nLeQ2rbQOt5vNE38BJ4jKDm0V5DGat9MssCAJRv54psIxDi1gAFxglBA5Phza9H8y\njFJSSLjIwrWclILG4kg7\n=cke4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T08:29:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/a25516592038e7a997d656c331b53c7c49ab2cea","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGEyNTUxNjU5MjAzOGU3YTk5N2Q2NTZjMzMxYjUzYzdjNDlhYjJjZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/fa7e8616e425e77b271525da1441c07bdfcf5d0c","sha":"fa7e8616e425e77b271525da1441c07bdfcf5d0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/fa7e8616e425e77b271525da1441c07bdfcf5d0c"}],"sha":"a25516592038e7a997d656c331b53c7c49ab2cea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/a25516592038e7a997d656c331b53c7c49ab2cea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/fa7e8616e425e77b271525da1441c07bdfcf5d0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:01Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T08:29:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): let only the render decide whether a page is dynamic (#3698)\n\n* fix(app-router): let only the render decide whether a page is dynamic\n\nThe pre-render probe calls layouts and the page outside React''s render,\nwhere React cache() has no request scope. A value a layout stores through\ncache() (next-intl''s setRequestLocale) is missing there, so a component\nfalls back to headers() and the probe marked the whole route dynamic: no\nprerender, no-store responses.\n\nNext.js has no probe; its render alone classifies the page, and vinext''s\nrender runs the probed layouts and page again. Run the probe in a detached\ndynamic-usage scope, and count its usage only when its special-error\nresponse replaces the render.\n\nFixes #3671\n\n* fix(app-router): rerun cacheForRequest factories after a detached probe\n\nThe probe shared the request''s cacheForRequest() store with the render,\nso a factory that read cookies() or headers() during a layout probe handed\nits value to the render without marking it dynamic, and the render could\nbe stored. Give the detached probe its own store.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep a detached probe''s fetch observations out of the request\n\nThe page probe shared the request''s fetch observation and tag\ncontainers, so a fetch only the probe made could classify the render or\ntag its ISR entry. Give the detached probe its own, as runLayoutProbe\nalready does.\n\n* test(cloudflare): expect the pending policy on an RSC render that turns dynamic after headers\n\nThe page probe no longer marks the request dynamic before the render, so\nan RSC response whose page reads cookies() after awaiting params streams\nwith the pending policy. It is still never stored.","tree":{"sha":"4133f346dac67700159e9ac1f5246b8863fd36d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/4133f346dac67700159e9ac1f5246b8863fd36d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/fa7e8616e425e77b271525da1441c07bdfcf5d0c","verification":{"payload":"tree 4133f346dac67700159e9ac1f5246b8863fd36d8\nparent fc06b50345838ff94fdc54522ae078731b7cef91\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791361741 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791361741 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): let only the render decide whether a page is dynamic (#3698)\n\n* fix(app-router): let only the render decide whether a page is dynamic\n\nThe pre-render probe calls layouts and the page outside React''s render,\nwhere React cache() has no request scope. A value a layout stores through\ncache() (next-intl''s setRequestLocale) is missing there, so a component\nfalls back to headers() and the probe marked the whole route dynamic: no\nprerender, no-store responses.\n\nNext.js has no probe; its render alone classifies the page, and vinext''s\nrender runs the probed layouts and page again. Run the probe in a detached\ndynamic-usage scope, and count its usage only when its special-error\nresponse replaces the render.\n\nFixes #3671\n\n* fix(app-router): rerun cacheForRequest factories after a detached probe\n\nThe probe shared the request''s cacheForRequest() store with the render,\nso a factory that read cookies() or headers() during a layout probe handed\nits value to the render without marking it dynamic, and the render could\nbe stored. Give the detached probe its own store.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep a detached probe''s fetch observations out of the request\n\nThe page probe shared the request''s fetch observation and tag\ncontainers, so a fetch only the probe made could classify the render or\ntag its ISR entry. Give the detached probe its own, as runLayoutProbe\nalready does.\n\n* test(cloudflare): expect the pending policy on an RSC render that turns dynamic after headers\n\nThe page probe no longer marks the request dynamic before the render, so\nan RSC response whose page reads cookies() after awaiting params streams\nwith the pending policy. It is still never stored.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxgLNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAh4cQAG1QFWcEL5KdGAokt96Mf0pC\nxU7VGIjUeFVfPLHaZbHjanCoixP1juh6pllmqzlDJPVWB6kkV2VQBbBzU61SyklM\n08PkZ2KhILlTZk7QDIz+0mjllMdfG5KLEtwJCXBYY/ikksH1mMKeTZU4UltIHLpS\nMCCC67BKQsihi72pxaFesMW78AZh+SHAJ7wa3QaSO/fek+1v4ICTUUgSBOpnidjQ\nusxe1Dd2Vh4FrSKKdWiMjjGxOr06rPn8RgeoyFFzs1bdLbJvzm+9bTVJ7NL+L6Bj\n9+owzI+RjRqp+72NwKq0UeCQ0phbyVdHdTUjstq8BjAJg6LFDSdX7wFw1y8B/kpn\n/DYL9jTlVinmu98O4otnqvWBI9uRNpEIXR5