ubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/fc06b50345838ff94fdc54522ae078731b7cef91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:36:42Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:36:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dev): keep the dev server alive when a request body is cancelled (#3726)\n\nsrvx builds dev request bodies with Node''s Readable.toWeb(). Its pull()\nresumes the IncomingMessage on nextTick; if the body is cancelled before\nthat tick, flow() still emits buffered chunks and the adapter''s onData\nthrows ERR_INVALID_STATE (\"Controller is already closed\") inside the\nnextTick callback, killing the dev server. Rejecting an oversized Server\nAction hits this window, which made the app-router E2E shard flaky.\n\nNode main already ignores data after cancel in onData; absorb exactly that\nerror in the existing process backstop.","tree":{"sha":"59d0f87067c8d51e191b25d4ca7ccd62a6899fd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/59d0f87067c8d51e191b25d4ca7ccd62a6899fd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/fc06b50345838ff94fdc54522ae078731b7cef91","verification":{"payload":"tree 59d0f87067c8d51e191b25d4ca7ccd62a6899fd5\nparent 4c333eed23d4d5533f9ed440837384074cf0f802\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791319002 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791319002 +0100\n\nfix(dev): keep the dev server alive when a request body is cancelled (#3726)\n\nsrvx builds dev request bodies with Node''s Readable.toWeb(). Its pull()\nresumes the IncomingMessage on nextTick; if the body is cancelled before\nthat tick, flow() still emits buffered chunks and the adapter''s onData\nthrows ERR_INVALID_STATE (\"Controller is already closed\") inside the\nnextTick callback, killing the dev server. Rejecting an oversized Server\nAction hits this window, which made the app-router E2E shard flaky.\n\nNode main already ignores data after cancel in onData; absorb exactly that\nerror in the existing process backstop.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxVvaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk80QAFPMv460PowXtr50uuM9dUEB\nN/71e6A03ccLDKu3XaSNTZPpOftb7jnRmgJIQlpCPiq3pel2OOQbSsUy/ghag2UA\nPQ7En7SL+gEeuQ7njjxLguHWs/yoo+psBtAmBjikTyw4dCrWyAm1+1wspJCZk1RK\n7aEN4/7cE3nxvmnH6CD9Py64zmyW8W85m3zk2J3AOAF6YZeTNriKTIwZF/7GS3Ro\nNW8WQ9bzZWl5d08HPKfZAA9dsF+1CSI8wv4FT4y4nxGQC03Ctak4Zj7dvGwoxma0\nxNzaGtvdWuJzPCIAMZ27lp9bOVgQBz/MLHe8xaJHaxeX6KBwajHNdCgihePc50+x\nfFgi9iDqIIeL1GL/+UbLoJNcs+NxTPU167oM1NlLWbbXWlkDBNzyp0QH3kgL6xpi\nGoULg4ZzNua8Yi5lJuaaawa7EdXPOsyvM6ys6YhrrOjumt+mOzVvjb/Wm4Xb9+xN\nyMY6ci2Ftjjb+GM/qw0efpCc51Df2C4aTIFLjUKsdBe3Lsd5cUJssaQh27V7Dph9\nJrXFLTO0elTUh9v0Hx/sS9AHS8MNCOTEAGZ6tOUKxoDy96tTic8YyR8MMTTMe00x\n8O6Bz6qHiGVUyl10cGvT1XLwHhLBchxoHK58VjSPZG9Dl4WEVHK0rk+0fnnDUrtx\ntvWLk/ifL3MRw8cwNdxx\n=omZs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:36:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/fc06b50345838ff94fdc54522ae078731b7cef91","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGZjMDZiNTAzNDU4MzhmZjk0ZmRjNTQ1MjJhZTA3ODczMWI3Y2VmOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/4c333eed23d4d5533f9ed440837384074cf0f802","sha":"4c333eed23d4d5533f9ed440837384074cf0f802","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/4c333eed23d4d5533f9ed440837384074cf0f802"}],"sha":"fc06b50345838ff94fdc54522ae078731b7cef91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/fc06b50345838ff94fdc54522ae078731b7cef91"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/4c333eed23d4d5533f9ed440837384074cf0f802/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:35:48Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:35:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(use-cache): serve stale entries and regenerate them in the background (#3713)\n\n* fix(use-cache): serve stale entries and regenerate them in the background\n\nA dynamic render recomputed a stale ''use cache'' entry before responding.\nLike Next.js, serve the stale value and regenerate it in the background,\nwithout propagating that regeneration''s cache life or tags into the\nrequest. ISR regeneration and prerendering still regenerate it first.\n\n* fix(use-cache): keep a background regeneration''s fetch tags out of the request\n\n* fix(use-cache): regenerate stale entries first while prerendering and keep nested stale serving in the background","tree":{"sha":"df64d9f8fa32accd17fd0e6b0328213ee11fd1ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/df64d9f8fa32accd17fd0e6b0328213ee11fd1ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/4c333eed23d4d5533f9ed440837384074cf0f802","verification":{"payload":"tree df64d9f8fa32accd17fd0e6b0328213ee11fd1ff\nparent 75f45a98bcfb5720665e538d485339407e1816df\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791318948 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791318948 +0100\n\nfix(use-cache): serve stale entries and regenerate them in the background (#3713)\n\n* fix(use-cache): serve stale entries and regenerate them in the background\n\nA dynamic render recomputed a stale ''use cache'' entry before responding.\nLike Next.js, serve the stale value and regenerate it in the background,\nwithout propagating that regeneration''s cache life or tags into the\nrequest. ISR regeneration and prerendering still regenerate it first.\n\n* fix(use-cache): keep a background regeneration''s fetch tags out of the request\n\n* fix(use-cache): regenerate stale entries first while prerendering and keep nested stale serving in the background","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxVukCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt1AQAC4OZ/rXE/Fhl20qxtkHtfR4\nzHkxhxrJfYxMClBD3lI/kulQHGoOYqDTQb41KVYuGKVtc4z/mWW4dQNejLyS3R1s\nzVmDzbIdKcaJZ7bFw3js6tmHJ5dcp9FUojj2uvUI6tkEE7bZcJYgMPg8tuS6Nmql\nUqdt4JAl3qoEAqRcTUiGZbgLgR5vbmZjHnA92G7/i/w5m6f5J3jRx0dosSaII0ZL\nqQYDA5IpBB3xxhu4dIPySX/fjFda5LvyY9N0s6F1zyn17hpJ8TjZEqCQruYE+1EM\n/Jrgg7y5DOJ2s4sSy77xcHt0nWAHNwSGV87K9XsP0o2lFcQmWlLs288XvaY4GGdf\nSXEu3KJ7HXODeX2lYsVcZBuGsBQVcoVcNpK3vm0KMMzdufQ3jjl/CSXNlgrPk2jF\n8qItxW8l61K8lDQvQtmbHEOXa9B/rIG2yt6Q+6cr/WmJAbHqxEkCvGpQp06tZxHf\nCx0IpDDkv5uHPWL9M2k3ts8+treQBoGtMk78J1KfNqkVxChCGQB++AAZsCFlZc1D\nTLcxCEF8EKzi4DOiy+MrbZB2cmz+04wtkFaYK2E75N9PvmudQA80weaSu6XM/7xz\njB8wsn93vua206EO9vNLtOyAJlttXngFcGsR9rECM731g9Gsp29/HjFSPr3IWZTK\nDi0qGjFYpK6lIVlxm9GW\n=ibAl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:35:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/4c333eed23d4d5533f9ed440837384074cf0f802","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDRjMzMzZWVkMjNkNGQ1NTMzZjllZDQ0MDgzNzM4NDA3NGNmMGY4MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/75f45a98bcfb5720665e538d485339407e1816df","sha":"75f45a98bcfb5720665e538d485339407e1816df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/75f45a98bcfb5720665e538d485339407e1816df"}],"sha":"4c333eed23d4d5533f9ed440837384074cf0f802","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/4c333eed23d4d5533f9ed440837384074cf0f802"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111243485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedElBanna80","id":111243485,"login":"AhmedElBanna80","node_id":"U_kgDOBqFw3Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/75f45a98bcfb5720665e538d485339407e1816df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:02:25Z","email":"111243485+AhmedElBanna80@users.noreply.github.com","name":"AhmedElBanna80"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T15:02:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(config): pass the real defaultConfig to function-form next.config (#3687)\n\n* fix(config): pass the real pageExtensions default into function-form configs\n\nA next.config.js/.ts exported as a function receives (phase, { defaultConfig })\nper the Next.js config API. vinext always passed an empty object, so a config\nlike the one in Next''s own custom-page-extension compat fixture --\n\n  module.exports = (phase, { defaultConfig }) => ({\n    pageExtensions: [...defaultConfig.pageExtensions, ''page.js''],\n  })\n\n-- throws \"defaultConfig.pageExtensions is not iterable\" at build time.\n\nPass defaultConfig.pageExtensions (vinext''s own DEFAULT_PAGE_EXTENSIONS,\nmatching Next''s config-shared.js defaultConfig.pageExtensions) at both call\nsites: the direct function-config path in resolveConfigValue, and the\ngenerated virtual-module loader used for TS config files.\n\n* test(config): cover the function-form defaultConfig.pageExtensions fix\n\nMutation-proved: both assertions fail with the pre-fix defaultConfig: {}\n(\"defaultConfig.pageExtensions is not iterable\" for the CJS case, a wrong\narray for the TS case) and pass with the fix.\n\n* test(config): exercise function-form defaultConfig through a real fixture\n\nSwitch the app-route-file-collision fixture''s next.config.mjs to the\nfunction form used by Next.js''s custom-page-extension e2e fixture\n(`[...defaultConfig.pageExtensions, \"md\", \"mdx\"]`), so the existing\ndev-server suite covers the virtual-module loader path end to end. Share\none createFunctionConfigDefaults() helper between both call sites so the\ndirect and generated-module paths cannot drift.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"dd96d2e43e3a331bbb8b2d6a6104e5d0f3490b6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/dd96d2e43e3a331bbb8b2d6a6104e5d0f3490b6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/75f45a98bcfb5720665e538d485339407e1816df","verification":{"payload":"tree dd96d2e43e3a331bbb8b2d6a6104e5d0f3490b6d\nparent 8abf2ce34ddd6eeb07e66c19b3246caa47abc585\nauthor AhmedElBanna80 <111243485+AhmedElBanna80@users.noreply.github.com> 1791298945 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791298945 +0100\n\nfix(config): pass the real defaultConfig to function-form next.config (#3687)\n\n* fix(config): pass the real pageExtensions default into function-form configs\n\nA next.config.js/.ts exported as a function receives (phase, { defaultConfig })\nper the Next.js config API. vinext always passed an empty object, so a config\nlike the one in Next''s own custom-page-extension compat fixture --\n\n  module.exports = (phase, { defaultConfig }) => ({\n    pageExtensions: [...defaultConfig.pageExtensions, ''page.js''],\n  })\n\n-- throws \"defaultConfig.pageExtensions is not iterable\" at build time.\n\nPass defaultConfig.pageExtensions (vinext''s own DEFAULT_PAGE_EXTENSIONS,\nmatching Next''s config-shared.js defaultConfig.pageExtensions) at both call\nsites: the direct function-config path in resolveConfigValue, and the\ngenerated virtual-module loader used for TS config files.\n\n* test(config): cover the function-form defaultConfig.pageExtensions fix\n\nMutation-proved: both assertions fail with the pre-fix defaultConfig: {}\n(\"defaultConfig.pageExtensions is not iterable\" for the CJS case, a wrong\narray for the TS case) and pass with the fix.\n\n* test(config): exercise function-form defaultConfig through a real fixture\n\nSwitch the app-route-file-collision fixture''s next.config.mjs to the\nfunction form used by Next.js''s custom-page-extension e2e fixture\n(`[...defaultConfig.pageExtensions, \"md\", \"mdx\"]`), so the existing\ndev-server suite covers the virtual-module loader path end to end. Share\none createFunctionConfigDefaults() helper between both call sites so the\ndirect and generated-module paths cannot drift.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQ2BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO4QQAKD/mdtKoFEKDorlrWEOviln\naZ+g2suQcvMK0Qsb+ulyB5+J3VSpJclMdwos7UsuZNxck2cP3TqMkl+X72o/+E7C\nu3Lb5dx61oNJoxe6gZMiox3mcNXE0SaxYSntjkrDRUcrk9PvsETsQ3qSOnmfQ1hN\nx2uaQgzzNtL1Qc9eYF13GlKpjtAkuPMQmDhbBFzFrKtN21JlYwZ+Cgw6xYBgA4So\nQxRseFNW4mgm3VXeoTTg+7o0Sm3eZ5gSla6na6Exuz7tAIr6wbOoYHnLpuMUh54e\nzT+LY+sERp63vYCpsEj8W/Q6abY5dC8NVqgrmno5jsQHQ5rDvsXSf2I4E8mcf8M0\nCO6dodePaBicQgHJBxyZcuqD69zBeLE8hH6+pYiwd1OcQ95npyiuiH9ORFE66WA5\nXVlJXW8fs6v3J8lPiIpzpjEH6I8rzLSDyO7ie+u7dAsFp5hIMZn/xBRO/o+lcAa9\ncdsJszIZXPJUTpLyGh6bY5qDldOdBKbvepnSOWGKSYtgI5B+YsrSOVYqrB3GzThk\nsulIEIA4pe3lQTtg9lyIrUEjr9gZceN93PT7nlH61spUCZRG7iq8TACVGTxI4bGV\nXlo81u3HtgWlIiL8t/H4xO2dv8kig/I8tm2K7G5FjFwGW8Cy4/i+IyxtX7Rh2A/R\np7EMCLxQ55ybscSHLUQH\n=6jzP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T15:02:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/75f45a98bcfb5720665e538d485339407e1816df","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDc1ZjQ1YTk4YmNmYjU3MjA2NjVlNTM4ZDQ4NTMzOTQwN2UxODE2ZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/8abf2ce34ddd6eeb07e66c19b3246caa47abc585","sha":"8abf2ce34ddd6eeb07e66c19b3246caa47abc585","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/8abf2ce34ddd6eeb07e66c19b3246caa47abc585"}],"sha":"75f45a98bcfb5720665e538d485339407e1816df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/75f45a98bcfb5720665e538d485339407e1816df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/111243485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/AhmedElBanna80","id":111243485,"login":"AhmedElBanna80","node_id":"U_kgDOBqFw3Q","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AhmedElBanna80","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/8abf2ce34ddd6eeb07e66c19b3246caa47abc585/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:56:35Z","email":"111243485+AhmedElBanna80@users.noreply.github.com","name":"AhmedElBanna80"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:56:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(css): derive drafts.customMedia from lightningCssFeatures.include (#3681)\n\n* fix(css): derive drafts.customMedia from lightningCssFeatures.include\n\nexperimental.lightningCssFeatures.include/exclude was forwarded to\nlightningcss''s transform options, but @custom-media is draft CSS syntax\ngated behind lightningcss''s own drafts.customMedia parser flag — a\nseparate axis from the include/exclude transform mask. Without it,\n@custom-media failed to parse at all.\n\nNext.js derives drafts.customMedia from the same include list\n(packages/next/src/build/webpack/loaders/lightningcss-loader/src/loader.ts):\nwhen custom-media-queries is included, drafts.customMedia is turned on too.\nPort that derivation so vinext matches.\n\nAdds a regression test mirroring Next.js''s\ntest/e2e/app-dir/experimental-lightningcss-features custom-media-queries\ncase.\n\n* fix(css): subtract exclude before deriving drafts.customMedia\n\nNext.js computes the include mask as include & ~exclude before checking\ncustom-media-queries, so excluding the feature keeps the draft parser\noff. Match that, and fold the custom-media rule into the shared\nlightningcss test fixture with a build helper.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"87d548685ca017d3072d571db9e69f3275f0790e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/87d548685ca017d3072d571db9e69f3275f0790e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/8abf2ce34ddd6eeb07e66c19b3246caa47abc585","verification":{"payload":"tree 87d548685ca017d3072d571db9e69f3275f0790e\nparent d235c923ab045e15d3ccb082e3107b1dbd9462ce\nauthor AhmedElBanna80 <111243485+AhmedElBanna80@users.noreply.github.com> 1791298595 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791298595 +0100\n\nfix(css): derive drafts.customMedia from lightningCssFeatures.include (#3681)\n\n* fix(css): derive drafts.customMedia from lightningCssFeatures.include\n\nexperimental.lightningCssFeatures.include/exclude was forwarded to\nlightningcss''s transform options, but @custom-media is draft CSS syntax\ngated behind lightningcss''s own drafts.customMedia parser flag — a\nseparate axis from the include/exclude transform mask. Without it,\n@custom-media failed to parse at all.\n\nNext.js derives drafts.customMedia from the same include list\n(packages/next/src/build/webpack/loaders/lightningcss-loader/src/loader.ts):\nwhen custom-media-queries is included, drafts.customMedia is turned on too.\nPort that derivation so vinext matches.\n\nAdds a regression test mirroring Next.js''s\ntest/e2e/app-dir/experimental-lightningcss-features custom-media-queries\ncase.\n\n* fix(css): subtract exclude before deriving drafts.customMedia\n\nNext.js computes the include mask as include & ~exclude before checking\ncustom-media-queries, so excluding the feature keeps the draft parser\noff. Match that, and fold the custom-media rule into the shared\nlightningcss test fixture with a build helper.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQwjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABYUQAF0A0ayRuoGrmCYfOiYM+DMN\npHPUDllWcMEZyrFkJysbOZSgDWMNBlQsGZj2pNqoqNQrx6XVTRkTKrzNigjMIdcu\nvSQCgbG43+Dd+jhsD37phMs/qBBL5DRIJoZgEjxnLeu+cFcpiZRNGKBiI1pHbq3i\n5IPvecDJFgo/sckZCkyRh1648SPfBGRM8SeWfDBbKmA1tO4zTkmN96SMGtzCbSuS\nC0K4oM5jYwzomf8yFWxeuUlkgLUlmZuNBc32VYl5S+Cfav5ezAiIVCmtZe+coVQB\nv03Ykok4QCbcu2TBpaaHGhw09Gw/jYc/WOX0MfVjdMs1iqqs4o8sMSRmo3byOvgN\n4gcrH9i7+W6AXf+FYpBmnvO/xHuTZOYZAQFw5DQwGLIUp8yjO+WIF06vUz6U/JBS\nquP4NN9mlw9hMgO4Hh8h5VyUnnb7lygtVdcnIeLVE+MhaX3pRc/HysrTLg6rpylz\n+8OA2Igo1nQ7iENhLsppeaBbOxpCYvMZPJ0zuhcsZGkhjJW9quAYfeQJoYc2BfB+\nJSHPI6mpN2F74zKVePEsnJjrkmbKPuxW0/vBt0vm0uRzjAdyKFU