s","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/418cf4cdb4f8fc6c3fcfd9a6b698de1cf62d7262","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDQxOGNmNGNkYjRmOGZjNmMzZmNmZDlhNmI2OThkZTFjZjYyZDcyNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/21d4c026c88ad85e1a76df2bc96ce369a79553dc","sha":"21d4c026c88ad85e1a76df2bc96ce369a79553dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/21d4c026c88ad85e1a76df2bc96ce369a79553dc"}],"sha":"418cf4cdb4f8fc6c3fcfd9a6b698de1cf62d7262","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/418cf4cdb4f8fc6c3fcfd9a6b698de1cf62d7262"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/21d4c026c88ad85e1a76df2bc96ce369a79553dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T09:15:21Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T09:15:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(response-store): mark tag invalidations stale instead of regenerating them (#3712)\n\n* feat(response-store): mark tag invalidations stale instead of regenerating them\n\nAdd `invalidate({ tags, pathPrefixes, expire })` to the Response Store. It\nmarks matching entries stale without regenerating them: reads keep serving\nthem through their stale-while-revalidate window, capped at `expire`, and\nthe next read regenerates them like any stale entry.\n\nEach match moves to a new revision with its freshness ended, and its R2\nobject is rewritten as a stale copy through the existing durable tombstone\nqueue, so writes reserved before the invalidation cannot publish over it.\nWorkers Cache invalidates the edge responses of entries with a revalidator\nand purges the others, whose next read then reports `BLOB-STALE`.\n\nThe vinext data adapter now calls `invalidate()` for `revalidateTag(tag,\nprofile)`, as Next.js marks those tags stale rather than recomputing every\nentry, and revalidates non-replayable entries the Store reports stale.\n`revalidatePath` and expired tags still purge.\n\n* fix(response-store): keep repeated invalidations stale and persist tag expire deadlines\n\n- Carry an undrained invalidation''s R2 source revision forward, and accept\n  a stale copy of it in R2, so back-to-back invalidations no longer\n  tombstone the entry.\n- Keep a pending purge''s hard edge purge when an invalidation replaces it,\n  and purge rather than invalidate the edge whenever R2 ends up tombstoned,\n  including on a retried drain.\n- Persist each tag''s `expire` deadline and cap publications before it, as\n  Next.js expires entries written before the deadline.\n- Stream the R2 body into the stale rewrite instead of buffering it.\n- Store adapter entries without a revalidator with `expiryBehavior: \"miss\"`.\n- Reject a non-number `expire`.\n\n* fix(response-store): fence a first write a path invalidation matches and report recorded tags\n\nA path-only invalidation now advances the revision of matching keys whose\nfirst write is still in flight, as purge does, so that write cannot publish\nfresh. A tag invalidation reports a backing-store update even without\nmatches, since it records the tags'' fence and expire deadline.\n\n* test(response-store): expect stale-then-regenerate after revalidateTag and mock invalidate\n\n* test(response-store): wait for stored bodies and use a long-lived fixture for lazy tag revalidation\n\n* test(response-store): verify a recorded tag deadline expires a later entry","tree":{"sha":"9f06ce98b3584f041d0df6aefecd1c2883a2e577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/9f06ce98b3584f041d0df6aefecd1c2883a2e577"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/21d4c026c88ad85e1a76df2bc96ce369a79553dc","verification":{"payload":"tree 9f06ce98b3584f041d0df6aefecd1c2883a2e577\nparent fff70818efac65c3117b1c1d8787d7ec1aea3802\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791278121 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791278121 +0100\n\nfeat(response-store): mark tag invalidations stale instead of regenerating them (#3712)\n\n* feat(response-store): mark tag invalidations stale instead of regenerating them\n\nAdd `invalidate({ tags, pathPrefixes, expire })` to the Response Store. It\nmarks matching entries stale without regenerating them: reads keep serving\nthem through their stale-while-revalidate window, capped at `expire`, and\nthe next read regenerates them like any stale entry.\n\nEach match moves to a new revision with its freshness ended, and its R2\nobject is rewritten as a stale copy through the existing durable tombstone\nqueue, so writes reserved before the invalidation cannot publish over it.\nWorkers Cache invalidates the edge responses of entries with a revalidator\nand purges the others, whose next read then reports `BLOB-STALE`.\n\nThe vinext data adapter now calls `invalidate()` for `revalidateTag(tag,\nprofile)`, as Next.js marks those tags stale rather than recomputing every\nentry, and revalidates non-replayable entries the Store reports stale.\n`revalidatePath` and expired tags still purge.\n\n* fix(response-store): keep repeated invalidations stale and persist tag expire deadlines\n\n- Carry an undrained invalidation''s R2 source revision forward, and accept\n  a stale copy of it in R2, so back-to-back invalidations no longer\n  tombstone the entry.\n- Keep a pending purge''s hard edge purge when an invalidation replaces it,\n  and purge rather than invalidate the edge whenever R2 ends up tombstoned,\n  including on a retried drain.\n- Persist each tag''s `expire` deadline and cap publications before it, as\n  Next.js expires entries written before the deadline.\n- Stream the R2 body into the stale rewrite instead of buffering it.\n- Store adapter entries without a revalidator with `expiryBehavior: \"miss\"`.\n- Reject a non-number `expire`.\n\n* fix(response-store): fence a first write a path invalidation matches and report recorded tags\n\nA path-only invalidation now advances the revision of matching keys whose\nfirst write is still in flight, as purge does, so that write cannot publish\nfresh. A tag invalidation reports a backing-store update even without\nmatches, since it records the tags'' fence and expire deadline.\n\n* test(response-store): expect stale-then-regenerate after revalidateTag and mock invalidate\n\n* test(response-store): wait for stored bodies and use a long-lived fixture for lazy tag revalidation\n\n* test(response-store): verify a recorded tag deadline expires a later entry","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxLwpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdWwQAGqAi/RkU9Zm375YnhAgZTfC\nMJuZaD1fuE45l+GU6L5xpytSCQb2l/HSkxIgy6J43D6UCKQVqFg/7WQ51cIfs5vK\nBq/bdWHwzEiWGTB3jpHZ+8wBhfPu6ms+wkAOjr9+Covo3vU26K4zpS9oN4wIb7Jb\ndboHIrv2rjFYqH8ZLFDkDJZ74sUcSRz+2D1ssDJB00w6SwP9ScI/7igW+bwFPbFJ\ni8iuPt2jAeo40H2VhDZoSxpZKOPAtroCxlxL47k4zRIJBNKVTgmOeiEISgwriymd\nVk5EuKrtgtty2u/uYbwhmUe5MugrnZIPH+9xaDU+OCia64hfFSQI1a/YYEKGIwCG\nSvNMEpSdFq/MbfqNCMthBmEzqjhClhhUwBWMnFuEFwS/+idTgqi2yZV/Y+UqVn/N\niKuI4YHhn0vBq0nW5yE/FEIEYk0KVTkLpP1oMLO3skHzkFzRNMLJ4LjwSrO2ktp8\npuhhI1Z4QvHAZfYm3LO0C5klw5df3rxh5kmPZ1iEWtAk64Kqkt13Sj/ceF80hErR\nUoWfKtg3tTnvTIt8gzyJZBBQMqE0btTSysEt0nuSoQMPNLvMm6qlnl8jhE4o92eq\nKz8aVnoxyd1flqBmFb+k110cJ70WqCsTWbux7tYPjwkPc11VGjF0rp+9n1NnNHRe\nZe6GrqNib/qk+6iuuCt+\n=B4nv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T09:15:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/21d4c026c88ad85e1a76df2bc96ce369a79553dc","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDIxZDRjMDI2Yzg4YWQ4NWUxYTc2ZGYyYmM5NmNlMzY5YTc5NTUzZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/fff70818efac65c3117b1c1d8787d7ec1aea3802","sha":"fff70818efac65c3117b1c1d8787d7ec1aea3802","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/fff70818efac65c3117b1c1d8787d7ec1aea3802"}],"sha":"21d4c026c88ad85e1a76df2bc96ce369a79553dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/21d4c026c88ad85e1a76df2bc96ce369a79553dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/fff70818efac65c3117b1c1d8787d7ec1aea3802/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:35:27Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:35:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): leave streamed generated metadata out of loading-shell prefetches (#3705)\n\n* fix(app-router): leave streamed generated metadata out of loading-shell prefetches\n\nA prefetch={true} link makes vinext fetch the full payload and, alongside it,\nthe route''s loading shell for rewrite reuse. The loading shell omits the page\nbut still rendered the streamed generateMetadata() tags, so a dynamic title\nwas sent twice. Before #3660 it was hidden by ordering: metadata resolved\nbefore the render and streamed ahead of the page. Now it resolves inside the\nrender and streams after the page, as in Next.js, so the shell''s copy shows up\nas a duplicate in Next''s segment-cache metadata test.\n\nLeave the streamed metadata body out of loading-shell renders, like the page.\nNext.js''s prefetch shell leaves a dynamic head out the same way. The full\npayload still carries it, and generateMetadata() still shares React cache()\nwith the page.\n\nThe segment-cache metadata port now matches responses with router-act''s\nrules (request order, ordered claims, no repeated strings), and a unit test\ncovers the shell.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep generated metadata in loading-boundary prefetch shells\n\nThe previous commit left streamed generateMetadata() tags out of every\nprefetch-loading-shell render. That mode also serves ordinary auto\nprefetches of routes with a loading boundary, and Next.js 16.2.7 keeps\nthe head there: walkTreeWithFlightRouterState() returns rscHead with the\nloading shell, and only short-circuits to a [null, null] head when no\nloading boundary exists.\n\nPort that rule. Leave the streamed metadata out only when the shell has\nno loading boundary, which is the case for the auxiliary shell beside a\nprefetch={true} full prefetch in Next''s segment-cache metadata test.\n\nThe segment-cache metadata port now waits for the auxiliary\nloading-shell request and for every request of the reveal to settle\nbefore checking for duplicates, instead of a fixed sleep that let a late\nshell response escape the check.\n\n* test(app-router): require a successful loading-shell response before the duplicate check\n\n* fix(app-router): ignore params-only slot overrides when finding prefetch loading shells\n\nThe loading-shell scan passed every slot override to\ncreateAppPageSlotLoadingEntries(), which drops a slot''s nested loading\nboundaries whenever an override is present. An inherited slot with its\nown param names gets a params-only override, so the scan missed its\nnested loading.tsx while the slot renderer, which only counts overrides\nthat replace the page or layouts, still rendered it. The shell then lost\nits LoadingBoundary marker and its streamed generateMetadata() tags.\n\nShare the renderer''s tree-changing-override check with the scan.","tree":{"sha":"647b14c7fdd5e8a80510ad083681ee97545af751","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/647b14c7fdd5e8a80510ad083681ee97545af751"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/fff70818efac65c3117b1c1d8787d7ec1aea3802","verification":{"payload":"tree 647b14c7fdd5e8a80510ad083681ee97545af751\nparent cc7e6d03f8d62816839b1c8c4d91ede5d6a05a47\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791243327 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791243327 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): leave streamed generated metadata out of loading-shell prefetches (#3705)\n\n* fix(app-router): leave streamed generated metadata out of loading-shell prefetches\n\nA prefetch={true} link makes vinext fetch the full payload and, alongside it,\nthe route''s loading shell for rewrite reuse. The loading shell omits the page\nbut still rendered the streamed generateMetadata() tags, so a dynamic title\nwas sent twice. Before #3660 it was hidden by ordering: metadata resolved\nbefore the render and streamed ahead of the page. Now it resolves inside the\nrender and streams after the page, as in Next.js, so the shell''s copy shows up\nas a duplicate in Next''s segment-cache metadata test.\n\nLeave the streamed metadata body out of loading-shell renders, like the page.\nNext.js''s prefetch shell leaves a dynamic head out the same way. The full\npayload still carries it, and generateMetadata() still shares React cache()\nwith the page.\n\nThe segment-cache metadata port now matches responses with router-act''s\nrules (request order, ordered claims, no repeated strings), and a unit test\ncovers the shell.\n\n* fix(app-router): keep generated metadata in loading-boundary prefetch shells\n\nThe previous commit left streamed generateMetadata() tags out of every\nprefetch-loading-shell render. That mode also serves ordinary auto\nprefetches of routes with a loading boundary, and Next.js 16.2.7 keeps\nthe head there: walkTreeWithFlightRouterState() returns rscHead with the\nloading shell, and only short-circuits to a [null, null] head when no\nloading boundary exists.\n\nPort that rule. Leave the streamed metadata out only when the shell has\nno loading boundary, which is the case for the auxiliary shell beside a\nprefetch={true} full prefetch in Next''s segment-cache metadata test.\n\nThe segment-cache metadata port now waits for the auxiliary\nloading-shell request and for every request of the reveal to settle\nbefore checking for duplicates, instead of a fixed sleep that let a late\nshell response escape the check.\n\n* test(app-router): require a successful loading-shell response before the duplicate check\n\n* fix(app-router): ignore params-only slot overrides when finding prefetch loading shells\n\nThe loading-shell scan passed every slot override to\ncreateAppPageSlotLoadingEntries(), which drops a slot''s nested loading\nboundaries whenever an override is present. An inherited slot with its\nown param names gets a params-only override, so the scan missed its\nnested loading.tsx while the slot renderer, which only counts overrides\nthat replace the page or layouts, still rendered it. The shell then lost\nits LoadingBoundary marker and its streamed generateMetadata() tags.\n\nShare the renderer''s tree-changing-override check with the scan.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxDQ/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjNMQALGeio/KBmwdhmetVGVzkeIr\nzLQ5t0pJjqWptUB6QJqph1w2ryiPDnnarYmJp+ubh45VE+EBvS8HtlU6f3vrqV6r\nTu2UHQsGC16+EXjccaQtwQ7ELJdt13u+e5+GLzvQgJnmRAWDllttPZk1/WWqLvvF\nN6HGNgU07L9+snY+LOdiRhcCQ7ILkgUCtx8acsyGcn5VZbppmqUSvb/jxXf3l3yT\nIv2ER6vyoYH7IWd7prh/mq72+oMh2nnjMTOv