github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/fff70818efac65c3117b1c1d8787d7ec1aea3802"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/cc7e6d03f8d62816839b1c8c4d91ede5d6a05a47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:04:02Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:04:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(use-cache): regenerate entries past their expire instead of serving them (#3703)\n\nThe runtime only rejected stale entries, so a cache handler reporting\ncacheState \"expired\" (the memory handler, or the Response Store adapter\nfor entries it cannot regenerate) had its value served as a fresh hit.\nLike Next.js, treat an entry past its expire as a miss.","tree":{"sha":"70561d0852eef35978bcd3ad36e2bcda9ad7d899","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/70561d0852eef35978bcd3ad36e2bcda9ad7d899"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/cc7e6d03f8d62816839b1c8c4d91ede5d6a05a47","verification":{"payload":"tree 70561d0852eef35978bcd3ad36e2bcda9ad7d899\nparent c8939856e8a38d1e014eae15198aeac84b91dabb\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791241442 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791241442 +0100\n\nfix(use-cache): regenerate entries past their expire instead of serving them (#3703)\n\nThe runtime only rejected stale entries, so a cache handler reporting\ncacheState \"expired\" (the memory handler, or the Response Store adapter\nfor entries it cannot regenerate) had its value served as a fresh hit.\nLike Next.js, treat an entry past its expire as a miss.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxCziCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAusUQAASRq+5/gm33vq8/9oPS+gqW\ndQ+J0bTW+3j29UmIQtHWvLTBL3rgdqPvSd6kF1WK6gNsq8avnHH4L2pKjYvp0THK\njMVUZhvIGv7YGH4jGarT0iaN3glWbDRXj4oT3svne/nMns22zEU7ykQUDBvXH70R\nF1Kmk1aD1bWFzST4rlq576j54eNvfqmBTi13SUASHIPImgHN1QX3SYMUIjpb0LGf\na2BQvjf7X0NDPsQcdv/HRTdH42lohaigWCOViavYhIPZyQQLJW3Fa8CQgWXU1e+n\neE8t0yzZgJqDAYokbYX6p6GkaoZGLmaF2jLLDaEU2dyOlAn1lYazL+BoMjPwmUd6\n2xP/U+idRXhZOq4U9D02jhkW4a5mP3hjb22LNFfSZznIK9fmVYgO7/1W4H2cWcYc\nLzQEnqxZB5T3SBYnPtCu7qdKbrAtPYs6cIKeprRldgk3Gaky6dLQCdGWIPnIPxM1\nwQyO7NX0QD/LKWRsaQ/ZIvp8X+67KcMNUwDBO3/MHk5DHSgV0KzIKIVgreSgGrcV\nJ0LA4mBc3Lirn19iqNlSbKIQay3EY0X4p35d/iFcR0envYpjtmxKoITGHQnM1aKL\nNCZ4erx+iC1oNf1Rx0ROes5aFdoVWqu7s594+8j6//nOyacZVSvxX53/wLvMCnV6\nArKO7mUzhLTXAPpXhekf\n=fJE6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T23:04:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/cc7e6d03f8d62816839b1c8c4d91ede5d6a05a47","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGNjN2U2ZDAzZjhkNjI4MTY4MzliMWM4YzRkOTFlZGU1ZDZhMDVhNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/c8939856e8a38d1e014eae15198aeac84b91dabb","sha":"c8939856e8a38d1e014eae15198aeac84b91dabb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/c8939856e8a38d1e014eae15198aeac84b91dabb"}],"sha":"cc7e6d03f8d62816839b1c8c4d91ede5d6a05a47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/cc7e6d03f8d62816839b1c8c4d91ede5d6a05a47"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/c8939856e8a38d1e014eae15198aeac84b91dabb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:03:05Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:03:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cloudflare): store the other entries a Response Store page replay recomputes (#3704)\n\n* fix(cloudflare): store the other entries a Response Store page replay recomputes\n\nReplaying a page to regenerate one data entry dropped every other entry the\nreplay recomputed, so an expired sibling stayed expired until a request\nrecomputed it again. Store them as usual, as Next.js stores every entry a\nrevalidation recomputes; only the target entry is returned to the Store.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): wait for replay side writes and skip ones the Store can''t regenerate\n\n* fix(cloudflare): finish replay side writes when the replay fails\n\n* test(cloudflare): select the replay sibling by its encoded cache tag","tree":{"sha":"f74abab266dbbffa881dd34b97dd2caee9afd1d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/f74abab266dbbffa881dd34b97dd2caee9afd1d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/c8939856e8a38d1e014eae15198aeac84b91dabb","verification":{"payload":"tree f74abab266dbbffa881dd34b97dd2caee9afd1d8\nparent 7396db0473f7caff9c7ace6629c22e075cebdb99\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791241385 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791241385 +0100\n\nfix(cloudflare): store the other entries a Response Store page replay recomputes (#3704)\n\n* fix(cloudflare): store the other entries a Response Store page replay recomputes\n\nReplaying a page to regenerate one data entry dropped every other entry the\nreplay recomputed, so an expired sibling stayed expired until a request\nrecomputed it again. Store them as usual, as Next.js stores every entry a\nrevalidation recomputes; only the target entry is returned to the Store.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): wait for replay side writes and skip ones the Store can''t regenerate\n\n* fix(cloudflare): finish replay side writes when the replay fails\n\n* test(cloudflare): select the replay sibling by its encoded cache tag","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxCypCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOrsQAG5y8jMvC1h/Apn83z8Rd4V2\n0xy0HA4Tz4aGoX44/ELBU6R+vkIaANpOJeFwj2teZpMy+R5EjH8YYlPiZxC7LlG1\nDx6Q/ZjdZgNaAYc9f2R+ezjrvyxKxCmdVLKGTJL2LdTBpBBIEBY9WdmLPGhZAvsQ\nEdyBm8nunf3aziIgxPREpHHdHb0SQHM3AlkvVPddxkmcO26EnLn9lyS2lKaXGgbI\n7HG9wt2HuQvixskMh+Zh6M00VuSqxBGJdCFGYm2uOwRDZJxo7dj5jDMMD0oiKQ4j\nOptsbm2Pa6MFqbURm+5NKuLWJbMLn1toKWbzA/GBOxpy+RynVly1lWl+GHWPvtA7\nQ9PXJ61+5IHNcWU1hMTxn971WwACNGAYEJ4B6wxXA59AwwM4V4sIdXUb6Fh9wYwG\n7PEjnK2xswKkZIZVU7+/ERDoiltCUq8iHDXr6jPupACOkoovPrF2PsbIsbxYy0uc\nNeQ7y3Ez0EbQfyZRDvKtvcylyPZudPfOWP/J4u/nyc9JrMfOOQd88mCYd5thT+zX\nyShoN1TYooqDJF0qwk9YRlWulvo9s9AwrN2ALHZHl6rbDFAop/RNp9k3GAnXfPDy\nAaVM1jZ+Ic0LRnaa4aAxptSPVyujp0DLdZep4x06v0jHnW2wdT7XrxY8yIaRNs5N\nwdyxKcm6imLrJ/ui9/s5\n=77fS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T23:03:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/c8939856e8a38d1e014eae15198aeac84b91dabb","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGM4OTM5ODU2ZThhMzhkMWUwMTRlYWUxNTE5OGFlYWM4NGI5MWRhYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/7396db0473f7caff9c7ace6629c22e075cebdb99","sha":"7396db0473f7caff9c7ace6629c22e075cebdb99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/7396db0473f7caff9c7ace6629c22e075cebdb99"}],"sha":"c8939856e8a38d1e014eae15198aeac84b91dabb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/c8939856e8a38d1e014eae15198aeac84b91dabb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/7396db0473f7caff9c7ace6629c22e075cebdb99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:00:02Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:00:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(cjs): strip the optimizer''s export facade without esbuildOptions (#3709)\n\n* refactor(cjs): leave CommonJS in the dep optimizer to Rolldown\n\nvite-plugin-commonjs registers an optimizeDeps pre-bundle plugin through\noptimizeDeps.esbuildOptions.plugins, which Vite 8 converts for its Rolldown\nscan and optimizer. Rolldown already handles CommonJS there, including\nrequire() and dynamic require() discovery, so that plugin''s conversion only\nadds export facades vinext then had to strip by wrapping its esbuild setup.\n\nvinext''s filter now converts only while its transform wrapper is delegating,\nso the pre-bundle plugin converts nothing. This removes the dependency on\nesbuildOptions.plugins, the pre-bundle plugin''s name and Vite''s esbuild shim.\n\n* refactor(cjs): strip the optimizer''s export facade in a Rolldown transform\n\nTurning vite-plugin-commonjs''s pre-bundle plugin off lost its dynamic\nrequire() expansion: Rolldown leaves `require(`./locales/${name}.json`)` in a\npre-bundled linked package to a runtime require, which throws.\n\nKeep the plugin converting in the optimizer and drop the facade from ESM\noutput with a vinext Rolldown transform hook in the client optimizer''s\nrolldownOptions.plugins instead. That still removes the esbuild setup/onLoad\nwrapping and vinext''s dependency on optimizeDeps.esbuildOptions.plugins.\nThe linked package test now executes a dynamic require().\n\n* fix(cjs): map the optimizer''s facade removal with MagicString\n\nThe optimizer hook returned the stripped code with map: null, so code\nvite-plugin-commonjs appended after the facade (its dynamic-require runtime)\nmapped to the removed facade lines. The loaded code is the optimizer''s source,\nso remove the facade with MagicString and return its map.","tree":{"sha":"5cc06497083993793518e39f07d32d5d8428330b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/5cc06497083993793518e39f07d32d5d8428330b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/7396db0473f7caff9c7ace6629c22e075cebdb99","verification":{"payload":"tree 5cc06497083993793518e39f07d32d5d8428330b\nparent c2574d07958664810181f8adb775787d57bbcc87\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791241202 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791241202 +0100\n\nrefactor(cjs): strip the optimizer''s export facade without esbuildOptions (#3709)\n\n* refactor(cjs): leave CommonJS in the dep optimizer to Rolldown\n\nvite-plugin-commonjs registers an optimizeDeps pre-bundle plugin through\noptimizeDeps.esbuildOptions.plugins, which Vite 8 converts for its Rolldown\nscan and optimizer. Rolldown already handles CommonJS there, including\nrequire() and dynamic require() discovery, so that plugin''s conversion only\nadds export facades vinext then had to strip by wrapping its esbuild setup.\n\nvinext''s filter now converts only while its transform wrapper is delegating,\nso the pre-bundle plugin converts nothing. This removes the dependency on\nesbuildOptions.plugins, the pre-bundle plugin''s name and Vite''s esbuild shim.\n\n* refactor(cjs): strip the optimizer''s export facade in a Rolldown transform\n\nTurning vite-plugin-commonjs''s pre-bundle plugin off lost its dynamic\nrequire() expansion: Rolldown leaves `require(`./locales/${name}.json`)` in a\npre-bundled linked package to a runtime require, which throws.\n\nKeep the plugin converting in the optimizer and drop the facade from ESM\noutput with a vinext Rolldown transform hook in the client optimizer''s\nrolldownOptions.plugins instead. That still removes the esbuild setup/onLoad\nwrapping and vinext''s dependency on optimizeDeps.esbuildOptions.plugins.\nThe linked package test now executes a dynamic require().\n\n* fix(cjs): map the optimizer''s facade removal with MagicString\n\nThe optimizer hook returned the stripped code with map: null, so code\nvite-plugin-commonjs appended after the facade (its dynamic-require runtime)\nmapped to the removed facade lines. The loaded code is the optimizer''s source,\nso remove the facade with MagicString and return its map.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxCvyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAphoQAG2n7uqVegkzIECKTXw2Extn\nTzUfSAr0QMcd5wbSzN4pqvbNab2GK1+6ct7DYSEhfmvrXpzkIWfPxoBAb/bHRkwi\nU9tj5LJ76rApEO0XjKs2jUpIPP+sJRDWzbzR0n336DVdaFMEn0Sp291so6ABROzo\n417LNtOYP2l3hWRGkeoatO+ROMGWupXWHgrp7ojcKGftjOwqxI+HLE2TFTbjvynu\nGpkz7SBCNRn4UGq4v/QYXxNFk2dQOxZtFliTfNbyZx4+jEVurwuQRu4a+Dpub6AO\n6fI2Q/XQax9QFy6yhTlrYLgHqYAf4jUnj1N5bO18K54RaRte2WqIoiTmqUngbZFs\nzfo6LXiEXdJfUMJ61x17I9vtjwF4MqCfGtwSUahAif/yG3feiq/jVDulWZ6eQcVd\nzMlfnjZSD9PNG6rWsHsBbwcHzMJH8Kw6ZHrl+NaOZY8XOvinji9t4aW5QEKP8Db4\numyB0kgMwpobdNQtooqMWtfpaSTNQxHmwXDpOn7yEqmiJIasBLtnHy22oEoGsRht\nWOyO1D1rIv+SG0me1OBAOsFt1vNVkIpKxIbtqTt3zqNRfNBPxmefFuYiLLQQT6HC\nVrPUFbutL/haJOxNEcjXzn6uK5T2A+qcs9wodPWMeggzkf0N6ZjrhOADTLCC4PDF\nq/uWcuIrTA6FGgvjayWJ\n=uDNe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T23:00:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/7396db0473f7caff9c7ace6629c22e075cebdb99","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDczOTZkYjA0NzNmN2NhZmY5YzdhY2U2NjI5YzIyZTA3NWNlYmRiOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/c2574d07958664810181f8adb775787d57bbcc87","sha":"c2574d07958664810181f8adb775787d57bbcc87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/c2574d07958664810181f8adb775787d57bbcc87"}],"sha":"7396db0473f7caff9c7ace6629c22e075cebdb99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/7396db0473f7caff9c7ace6629c22e075cebdb99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/c2574d07958664810181f8adb775787d57bbcc87/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T22:56:52Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T22:56:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cloudflare): soft-invalidate Workers Cache for stale-while-revalidate invalidations (#3707)\n\n* feat(cloudflare): soft-invalidate Workers Cache for stale-while-revalidate invalidations\n\nUse ctx.cache.invalidate() where Next.js semantics allow serving stale while\nthe edge refetches in the background:\n\n- Workers Cache CDN adapter: revalidateTag(tag, profile) with a non-zero\n  expire invalidates instead of purging. updateTag, revalidatePath, single-arg\n  revalidateTag and expire: 0 still purge.\n- Route invalidation through the cache-bearing VinextCachedResponse\n  entrypoint, like purge.\n- Workers Response Store refresh() invalidates the prior edge responses after\n  committing the regenerated revisions to R2.\n\nRuntimes without invalidate() (including current Miniflare) fall back to a\nhard purge. Bumps @cloudflare/workers-types to 5.20261004.1 for the type.\n\n* refactor(cloudflare): share the stale-tag rule and invalidate fallback\n\nAddress self-review findings:\n\n- Classify stale vs expired tag invalidations with one helper used by the\n  Workers Cache adapter and the Response Store data adapter, so durations\n  without expire (e.g. {}) are stale in both, matching Next.js.\n- Move the invalidate-or-purge fallback into one shared module.\n- Rename internals that now perform invalidations as well as purges.\n\n* docs(cloudflare): describe the purge fallback as a local Miniflare shim","tree":{"sha":"59498928388dc551daad74600433cdf18df13be9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/59498928388dc551daad74600433cdf18df13be9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/c2574d07958664810181f8adb775787d57bbcc87","verification":{"payload":"tree 59498928388dc551daad74600433cdf18df13be9\nparent f3505ce2681ab607766e3c66bcdd4e8a1ea000ea\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791241012 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791241012 +0100\n\nfeat(cloudflare): soft-invalidate Workers Cache for stale-while-revalidate invalidations (#3707)\n\n* feat(cloudflare): soft-invalidate Workers Cache for stale-while-revalidate invalidations\n\nUse ctx.cache.invalidate() where Next.js semantics allow serving stale while\nthe edge refetches in the background:\n\n- Workers Cache CDN adapter: revalidateTag(tag, profile) with a non-zero\n  expire invalidates instead of purging. updateTag, revalidatePath, single-arg\n  revalidateTag and expire: 0 still purge.\n- Route invalidation through the cache-bearing VinextCachedResponse\n  entrypoint, like purge.\n- Workers Response Store refresh() invalidates the prior edge responses after\n  committing the regenerated revisions to R2.\n\nRuntimes without invalidate() (including current Miniflare) fall back to a\nhard purge. Bumps @cloudflare/workers-types to 5.20261004.1 for the type.\n\n* refactor(cloudflare): share the stale-tag rule and invalidate fallback\n\nAddress self-review findings:\n\n- Classify stale vs expired tag invalidations with one helper used by the\n  Workers Cache adapter and the Response Store data adapter, so durations\n  without expire (e.g. {}) are stale in both, matching Next.js.\n- Move the invalidate-or-purge fallback into one shared module.\n- Rename internals that now perform invalidations as well as purges.\n\n* docs(cloudflare): describe the purge fallback as a local Miniflare shim","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxCs0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA14UQAJBq5wWYa9FmeFAZFhx/KJ40\nniWBYPm/xt8n8YyZkdFCOwuM1GNciwnDf5lvB9PIju1AWMIN019hOOO4C1uV7laF\nPbk72QeRYfYSygfG0Jx9zi0uu79WE2YGwEi/sOtXEXqqDN+T5KveRQozzuqsjBk+\nhdYwLXm3qM91bj/jGZwYgZk6m1opmXgMSlJuu8K7S5f5ndCXF1iVBoDfuP+GxjF9\nb2Wpg63mSUW6jfHUR0ocWVr/6VuyI5M+qRMI7zuDkdgARLgIWssR6G61HOOc0NwP\nO1m0eVT4w+N7iTahRcdpq4UTtj9nYnGjFNZelwIn8MgI/L1aWJiN06W9pj+Y+7li\n+Tl1orU+RKeeh/kiS6gONusUAnBIOwfewopEuRjvF1LHV8auyFkl7lVNRJb4oqzF\n+wuVyVdFpKGpQ9EVV2s3OFcCS+3xzaOCSnLnD2uHeoyh9dNzNKtA/MMoz8T3kPNt\nBU/ejnJuv1NjjrjUxhB9eaCoib1VzfIBKU2V1ltSQb66KftbGTVOoFRXLK6+X3LY\nCr2RmK4/qjQjA571AOstMPZ2O0a+6ckgtimRjMNhIC9vRvdKGS8O1BNiV/2Z3e7s\nkS3dzKxUb09vp/gSOvsumofrUwT8WxrgCqPl+SWI0aXpzXjrbKsz8H+HMBpM0N92\naHxRHt9JbFoQAL7H537r\n=Hh28\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T22:56:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/c2574d07958664810181f8adb775787d57bbcc87","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGMyNTc0ZDA3OTU4NjY0ODEwMTgxZjhhZGI3NzU3ODdkNTdiYmNjODc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/f3505ce2681ab607766e3c66bcdd4e8a1ea000ea","sha":"f3505ce2681ab607766e3c66bcdd4e8a1ea000ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f3505ce2681ab607766e3c66bcdd4e8a1ea000ea"}],"sha":"c2574d07958664810181f8adb775787d57bbcc87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/c2574d07958664810181f8adb775787d57bbcc87"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f3505ce2681ab607766e3c66bcdd4e8a1ea000ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:50:56Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T13:50:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cjs): drop the CommonJS export facade from ESM like Next.js (#3667)\n\n* fix(cjs): skip project-local ESM that never calls require()\n\nvite-plugin-commonjs transforms any module outside node_modules that\nmentions `module`, `exports` or `require`. A linked workspace package''s\ndist resolves outside node_modules, and when it inlines a CommonJS\ndependency (tsdown/rolldown `__commonJS` wrappers) the plugin appends an\nexport facade for `exports.t` next to the bundle''s own `export { t }`,\nfailing the dev transform, the dependency scan and the build with\n\"Duplicated export ''t''\".\n\nA module that declares ESM exports and never calls require() has\nnothing to convert, so leave it alone, both in the transform and in the\nfilter the plugin''s optimizer loader consults directly. Mixed modules\nthat call require() (e.g. a page using `require(\"./random\")`) still go\nthrough the plugin.\n\n* fix(cjs): detect require() calls from the AST like vite-plugin-commonjs\n\n* fix(cjs): keep converting free module/exports references next to ESM exports\n\n* fix(cjs): drop the CommonJS export facade from ESM like Next.js\n\nNext.js (webpack and Turbopack) treats a module with ESM syntax as ESM:\nrequire() still works, but module/exports never become its exports.\n\nInstead of deciding up front with an AST walk whether to skip\nvite-plugin-commonjs, always let it convert require() and add its local\nmodule/exports polyfill, then remove the export facade it appended when the\noriginal module has top-level ESM exports. The same applies to its\noptimizeDeps pre-bundle plugin, which no longer needs a disk read per\ncandidate in vinext''s filter.\n\nThe ESM check (one top-level parseAst, no walk) only runs for modules whose\noutput has a facade. ESM that calls require() and also inlines CommonJS\nwrappers now works too.\n\n* fix(cjs): classify the plugin''s output instead of rereading the source\n\nThe pre-bundle path reread the file after the plugin''s loader finished, so a\nfile changed in between could be classified from a different revision than the\none transformed. The plugin only prepends imports and its polyfill, rewrites\nrequire() calls and appends the facade, so the module''s own top-level exports\nare still in its output. Check that output with the facade removed, which needs\nno source read in either path.","tree":{"sha":"e6c1459ef116e4d9266ff6c1f46c843e9795987b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/e6c1459ef116e4d9266ff6c1f46c843e9795987b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/f3505ce2681ab607766e3c66bcdd4e8a1ea000ea","verification":{"payload":"tree e6c1459ef116e4d9266ff6c1f46c843e9795987b\nparent 448b5f34da9cc151b8f1721655919e5849d0206e\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791208256 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791208256 +0100\n\nfix(cjs): drop the CommonJS export facade from ESM like Next.js (#3667)\n\n* fix(cjs): skip project-local ESM that never calls require()\n\nvite-plugin-commonjs transforms any module outside node_modules that\nmentions `module`, `exports` or `require`. A linked workspace package''s\ndist resolves outside node_modules, and when it inlines a CommonJS\ndependency (tsdown/rolldown `__commonJS` wrappers) the plugin appends an\nexport facade for `exports.t` next to the bundle''s own `export { t }`,\nfailing the dev transform, the dependency scan and the build with\n\"Duplicated export ''t''\".\n\nA module that declares ESM exports and never calls require() has\nnothing to convert, so leave it alone, both in the transform and in the\nfilter the plugin''s optimizer loader consults directly. Mixed modules\nthat call require() (e.g. a page using `require(\"./random\")`) still go\nthrough the plugin.\n\n* fix(cjs): detect require() calls from the AST like vite-plugin-commonjs\n\n* fix(cjs): keep converting free module/exports references next to ESM exports\n\n* fix(cjs): drop the CommonJS export facade from ESM like Next.js\n\nNext.js (webpack and Turbopack) treats a module with ESM syntax as ESM:\nrequire() still works, but module/exports never become its exports.\n\nInstead of deciding up front with an AST walk whether to skip\nvite-plugin-commonjs, always let it convert require() and add its local\nmodule/exports polyfill, then remove the export facade it appended when the\noriginal module has top-level ESM exports. The same applies to its\noptimizeDeps pre-bundle plugin, which no longer needs a disk read per\ncandidate in vinext''s filter.\n\nThe ESM check (one top-level parseAst, no walk) only runs for modules whose\noutput has a facade. ESM that calls require() and also inlines CommonJS\nwrappers now works too.\n\n* fix(cjs): classify the plugin''s output instead of rereading the source\n\nThe pre-bundle path reread the file after the plugin''s loader finished, so a\nfile changed in between could be classified from a different revision than the\none transformed. The plugin only prepends imports and its polyfill, rewrites\nrequire() calls and appends the facade, so the module''s own top-level exports\nare still in its output. Check that output with the facade removed, which needs\nno source read in either path.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw6tACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEsMQADN/OUpkXUmeYy/YHxwjkJyH\n+UpiQs5LibJr3JH9gPsRtkbcGwLDgk2FzpwQm9RtsPypVRvJK7FUfls/+Cmvh0EO\nkS+EzvUN5kpp0g6eoniMyppPL8p5scPveUmdJPdz6FnCP5cmQaMujMpyh0EHmMlI\ngsKSmzbaSqyk7BsGiQNQLKdevTpMOW8GJyzzF0Q7ENQoB2m5BBhNle2bDs5V8qmc\nudGLwXBV+cBqMKKzB2vzEReS2FL1eWzyWaQBtt6jsTnKGmLJBfnXZePKX4EAJ9DZ\ntJw19K8eKZzefSdiL5geTceUXweuhT1uwb8KsIb1I540eTQRjFkgrIHiP03bsbb3\nEwumTUCrksndntCac1G0MwQWo2PiVXfoaVxRairx8dh/Y5x8VsggyrC1IM5AyLEq\nYYWYjdBSZj+wUc58yA7akx7sOlP0bix9UgqckZxoaf2c7FTKItVnSU+uFCcSo7AA\nUEilbnqyNzlLVm42q3LafyKSz72S12gV9Jc07JxFCABU4PX77hqR9GZZZDHtj7Ct\nozjSpPcbb75MwtXgNiMwg7pIO1zc73jO9dsIFGAojVdtvDG5aoD8b4GBxUiZrSjF\nbjh8MWGzmkYA7Iw4RGDVkMdl7huiC8Ofla3dN+TbyVEwJfAnholGSXN93pbU7Jva\ntuGzsUj7hiVUY6B7jQ7a\n=3w2v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T13:50:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/f3505ce2681ab607766e3c66bcdd4e8a1ea000ea","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGYzNTA1Y2UyNjgxYWI2MDc3NjZlM2M2NmJjZGQ0ZThhMWVhMDAwZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/448b5f34da9cc151b8f1721655919e5849d0206e","sha":"448b5f34da9cc151b8f1721655919e5849d0206e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/448b5f34da9cc151b8f1721655919e5849d0206e"}],"sha":"f3505ce2681ab607766e3c66bcdd4e8a1ea000ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f3505ce2681ab607766e3c66bcdd4e8a1ea000ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/448b5f34da9cc151b8f1721655919e5849d0206e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:20:05Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:20:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(response-store): let writers opt hard-expired reads into a miss (#3696)\n\n* fix(response-store): let writers opt hard-expired reads into a miss\n\nA ''use cache'' entry whose arguments can''t be replayed falls back to the\npage-replay revalidator while keeping a finite expire. A hard-expired read\nthen waited for the page replay, and a page reading two such entries\nreplayed itself for each in turn (A -> B -> A) until the request hung.\n\nAdd a put() option expired: \"miss\" persisted with the entry. A read past\nthe SWR window returns a Response Store miss and starts no regeneration,\nso the caller recomputes, matching Next.js. refresh() still regenerates\nthrough the stored revalidator. vinext sets it for vinext:data entries.\n\n* test(response-store): cover conditional and large-header expired misses\n\n* fix(response-store): bump the storage layout for the expired-read policy\n\nR2 metadata now carries expiredRead. An older cache Worker sharing the r2-v1\nlayout during a service-binding rollback would republish entries without it,\nand the new Worker would read them back as regenerate.\n\n* refactor(response-store): rename the expired put option to expiryBehaviour\n\n* refactor(response-store): use US spelling for expiryBehavior","tree":{"sha":"283ae01cdb40ff00dda33caba38c97327834ece8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/283ae01cdb40ff00dda33caba38c97327834ece8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/448b5f34da9cc151b8f1721655919e5849d0206e","verification":{"payload":"tree 283ae01cdb40ff00dda33caba38c97327834ece8\nparent e040b13e0aac21140d637cdd61cdb48519c64064\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791199205 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791199205 +0000\n\nfix(response-store): let writers opt hard-expired reads into a miss (#3696)\n\n* fix(response-store): let writers opt hard-expired reads into a miss\n\nA ''use cache'' entry whose arguments can''t be replayed falls back to the\npage-replay revalidator while keeping a finite expire. A hard-expired read\nthen waited for the page replay, and a page reading two such entries\nreplayed itself for each in turn (A -> B -> A) until the request hung.\n\nAdd a put() option expired: \"miss\" persisted with the entry. A read past\nthe SWR window returns a Response Store miss and starts no regeneration,\nso the caller recomputes, matching Next.js. refresh() still regenerates\nthrough the stored revalidator. vinext sets it for vinext:data entries.\n\n* test(response-store): cover conditional and large-header expired misses\n\n* fix(response-store): bump the storage layout for the expired-read policy\n\nR2 metadata now carries expiredRead. An older cache Worker sharing the r2-v1\nlayout during a service-binding rollback would republish entries without it,\nand the new Worker would read them back as regenerate.\n\n* refactor(response-store): rename the expired put option to expiryBehaviour\n\n* refactor(response-store): use US spelling for expiryBehavior","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw4flCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAODIQABynOhrcnK6K5nrH6SlCj4U4\nXwE7FVUNkJHrBh/nsmfAYpqRXqP9gucFh7kJVT6/wWg6B/Nj/RFqIrDURM/E3rS3\n0PkYOkqq2avkpOcSFUuM+H13RHygkvMHmlZPeSMNcIkeuxx8EbG0FNZETxktNS3Q\nghjeAEPI0Svqfkm2XfS/n3rJl0+qVmg7UdOZViY7dfwSrZ7kWe4mguCdNXLeuJLn\n3tfGNVf9+t3jmEFXGL3hNajQ685kqxnbharsF6X+hWf69leStIu8axMiHEZ/hpvg\nANUjOhlIyj2llR7oH36w2Q11mM8fQyDTfraRjuZlVFpKbnzVpEsfcMKUemUhfO81\nJY3rjHmr3GWrPzkh71NlkpNJm0T9dvQGniiQLa9yaJkau7Ov+P72C4PHVG1a7UrS\nH4rVbbqoUrSd7vT16cASOBGYByYbZZ8UWiUc8kA+ZzSHftpq8Xca08V9IozBz1Zh\nIhT7M4TCeh1jX0YbhabOmK3+VcfB5AYwV6c+FS5r/LfMCxigy+Dg0Om+xIrzvAUq\nRUyW0l/v4WHy0Z4PX5jtTsAWSkmbmF+XzXHbhxHJMjtctoIEqBXz2/2A+DjcyToA\n2Wmx8ueBN7qA3HaT9IxQW9NgHtd28esq+fCYTSNxlTwRMMbe8AYWErYp7DO51Eby\nfmBLajZ0kIdPfzY6POo3\n=SjJB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T11:20:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/448b5f34da9cc151b8f1721655919e5849d0206e","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDQ0OGI1ZjM0ZGE5Y2MxNTFiOGYxNzIxNjU1OTE5ZTU4NDlkMDIwNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/e040b13e0aac21140d637cdd61cdb48519c64064","sha":"e040b13e0aac21140d637cdd61cdb48519c64064","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/e040b13e0aac21140d637cdd61cdb48519c64064"}],"sha":"448b5f34da9cc151b8f1721655919e5849d0206e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/448b5f34da9cc151b8f1721655919e5849d0206e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/e040b13e0aac21140d637cdd61cdb48519c64064/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:36:48Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T09:36:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(app-router): share React cache() between generateMetadata and the page render (#3660)\n\n* fix(app-router): resolve metadata inside the Flight render so it shares React cache() with the page\n\nReact only memoises cache() while a Flight request renders. vinext resolved\ngenerateMetadata()/generateViewport() before renderToReadableStream() started,\nso every cache()-wrapped loader they shared with the page ran twice, and\nmetadata could see different values than the page. cacheSignal() was also\nnull for loaders metadata called first.\n\nNext.js renders its cache()-wrapped metadata/viewport resolvers as components\nof the page tree (lib/metadata/metadata.tsx). Do the same: the head, its\nstreamed body tags and its error outlet are async server components that call\none resolveHead() memoised with React''s cache(). generateMetadata() and\ngenerateViewport() now run inside the page''s Flight render, share its cache()\nscope, and each separate render gets its own. Only the placement inputs\n(whether a segment has generateMetadata, the page''s searchParams) are still\ncomputed before the render. Every resolved head now has an outlet, because a\nresolution error can surface after the render has started.\n\nNo React internals are touched.\n\n* test(app-router): cover React cache() sharing between metadata and the page end to end\n\nPorts Next.js''s metadata cache-deduping e2e tests (initial load and client\nnavigation) and adds regression specs against app-basic in dev and in its\nproduction build: generateViewport() and the page, a layout and\ngenerateMetadata() sharing a loader that awaits connection(), cacheSignal()\ninside generateMetadata(), the RSC payload, the html-limited bot head, fresh\nvalues per request, and a cookies() loader on a revalidate page that must\nnever be stored or shown to another user. Also covers next-intl''s documented\ngenerateMetadata() pattern.\n\n* test(app-page-dispatch): render the head outlet in the fake Flight renderer\n\nMetadata now resolves inside the Flight render, so the test renderer renders\nthe head outlet entry alongside the page, as Flight renders every entry. The\nlayout probe test now asserts generateMetadata() runs after the probe and its\ndynamic usage still reaches the render.\n\n* test(app-page-dispatch): fail the fake Flight render on head outlet errors","tree":{"sha":"88cdd708e83cec7925a17967a7dcd462a70d2d8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/88cdd708e83cec7925a17967a7dcd462a70d2d8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/e040b13e0aac21140d637cdd61cdb48519c64064","verification":{"payload":"tree 88cdd708e83cec7925a17967a7dcd462a70d2d8c\nparent f5f431d5e4a306c00d0abd904e3c89a029d22fa3\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791193008 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791193008 +0100\n\nfix(app-router): share React cache() between generateMetadata and the page render (#3660)\n\n* fix(app-router): resolve metadata inside the Flight render so it shares React cache() with the page\n\nReact only memoises cache() while a Flight request renders. vinext resolved\ngenerateMetadata()/generateViewport() before renderToReadableStream() started,\nso every cache()-wrapped loader they shared with the page ran twice, and\nmetadata could see different values than the page. cacheSignal() was also\nnull for loaders metadata called first.\n\nNext.js renders its cache()-wrapped metadata/viewport resolvers as components\nof the page tree (lib/metadata/metadata.tsx). Do the same: the head, its\nstreamed body tags and its error outlet are async server components that call\none resolveHead() memoised with React''s cache(). generateMetadata() and\ngenerateViewport() now run inside the page''s Flight render, share its cache()\nscope, and each separate render gets its own. Only the placement inputs\n(whether a segment has generateMetadata, the page''s searchParams) are still\ncomputed before the render. Every resolved head now has an outlet, because a\nresolution error can surface after the render has started.\n\nNo React internals are touched.\n\n* test(app-router): cover React cache() sharing between metadata and the page end to end\n\nPorts Next.js''s metadata cache-deduping e2e tests (initial load and client\nnavigation) and adds regression specs against app-basic in dev and in its\nproduction build: generateViewport() and the page, a layout and\ngenerateMetadata() sharing a loader that awaits connection(), cacheSignal()\ninside generateMetadata(), the RSC payload, the html-limited bot head, fresh\nvalues per request, and a cookies() loader on a revalidate page that must\nnever be stored or shown to another user. Also covers next-intl''s documented\ngenerateMetadata() pattern.\n\n* test(app-page-dispatch): render the head outlet in the fake Flight renderer\n\nMetadata now resolves inside the Flight render, so the test renderer renders\nthe head outlet entry alongside the page, as Flight renders every entry. The\nlayout probe test now asserts generateMetadata() runs after the probe and its\ndynamic usage still reaches the render.\n\n* test(app-page-dispatch): fail the fake Flight render on head outlet errors","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw2+wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsb0QADEV10XPWMpL1sTYKF1AbVhv\n0MU9YBImEym6UJqj7cSOOhAi+hncrIomokeGqbm8TgVuZV+TXm/hOmZKEK1bnRkz\n1Y5UTYgwX0Rk0jCPM992WJRkbrIEKgDdg0JzcESAy8soZGcjMlNQbOChySp3EWOo\n3e316AmVIgw1uaaxY7JxcqdroAvR6T06tKTByLd+SaWjtlYdy1J4h/IrdbC5Y9ct\nHI4vOsP1BPhqu57lcXAEztHm8vkTITgaxLpY4gRYl6vui3So4Un2CNgYeTo9aOz2\no/Lzt4j0TS8C3yHblfqLYw0ewTEx1OEfW0DmzTzEo1Egi5EYfZW7FpBvQErsRMSi\nAkiLiVsRi77bhBfL1GwD1OXWlwZMHBYQrK/Za1aYS/YmhMLDes3IFlxOfxyDNNe2\nmQzG88icaYmvSuGeVeJ6iDU07Jg2Uu0b41YgCIw1m+1BO9UCjuEGvhmWor959FFo\nkmN7jmoqfhW2MIT5GJxkfVgJYn8gjdiVVailsCb9RBZ5uSy7iE1SGtbFacBL7I9h\ngePiYxI+9o04QlA6rPqVB45iTQlufvsz71c6j8ltmfZgIpNI0V2C3Rc01ocK5Czl\nqWxteE1pp4tZedKNtWb7x/ToMMqN0J0KYmuyjO8SPCFMsBFBCVgHvq/i+ARRyFv4\nTnnUAmw1fWNIaqJ2TfKo\n=z3vm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T09:36:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/e040b13e0aac21140d637cdd61cdb48519c64064","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKGUwNDBiMTNlMGFhYzIxMTQwZDYzN2NkZDYxY2RiNDg1MTljNjQwNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/f5f431d5e4a306c00d0abd904e3c89a029d22fa3","sha":"f5f431d5e4a306c00d0abd904e3c89a029d22fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f5f431d5e4a306c00d0abd904e3c89a029d22fa3"}],"sha":"e040b13e0aac21140d637cdd61cdb48519c64064","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/e040b13e0aac21140d637cdd61cdb48519c64064"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/f5f431d5e4a306c00d0abd904e3c89a029d22fa3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T08:59:27Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T08:59:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cloudflare): store Response Store data entries without expire as stale indefinitely (#3675)\n\n* fix(cloudflare): never hard-expire Response Store data entries regenerated by page replay\n\nunstable_cache and cached fetch pass revalidate without expire, and the\ndata adapter stored them with stale-while-revalidate=0, so every entry\nhard-expired once revalidate elapsed. Next.js never hard-expires these\nentries by time: past revalidate it serves the stale value and refreshes\nit in the background.\n\nHard expiry is also the one path where a read waits for the Store to\nregenerate the entry, and a vinext:data entry regenerates by replaying\nits page. A page that reads two such entries replayed itself for each in\nturn (A -> B -> A) until workerd ran out of memory.\n\nStore entries without expire with an unbounded stale window, as Next.js\ndoes. Entries regenerated by replaying the page (including use cache\nvalues whose arguments can''t be replayed) never hard-expire in the Store\neither; the adapter treats them as a miss past expire, like Next.js.\nCache-function entries regenerate without a page replay and keep the\nStore''s expiry.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): keep Store expiry for data entries that set expire\n\nTreating a page-replay entry past expire as a miss ran its regeneration\ntwice: the Store had already scheduled a background replay for the stale\nread, and the caller then ran the function in the foreground. Limit the\nchange to the Next.js parity fix for entries without expire.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): let the Store alone refresh a stale replayable data entry\n\nA stale Store hit has already scheduled the Store''s page replay. Cached\nfetch passes its revalidate into get(), so the adapter also reported the\nentry stale and the fetch shim refetched it a second time, doubling\nupstream work and racing two writes. Report caller-side staleness only\nfor fresh Store hits older than a shorter requested revalidate.","tree":{"sha":"0044cf086848cc76fef041183d87826a0821e72e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/0044cf086848cc76fef041183d87826a0821e72e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/f5f431d5e4a306c00d0abd904e3c89a029d22fa3","verification":{"payload":"tree 0044cf086848cc76fef041183d87826a0821e72e\nparent e5ada16269f18317aad9c9070d9ff64f62699e88\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1791190767 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791190767 +0100\n\nfix(cloudflare): store Response Store data entries without expire as stale indefinitely (#3675)\n\n* fix(cloudflare): never hard-expire Response Store data entries regenerated by page replay\n\nunstable_cache and cached fetch pass revalidate without expire, and the\ndata adapter stored them with stale-while-revalidate=0, so every entry\nhard-expired once revalidate elapsed. Next.js never hard-expires these\nentries by time: past revalidate it serves the stale value and refreshes\nit in the background.\n\nHard expiry is also the one path where a read waits for the Store to\nregenerate the entry, and a vinext:data entry regenerates by replaying\nits page. A page that reads two such entries replayed itself for each in\nturn (A -> B -> A) until workerd ran out of memory.\n\nStore entries without expire with an unbounded stale window, as Next.js\ndoes. Entries regenerated by replaying the page (including use cache\nvalues whose arguments can''t be replayed) never hard-expire in the Store\neither; the adapter treats them as a miss past expire, like Next.js.\nCache-function entries regenerate without a page replay and keep the\nStore''s expiry.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): keep Store expiry for data entries that set expire\n\nTreating a page-replay entry past expire as a miss ran its regeneration\ntwice: the Store had already scheduled a background replay for the stale\nread, and the caller then ran the function in the foreground. Limit the\nchange to the Next.js parity fix for entries without expire.\n\n* fix(cloudflare): let the Store alone refresh a stale replayable data entry\n\nA stale Store hit has already scheduled the Store''s page replay. Cached\nfetch passes its revalidate into get(), so the adapter also reported the\nentry stale and the fetch shim refetched it a second time, doubling\nupstream work and racing two writes. Report caller-side staleness only\nfor fresh Store hits older than a shorter requested revalidate.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw2bvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9kQQAHR2JSloCY2RAcNNAMFgi9dH\nPOwGMO0vLL7KdkaHOtNiZMQrucl4v+7LRmLYjz+Tu9/foVIDJSEFv9UI6FCXWVEP\nrlmClEuGHxC/+oFT73osZeN2oY1BvOLY1xXJQZHB17VwFdGNaN5X2zsIs2X3IrVx\nSP1QB7KrOlSMFWC08nRndxLfyyx/eHQnvCpFrAGZKF5COPxzamufO47m0fOoOBHC\nHOVDcXUJer/onfLg3O5cqkacmMf2EaC7pJ1qxcMWxixx6yi9IlXysv0zxJDyA5YM\nPjZZxpIejj7hGu+5OdMzqyWLS4q/j2GMVmiIWnDfYUB1/z6qn7GgcFNmokv0k6Rz\ndfKuz/KEcVXPvAFolVHyH177a9iYTK8qHB2chpk4wEyOMcguUmYG1qKGTwd7Y7SQ\nXMnGB7/04Fx99w6eYpiivP+EQcPhyPpgzRprn8HAMZ2QTsoO3RjkbfTYRZMifTk9\npR9yUs7pVxqnV8pv5VR0wEH/SIkVLefAqkV0vnDEANk/xUaUWvRIFE51QpkuoaMT\nsbVHNRIWaxRSt4XMQvRJm4Qme9MSHBkK5vN+wMzIA72GkDNjD2i84xoIMU9YRq0l\nOoQcgYdZLFwrunKQjAdvQ5mIyTRV5XRAZlKszI5MGP732N69MunMuVFtPWOkBwvp\nz5Dl5JpAVm+t4UsNxNNR\n=BwFf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T08:59:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"h