 initial route errors\n\n* fix(cache): capture completed browser policy and avoid duplicate staged cookies","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvkxnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuGEQAKUwVSgkZa6KnAYuvKvHeNVf\nrD33adtPhLduE/31px6eKn9CjkRZoFmfkBapHijJKXH/sEWrxr4M2VuhrERRb4CN\nvytBlPsJXpLYsiLAR+63UPTY+TB1LPSCJKmapkSVWeb4W5yOW6beie8uofrNvdXq\nXMS9Mir6e37WiFlzkQ2oU2xGjLAuVhvF2HN16HcA7RqnMvIfcvoK3wc/rRMKa6h0\nDU0TJP+UPGkHtRoFmYnuNZ4W2ztvSICVRL9UDoHr8OK6fgeSA+MxlQeXTmF1J0//\nSE4yb8JgnaFHQC7d0a+1dg57XXutpe0HSxcipoRngrNfPhkLCoe2po24/yVbo8Ym\n9kJDL2lQeZC9LAnx8GwYhPKvA33/i+B5yl7IyTT7ldBQJRg9mkRRPbYU4Px3LKQ+\nibOp0P6+UDvtbBHWyRA4LEhcqhqY0mZP8DQ3cqYYip2YguxbaA6p/iSoOSKUanQQ\nW+lr5G3rN1rGcCKjeIZd6Gd3QYkPrWiqcVU7eRlgOq9DQxehq1UA7mB8wkDg1jP6\nsrLn56Y258U6OhYOdhfBNQrq4dCwKB8xHeKQojdQH2p/l76qNL8eBSM4dMtdP0VD\nEBLaCNT4nrkDI3PsA3fo5qObmWulZ0V3yCSHbtrg/lIxfDE/4xr6tLvO8/8e1vgv\nG4XIcN07yeLMutLhunP2\n=sK/r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T12:04:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/46cc0b24439735af16e040140388c66c804f3f11","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDQ2Y2MwYjI0NDM5NzM1YWYxNmUwNDAxNDAzODhjNjZjODA0ZjNmMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/07a1c8399ac2f5b43b0e5b792795359c418f77fc","sha":"07a1c8399ac2f5b43b0e5b792795359c418f77fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/07a1c8399ac2f5b43b0e5b792795359c418f77fc"}],"sha":"46cc0b24439735af16e040140388c66c804f3f11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/46cc0b24439735af16e040140388c66c804f3f11"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/07a1c8399ac2f5b43b0e5b792795359c418f77fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:30:11Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:30:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(cloudflare): serve prerendered Pages Router from Static Assets (#3603)\n\n* fix(cloudflare): serve prerendered Pages Router from Static Assets\n\n* docs: retain original caching page description\n\n* fix(cache): preserve Pages prerender identity and error responses\n\n* test: resolve Pages Static Assets fixture dependencies in clean checkouts\n\n* fix(cloudflare): complete Pages Static Assets setup and error caching\n\n* test: register Pages Static Assets fixture entries with knip\n\n* fix(cache): preserve Pages prerender outcomes and locale snapshots\n\n* fix(cloudflare): preserve Pages asset settings and response statuses\n\n* fix(cloudflare): preserve prerendered Pages content types\n\n* fix(cache): isolate Pages static snapshots and private artifacts\n\n* fix(cache): separate normalized Pages keys from legacy entries\n\n* fix(cloudflare): preserve configured assets through request contexts\n\n* fix(prerender): keep canonical default-locale Pages URLs\n\nOnly qualify a default-locale prerender path with its locale when the\npath''s first segment names a locale. Warm plans, fallback-shell warming,\nand the root 404 document keep the public URLs visitors request, and\nmiddleware sees the same URL at build and request time.\n\nFallback-shell warming also skips getStaticProps notFound snapshots, and\nthe Static Assets adapter releases the unread not-found artifact body.\n\n* test(cloudflare): run Pages Static Assets E2E against deployed examples\n\nMove the Pages Router Static Assets fixtures into examples/static-assets-pages\nand examples/static-assets-pages-i18n so CI deploys them with PR preview\naliases, lists them in the preview comment, and smoke-tests them.\n\nThe E2E suite still builds both examples locally in the Playwright matrix, and\na deployed-e2e step now runs it against each PR''s previews. Deployed runs read\nthe build ID from page HTML and skip checks that need local build output or\ncustom Host routing. The preview and revalidation controls only respond when\nbuilt with VINEXT_E2E_CONTROLS=1, so deployed previews do not expose them.\n\n* fix(prerender): skip Pages snapshots served through rewrites\n\nA request-conditional beforeFiles or middleware rewrite can render another\npage for the headerless build request. During prerendering the Pages\npipeline now marks responses whose URL a rewrite changed, and the\nprerenderer leaves those paths to runtime instead of storing the rewrite\ntarget''s HTML, redirect, or notFound result under the source path.\n\nAlso move the Pages Static Assets E2E servers to ports that do not collide\nwith the Nitro projects on main.\n\n* fix(prerender): snapshot Pages only when the page render confirms its URL\n\nRewrites that resolve to public files, API routes, or proxies return before\nthe page renderer, so they never sent the rewritten marker and could still be\nfrozen as a snapshot. Prerender now requires the server to positively confirm\nan unrewritten page render (x-vinext-prerender-rewritten: 0); anything else is\nleft to runtime.\n\nHybrid App+Pages builds render Pages through the App handler''s Pages\nfallback, which never sent the marker. It now applies the same rule, so\nrewrites are detected there and hybrid Pages routes keep prerendering.\n\n* test(request-pipeline): expect the prerender rewritten marker in internal headers\n\n* fix(pages): address Static Assets review findings\n\n- Admit nonce-bearing requests to build-only dynamic paths through the\n  packaged entry; only cached HTML replay stays guarded by the nonce.\n- Require the unrewritten-page confirmation before packaging the custom 404.\n- Fall back to adapter-supplied assets in the App Router multi-stage entry,\n  matching the single-stage entry and the Pages request stage.","tree":{"sha":"5d7c1f7d8e1b316e7f0be9ac2207e4dedc6fc0c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/5d7c1f7d8e1b316e7f0be9ac2207e4dedc6fc0c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/07a1c8399ac2f5b43b0e5b792795359c418f77fc","verification":{"payload":"tree 5d7c1f7d8e1b316e7f0be9ac2207e4dedc6fc0c7\nparent 8a3155d0f54f9b1fbea0b1af662d00056726e1d6\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1790854211 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790854211 +0100\n\nfix(cloudflare): serve prerendered Pages Router from Static Assets (#3603)\n\n* fix(cloudflare): serve prerendered Pages Router from Static Assets\n\n* docs: retain original caching page description\n\n* fix(cache): preserve Pages prerender identity and error responses\n\n* test: resolve Pages Static Assets fixture dependencies in clean checkouts\n\n* fix(cloudflare): complete Pages Static Assets setup and error caching\n\n* test: register Pages Static Assets fixture entries with knip\n\n* fix(cache): preserve Pages prerender outcomes and locale snapshots\n\n* fix(cloudflare): preserve Pages asset settings and response statuses\n\n* fix(cloudflare): preserve prerendered Pages content types\n\n* fix(cache): isolate Pages static snapshots and private artifacts\n\n* fix(cache): separate normalized Pages keys from legacy entries\n\n* fix(cloudflare): preserve configured assets through request contexts\n\n* fix(prerender): keep canonical default-locale Pages URLs\n\nOnly qualify a default-locale prerender path with its locale when the\npath''s first segment names a locale. Warm plans, fallback-shell warming,\nand the root 404 document keep the public URLs visitors request, and\nmiddleware sees the same URL at build and request time.\n\nFallback-shell warming also skips getStaticProps notFound snapshots, and\nthe Static Assets adapter releases the unread not-found artifact body.\n\n* test(cloudflare): run Pages Static Assets E2E against deployed examples\n\nMove the Pages Router Static Assets fixtures into examples/static-assets-pages\nand examples/static-assets-pages-i18n so CI deploys them with PR preview\naliases, lists them in the preview comment, and smoke-tests them.\n\nThe E2E suite still builds both examples locally in the Playwright matrix, and\na deployed-e2e step now runs it against each PR''s previews. Deployed runs read\nthe build ID from page HTML and skip checks that need local build output or\ncustom Host routing. The preview and revalidation controls only respond when\nbuilt with VINEXT_E2E_CONTROLS=1, so deployed previews do not expose them.\n\n* fix(prerender): skip Pages snapshots served through rewrites\n\nA request-conditional beforeFiles or middleware rewrite can render another\npage for the headerless build request. During prerendering the Pages\npipeline now marks responses whose URL a rewrite changed, and the\nprerenderer leaves those paths to runtime instead of storing the rewrite\ntarget''s HTML, redirect, or notFound result under the source path.\n\nAlso move the Pages Static Assets E2E servers to ports that do not collide\nwith the Nitro projects on main.\n\n* fix(prerender): snapshot Pages only when the page render confirms its URL\n\nRewrites that resolve to public files, API routes, or proxies return before\nthe page renderer, so they never sent the rewritten marker and could still be\nfrozen as a snapshot. Prerender now requires the server to positively confirm\nan unrewritten page render (x-vinext-prerender-rewritten: 0); anything else is\nleft to runtime.\n\nHybrid App+Pages builds render Pages through the App handler''s Pages\nfallback, which never sent the marker. It now applies the same rule, so\nrewrites are detected there and hybrid Pages routes keep prerendering.\n\n* test(request-pipeline): expect the prerender rewritten marker in internal headers\n\n* fix(pages): address Static Assets review findings\n\n- Admit nonce-bearing requests to build-only dynamic paths through the\n  packaged entry; only cached HTML replay stays guarded by the nonce.\n- Require the unrewritten-page confirmation before packaging the custom 404.\n- Fall back to adapter-supplied assets in the App Router multi-stage entry,\n  matching the single-stage entry and the Pages request stage.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvkRDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWI0QACa9ah2caY8RohAR0X0sTQAy\np5X5fjP8J0pWRq92Vas/XPRH2cv4p8rJmELuFNaD1bx7Bn1A1irzkcEdKyY0P8ff\n7mOiKgLlq5/lYPIi7SLxpBFDK/4ntg4BGFI2Nh72Qsrk67wKQGzLiF2v8B3SO6Dj\nQA3eRpqu953Gf9f4ZNTZlbvppL2wq8QVf5D5VtqVNcOrZnFJJHV/YvQ2NWqeDx2M\nz0ftFDeQ4k7J8lNncx3b0BfXk9uuAXbp3hTuipljmPFlokHZr+2hVUWuGdAhyacp\nDiMUPBHKyfrzak01Dt8TTXjtNiCpIKCS+CKkHh2v+lG6ShE/f0lbb870HpwvvgES\nJ3o2wpcJN0BcQydviDm4AzmXXpjLAPpjP/qXorqswtAKqVXegUs+PX6qprnW6K+J\nHm0mitsFsdzmNg2Us1tx2Xm8jh33rGUnX7XWjkHGLsq7N5KreTpKrMJ2MA5sbl6M\nbo1itN5cJGXN6YaldIZ40jaFOWHM7Lcuw5EHYQQfZK5E1wOZyBAYP5l4utd9nSTK\npBUnVVdhOttXi1fpp2pG+Gh+IEsUoo2zp8UGIfIXBc6MvvwDBkkTYuihQxdsUpcO\nGQUQECQPfdP2smlfitH8rJMW2qaPTPJDODKYVMiqdW0TRseH8degW1kHMlbIdtW8\njf612E30QxtKe3j0NYca\n=T2TJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T11:30:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/07a1c8399ac2f5b43b0e5b792795359c418f77fc","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDA3YTFjODM5OWFjMmY1YjQzYjBlNWI3OTI3OTUzNTljNDE4Zjc3ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/8a3155d0f54f9b1fbea0b1af662d00056726e1d6","sha":"8a3155d0f54f9b1fbea0b1af662d00056726e1d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/8a3155d0f54f9b1fbea0b1af662d00056726e1d6"}],"sha":"07a1c8399ac2f5b43b0e5b792795359c418f77fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/07a1c8399ac2f5b43b0e5b792795359c418f77fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/8a3155d0f54f9b1fbea0b1af662d00056726e1d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:25:10Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T11:25:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shims): null a framed GET/HEAD body on a NextRequest''s Request input (#3649)\n\n* fix(shims): null a framed GET/HEAD body on a NextRequest''s Request input\n\nWorkers hands a GET/HEAD a non-null body when it is sent with one (or just\nContent-Length). #3621 dropped it from a Request init; the input side still\ncarried it into the NextRequest, so middleware, route handlers and edge API\nroutes saw a body Next.js never exposes (it nulls GET/HEAD bodies in\nNextRequestAdapter and the edge sandbox), and `new Request(url, request)` in\na route handler threw on the tracking Proxy.\n\nShare the GET/HEAD check with the init side and pass an explicit null body\nwhen the init keeps the input''s method and body. Also type the rebuilt init\ninstead of asserting it.\n\n* test(e2e): assert the route handler''s view of a framed HEAD body\n\nA HEAD response drops the JSON flags, so report request.body === null from\nthe route handler in a header and assert it.\n\n* test(e2e): frame the GET/HEAD probes with an empty chunked body\n\nSending body bytes the Worker never reads made wrangler dev''s ProxyWorker\nforwarding fetch fail on Linux CI, which wrangler treats as fatal, taking\nthe dev server down for the rest of the run. An empty chunked body still\nreaches the Worker as a non-null body (the tests fail without the fix) but\nleaves nothing unread on the connection.","tree":{"sha":"bdb1bc3927a14064015152d79438ed35de12d862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/bdb1bc3927a14064015152d79438ed35de12d862"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/8a3155d0f54f9b1fbea0b1af662d00056726e1d6","verification":{"payload":"tree bdb1bc3927a14064015152d79438ed35de12d862\nparent 6bc30743f925425fa55bfaa07d33f192b516d84f\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1790853910 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790853910 +0100\n\nfix(shims): null a framed GET/HEAD body on a NextRequest''s Request input (#3649)\n\n* fix(shims): null a framed GET/HEAD body on a NextRequest''s Request input\n\nWorkers hands a GET/HEAD a non-null body when it is sent with one (or just\nContent-Length). #3621 dropped it from a Request init; the input side still\ncarried it into the NextRequest, so middleware, route handlers and edge API\nroutes saw a body Next.js never exposes (it nulls GET/HEAD bodies in\nNextRequestAdapter and the edge sandbox), and `new Request(url, request)` in\na route handler threw on the tracking Proxy.\n\nShare the GET/HEAD check with the init side and pass an explicit null body\nwhen the init keeps the input''s method and body. Also type the rebuilt init\ninstead of asserting it.\n\n* test(e2e): assert the route handler''s view of a framed HEAD body\n\nA HEAD response drops the JSON flags, so report request.body === null from\nthe route handler in a header and assert it.\n\n* test(e2e): frame the GET/HEAD probes with an empty chunked body\n\nSending body bytes the Worker never reads made wrangler dev''s ProxyWorker\nforwarding fetch fail on Linux CI, which wrangler treats as fatal, taking\nthe dev server down for the rest of the run. An empty chunked body still\nreaches the Worker as a non-null body (the tests fail without the fix) but\nleaves nothing unread on the connection.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvkMWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA46AQABvkucXFvONDNjLcQ7YQp/rT\ntoHpJ/pTiGEK2RdF2YnIemiXvh+hDekncfNCnnqmSu1kxKXKfEmGxkMSYahauRI/\nsLKlCHe47Tz7J/TfmUQ02dDMBDvblsZulCIIpEH1140SwN3fHESz59fRbd/912So\nXjeEOU92KCVzCzbATzqYDX38ehhzcr22aIbjAGOUjwQNIDbDdIDdKRapS/ANQuLs\nSmi2847OiCunQyRCEV99r+KKb7ImF6qhXL7lmaZLv2lrmO+XsreLJDTSI51WkCeN\nL0uHJjiYeFfPBxyHkCa3kO/r1zDLqsB+w26qfsKv2BDoXGGyGF3QCbwBMaBD6r/4\n8GkyxJ0ByiKLhCTwkSwevY0QkC/k6OWtnTikRntRTjEyvcRBsRcVa4zgimQYqtqr\ny0wy5kQh3YnOsbA3zUl05wbDvNDVXPzgMMlYDFhpG8FsNE+n/T80MgeM6a14JaH2\nfCSuxbsJ66CFXsyFl0dAVIQ1/5goEDX3A6suiaes1ESGUtsIRQaLQWFyvVoBU+zw\nL+JaKR3DoRQA3pqyJAc3vO8EMxOdfKoPVreh17shLdaMJDnBrMeQjNprQkWQRC3g\nD+dqtEKY8i1i/TnoGo2+CA16OrO62XZY+6rbtfinAiDgGIokp/gwZ6CXFwEsPvAs\ndL+rB6J8Q98h5gqzsFef\n=CygJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T11:25:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/8a3155d0f54f9b1fbea0b1af662d00056726e1d6","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDhhMzE1NWQwZjU0ZjliMWZiZWEwYjFhZjY2MmQwMDA1NjcyNmUxZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/6bc30743f925425fa55bfaa07d33f192b516d84f","sha":"6bc30743f925425fa55bfaa07d33f192b516d84f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/6bc30743f925425fa55bfaa07d33f192b516d84f"}],"sha":"8a3155d0f54f9b1fbea0b1af662d00056726e1d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/8a3155d0f54f9b1fbea0b1af662d00056726e1d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5855137?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ash1day/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ash1day/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ash1day/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ash1day/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ash1day","id":5855137,"login":"ash1day","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4NTUxMzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ash1day/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ash1day/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ash1day/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ash1day/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ash1day/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ash1day","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/6bc30743f925425fa55bfaa07d33f192b516d84f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:45:06Z","email":"y4ashida@gmail.com","name":"Yoshihiro Ashida"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:45:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(shims): drop a framed GET/HEAD body from a Request init in NextRequest (#3621)\n\n* fix(shims): drop a framed GET/HEAD body from a Request init in NextRequest\n\nWorkers hands a GET a non-null body whenever it carries Content-Length or\nTransfer-Encoding, including Content-Length: 0. Since #3612 passes a Request\ninit to the Request constructor, such a request made `new NextRequest(url,\nrequest)` throw (\"Request with a GET or HEAD method cannot have a body.\"): the\nconstructor reads the route handler''s tracking Proxy as a dictionary. Before\n#3612 the spread dropped the body, so this is a new 500.\n\nNext.js nulls GET/HEAD bodies before user code runs. Do the same: rebuild the\ninit from method, headers, cache, redirect, signal and cf, with an explicit\nnull body so Workers doesn''t inherit a body from the input Request.\n\n* fix(shims): keep integrity and fetcher when rebuilding a framed GET init\n\nworkerd reads fetcher and integrity from a dictionary init too, so the\nrebuilt init dropped them and a framed GET came out with a null fetcher\nwhere an unframed one keeps it.\n\n* fix(shims): copy every standard Request field when rebuilding a framed GET init\n\nDropping mode, credentials, referrer, referrerPolicy and keepalive changed\nthe rebuilt request and could make a valid one throw, e.g. only-if-cached\nwith same-origin mode falls back to cors.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","tree":{"sha":"5024cf7b822f91dfe35b8b5d1e17838af8703949","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/5024cf7b822f91dfe35b8b5d1e17838af8703949"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/6bc30743f925425fa55bfaa07d33f192b516d84f","verification":{"payload":"tree 5024cf7b822f91dfe35b8b5d1e17838af8703949\nparent 175b92f5a3658138d063970710c760344f6635e9\nauthor Yoshihiro Ashida <y4ashida@gmail.com> 1790847906 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790847906 +0100\n\nfix(shims): drop a framed GET/HEAD body from a Request init in NextRequest (#3621)\n\n* fix(shims): drop a framed GET/HEAD body from a Request init in NextRequest\n\nWorkers hands a GET a non-null body whenever it carries Content-Length or\nTransfer-Encoding, including Content-Length: 0. Since #3612 passes a Request\ninit to the Request constructor, such a request made `new NextRequest(url,\nrequest)` throw (\"Request with a GET or HEAD method cannot have a body.\"): the\nconstructor reads the route handler''s tracking Proxy as a dictionary. Before\n#3612 the spread dropped the body, so this is a new 500.\n\nNext.js nulls GET/HEAD bodies before user code runs. Do the same: rebuild the\ninit from method, headers, cache, redirect, signal and cf, with an explicit\nnull body so Workers doesn''t inherit a body from the input Request.\n\n* fix(shims): keep integrity and fetcher when rebuilding a framed GET init\n\nworkerd reads fetcher and integrity from a dictionary init too, so the\nrebuilt init dropped them and a framed GET came out with a null fetcher\nwhere an unframed one keeps it.\n\n* fix(shims): copy every standard Request field when rebuilding a framed GET init\n\nDropping mode, credentials, referrer, referrerPolicy and keepalive changed\nthe rebuilt request and could make a valid one throw, e.g. only-if-cached\nwith same-origin mode falls back to cors.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: James <james@eli.cx>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqviuiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPqMQALEbtNF4qBZcCFES7JF/OUCv\nhlBih4NgZGPCKQJ3QWH0xvkJ9rKJ8KRNWCz2Gs2nb7RCIibfrc0+OTqMYIJZ9ljQ\nRy0VR63w6ZCjSv2LBLOyHvqfAVS6P4EzHkaEAGRz4OBmCkFLlEQkpJZQpldfgD6Z\ncm9eocNWLdafhTx0+MGi28OEBfstD3G0u0WCwREFBkh/WRiu/Wo7ysiM3WZDfV+2\nCVzz+naPGR1FlJx/3WWRyL/P6j+zpPPoe++pV6k9b7GCSMyipabZMcmROtdJznIN\nZx5UBiprJGJ5FmuSs6Z9L797rQiZslmz0B0AuBCpoHHxIsFV3SqDyak3at5NSSqJ\nlw0IDP0fdErzIB9pweNTkRmhARSZqJeU6lw5F+Vt/5uOCzeKk5UsgPyNh4LMxTcN\nrqpa/xOIVN1yJ3AVmY2kljuZvElVubC5GQ+N8xst8dFlwAHYd94fiv7IVz4wArq3\nM/yT2KC6v1rkay+vqtIm0ObYJE1tWhjFVbikoU2zgTifr1SErAwv7ck7/wvUiB7u\nilt+rE7C8YLIdu0I4RXHCPGDuucmdeVqkZ5F00p3WBCgCdnuzjO15os2CdtlahWt\ntIym3cPwa8BgermOiP8qAliBfqCLw6rY+/cVNBIbqOaUeZpTYpjfRcmbD8kKOIXr\nMUyNN0iVyqouUnCXl6WP\n=IeM6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T09:45:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/6bc30743f925425fa55bfaa07d33f192b516d84