x/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/28bec45711ce4fdc0e26b1ebea3945e20d1f968b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:54:36Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T13:54:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(build): skip the scan-time typeof window fold when it cannot change imports (#3596)\n\n* perf(build): skip the scan-time typeof window fold when it cannot change imports\n\nplugin-rsc''s import-scan builds reduce every module to its import\nspecifiers, and static import declarations cannot sit inside a foldable\nbranch. The scan-time typeof window / process.browser fold can therefore\nonly change the scanned graph by pruning a dynamic import with a static\nspecifier or an import.meta.glob call.\n\nGate the fold in scan builds with a regex prefilter for dynamic import\nand import.meta syntax, then use the parser''s native module record\n(dynamicImports / importMetas) to bail before materializing and walking\nthe ESTree when no such expression exists. Plain import.meta.url and\nimport.meta.env reads are ignored because they never name a module.\n\n* fix(build): keep phase imports in the scan-time typeof window prefilter\n\nimport.source() and import.defer() carry static specifiers that scan-strip\nkeeps, so a fold can prune them. Widen the prefilter to match them and rename\nthe module-record check so the two gate stages are easier to tell apart.\n\n* fix(build): only skip the scan-time typeof window fold with native define folding\n\nWrite-less builds that are not plugin-RSC scans rely on the custom fold on\ntoolchains before Vite 8.1.4 / Rolldown 1.1.4, so keep the full fold there.\n\n* fix(typeof-window): admit any import. member in the scan prefilter\n\n* fix(build): keep the scan-time typeof window fold for foldable requests, TS import types and unbundled clients\n\n- Treat a dynamic or phase import whose request contains a fold target\n  (e.g. `import(typeof window)`) as scan-observable, since folding can turn it\n  into a literal the scan lexer keeps.\n- Treat `import(` in TypeScript sources as scan-observable: the module record\n  omits `import(\"x\")` types that the scan lexer still sees in unstripped files.\n- Only skip the fold for bundled environments; Vite''s define transform does\n  not run for unbundled client environments.\n\n* fix(typeof-window): keep scan fold for any dynamic import and key cache by gate mode","tree":{"sha":"1023c5aa566f8d52093804f7e0de211113244ff4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/1023c5aa566f8d52093804f7e0de211113244ff4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/28bec45711ce4fdc0e26b1ebea3945e20d1f968b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1023c5aa566f8d52093804f7e0de211113244ff4\nparent 1633676f2796c3579f828102a98214181861303c\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1790776476 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790776476 +0100\n\nperf(build): skip the scan-time typeof window fold when it cannot change imports (#3596)\n\n* perf(build): skip the scan-time typeof window fold when it cannot change imports\n\nplugin-rsc''s import-scan builds reduce every module to its import\nspecifiers, and static import declarations cannot sit inside a foldable\nbranch. The scan-time typeof window / process.browser fold can therefore\nonly change the scanned graph by pruning a dynamic import with a static\nspecifier or an import.meta.glob call.\n\nGate the fold in scan builds with a regex prefilter for dynamic import\nand import.meta syntax, then use the parser''s native module record\n(dynamicImports / importMetas) to bail before materializing and walking\nthe ESTree when no such expression exists. Plain import.meta.url and\nimport.meta.env reads are ignored because they never name a module.\n\n* fix(build): keep phase imports in the scan-time typeof window prefilter\n\nimport.source() and import.defer() carry static specifiers that scan-strip\nkeeps, so a fold can prune them. Widen the prefilter to match them and rename\nthe module-record check so the two gate stages are easier to tell apart.\n\n* fix(build): only skip the scan-time typeof window fold with native define folding\n\nWrite-less builds that are not plugin-RSC scans rely on the custom fold on\ntoolchains before Vite 8.1.4 / Rolldown 1.1.4, so keep the full fold there.\n\n* fix(typeof-window): admit any import. member in the scan prefilter\n\n* fix(build): keep the scan-time typeof window fold for foldable requests, TS import types and unbundled clients\n\n- Treat a dynamic or phase import whose request contains a fold target\n  (e.g. `import(typeof window)`) as scan-observable, since folding can turn it\n  into a literal the scan lexer keeps.\n- Treat `import(` in TypeScript sources as scan-observable: the module record\n  omits `import(\"x\")` types that the scan lexer still sees in unstripped files.\n- Only skip the fold for bundled environments; Vite''s define transform does\n  not run for unbundled client environments.\n\n* fix(typeof-window): keep scan fold for any dynamic import and key cache by gate mode","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvRScCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzg8QAG6EoDXy1IvatXVEWT8XRKoq\nZKDXeznHC0xcvBcHr5gKI2EWw4M0cvihPYBEn0aB2Sm0Unw8XfWQbljHozTmc9aQ\ny0htJbnYEve/ebZI++QxNARZRspKjYEa9uZTYo0jB4RFVwyR3XsRo9kDu34QsCQh\nW+licPY/WHWCtBPM1ony9UpAitjQ0gK23yg1BwoEFDYT0MRMRbupyzuyUad1zrxT\nCWbuasS+9UvvBSC7msWWSmHMlJDl1JOhPVqQIMkFXVJJDZ8H+nNv/JgIRZydfhdL\nJIEzswOMU0qSmvI/jVJ08SHpKYTcfg7tp5CUCvVfKNWV7tce7/DONbPr1S9U4MtN\nU0F7835BdszHHq8quB4GRd2uQ4Guw56BYfSkZEjy4TjEKXtNZZJUkrGY6D84DKLl\nvlLem/HE6vWeqJut/C77sDKCCYLeZAf6HJ6jGoaKpAjXGMHC8IvEyXqPzi24Ho1e\nujW/sCr9vpm085QjDrbEnIiGJ8E8I+41aiXsXlNRfjbtZNUr09W0Qmb7lBwS3i54\nyENaGvbc9KvFqFwrFUj4JeQBacwGwfgoKMGVLndpX1nI7o/uGxg3