vatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/3e038ddea7db5cfca83edd901fc1195e549a3fbd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:01:43Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:01:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(build): skip unused sourcemaps in vinext source transforms (#3552)\n\nmagicStringTransformResult eagerly generated a high-resolution sourcemap\nfor every changed module, including multi-MB dependencies, even in builds\nwhere build.sourcemap is off and the map is discarded.\n\nGenerate the map lazily on first read, and have the transforms that run\nover dependency code (ignore-dynamic-requests, import-meta-url,\ntypeof-window-scan, og-harfbuzz, og-inline-fetch-assets) return\n`map: null` when the build environment has sourcemaps disabled, matching\nVite''s own `config.build.sourcemap ? s.generateMap(...) : null`. The\ndecision is made per call because these transform caches are shared\nacross environments. Dev and builds with sourcemaps enabled are unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"d3b2c1b4756054f22e55fe24a176787f886d92e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/d3b2c1b4756054f22e55fe24a176787f886d92e5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/3e038ddea7db5cfca83edd901fc1195e549a3fbd","verification":{"payload":"tree d3b2c1b4756054f22e55fe24a176787f886d92e5\nparent 44ef71c49bd9edeb1b21891a5530dc8cfd4b3bc7\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1790694103 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790694103 +0100\n\nperf(build): skip unused sourcemaps in vinext source transforms (#3552)\n\nmagicStringTransformResult eagerly generated a high-resolution sourcemap\nfor every changed module, including multi-MB dependencies, even in builds\nwhere build.sourcemap is off and the map is discarded.\n\nGenerate the map lazily on first read, and have the transforms that run\nover dependency code (ignore-dynamic-requests, import-meta-url,\ntypeof-window-scan, og-harfbuzz, og-inline-fetch-assets) return\n`map: null` when the build environment has sourcemaps disabled, matching\nVite''s own `config.build.sourcemap ? s.generateMap(...) : null`. The\ndecision is made per call because these transform caches are shared\nacross environments. Dev and builds with sourcemaps enabled are unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu9LXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlHwQAILys6cGsBg/6SjUl+ytMZYE\ngvTj63yTXIOpXlORLhRcSFq/yZzULWFv+Nbaulv00iEDf6ISAs4n9EeOoPWcYMnx\nEsaugoM0qNAnqE/3QSGjTbn3AQqGoHRUlKFk/p8h7eK4Z6iPbwvFZlTm0BR+YYp6\n3O7tsGFL4q4g9Iu9Z6YxQnE/jyllkA+uSONk9SeoKxaI0zEkIdMyqdbfvWDWVSvs\nFuyiUewTyObK2KGSuVqRauKG/Rxk+kSlx4Ym2DI3JG/fNBKRVVfsXnQXHUMmcme/\nkuliK/l5ZNu05K+1iZZoJDybHOE7eZFQmGBdpAuzjt1TTWirUSv9TYyH4LkVzjQ6\nUJAFScfEPq/LeFT4TEzT8DFpwEoo9UXXJkMUOuUWZ1NrPQQnkdBpu1TzE/sX293u\nC7tFEooyj/2RBTpnFrNCrxrYuFnEdyib8ECiEWiAV2Cuveh8YhYlPmzkkSm6h3yT\noiDyjZDG6Tcck8MQApKB93kTvV/ernJdByqbezcYgcAdgk7b0YqJaDC56ttebr4B\nyTjzDS/qAlbXG4zFVSlgsV2tUBNn/ZdJgiDWF/W1fzL6JajxCFrA6iJwDXxVGYci\nBXdaJsRftF2GUg0+I2JVZSI5BPS3BrHINk3lZbWZnIvtmZIl7j1kr+p6EjTdE5T1\nfP0rlk6attnISfzfjft2\n=NJPn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T15:01:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/3e038ddea7db5cfca83edd901fc1195e549a3fbd","node_id":"C_kwDORXYnQNoAKDNlMDM4ZGRlYTdkYjVjZmNhODNlZGQ5MDFmYzExOTVlNTQ5YTNmYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/commit/44ef71c49bd9edeb1b21891a5530dc8cfd4b3bc7","sha":"44ef71c49bd9edeb1b21891a5530dc8cfd4b3bc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/44ef71c49bd9edeb1b21891a5530dc8cfd4b3bc7"}],"sha":"3e038ddea7db5cfca83edd901fc1195e549a3fbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/3e038ddea7db5cfca83edd901fc1195e549a3fbd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10815538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/james-elicx","id":10815538,"login":"james-elicx","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODE1NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/james-elicx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/commits/44ef71c49bd9edeb1b21891a5530dc8cfd4b3bc7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:25:22Z","email":"james@eli.cx","name":"James Anderson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:25:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(build): avoid repeated realpath calls in middleware export validation (#3553)\n\n* perf(build): avoid repeated realpath calls in middleware export validation\n\nvinext:validate-middleware-exports called realpathSync on both the module\nid and the middleware path for every transformed module. Resolve the\nmiddleware path once in config(), next to middlewarePath, so it is\nrefreshed whenever the config is resolved again (including\nserver.restart() with an inline plugin). Module ids reuse the\ncanonicalizePageTransformPath memo, which is owned by the vinext() instance\nand never invalidated, as for the page transforms. Skip virtual ids with a\nnative hook filter, since middleware is never a virtual module.\n\nAdd dev-server tests for a symlinked proxy.ts, including after a server\nrestart.\n\n* fix(build): clear canonical path memo on config resolution\n\nWith resolve.preserveSymlinks, Vite keeps the logical module id, so a\nrealpath memoized before server.restart() could skip middleware export\nvalidation after proxy.ts became a symlink.","tree":{"sha":"1f486980549e469bf5f7b59dd8f57b855be3785a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/trees/1f486980549e469bf5f7b59dd8f57b855be3785a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cloudflare/vinext/git/commits/44ef71c49bd9edeb1b21891a5530dc8cfd4b3bc7","verification":{"payload":"tree 1f486980549e469bf5f7b59dd8f57b855be3785a\nparent 36606eabd8b27a4c963278154768f5381a45573e\nauthor James Anderson <james@eli.cx> 1790691922 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790691922 +0100\n\nperf(build): avoid repeated realpath calls in middleware export validation (#3553)\n\n* perf(build): avoid repeated realpath calls in middleware export validation\n\nvinext:validate-middleware-exports called realpathSync on both the module\nid and the middleware path for every transformed module. Resolve the\nmiddleware path once in config(), next to middlewarePath, so it is\nrefreshed whenever the config is resolved again (including\nserver.restart() with an inline plugin). Module ids reuse the\ncanonicalizePageTransformPath memo, which is owned by the vinext() instance\nand never invalidated, as for the page transforms. Skip virtual ids with a\nnative hook filter, since middleware is never a virtual module.\n\nAdd dev-server tests for a symlinked proxy.ts, including after a server\nrestart.\n\n* fix(build): clear canonical path memo on config resolution\n\nWith resolve.preserveSymlinks, Vite keeps the logical module id, so a\nrealpath memoized before server.restart() could skip middleware export\nvalidation after proxy.ts became a symlink.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqu8pSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm6kQAE7wJL8CDxu6jsBRj+PjjgIq\n/M2uQD8DALFwni01ws2ZChQ9a/PtzS0VTZJhwvBAh/rlKFgLLhMwpv+gQ16NIe+h\nLhSh74nAxry1uGXBdy2/NoRFG/alqvWxFXsgcl5rR7ISrzxRO36ApvigGqvpjTWP\ns1AAeyWfvDVOd4y03gKKgZmxI6MdmF1AgOPKR2CEPJAThbpRABfgKdcF5U1tTfRn\n/t/MVL+rd8q+yqztgJboDYbo5Wc4Cx5uYbvTpA+/Rm5QBFGM7wpO1H3LlaiJtGon\nJzoBNwoeunRqm5pAmCc/gZaXYp5+V4NTz0tefl6wp3u3gX4qN9yhsUxIONPiwMWA\nPeSNFvOBlgEgfKpNaiFJ2bv246Q82SsJm/p/GozzkHTWl9kMOn046hFcbvBbZnx/\nZ9q2YANfu+qY62nwekZVtcwzhXaGxIY3cuIZWC0uaiXHuTFqM4MZgPuD+XRSUwqZ\nhF/o2aRBrNiAgSXZ1Z