alidDevIO/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalidDevIO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalidDevIO/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WalidDevIO","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WalidDevIO/traefik2consul-agent/commits/2bf2b989b7400ce02215c6a16600daf7b0e8bf54/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:32:27Z","email":"admin@walidlab.dev","name":"WalidDevIO"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T20:32:27Z","email":"admin@walidlab.dev","name":"WalidDevIO"},"message":"feat: add multi-instance support and cluster management API/UI\n\n- **Multi-instance support**: The agent can now aggregate multiple Traefik L2 instances simultaneously using the `TRAEFIK_INSTANCES` configuration or via the runtime API.\n- **Cluster mode (default)**: Added a new `cluster` mode that runs a Flask-based REST API alongside the sync engine.\n- **Management Dashboard**: Introduced a clean, sober web UI (served on port 8099) to monitor sync status and dynamically add/remove Traefik instances without restarting the agent.\n- **Dynamic Configuration**: Instances managed via the API update the synchronization engine at runtime thread-safely. Added `DISABLE_UI` option for environments needing only the API.\n- **Refactoring**: Renamed `node_name` to `cluster_name` for accuracy in aggregation mode. Services are now registered with an `<INSTANCE>` suffix to avoid collisions.\n- **Environment & Docker**: Streamlined `Dockerfile`, `.env.template`, and `compose.yml`. Integrated a `test.compose.yaml` with a working test stack.\n- **Documentation**: Updated `README.md` with the new architecture diagram, environment variables, multi-instance configuration, and a strict DMZ/public exposure security warning.","tree":{"sha":"7a9b00b1bdf6be8c45a76dfa888e44e7517ab60a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WalidDevIO/traefik2consul-agent/git/trees/7a9