ype":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/manologargue","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/manologargue/process-mining-charts/commits/e3ed31fd4f606edc4ede502bb7a2b570355e42c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-13T09:07:40Z","email":"65821656+manologargue@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Manuel García"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-13T09:07:40Z","email":"65821656+manologargue@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Manuel García"},"message":"feat: async DFG computation via Celery\n\nReplace synchronous pm4py execution with a Celery task so the Flask\nworker thread is freed immediately on each request.\n\n- POST /api/dfg-from-rows returns 202 + task_id instead of blocking\n- New GET /api/task/<task_id> endpoint for polling (pending/ready/error)\n- celery_app consolidated into tasks.py (no separate module)\n- config.py adds CELERY_BROKER_URL / CELERY_RESULT_BACKEND env vars\n- requirements.txt adds celery[redis]>=5.3\n- conftest.py: Celery eager + in-memory backend for tests (no broker needed)\n- test_api.py: post_dfg follows two-step flow transparently\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"624968ec88838a345d2019227752a65c29870044","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/manologargue/process-mining-charts/git/trees/624968ec88838a345d2019227752a65c29870044"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/manologargue/process-mining-charts/git/commits/e3ed31fd4f606edc4ede502bb7a2b570355e42c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65821656?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manologargue/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manologargue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manologargue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/manologargue/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id